INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('0d106081-3790-4438-99d3-435c27ee6898'), 'Maurice Binder designed the gun barrel opening at the last minute, by pointing a pinhole camera through a real gun barrel. The actor in the sequence is not Sir Sean Connery, but stuntman Bob Simmons. Connery didn''t film the sequence until Thunderball (1965)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c133852-0bb7-4887-86cc-7e5983e5d955'), 'This was chosen to be the inaugural movie in the James Bond film franchise as the plot of the source novel was the most straightforward. It had only one major location (Jamaica) and only one big special effects set piece', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7c378f4c-6c6f-424f-9317-dc0ee3d4fefe'), 'In a 1987 interview, Sir Sean Connery said he wore two hairpieces in this film. He began losing his hair when he was 17, and he began wearing a hairpiece in 1958. The Bond filmmakers used varying techniques to make the most of what was left. By the time of Goldfinger (1964), Connery''s hair was too thin, so various toupees were used for his last Bond outings', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3f7023b9-a3fe-4287-872d-83a991c40691'), 'As detailed as Dr. No''s underwater lair was, one vital element was nearly forgotten: background plates of fish swimming in the sea to be added to the thick-glass window. The necessary film was quickly found among library footage the day before it was to be filmed. When it turned out the footage featured extreme closeups of fish, it was decided to have Dr. No explain that the window works as a magnifying glass', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b194ff81-70ef-40b4-9d09-d0359f46f81a'), 'A Francisco de Goya painting of the Duke of Wellington, stolen in August 1961 from London''s National Gallery, is found on an easel next to the stairs in Dr. No''s dining area, which is why Bond stops to notice it as he passes it while going up the stairs. It was recovered in 1965. When this movie first came out, British audiences laughed upon seeing the Goya, knowing it had been stolen. According to director Terence Young, the idea for the stolen painting prop came from the film''s Irish co-screenwriter Johanna Harwood. A clip of this scene is featured in The Duke (2020), which dramatized the theft', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6321c038-ba93-4c96-9a84-f67c5bf5f3c3'), 'Much is made of Ursula Andress''s first appearance in the film - but in the novel, Honey Ryder emerges from the sea completely naked. When she spots Bond, she drops her shells so that one hand can cover her crotch, while the other hand hides her broken nose. This would have been impossible to depict in a big studio film at the time, due to the Hays Code censorship rules, which led to the use of Honey''s iconic white bikini. Even when censorship attitudes softened somewhat over the following years, the James Bond series has generally stayed away from depictions of nudity to keep the movies accessible to broad audiences', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fc9e7e60-314f-4a76-973f-b4a6596d2a2d'), 'Ian Fleming didn''t originally like the casting of Sir Sean Connery as James Bond, as Bond was English, whereas Connery was Scottish; Bond was from an upper-class background while Connery came from a working-class background, and where Bond was refined and educated, he felt Connery was too rugged. After seeing this movie however, Fleming softened and decided that Connery was perfectly cast. In the novel "On Her Majesty''s Secret Service", Bond was revealed to have Scottish ancestry, and Bond''s girlfriend Theresa "Tracy" Vicenzo was described with Ursula Andress'' details. Ironically, Fleming initially thought the young Roger Moore (who eventually took over the James Bond role from Connery) would be ideal in all respects, but Moore wasn''t available', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d6416392-daa2-424f-b60a-fe76724fad94'), 'Sir Sean Connery''s suits for this film were made by Saville Row tailor Anthony Sinclair. Sinclair stated that a truly great bespoke suit would be able to stand up to a good deal of abuse - such as grabbing by the lapels - and still look great afterwards. To prove his point, Connery was asked to sleep in his suit. When he woke up the next morning he was stunned to see that it looked fantastic', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cfe51e2e-2e31-4115-b055-ea3fa22bc8fc'), 'Honey Ryder emerging from the sea is one of the most iconic scenes in the James Bond film franchise, and something that Ursula Andress is famed for to this day. Andress admits bewilderment: "It''s a mystery. All I did was wear this bikini, not even a small one, and whoosh! Overnight, I made it."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d2b0dd8e-87e4-4b7b-935a-7188d74c9844'), 'After viewing this movie, James Bond creator Ian Fleming reportedly described it as being, "Dreadful. Simply dreadful."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8713a646-b44b-4520-9295-90772c8e2f0b'), 'When Bond enters his apartment at the beginning, and finds Sylvia Trench playing golf, she was originally supposed to be nude, but the censors objected to this', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('33b2e4f3-955b-45bf-8f7b-ca2740d5e80a'), 'Dolores Keator was given the role of Strangways'' secretary because she owned the house in which the crew were shooting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab37a686-2a6d-4b40-8942-85feb896ea9c'), 'Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli, the original producers of the James Bond movies, cast Sir Sean Connery because they liked how he was a big, tough-looking man who nonetheless moved gracefully "like a cat"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('25c0d6b2-ed2d-4a2e-adf9-7ff65d6e6ae3'), 'Ursula Andress and Sir Sean Connery fought over a record player so they could practice the song Honey and Bond sing together, "Under the Mango Tree", which is notable for being the only instance of Bond singing in the entire film series. Recalling the incident, Andress said "[Connery] didn''t need the practice, because he sings much better than I do. I can''t carry a tune." Nikki Van der Zyl ended up dubbing for Andress as her singing voice', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('58e17f8a-94a5-4568-9d9a-b96a42734e15'), 'During the initial briefing, M says that he recently was put in charge of MI7. Bernard Lee originally said MI6 during the take, but this has been overdubbed, possibly for fear of offending the real-life organization. In later Bond movies, however, 007 clearly works for MI6', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc2c10a3-5b1d-42f1-9b14-8415db5f497d'), 'The first scene Sir Sean Connery filmed as James Bond is the sequence in the Kingston Airport where he passes a female photographer and holds his hat up in front of his face. The filming date was January 16, 1962', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec75de40-6990-4cd8-b55f-f5181b6238bf'), 'The armorer who gives Bond his Walther PPK at the start of the movie is Major Boothroyd, who in the next movie, From Russia with Love (1963) was played by Desmond Llewelyn. Beginning with Goldfinger (1964), the "armorer" would forever be known as "Q" for "Quartermaster". The character of Boothroyd first appeared in Ian Fleming''s original Dr. No novel. He was named for Geoffrey Boothroyd, who wrote to Fleming complaining about Bond''s use of a Beretta in the early Bond books and recommending Bond use a Walther PPK instead. The real-life Boothroyd appears in a vintage featurette included on the Blu-ray, demonstrating the relative effectiveness of Bond''s Beretta, PPK, and his own favorite gun, the Ruger .44 Magnum. This detail was included in the novel, and later included in this movie, establishing part of the Bond legend. Q is based loosely on Charles Fraser-Smith, who designed spy gadgets called "Q-devices" named for Q-ships, the Royal Navy''s disguised warships of World War I for MI6', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1586606d-1859-4a52-a0f8-86bc00d946b4'), 'Author Ian Fleming wanted his cousin Sir Christopher Lee to play the role of Dr. No. Lee appeared as Francisco Scaramanga in the Bond movie The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), and also played Dr. Fu Manchu - the character that inspired Fleming to create Dr. No - in several movies. Fleming also asked Noël Coward to play the part of Dr. No. Coward turned down the part by replying with a telegram that read, "Dr. No? No! No! No!" One of Coward''s objections was having to wear metal hands. Max von Sydow turned down the part in order to play Jesus Christ in The Greatest Story Ever Told (1965), and would finally play a Bond villain in Never Say Never Again (1983). The role went to Joseph Wiseman, the only early Bond villain not to have his voice dubbed by another actor', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cc56aa00-125d-4bd9-b191-562ae2ce9303'), 'Due to the low budget, only one sound editor was hired, normally there are two, for sound effects and dialogue. Many pieces of scenery were made in cheaper ways, with M''s office featuring cardboard paintings and a door covered in a leather-like plastic. The room where Dent meets Dr. No cost only £745 to build, and the aquarium in Dr. No''s base consisted of magnified stock footage of goldfish. Furthermore, when art director Syd Cain found out his name was not in the credits, producer Albert R. Broccoli gave him a golden pen to compensate, saying that he did not want to spend money making the credits again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2bf246e6-c449-4d9c-8216-ed8d4aaf8eca'), 'Sir Sean Connery was so nervous during filming that he said "Connery, Sean Connery", according to Eunice Gayson who played Sylvia Trench. While filming the scene where Bond introduces himself to her, he kept fluffing the now famous line by giving his real name. He came out with other permutations like "Sean Bond" and "James Connery". The director, Sir Terence Young told Gayson to take him away for a drink or two to calm his nerves', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('12225c2a-1cec-4271-8bf3-5f3b8189fee6'), 'Ursula Andress'' salary for her appearance in this movie was $6,000 which is about $55,000 in 2022', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4629a6cb-7732-45ff-b73a-f9bb97a1fab2'), 'Although there are persistent rumors that Ursula Andress was naked in the shower scene to decontaminate her of radiation, closer inspection reveals that she is wearing a nude-colored one-piece swimsuit', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1d04cbe1-7821-4f88-ad6b-60e62c14bb4a'), 'In this first Bond movie, two other people - both of them Bond girls - introduce themselves "the Bond way". On the Caribbean beach, Ursula Andress gives her name as "Ryder... Honey Ryder". Also, in the casino at the beginning - before Sir Sean Connery has uttered more than a handful of words in the movie - Eunice Gayson presents herself as "Trench, Sylvia Trench". When Connery then replies, "Bond, James Bond", it is to poke sweet fun at the young lady, by mimicking her cadence. It is quite likely, therefore, that, at the time, there was no intention of having 007 use that exact type of presentation again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('71deb84a-4451-4367-a20c-d76927ddd470'), 'United Artists were reportedly not happy with the film and opened it with little publicity but by word of mouth it earned an enormous profit causing a chastised United Artists to more than double the budget for the next film "From Russia with Love"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8c5d16d-de01-41a9-a5b2-ed105380bf74'), 'At first, Eunice Gayson was to play Miss Moneypenny and Lois Maxwell was to play Sylvia Trench, but they switched roles. Director Terence Young said that when he looked at Gayson she seemed to smell of sex, whereas Maxwell seemed to smell of soap', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4ea80832-8005-4afe-a17b-33967bae8396'), 'The filming of Honey Ryder walking out of the sea and meeting James Bond was shot at Laughing Waters Beach on the Laughing Water Estate, owned by Mrs. Minnie Simpson in Ocho Rios, St. Ann, Jamaica. Mrs. Simpson had been a fan of Ian Fleming''s James Bond novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('44da1f03-b9e4-4788-971d-38291cb2b2f5'), 'Owing to the limited wardrobe budget, Lois Maxwell wore her own clothes as Miss Moneypenny, as did other actors in similarly small parts', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6b74cdf8-c398-48ef-aa28-75d465353599'), 'On June 20, 1961, United Artists agreed to finance this movie after many studios rejected it on the grounds of "too British" and "too blatantly sexual"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8fca45d8-3213-46c5-87e1-8b08afa39555'), 'Bernard Lee was cast one day before studio filming started. According to Terence Young, he got the part of M because everyone else was away', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c1257ed0-20cc-4a14-af9b-8b8785ae11e8'), 'In 2019, Cary Grant''s daughter Jennifer Grant revealed that her father later regretted turning down the role of Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a8b4aaef-5907-43bd-a26a-b18f1d737a5e'), 'The first of three times James Bond''s apartment is shown; the others are Live and Let Die (1973) and Spectre (2015)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6686daae-7174-4f17-bc92-684107a8f682'), 'Sir Sean Connery is the godfather of Ursula Andress'' son, Dimitri Hamlin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('941a32c9-15e9-4ed1-8530-38066997f0dc'), 'In the source novel, the full names of Honey Ryder and Dr. No are Honeychile Rider and Dr. Julius No. Honeychile is the last surviving member of an old sugar plantation family, and was raised by the family servants. The freelance photographer is named Annabel Chung. Puss-Feller''s name means he wrestled an octopus, but this movie changed this to an alligator, rendering the name meaningless. The Professor was not named Dent, and was not a villain. Strangways and Quarrel were old friends of Bond from the Live and Let Die novel. There was no evil chauffeur and no Felix Leiter, the latter was in other novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a13dc45d-c00c-41eb-9645-a4487a08dee4'), 'In the original novel, the scene in which Bond escapes "imprisonment" worked a little differently. Dr. No actually had an obstacle course set up to challenge Bond. At the end of the obstacle course, there was a seaside cage, with a giant squid inside. This movie altered and toned down all of this, and the "obstacle course" idea got lost in the translation from novel to movie. In the following scene, a sequence involving Honey Ryder being tied to the ground and attacked by a swarm of crabs was scrapped, because many of the crustaceans arrived frozen, dead, and damaged. In the movie, as shown, water was the threat instead', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('09289153-3d1f-4f64-8fe9-903709ea18d3'), 'Two weeks before filming was due to start, the part of Honey Ryder was still to be cast. The producers then saw a photograph of a then-unknown Ursula Andress in a wet t-shirt, and offered her the part without even meeting her. Some sources claim that the photograph featured Andress in a wet t-shirt competition', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bdabd80e-3c8d-46bc-a53c-47bdd3b9ee83'), 'This is the only Bond film where James Bond never leaves British territory; he is only seen in London and Jamaica', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ea83fde-6ac9-48a7-8b82-0ee72bd9acad'), 'The white bikini worn by Ursula Andress in the movie was sold by her at Christie''s Auctions in London on February 14, 2001 for £35,000. It was purchased by Robert Earl of Planet Hollywood, and with commission and tax fees, the total was actually around £41,000. Before the auction, the bikini had been estimated to fetch £40,000. The bikini top originally was made from an underwire bra sold from a Saks Fifth Avenue in New York City. Costume designer Tessa Welborn ordered three of the bras, covering them in cotton, and refined the design. The belt seen in the movie was made from a white webbing Army belt, with brass fittings and a scabbard. After this movie''s release, bikini swimwear sales skyrocketed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e532125-17cf-4be8-91e3-f3bd9edc5dae'), 'The novel "Dr. No" was Ian Fleming''s follow-up to From Russia with Love (1963). The movie scene of Bond getting his Walther is very similar to the corresponding scene in the book: M says that Bond''s Beretta jammed on his last job, referring to Bond''s mission to recover the Spektor (called "Lektor" in the movie) decoder in the novel "From Russia with Love", specifically its final scene in which Bond encountered Rosa Klebb. In that book scene, Klebb (in contrast to the film) managed to poison Bond by kicking him with a venom-tipped blade hidden in her shoe; a few moments later Bond started feeling ill and collapsed; in that point, the novel ends with a cliffhanger. In the beginning of the novel "Dr. No", it is revealed that René Mathis saved Bond''s life by performing CPR, keeping him alive till Bond received a medical treatment; this passage was omitted from the film "Dr. No", since the order of the films is reversed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b905d844-26f1-48a9-bfb1-dca24887dfc5'), 'A sequence extracted from the final cut had Dr. No forcing Bond to radio Felix Leiter, telling him that he had discovered nothing of any interest on Crab Key, in return for a less painful death for both Bond and Ryder', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('027a5834-e991-4a87-8ec2-98fe07896060'), 'The movie''s line "Bond. James Bond", was voted as the number twenty-two movie quote by the American Film Institute, and as number fifty-one of "The 100 Greatest Movie Lines" by Premiere', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('52e1718a-819a-4c01-b6c1-e4c42e491363'), 'First feature film filmed on-location in Jamaica, although the production crew was British. At the time of filming, Jamaica was part of the West Indies Federation, and a British Crown Colony. Jamaica became independent from the United Kingdom on August 6, 1962, just two months prior to the release of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3c2943c0-0ea1-4afa-9023-c6454319166c'), 'Contrary to popular belief, "Bond, James Bond" is NOT the first line he says. The first line he says is "I admire your courage, miss...", then he says the line, when his face is shown', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2c7db398-f804-478e-8304-041052938c91'), 'This movie won a Golden Globe Award for Ursula Andress as Best Newcomer in 1964', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b774d195-0798-49dd-9334-23bfa459c1a2'), 'Julie Christie was almost cast as Honey Ryder, but Albert R. Broccoli reportedly thought her breasts were too small', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('900dd8b7-7323-46cb-a04a-d0394e271d3c'), 'A deleted scene featured Honey Ryder waiting in her room in the finale, armed with a bottle of booze. When Bond arrives, she collapses into his arms and Bond catches both her and the bottle. With a manly dash, he pops the cork from the bottle with his teeth, takes a good belt, throws the bottle away and sweeps Ryder into his arms, carrying her to safety', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('870c7a33-8fd2-4c9b-a696-175639f9ff6e'), 'Author Ian Fleming served in British Naval Intelligence during World War II and was acquainted with David Niven, then a Major with the British Commandos. Niven was Fleming''s first choice to play James Bond. In fact, Fleming referred to Niven by name in the novel "You Only Live Twice", the only real actor ever to be mentioned in a Bond novel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c7cd6fe7-50ea-4878-b392-821a6f6745f3'), 'Harry Saltzman picked Joseph Wiseman for the title role because of his performance in Detective Story (1951). The actor had special make-up applied to evoke Dr. No''s Chinese heritage', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8eb56e6d-659b-44b2-9b0a-b321695bed3f'), 'Ursula Andress hated filming the scene where Bond, Ryder, and Quarrel confront the "Dragon" tank, as the marshes and swamps stank badly', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('67624c1a-a6b9-4d9f-9df4-8b641709ba33'), 'This James Bond film features Jamaica as a major filming location. Five of the actual original James Bond novels and short stories written by Ian Fleming at the Goldeneye estate in this country featured Jamaica as a setting. They were (in order): The novel ''Live and Let Die'' (1954); the novel ''Dr. No'' (1958); the short story ''For Your Eyes Only'' (1960); the novel ''The Man with the Golden Gun'' (1965); and the short story ''Octopussy'' (1966)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9aa8c957-90f8-400e-acbf-8289a66e9b42'), 'Ursula Andress returned to Jamaica for the first time since making this movie in 1996 to appear as the guest of honor at an official James Bond Festival', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0bcb0f7-c4f7-401c-994c-babcab4c5d8e'), 'John Stears was asked to help with the miniatures. He had only a budget of £1,000 for the effect of the destruction of Dr. No''s fortress. In the next Bond outing, Stears took over as special effects supervisor', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ba3d7fb4-77ef-44e6-8fb7-32ad83037f04'), 'The world premiere was held on October 5, 1962 at the London Pavilion, Piccadilly Circus, London. It was attended by Sir Sean Connery, Zena Marshall, and Ian Fleming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5671cb4a-d3ab-4a41-bc24-3730ba04d24a'), 'This was the first James Bond movie, but Sir Sean Connery was not the first James Bond. That honor belongs to Barry Nelson, who played Bond in Climax! (1954) season one, episode three, Casino Royale (1954)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('81d915fd-9465-4d02-b553-6950ff2ead3f'), 'The scene where Bond uses a pillow-trick to fool Professor Dent is taken from the book "The Spy Who Loved Me"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('67a0dd55-50f5-4ef0-8974-277f0d42fa05'), 'The gun Bond puts the silencer on at Miss Taro''s house is not his famous PPK. It''s a FN 1910 easily distinguishable by the FN logo on the grip. The reason is that the prop department couldn''t get a silencer fitting the PPK', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6dcf1c8c-7c6d-4ce2-825d-1d6190af2516'), 'In 1999, it was ranked number forty-one on the British Film Institute''s 100 Greatest British Films of the 20th Century', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Dr. No'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('7e026a71-0718-49e4-8f9b-32d2a49dc38d'), 'Sir Sean Connery called this movie his personal favorite of his Bond movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40b4f2d7-779e-49f0-9d28-542bf8ee67f3'), 'Final James Bond movie released during Ian Fleming''s lifetime. He died one month before Goldfinger (1964) was released in the UK', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4191d9f5-efed-4747-bf9c-9d9d6a36a016'), 'Steven Spielberg was convinced to cast Robert Shaw in Jaws (1975) after watching him in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7635aa4b-1f6c-455e-83b9-9fd8aa7fb9b3'), 'The knife shoe used by Rosa Klebb was an actual weapon used by the K.G.B', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('456d6ac6-efca-4681-b68b-247a12a7de5a'), 'Sir Sean Connery was outfitted for this movie with eight specially tailored Saville Row suits, each one costing approximately $2,000', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('29db1e22-b8ad-461d-a71c-0b45fe2509ff'), 'The scene in which James Bond and Tatiana Romanova first meet in the hotel suite has since been used as an audition scene for potential Bond actors and Bond girls. This can be seen in the "making of" documentaries for other Bond movies, including Octopussy (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bcd89a7f-6011-4b79-a761-37436bb18708'), 'This movie broke box-office records, and was responsible for launching Sir Sean Connery as a major star, rather than Dr. No (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('602f49b8-c9b4-4e07-8564-bff2a44ce2a9'), 'Then-President John F. Kennedy listed Ian Fleming''s book as among his top ten favorite novels of all time. That list was published in Life Magazine on March 17, 1961. Possibly as a result, the producers decided to make this the second James Bond movie. According to the book "Death of a President" (1964) by William Raymond Manchester, this was the last movie J.F.K. ever saw, in a private screening in the White House, November 20, 1963, two days before his assassination', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('788d21ae-39bc-4921-8860-2ae2a3f5a060'), 'Pedro Armendáriz was terminally ill during filming. He had cancer, which he likely contracted due to filming The Conqueror (1956) in the Utah desert near a U.S. nuclear test site. Armendáriz accepted this role partially to provide financial security for his wife. The shooting schedule was altered to film his scenes while he was still physically able. Towards the end of filming those scenes, director Terence Young had to double for the actor in some of his long shots. One month after all of his scenes were completed, Armendáriz shot himself in a Los Angeles hospital', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e46ac47-18f5-4aef-a53a-6585cb9ecbed'), 'Director Terence Young disliked Daniela Bianchi''s legs, and used a stand-in for the scene where Bond spies on the Russian embassy in Istanbul with a periscope. Additionally, film editor Peter R. Hunt tried to excise as much footage of the actress walking as he could, finding her quite splay-footed which he felt made Tatiana look somewhat ungainly', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2f1eaae0-75e4-43de-ab93-69fe6c1d4c89'), 'This movie marks the last appearance of Sylvia Trench, who also appeared in Dr. No (1962). The original plan was for Trench to appear in each movie as Bond''s regular girlfriend, continually frustrated when Bond is called away for his next assignment', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d489a30b-c823-420e-a62f-d3cdf154d360'), 'Over 3,500 people flocked to the Sirkeci Railway Station in Istanbul to watch filming, which caused delays in shooting. Terence Young had stuntman Peter Perkins create a distraction by hanging upside down from a balcony nearby so filming could proceed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9438bb49-0a2c-4118-ad5c-0f1a1d23b9eb'), 'Hoping for an end to the Cold War, producers Albert R. Broccoli and Harry Saltzman didn''t want James Bond''s main enemy to be Russian, so for the movie version, his nemesis is the fictitious criminal organization S.P.E.C.T.R.E., seeking revenge for the death of their operative, Dr. No (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fbffaca4-9936-4a55-8f3b-239c24a1e570'), 'The helicopter carrying director Terence Young during filming crashed over water, trapping him below the surface for a considerable time in an air bubble inside the copter''s canopy. He was rescued, and then immediately went back behind the camera with his arm in a sling. Producer Harry Saltzman considered replacing him with Sir David Lean, but producer Albert R. Broccoli insisted that Young finish the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7c69b221-be5b-46b7-9a51-1a890de5448a'), 'Twenty-one-year-old Daniela Bianchi was the youngest actress to play a leading Bond girl', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77fa1b39-afaf-4b86-8bbe-3c676b218df4'), 'As a guest on The Tonight Show (1962), Robert Shaw said that he had to stand on a wooden crate when filming scenes opposite Sir Sean Connery because he was four inches shorter than Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c32ca477-3678-4d6b-9362-ac87986cbe29'), 'To prepare for a fight scene in which he''s badly mauled by an enemy agent, Sir Sean Connery smeared his coat with earth and hung it up in readiness for the next days shooting. However when he went to put it on he found that a well meaning wardrobe mistress had cleaned and pressed it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e4e83a28-7062-4bd4-bf32-8ae7dbd2b434'), 'Although he had his reservations about the choice of Sir Sean Connery for the part of James Bond, after seeing him in this movie, Ian Fleming was completely won over by the actor. In fact, as a result, Fleming added a Scottish ancestry to Bond''s character in later novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d5692e40-89fa-4b0b-8075-c8ec92556fec'), 'The moves in Kronsteen''s chess game are from the game between Boris Spassky and David Bronstein at the U.S.S.R. Championship in Leningrad in 1960', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87a30bc8-11f9-4b00-9c19-c2a8d0f049e9'), 'The brutal fight in the train compartment between James Bond and Donald "Red" Grant lasts only a few minutes on-screen, but took three weeks to film. Most of it was performed by the actors, rather than doubles', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a45087dd-ddea-4a88-89e0-d5928ca022c5'), 'The picture on the wall of the lobby of the Russian embassy is that of Cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('57023479-3799-4670-89f0-2f5afb42f8b7'), 'Vladek Sheybal, a highly regarded Polish actor, was hesitant to accept a role in a Bond movie because he thought it might not be a good career move. His friend Sir Sean Connery persuaded him to sign on, and it helped his career enormously', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bd3a7b3f-c05d-4e7e-aa31-8c5b4cb4958c'), 'The collapsing rifle given to Bond isn''t a gimmick, but was an Armalite AR-7 survival rifle which was a production item which actually does disassemble and fit into its stock. However, it fires the .22 long rifle cartridge, not the .25 caliber as was stated in this movie. As of 2015, it is still in production by the Henry Repeating Firearms company. It is one of very few firearms that will float when dropped into water', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ddfc102a-f488-4447-9ede-cb8c22bfe4c0'), 'The headquarters of criminal spy organization S.P.E.C.T.R.E. is actually the main office administration building of Pinewood Studios', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fba30316-d3ef-4f6c-8395-f748ef249dcc'), 'Daniela Bianchi''s driver fell asleep during the commute to a 6 a.m. shoot and crashed the car. The actress'' face was bruised, and Bianchi''s scenes had to be delayed two weeks while these facial contusions healed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6fc7bcf3-7e72-47e5-91c5-2c711700e8dc'), 'First Bond movie to end with the declaration "James Bond will return in ...", in this case, it was Goldfinger (1964). A tradition that continued until it was used for the last time at the end of Octopussy (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4287aa4c-c5cb-4664-aae3-5f1f97747004'), 'During the helicopter sequence toward the end of the movie, the inexperienced pilot flew too close to Sir Sean Connery, endangering him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('19c8a90c-49dd-4cd4-bcd4-b492eefa7660'), 'A scene was cut just before Bond meets Romanova on the ferry. Bond tries to lose his mysterious pursuer and hops into a taxi. Bond takes control of the taxi''s brakes, causing the pursuing Bulgarian to run into the back of the taxi, and a third car to join the pile-up. The driver of the third car turns out to be Kerim Bey. When the angry Bulgarian protests to Bey, he is told "My friend, this is life", while Bond makes his escape in the British Embassy''s Rolls-Royce. Terence Young shot the scene 10 times to get the long ash on Bey''s cigar that Pedro Armendáriz insisted on. It wasn''t until a private screening one week before the movie''s release that Young''s 12-year-old son noticed that the Bulgarian had already been killed by Grant in the mosque, so it was cut', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3254e0fb-2a16-4a62-8909-7ad5a40d557c'), 'In 1950, a U.S. naval attaché was assassinated and thrown from the Orient Express train by a Communist Agent. This story inspired Ian Fleming''s novel "From Russia With Love". Fleming''s own experience at an INTERPOL Conference in Istanbul, Turkey provided the setting. To Paris with Love (1955) provided the title', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6780d009-6051-4d3e-8ed0-8a93b29516e7'), 'In this movie, James Bond does not say "Bond, James Bond" despite the fact that he does say it in the book on which this movie was based', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c7847755-0cd3-43f8-b2a3-a99edb8328cf'), 'The love scene between Sir Sean Connery and Daniela Bianchi caused censorship problems in Britain. In the scene, a sweating S.P.E.C.T.R.E. cameraman films James Bond and Tatiana Romanova in bed from a cabinet de voyeur. The British Board of Film Censors mandated to producers Albert R. Broccoli and Harry Saltzman that the voyeurism in the scene was too explicit, and to keep the footage of the cameraman as minimal as possible, or face risking having the whole sequence censored', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ba75a6c2-86ed-4229-ac6e-722425a86387'), 'Kronsteen''s opponent in the chess match is Canadian. Since this movie is set before the adoption of the current Maple Leaf flag in 1965, the official flag of Canada was still the British Union Jack. However, to distinguish themselves from Britain, Canadians utilized the Canadian Red Ensign defaced with the Canadian Arms on the fly as a de facto national flag, and this is the flag displayed on the podium at the match', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8cc273f-684a-421f-a4c9-0b56e43bf7f0'), 'Several years earlier, Sir Alfred Hitchcock had been considered to direct, with James Bond being played by Cary Grant, and Grace Kelly lured out of retirement to play Tatiana Romanova. These ideas were scrapped after Vertigo (1958) failed at the box office. The helicopter chase scene is a homage to Hitchcock''s cropduster sequence in North by Northwest (1959)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('43c3eedc-c9d6-4c27-9de3-88b2b1bda1e1'), 'Robert Shaw introduced Sir Sean Connery to the game of golf while filming this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2843eab5-8693-4ce0-9004-4045445d4187'), 'The helicopter and boat scenes were meant to be shot in Istanbul, but were moved to Scotland. The speed-boats could not run fast enough due to the many waves in the sea, and a rented boat filled with cameras ended up sinking in the Bosphorus. A helicopter was also hard to obtain. The special effects crew were nearly arrested trying to get one at a local air base', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f7c1b62-86d7-4948-bac8-ac92b8f95aa5'), 'The gadget Bond uses to check his hotel telephone for bugs is actually a device called an Elcometer. It is used to check the thickness (in thousandths of an inch) of surface coatings, usually paint, on ferrous surfaces. The needle moves sharply across the scale because, though the bodies of that type of telephone were plastic, their bases were painted steel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1569563e-a792-4364-ac2e-490558d3c760'), 'The video game From Russia with Love (2005), released 42 years after this film, includes Sir Sean Connery''s likeness and voice. It''s Connery''s last performance as James Bond, and he voiced it 22 years after Never Say Never Again (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('61803f45-4633-47fa-b4f5-e573c5293fce'), 'While this movie was in pre-production, the historic route of the Orient Express was changed. Since the nineteenth century, the westward-bound Orient Express stopped in Bucharest, Budapest, Vienna, Munich, and Strasbourg before arriving in Paris. But, beginning in 1962, the train followed a more southerly route, stopping in Sofia, Belgrade, Venice, Milan, and Lausanne. Changes in the script were made to accommodate the re-routing', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5503145a-ac06-4051-9573-73eaa17f889d'), 'Lois Maxwell named this as her favorite 007 movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da505e5a-55e6-4df5-afca-4e217edb793c'), 'The building where James Bond meets Tatiana is called the Hagia Sophia. It was originally a church that was converted to a mosque in 1453. It was turned into a museum under a secular government in 1935, but became a mosque again in 2020. It is frequently featured in art history texts as an example of a domed Basilica', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d502d771-3370-475a-9942-7e90cf3dc67b'), 'In the original novel, Colonel Rosa Klebb is explicitly a lesbian. Because Rosa Klebb is supposed to have been a secret defector (as stated in both the book and film), when Tatiana goes to meet Klebb to get her assignment, the meeting doesn''t happen in an office but Klebb''s apartment. During the course of the meeting, Klebb flirts with Tatiana, making her uncomfortable. Later, Klebb excuses herself from the room and when she returns, she has removed her Russian military uniform and is only wearing lingerie. Tatiana freaks out and runs out of the apartment. Not only for the simplicity of the narrative but to avoid having the important meeting censored because homosexuality was heavily outlawed at the time, the lesbianism is toned down to Klebb merely her inappropriately touching Tatiana''s knee. Which Tatiana shies away from', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9cbea99c-e5db-4c1f-a78d-9a6b7f74d996'), 'Robert Shaw originally turned down the role of Donald "Red" Grant, calling the script "rubbish". His then-wife Mary Ure convinced him to take the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('49684206-96e2-42f8-a8bd-cc15536d1208'), 'According to Robbie Collin in the U.K. newspaper The Telegraph, "Bond author Ian Fleming invented S.P.E.C.T.R.E. in 1959 to replace James Bond''s usual Soviet enemies. Fleming believed the Cold War might be about to end and wanted to keep his spy thrillers relevant." Fleming''s S.P.E.C.T.R.E. Executive Cabinet included "21 people including former Gestapo members, Soviet spy group S.M.E.R.S.H., Josep Tito''s (Josip Broz Tito''s) secret police, Italian, Corsican, and Turkish organized crime gangs", its goals were "profiteering from conflict between the superpowers, eventual world domination", and its methods included "counter-intelligence, brainwashing, murder, extortion using weapons of mass destruction (nuclear, biological and orbital)."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('20c15cca-0b02-413d-aa5c-38d53b883bdc'), 'In the books, Bond often drives his beloved Bentley. The car appears in this movie for the only time in the films', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35430709-4cee-413c-b4cd-eb55d7e241cf'), 'The S.P.E.C.T.R.E. training school was inspired by the gladiator school from Spartacus (1960)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fcc593ff-9c7e-4703-9c5f-f972742417d9'), 'Daniela Bianchi said in an interview that the walk-through nude scene in the bedroom where Tatiana meets Bond was done by a body double and not her because she refused to take her clothes off. She was also angry they used a double because for years after people thought it was her naked, including her family', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fb640038-4c1f-458b-8e87-95a02c3b5cf9'), 'Special permission was granted to film in Saint Sophia''s Mosque which had never granted permission before', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('85afc792-4da0-4851-9ba6-fbade28d0df8'), 'Location manager William Hill was forced to play the role of Captain Nash at the last minute, when the actor hired for the role couldn''t make it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f62056bd-16c6-45fa-8fcb-8701204fb31d'), 'Colonel Rosa Klebb was based on an actual Russian Colonel that Ian Fleming once wrote about in the Sunday Times. Katina Paxinou was the producers'' first choice for the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2778893f-70ee-4141-ac2e-4f2d0ca198d8'), 'According to an interview with the Hollywood Reporter''s Robert Osborne, producer Albert R. Broccoli named this movie, The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), and Goldfinger (1964) as his three favorite James Bond movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'From Russia With Love'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d65a876-51df-4a00-be8c-0cee6368e3d6'), 'The movie was the fastest grossing movie in movie history when it was released, and was entered into the Guiness Book of World Records', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b40dc419-413d-4b5e-928d-7eb66586fca3'), 'Aston Martin was initially reluctant to part with two of their cars for the production. The producers had to pay for the Aston Martin, but after the success of the movie, both at the box office and for the company, they never had to spend money on a car again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8bef8f8-d24b-4702-8d19-21af8970d1d6'), 'Though he had been considered for, but never appeared in a Bond movie, Sir Michael Caine was the first person to hear the completed score for this movie. After he and roommate Terence Stamp were ejected from their apartment, Caine asked friend John Barry if he could use the spare bedroom at Barry''s London residence. As they were good friends, Barry agreed and so for several months, Caine crashed with Barry and was there the sleepless night he completed his iconic score. At breakfast the following morning, Barry played his composition for Caine, the first time he''d performed it for anybody', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c8716d74-d557-44f2-92c2-451203899acf'), 'When Dame Shirley Bassey recorded the theme song, she was singing as the opening credits were running on a screen in front of her, so that she could match the vocals. When she hit her final high note, the titles kept running and she was forced to hold the note until she almost passed out. (This echoes the experience of Sir Tom Jones when recording the Thunderball (1965) theme.) She has told the story that she only managed to hold the note after removing a restricting bustier she was wearing', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('78c9849a-ac28-415e-ae8c-68011940bae7'), 'The re-creation of the Fort Knox repository at Pinewood Studios was incredibly accurate, considering no one involved in this movie had been allowed inside the real location for security reasons. The set looked so real that a 24-hour guard was placed on the Fort Knox set at Pinewood Studios so that pilferers would not steal the gold bar props. A letter production from the Fort Knox controller congratulated Sir Ken Adam and his team on the re-creation. Auric Goldfinger''s 3-D model map used for his "Operation Grand Slam" is now housed as a permanent exhibition at the real Fort Knox', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc0ecdda-0fae-4546-8860-6740e4b0b7fb'), 'First appearance of a laser beam in a 007 movie. In the original script, the scene had a spinning buzzsaw (as in the novel) until it was decided that such an image had become commonplace and unoriginal', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8da2c63c-8730-4978-8c20-500e2c37a77b'), 'Pussy Galore introduces herself to James Bond, who replies "I must be dreaming." The original script had Bond replying "I know you are, but what''s your name?" This was deemed too suggestive and was changed or bleeped in some markets around the world', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('adbb3abc-a3ba-4c55-bf74-508af722f236'), 'The producers wanted Orson Welles to play Auric Goldfinger, but he was too expensive. When Gert Fröbe began arguing over his salary, he wanted ten percent from the movie''s earnings, which prompted the producers to wonder whether Welles would have been cheaper after all', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e3f53c52-e693-475f-908d-75b9e3a8c069'), 'Ian Fleming partially based the title character of his original 1959 novel "Goldfinger" on the controversial Modernist architect Erno Goldfinger. When he learned that Fleming was naming the villain of his new James Bond novel "Goldfinger", the architect threatened to file a lawsuit against Fleming''s publisher in an effort to stop the book''s publication. Fleming''s publisher then contacted the author to inquire whether Fleming might consider renaming the character, and the novel. Fleming replied that he''d be delighted to alter the name, if he could change the name of the character, and the novel, to "Goldprick". Fleming''s publisher quietly settled the architect''s lawsuit out of court', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b646173f-37f0-4ec8-b66a-354691329c9c'), 'Sir Sean Connery hurt his back during the fight sequence with Harold Sakata (Oddjob) in Fort Knox. The incident delayed filming, and some say that Connery used the injury to get a better deal out of the producers for the next 007 movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77bbbee1-e4bc-49d6-95d7-84d1a4347b48'), 'Sir Sean Connery never traveled to the United States to film this movie. Every scene in which he appears to be in the U.S. was filmed at Pinewood Studios outside London. This explains why Bond flips a light switch down to discover the golden corpse of Jill, as British light switches are generally turned on by flicking them down instead of up. According to director Guy Hamilton, Cec Linder (Felix) was the only main actor in the Miami sequence who was actually there. Sir Sean Connery, Gert Fröbe, Shirley Eaton, Margaret Nolan, and Austin Willis, who played Goldfinger''s card victim, all filmed their parts when filming started in Britain, with rear projections used, and in the case of Fröbe and Wallis, stand-ins used for the long shots', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('91f4805d-79ec-48f3-930b-30ae995e964e'), 'Gert Fröbe once said of his role as Goldfinger: "I am a big man, and I have a laugh to match my size. The ridiculous thing is that since I played Goldfinger in the James Bond film, there are some people who still insist on seeing me as a cold, ruthless villain, a man without laughs."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7bf4fc3-ea34-434f-99db-faf2b0520573'), 'Gert Fröbe spoke very little English, so British actor Michael Collins dubbed his voice. Director Guy Hamilton instructed Fröbe to speak his lines (in German) quickly, which would assist the dubbing. Reportedly though, Fröbe was speaking English in a few scenes which reduces the awareness of the dubbing. In the trailer, Fröbe''s own heavily accented voice is heard when Goldfinger tells James, "Choose your next witticism carefully, Mr. Bond, it may be your last." Fröbe dubbed his own voice in the German dubbed version of the movie, too', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8cb94855-7df1-4996-9fda-31c511929b68'), 'As with the first two James Bond movies, Ian Fleming visited the set during April 1964. He visited D Stage at Pinewood Studios where they were filming the U.K. set of the Fontainebleu Hotel pool scene. Sadly, he died a little less than a month before the movie''s release on August 12, 1964', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('424c8f46-c1a5-4f48-9124-abe8292d8aeb'), 'Goldfinger was so popular that some theaters were holding showings 24 hours a day to meet demand', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2c52b42e-aac6-43d0-9c9a-f4e3973623f8'), 'During promotion, Honor Blackman took delight in embarrassing interviewers by repeatedly mentioning her character''s name', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5414afb3-ef25-497c-9158-c392cdb4fd2b'), 'The first Bond movie to be shown on U.S. commercial television, on Sunday, September 17, 1972, earning the highest Nielsen ratings for a single movie on television up to that time. Forty-nine percent of the nation''s viewers tuned in that night, and ABC, which showed the movie, retained the exclusive commercial U.S. television rights to the Bond film series for the next twenty-eight years', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5ede0ed8-d6ee-4dfd-9e7b-ff3fe4d33a79'), 'Sir Sean Connery, who was married to Diane Cilento at the time, wore a flesh-colored bandage (clearly seen in some production stills) over his wedding ring while filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0ff40186-2a28-4bf5-bce8-a3dd031df2db'), 'It''s in this movie that Q''s character really clicked. Director Guy Hamilton advised Desmond Llewelyn to inject humor into the character, thus beginning the friendly antagonism between Q and Bond that became a recurring trend in the films', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f22a9976-3c55-41a1-889b-0a5c1c82cb9d'), 'During the Fort Knox fight, the clock on the bomb was originally intended to stop at the time 0:03, but then the producers decided to stop it at Bond''s ID number, 0:07. Bond''s subsequent dialogue still refers to "three more ticks"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('44c3936d-e3e0-4b82-b1c8-5998573bb5eb'), 'The role of Oddjob was the first screen role for Japanese-American weightlifter and professional wrestler Harold Sakata. It was such a success that it started a second career in movies, television and commercials. For some of these appearances, he would be billed as ''Harold "Oddjob" Sakata.'' He also appeared in The Poppy Is Also a Flower (1966), which was based on an Ian Fleming story and directed by Bond director Terence Young', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e1243605-6a35-4467-96d3-4655a4b10bcd'), 'Goldfinger wears yellow or a golden item of clothing in virtually every scene. In the one that he appears not to, in which he wears a U.S. Army Colonel''s uniform, he carries a golden revolver. Thus, in the chronology of James Bond films, he is the first "man with a golden gun"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ffe722e8-dfbd-4c6b-8f32-46f3103f343e'), 'This was the second most popular Bond movie with paying audiences, racking up 130 million ticket sales. The next Bond movie, Thunderball (1965), surpassed it in popularity, with 140 million paid admissions. The success of this movie and Thunderball (1965) propelled Sir Sean Connery to the top of Quigley Publications'' annual Top Ten Money Making Stars poll in 1965, the only British male star to be number one', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('631958ec-0550-4906-b2b8-31b10c1ff8eb'), 'Sir Alfred Hitchcock''s favorite scene was when the old lady fires a machine gun', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('801c825c-3150-4c40-bf21-8c13c6fa109d'), 'Steven Spielberg cites Goldfinger as his personal favorite of all the Bond movies and even owns an Aston Martin DB5 due to the impact this movie had on him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('055d94b8-ec67-4d03-b7de-8fdcf92c3ed8'), 'After attending the premiere in Rome, Federico Fellini was asked by a journalist what he thought of the movie. His enthusiastic answer was "Questi sono i film che fanno andare avanti il cinema!" ("This is one of those films that make cinema carry on!")', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('41ad187f-70c0-4d77-8eab-e3c17c83daa0'), 'The exchange between Bond and his caddy about Goldfinger''s golf ball ("If that''s his original ball, I''m Arnold Palmer.") had the caddy standing on the ball in the novel. This is switched so Bond hid the ball for the movie, as producer Harry Saltzman thought it would give Bond a more cheeky image', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5a036167-51c6-4bd9-bbd9-da2820e8e097'), 'The scenes of people around Fort Knox passing out from being gassed were shot using the same group of soldiers moving to different locations', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d950260f-2b5f-45cd-881e-c2d35a06e962'), 'To shoot Pussy Galore''s Flying Circus gassing the soldiers, the pilots were only allowed to fly above 3,000 feet. Director Guy Hamilton recalled this was "hopeless", so they flew at about 500 feet, "and the military went absolutely ape."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('247077ef-c8a3-4607-8bc7-10d0043fb243'), 'Producers Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli were so determined to get Honor Blackman for the part of Pussy Galore that they had the actress'' ability to perform judo written into the script', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('62428a8e-2f04-477f-847e-7f7b5c800497'), 'In the original end title credits, which featured the famous "James Bond will return in..." teaser, the next movie advertised was On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969). However, when the producers began pre-production, they were unable to secure the Swiss locations needed for the movie, and decided to make Thunderball (1965) instead. The end title teaser was later changed to advertise "Thunderball"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('201407ba-b4eb-4512-bf29-0cc7701cba18'), 'Due to the popularity and success of this movie, and its spy car the Aston Martin DB5, the vehicle gained the nickname, "The Most Famous Car in the World". Sales of the Aston Martin DB5 increased by fifty percent after the release of the movie. The Bond movie The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) featured the Lotus Esprit, and sales also increased for that car after the movie premiered', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4043e6c-21c5-4f8b-b846-c6f9e9094f0a'), 'Worried studio executives from United Artists considered changing the name of Pussy Galore to Kitty Galore. The name Pussy Galore was not included on any trading cards during the movie''s original release, as they were aimed at youth. However, later released cards such as those as part of the "007 Spy Files" in 2002 do specify the name "Pussy Galore"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f138dec1-9971-40a5-886b-3b6dd831d5fa'), 'Equipment and gadgetry was developed for the Aston Martin car which was not used in the finished movie. This included: front and back over-riders for ramming other vehicles, a weapons tray under the driver''s seat, a headlights chamber containing triple-spiked nail clusters for firing at enemies, a radio telephone inside the driver''s door paneling, and a Thermos with a built-in hand grenade', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e27c22bd-c11a-4253-9d72-a164e8fca908'), 'Gert Fröbe was doubled in scenes where Goldfinger plays golf, as he couldn''t get the hang of the game', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ae0261a9-2540-4aa7-a517-a76e110185f0'), 'There were two Aston Martins created for this movie. One is owned by a private collector, who paid over $4 million in 2010. The other one was purchased by a private collector in 1986 for $250,000. That car was parked at an airport in Boca Raton, Florida when, in June 1997, it was stolen under suspicious circumstances. The thieves broke into the guarded Boca Raton airport. The alarm wires of the hangar were cut, and even though the keys were not in the car, the car vanished without a trace. On December 31, 2021 it was reported to have been located "somewhere in the Middle East" and efforts were being made to return the car, valued at $25 million, to its rightful owner', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c96b0173-b669-4b81-9c6f-a72f8d851f54'), 'During the opening titles sequence, all excerpts are scenes from this movie except some footage from the From Russia with Love (1963) helicopter chase sequence and the Crab Key explosion from Dr. No (1962). All of these scenes in the opening titles are projected onto the gilded body of Margaret Nolan, who played Dink in the film. Her appearance in this sequence is longer than Shirley Eaton appears in the film, and she wears a blue bikini (also featured on the soundtrack cover) which Eaton does not wear in her scenes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0da33ae2-5afa-474b-ab3d-6cd551e97a8a'), 'Oddjob never speaks in this movie. His only dialogue is an "Aha!" on the golf course, two "Ah"s when ordering men to pick up Tilly after she is hit with his hat, a grunt when he hands Bond a gas mask at the back of the army truck, and his scream at the conclusion of his fight with Bond. The source novel explains he is unable to speak due to a cleft palate', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35e94504-4f43-4407-9758-6c53b9873758'), 'The title song is the first of three title songs sung by Dame Shirley Bassey for Bond movies, the others being title songs for Diamonds Are Forever (1971) and Moonraker (1979). The "Goldfinger" song was the first James Bond title song to crack the Billboard Top 10, peaking at number eight in February 1965', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8997c224-8958-441b-9281-f7b5df29cd4a'), 'Jack Lord was approached to return as CIA agent Felix Leiter, but he declined. He had played him in Dr. No (1962). The role was re-cast, beginning a succession of different actors in the role. Only David Hedison and Jeffrey Wright played the role more than once. In this movie, Austin Willis was originally cast as Felix Leiter and Cec Linder as Simmons. However, they were asked to swap parts shortly before production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dd0437b9-b04c-4aae-9844-b4d6a0fc3918'), 'This is the only movie where Sir Sean Connery''s James Bond orders a Martini shaken not stirred. In Dr. No (1962), everyone who served him a martini said it himself or herself', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ed7b358-1399-4b21-a0db-c2c0573114ba'), 'This movie earned back its production costs of £3 million in just two weeks', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('357671b2-83ff-4859-a001-262bd0f359f6'), 'First appearance of the Q-Branch workshop and its gadget testing gags', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('743001ef-413a-46eb-b9c5-c72b1ad93f3c'), 'The golf scenes in the movie were shot at the Stoke Poges Golf Club, Slough, England, not far from Pinewood Studios. There is now a James Bond themed bar at the golf course. The interest in golf developed by Sir Sean Connery is said to have spawned during this filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('821ed87e-2a5b-45ae-8fc9-e4dedbf83811'), 'The idea of the Aston Martin''s revolving number plates came from director Guy Hamilton, who had just been frustrated at receiving a parking ticket. The various revolving license plate numbers for James Bond''s Aston Martin DB5 were 4711-EA-62 (France), LU 6789 (Switzerland), and BMT 216A (U.K.)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b66997c9-c97a-4019-a5ef-aba0b1549ed4'), 'In the Ian Fleming novel, Pussy Galore is a lesbian, which is why she gives Bond the cold shoulder to start with. Her team are known as the Cement Mixers. Ian Fleming based the character of Pussy Galore on neighbor, friend, and lover Blanche Blackwell. The "Pussy" name was derived from agent Pussy Deakin a.k.a. Livia Stela. The "Pussy" name is also said to have been named after Fleming''s pet octopus. The octopus also inspired the title of the James Bond short story and then movie Octopussy (1983). "Octopussy" was also the name of a coracle given to Ian Fleming by Blanche Blackwell as a present for staying at Goldeneye', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('092b7b0c-aae3-486e-8aca-bff02bd5d402'), 'First movie to feature a title song that plays over the opening credits. From Russia with Love (1963) had a title song, but it played over the closing credits', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e05fc0c-378a-4554-953c-23c25134f443'), 'Some of Pussy Galore''s all-woman Flying Circus were played by men wearing blonde wigs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4bc3b14a-0c38-44c0-a1e8-31cebed23825'), 'Despite her impressive movie debut as Tilly, this was model Tania Mallet''s only major movie appearance. She had previously tested for the Tatiana Romanova part in From Russia with Love (1963)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9030f53e-57e8-4e15-b79c-a4ba027edd2b'), 'This won the first Academy Award for a James Bond movie. It was for Best Sound Effects and it was won by Norman Wanstall. Thunderball (1965) won a Special Visual Effects Oscar the following year and producer Albert R. Broccoli was awarded the Irving Thalberg Award in 1982. The first Bond movie to receive the gilded statuette was the one with the gilded girl', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('586079c6-1f42-491a-a34f-85221a6d00eb'), 'In the novel, Tilly Masterton is captured alive in Switzerland, becomes enamored of Pussy Galore, and is killed by Oddjob in the battle of Fort Knox. Oddjob survives that confrontation, only to be sucked out the plane''s window in their next conflict. Bond then kills Goldfinger by strangling him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('17cb3ebd-d863-4154-beb9-cd83783f24ba'), 'The vault door used in the Fort Knox scene is now located in Bank of the West in Los Altos, California. Although, considering the set was built in Pinewood Studios, and the left over set was re-purposed as "stock" scenery, this is debatable', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a12eb4ae-26e9-42f3-be67-2388170e3b87'), 'In order to simulate the sound of crumpling metal in the car compactor, sound effects editor Norman Wanstall used the sound of crumpling beer cans', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('20f5d91f-bafb-47cd-9dfd-b7d7f35a8ead'), 'Tilly Masterson''s Ford Mustang was supposedly the first appearance by a Mustang in a movie. The Mustang was introduced in April 1964, and this movie was released in December. Ford supplied many cars to the movie, including the CIA agents'' Thunderbird, all of Goldfinger''s goons'' cars, and the Lincoln Continental that is crushed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0b3bebc3-1b7c-4263-84a3-f1242e45849a'), 'Auric Goldfinger is the name of the gold-obsessed villain. "Auric" means gold or golden. The villain''s first name, Auric, is related to the Latin word for gold, "aurum", and the periodic table code AU for the same. The license plate on Goldfinger''s twelve-cylinder 1937 Rolls-Royce Phantom III Sedance de Ville reads "AU 1" for the same reason. So, bizarrely, his name is theoretically also alternatively "Gold Goldfinger", or "Golden Goldfinger", or "Aurum Goldfinger"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('89dd90f0-5dde-4b73-9b7f-fc5269345a28'), 'Producers Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli wanted to cast Gert Fröbe after seeing him in the German thriller It Happened in Broad Daylight (1958). In that movie, Fröbe played a psychopathic serial killer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('277ce359-0228-430d-a11a-9e7184d4659d'), 'This was the first film that future Bond Pierce Brosnan saw in the theater', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8fac49e-53c1-4358-bd49-f6e46ae7aac6'), 'A scene where Felix would be explaining to the townspeople the plan of faking their deaths to trick Goldfinger was cut, as it made Felix seem "too heroic" compared to Bond. Ironically, it was Felix and his fellow CIA agents who would save Fort Knox and Bond. The scene was leaked on-line, but quickly removed by EON, and has never been officially released', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2eb9ca85-9f44-436b-80d8-a10f7eca0791'), 'The battle aboard Goldfinger''s jet was originally a longer sequence, where Bond fought Goldfinger and one of his henchmen. The henchman can be glimpsed when Goldfinger steps into the cabin, and his body can be seen tumbling around inside the airplane, after the window is shot', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('52652e82-185c-4f29-b29b-c47ec3bf4f8a'), 'According to Auric Goldfinger, in 1964 values, Fort Knox held $15 billion worth of gold. "In its vaults are $15 billion, the entire gold supply of the United States." If adjusted for inflation, that amount would be equivalent to almost $115 billion as of March 2016. However, since the price of gold has appreciated almost five times as much as the rate of inflation, that amount of gold would be worth about $520 billion', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2eb3579a-ea85-4b74-a902-517c8594424f'), 'The steel rimmed bowler used by Oddjob sold for £62,000 in 1998', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9c1ec5cf-bba0-411a-986b-7c2aae9e77ba'), 'For a long time, this movie was tied with Dr. No (1962) as the shortest James Bond film, with a running time of one hour and fifty minutes. Quantum of Solace (2008) became the shortest at one hour and forty-six minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('79f2ba85-8e00-449b-9148-7c1a51499eaa'), 'Auric Goldfinger and his henchman Oddjob are considered two of the great movie villains. Like many great movie villains, the actors portraying them are quite the opposite of their screen characters. Fellow cast members have remarked how charming and friendly Gert Fröbe and Harold Sakata were off-camera. Co-producer Albert R. Broccoli cast Fröbe, and had him singing and dancing, in Chitty Chitty Bang Bang (1968)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('219ec111-a6b1-4be9-a19d-1b9a3545f606'), 'While the American censors did not interfere with the name in this movie, they refused to allow the name "Pussy Galore" to appear on promotional materials, and for the U.S. market, she was subsequently called "Miss Galore" or "Goldfinger''s personal pilot."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8ecf4b88-62bb-443a-9fac-996a96b9571d'), 'The surname of Tilly Masterton and Jill Masterton in the novel was changed to "Masterson" for the movie. Ian Fleming is said to have based the "Masterton" name on Sir John Masterman, a leading Oxford University academic and former MI5 agent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('aea33366-e0f6-4bf8-ab64-364f8346cc31'), 'Shortly after this movie came out, Corgi toys released a die cast model of the DB5, a silver one and a limited edition gold one', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('70ff13a3-04a5-458a-835c-a761cd4489c0'), 'In the original novel, the car driven by Bond is not an Aston Martin DB5, but an earlier model, an Aston Martin DB3. There were significantly fewer gadgets and features in this make. All James Bond had were reinforced bumper guards and a secret compartment for a Colt .45 pistol', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a9a6e8b2-9334-4165-9702-3434bd7a05fd'), 'As Goldfinger''s car is being loaded into the airplane to Geneva, his license plate (AU 1) is visible. Au is the chemical symbol for the element gold', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldfinger'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('23d8f526-e114-4c0a-abbc-501402cb234d'), 'Bond''s jetpack was actually flown by engineer Bill Suiter. He was one of only two people in the world qualified to fly it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c8f482c4-5f28-4f3d-890c-4e7ee3de3c18'), 'The only Bond movie where we get a glimpse of all 00 Agents in one shot. They are summoned to M''s briefing, and 007 is the last to join in. He sits down in the only available chair, the seventh from the left. Only one of the other 00s is revealed, however, as they are filmed from behind. the total number of chairs and agents is 9', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('166b6ec8-59f2-40e2-8b97-11d5acbbc19b'), 'In the underwater scenes, where Bond encounters sharks, Sir Sean Connery was supposed to be protected by clear plastic panels shielding him from sharks in close-ups. However, the panels only extended about three feet in height and sharks could swim over them. As a result, in some scenes (notably during the pool fight at Largo''s mansion), Connery got much closer to the real sharks than he wanted. Director Terence Young said in an interview that scenes used in this movie where Bond reacts in fright at the approach of a shark were miscues, in which Connery was reacting with genuine terror as a shark approached unobstructed by plastic shielding. Production designer Ken Adam build a Plexiglas partition inside the pool. The barrier was not a fixed structure, so when one of the sharks managed to pass through it, Connery fled the pool, seconds away from attack. Adam said: "He never got out of a pool faster in his life - he was walking on water."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('24f17440-a5ab-4c12-a736-c7678e97ca51'), 'Sir Sean Connery performed the gun-barrel sequence for the first time because of the new Panavision process used in the movie. Beginning with this movie, the sequence would be performed by the actor playing Bond in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1211712c-60a1-4d14-a8bf-ad12b0f5d3d0'), 'The budget for this movie was more than the combined budgets of the first three Bond movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c53d9d45-67c3-4671-9fb7-698acf7280f8'), 'he dictionary definition of the word "thunderball" is a military term used by U.S. soldiers to describe the mushroom cloud seen during the testing of atomic bombs. Hence its use as a title, because this would be the result of S.P.E.C.T.R.E. detonating the stolen atomic bombs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('681f55a8-71d4-4ddc-8f3f-5f71ed5bffb2'), 'To prevent anyone using the Vulcan bomber mock-up for future filming, the production team blew up the plane with dynamite. The framework left behind has since become a reef', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d63f3bd6-d587-48e5-82b0-e249d4d64b8a'), 'In keeping with her name, Domino''s clothes are always in black and white, except for the red dress she wears on her date with Bond at the festival', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('873e61b9-0fc6-48c5-b67d-2a131836703e'), 'The line where Fiona derides Bond''s ability to turn women to the side of right and virtue was taken from a critique of Goldfinger (1964), where the critic derided Bond''s ability to turn Pussy Galore away from Goldfinger', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c104f78-b865-42d7-8757-413c3e0a8d6f'), 'This was the most popular Bond movie, with paying audiences racking up 140 million ticket sales. Goldfinger (1964), with 130 million ticket sales, ranks number two in popularity', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cbd034d9-0651-4dd5-8e34-7c3cc04f5237'), 'Martine Beswick recalled an incident involving Sir Sean Connery. "One time, we''d finished filming for the day, and there were hundreds of people milling around on the beach, all roped off watching. Sean called to the set hairdresser, "Here, you", and then he simply pulled off his toupée and threw it at the hairdresser. The hairpiece sailed over like a Frisbee and as the hairdresser caught it, Sean said something like, ''That''s it, I''m off.'' Everyone just collapsed. It was the funniest thing."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('22c0f7c3-b42b-4436-9788-c2ea281447f7'), 'Largo''s two-section yacht, the Disco Volante, was adapted from a hydrofoil vessel called "The Flying Fish". It cost $500,000 to acquire from Puerto Rico and transfer to Miami for refitting and refurbishment. It was given a cocoon shell, which was fifty feet long, and could be separated from the main boat, as seen in the movie''s finale', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5360f3c8-c251-4f95-8ab6-ea26dd5ad8c9'), 'The character of Count Lippe is a reference to Ian Fleming''s old friend from his days as an intelligence officer, Prince Bernhard of the Netherlands. Bernhard was born as Bernhard von Lippe Biesterfeld. He was very pleased by the reference', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7389bef-245a-4661-9155-8ab043187bb8'), 'The rocket-propulsion jet-pack seen in this movie was originally designed and invented for military use. It is also known as the Small Rocket Lift Device (S.R.L.D.). The original intention, as conceived during the 1950s, was for soldiers to be able to improve their agility, depth-of-field, and ability to commandeer terrain by being able to jump over impeding landmarks and waterways. The Bell Aerosystems Rocketbelt model was used for this movie. Its flight goes for 21 seconds, and provides 1,000 brake horsepower', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c11b0c28-9dac-4b29-ac1a-070a33438e21'), 'When told he would be inside a swimming pool with real sharks, Sir Sean Connery''s response was: "Not bloody likely!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('49804dc9-a1a1-4deb-9e55-bedb6259b0cc'), 'Martine Beswick played one of the Gypsy girls in From Russia with Love (1963), and Paula Caplan in this movie. She is well-tanned in this movie, but before shooting, she was pale white due to years of stage work in England. As a result, before filming in Nassau she was required to spend approximately two weeks sunning herself to get the proper tan of a native girl', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3ece9bc4-d33e-487d-b63a-1b41c4f90dd3'), 'Claudine Auger beat out 150 candidates to play Domino', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('adff633c-5aef-4b3c-b217-a6ea624d92e5'), 'James Bond''s "Geiger counter" watch is a modified Breitling Top Time Ref. 2002, manufactured in 1962. It was the only one produced for the movie and the only Breitling watch ever used in a James Bond movie. The watch disappeared during filming and remained a mystery, until it surfaced in 2013 at a "car boot" sale (British flea market), where it was purchased for a mere twenty-five pounds. Once Breitling and several experts verified its authenticity, it was then sold at Christie''s Auction for £103,875 pounds ($163,383 U.S.D.)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0f835ea1-4027-40bf-885f-13f9bf55b250'), 'It''s rumored that a Royal Navy engineer approached the producers after this movie''s release to ask them how they designed the mini-rebreather. Apparently, he had been working on something similar, but could not figure it out. He was devastated when the producers told them their secret. The actors were holding their breath. The amount of time one had to breathe underwater in the movie, utilizing the Rebreather mini-aqualung, was four minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d6761992-6804-43a5-9a8c-a2944e7f7217'), 'By the time of production in 1965, the popularity of the James Bond film franchise had resulted in a proliferation of other espionage movies and television series. As a nod to this trend in popular entertainment, during the meeting of the 00 agents in M''s office, the plan was originally to have the stars of other spy-related entertainment appear as their popular characters--Robert Vaughn and David McCallum from The Man from U.N.C.L.E. (1964), James Coburn from Our Man Flint (1966), Sir Michael Caine as Harry Palmer, Dean Martin as Matt Helm, Robert Culp and Bill Cosby from I Spy (1965), and others. However, due to the salaries required by the actors for cameo appearances, and time constraints, the producers were forced to abandon the gimmick', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec4f34d2-d3c9-47b6-8ece-9a079a578a6f'), 'While there really is an area known as the "Golden Grotto" in the Bahamas (now rechristened the "Thunderball Reef"), the Golden Grotto sharks that Largo keeps in his swimming pool, and describes as "the most dangerous, the most savage" shark species of them all, are entirely fictional. The Bull/Zambezi shark is regarded as the most dangerous to man in all tropical waters', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('529484f6-f276-40f3-83b9-87f1974e1ac6'), 'During the recording of the title song "Thunderball", Sir Tom Jones asked the song''s writer what the "strikes like thunderball" line meant. The song''s composer allegedly replied that he didn''t know. Jones nearly fainted after recording the nine-second final high note at the end of recording the song. This echoes a story told by Dame Shirley Bassey who, when recording the Goldfinger (1964) theme, could only hold the final note after removing her constricting bustier', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e02bd17-997c-4970-baf9-c497b0a49ba0'), 'Claudine Auger''s heavily accented English was deemed too "French-thick" by the filmmakers after shooting initial scenes of her. Nikki Van der Zyl, who dubbed Ursula Andress'' voice in Dr. No (1962), was brought back to dub Auger''s lines. For similar reasons, Adolfo Celi (Largo) had his lines dubbed over by Robert Rietty, to hide his thick and distinctive Sicilian accent. In spite of her native tongue, Claudine Auger''s voice had her lines dubbed over sardonically by Nicole Maurey, a former French actress who was better known for her appearances in Hollywood movies such as The Day of the Triffids (1963) and The Scapegoat (1959) co-starring Sir Alec Guinness, in the French dub version', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f3f99dbb-c9b4-4de7-bd55-9b41354484af'), 'When Bond and Domino meet underwater and disappear behind a rock, the scene was originally supposed to show Domino''s bikini float out from behind the rock. Producer Albert R. Broccoli vetoed this, because he felt it was too suggestive', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a0ee2e64-9087-440f-98cc-3b305d527e70'), 'Final James Bond movie directed by Terence Young', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1bb215bc-2598-49a1-8ff8-d743481922dc'), 'The gun-barrel sequence that opens this movie marks not only the first time the actor portraying Bond performed the scene, but is also the first instance in the film franchise where the dot opens up to reveal the first scene in the story', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eca9484b-efe0-4088-8957-8d8345feb806'), 'As overseen by John Stears, the special effects explosion of the Disco Volante was so powerful it shattered and blew out windows about twenty to thirty miles away in Nassau''s Bay Street, where the movie''s Junkanoo Mardi-Gras sequence was filmed. Reportedly, he had not known how potent and strong a mix the experimental rocket fuel was in order to create the explosion', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e9b055a-961a-48ea-91ef-6c1781c5d719'), 'In Italian, "Disco Volante" translates as "Flying Saucer"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bee8d381-0f06-4d26-9d81-de36654ed93e'), 'According to "Bond Gadget Designer" Sir Ken Adam, the jetpack that Bond uses to escape his enemies was no special effect, but a real jetpack provided by the U.S. Air Force. Initially, Sir Sean Connery was to fly the jetpack without a helmet (and some publicity photos of him with the jetpack were made with him without a helmet). This was because he would have looked more debonair. It was later decided that he wear a helmet in the scene. This was for risk and safety reasons, as the pilot refused not to wear a helmet, and the scenes had to match', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3fd52594-b031-4c45-9253-3147f214eb3e'), 'The only individual James Bond movie to win a Visual or Special Effects Academy Award. It was for Best Effects, Special Visual Effects, and awarded to John Stears. Moonraker (1979) was nominated for Best Effects, Visual Effects, but did not win. Albert R. Broccoli received the Irving Thalberg Memorial Award from the Academy for producing the group of James Bond movies in 1982. Goldfinger (1964) won the first Bond Oscar for sound effects. BAFTA nominated production designer Ken Adam for an award', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e180128-dc8e-4110-8781-2fdabe082e49'), 'Supervising editor Peter R. Hunt claims that the scene with a dog urinating in the shot during the Junkanoo (at around one hour and 27 minutes) was at first left on the cutting room floor, feeling that the footage wasn''t that great. However the producers, who noticed the take as they checked the dailies, enjoyed the shot so much that they demanded it remain in the movie. Also, in the parade behind the dog, a group who arrived for filming as part of the parade dressed up wearing "007" on their hats. Filmmakers attempted to edit around the group, but the dog''s impromptu nature call kept the "007" group in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('794e9027-2acf-4bcb-b23b-4f95edcc38a0'), 'According to the "behind-the scenes" DVD commentary, one of the seated 00 agents in the conference room scene (where Bond walks in late) is a woman, the only time that a female 00 agent was portrayed in the James Bond series until No Time to Die (2021). Although never shown directly, she is seated third from the left, making her Agent 003 (Bond, appropriately enough, is seated seventh from the left, since he is Agent 007)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2dcb3e58-6c62-4b9b-b1e5-3633650a316a'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli pursued Raquel Welch for the role of Domino after seeing her on the cover of Life Magazine. She had to drop out in order to appear in Fantastic Voyage (1966)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ba5e2b8a-7df5-42e7-bcc9-743c309799fd'), 'Stuntman Bill Cumming was paid a $450 bonus to jump into Largo''s shark-infested pool', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5fe839fb-5956-4006-9dc6-99c373ad1c1d'), 'Sixty divers participated in the climactic underwater battle', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d39ca40-5218-470a-95ba-fce29d7b2f75'), 'In North America, this was the second highest-grossing movie of 1966, after Doctor Zhivago (1965)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3a866b2c-f954-4164-9b8a-758d46976868'), 'First time a Bond movie was released in the U.S. before the U.K', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e03cd4c2-08e9-4973-9697-9e7972488ed9'), 'The AMC channel erroneously cited this as Sir Sean Connery''s favorite during its recent Bond retrospectives. Connery''s favorite of the movies was From Russia with Love (1963), one of the most critically acclaimed in the film franchise. He confirmed that in a 2002 interview with Sam Donaldson for ABCNews.com', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fb63c1a6-9f39-4aaf-a4f3-c588ac28dabb'), 'Goldfinger (1964) director Guy Hamilton was originally offered the directing job by producers Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli. However, due to fatigue at the time, he felt he could not add anything more, and turned it down. He considered himself worn out and "creatively drained"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4a73fa6a-0836-4d9b-a385-b4f906f1ffdc'), 'Fiona Volpe was originally Irish, and called "Fiona Kelly" in earlier drafts of the script. But the surname was changed to suit the Italian nationality of Luciana Paluzzi, who was cast after being rejected for the role of Domino. The character does not appear in the novel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fc67e698-d2c1-4f67-a0c5-d65675637404'), 'In at least two shots in the scene where Number One accuses his underlings of embezzlement, the unnatural eye movements and blinking motions of the actors reveal that the film is actually being run backwards', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b8ad9a49-c189-490f-8a86-5c079f623a6f'), 'A timely reference to the British Great Train Robbery of 1963 was inserted into the script at the last minute. This can be heard during the S.P.E.C.T.R.E. meeting after the opening credits. In the movie''s story, agent Number 5 reported that S.P.E.C.T.R.E. was paid a £250,000 consultancy fee for the British Great Train Robbery. The Great Train Robbery was the robbery of a Royal Mail train traveling from Glasgow to London, on the West Coast Main Line, in the early morning hours of August 8, 1963. It took place at Bridego Railway Bridge, Ledburn, near Mentmore, in Buckinghamshire, England. After tampering with the line side signals to bring the train to a halt, a gang of 15 men attacked the train. With careful planning based on inside information from an individual known as "The Ulsterman", whose real identity has never been established, the robbers escaped with over £2.61 million. The bulk of the stolen money has never been recovered. The gang did not use any firearms, though the train driver was beaten over the head with a metal bar and suffered serious head injuries. Coincidentally, Sir Sean Connery later starred in The Great Train Robbery (1978), which is about a different caper that occurred in the 1850s', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f9df89a8-1055-4028-9e9a-4707a3c0ae2e'), 'This movie and From Russia with Love (1963) are the only Bond movies to use the wipe editing technique in scene transitions', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87989ba8-1e1f-40f5-a646-f42f86570991'), 'Main title designer Maurice Binder returned to the franchise after being absent from the previous two Bond movies, From Russia with Love (1963) and Goldfinger (1964). He had designed the opening titles for Dr. No (1962), and continued on every Bond movie after this one until his last on Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e415f5a-06a3-4304-831f-dade0693c433'), 'When Bond and Domino are rescued by winch at the end of the movie, it was actually by a then-real sea rescue method known as sky-hooking. It is an out of date practice today, as more advanced helicopter rescue methods are used, such as those seen in The Guardian (2006). In The Dark Knight (2008), the rescue method is mentioned as Skyhook and is used to retrieve Batman and Lau', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c1a658d6-6b48-414c-8b72-5ef34b5f5400'), 'Some release prints did not show "James Bond will be back in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)" at the end of the credits. Difficulties in scheduling and shooting during winter meant that movie was postponed, and You Only Live Twice (1967) became the next James Bond movie. The solution put forward by supervising editor Peter R. Hunt was simply to remove the title from the final credits', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b5073896-37b7-42cb-a3c0-354c26513730'), 'According to Behind the Scenes with ''Thunderball'' (1995), in the scene were Bond climbs out of the shark tank right as a shark makes a run at him, the shark in question was dead and pulled by a wire', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4288d5b1-8f3c-413c-9e82-6666ab66a1c4'), 'Molly Peters (nurse Patricia "Pat" Fearing) was the first Bond Girl to be seen taking her clothes off on-screen, where previous movies only showed Bond''s lovers after the fact. Molly strips off her nurse''s uniform when she and Sir Sean Connery make love in the steam room. Her bare bottom pressed up against the steam room glass is also the first nudity shown in the franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35f55490-31af-4a99-991c-49f42b686c9f'), 'An excellent swimmer, Claudine Auger did all her own underwater scenes, including a love scene with Sir Sean Connery on the sea bed, during which she lost her bikini top', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4321ca09-8395-4c3b-b284-a96049045d84'), 'Members of the cast and crew were interviewed several times about this movie while it was being shot, due to the immense popularity of the Bond film franchise. However, Sir Sean Connery consented to just one interview, and it was with Playboy Magazine', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2bf51ea9-bd0e-4708-a8cb-a71b1114e5bb'), 'The tapestries on the walls of the MI6 conference room (one of which conceals a screen) depict part of the Ancient Greek myth of Jason. The originals were made at the Gobelins Manufactory in France in the 1770s. Several sets were made, one of which is in the Royal Collection and displayed at Windsor Castle', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('592d7f91-9465-4266-b30a-b0eb3f27bf5c'), 'Stuntman Bob Simmons appeared to have made a very narrow escape from the car explosion stunt during filming at Silverstone Racetrack, Northamptonshire, England. Director Terence Young raced to the scene, whereupon Simmons surprised him from the side road as a gag. People watching the stunt generally didn''t see Simmons exit the vehicle before the explosion, probably due to his exit point being in a blind spot to the point-of-view of those overseeing the stunt', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9809e878-6d46-43f9-bfe3-cc1122a3d307'), 'Most of the underwater scenes had to be done at lower tides, due to the sharks in the Bahamian Sea', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d99e511f-2d78-477a-bb5f-a61d2484dede'), 'When S.P.E.C.T.R.E. divers are retrieving the two atomic bombs from the Vulcan bomber, clearly marked on the bombs amongst the technical data is the phrase "HANDLE LIKE EGGS"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('02571726-21fb-4a87-9562-dcc2c14263f7'), 'Approximately 25% of the screen time takes place underwater', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1d330b9e-a855-40e2-8dda-4437b364848a'), 'A character called Fatima Blush was originally created by Ian Fleming as a double agent and existed in early treatments and outlines of this movie. She does not appear in either the book, or movie Thunderball (1965), but does in its remake, Never Say Never Again (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('beaceff6-5bb3-43d2-88fd-4156facd8e13'), 'The name of the organizational front that the headquarters of the criminal S.P.E.C.T.R.E. organization operated out of in Paris, France, was the International Brotherhood for Stateless Persons', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f14458f7-d15b-4eb3-8409-9bcf3166054d'), 'While filming in Paris, Sir Sean Connery took the opportunity to attend his first premiere of Goldfinger (1964). While driving down the Champs-Elysees, his Aston Martin DB5 was invaded by a frenzied female fan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('24f0c586-170b-441f-8df3-eab0c7bb838a'), 'James Bond does not drink a vodka martini "shaken, not stirred" in this movie, but he does order a Dom Perignon 55 champagne by a swimming pool while dining with Domino', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4286ad9f-8159-4621-a17d-cc27f6af56df'), 'In the trailer for this movie, Bond says the line, "The things I do for England." It is ironic because Sir Sean Connery was proudly Scottish and Bond, a ''British'' agent, was also of Scottish ancestry. The line was cut from the final version of this movie, and then used in the next Bond movie, You Only Live Twice (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c44de622-a831-4760-81a9-3c481656ef88'), 'Ian Fleming himself wrote an early draft of this movie, and wanted Sir Alfred Hitchcock to direct. His script took inspiration from Hitchcock''s North by Northwest (1959), with James Bond being more akin to Cary Grant''s character Roger Thornhill than the "ruthless, sadistic and misogynistic" Bond of the novels. Producers Albert R. Broccoli and Harry Saltzman did in fact approach Grant to play Bond, but Grant felt he was too old, and didn''t want to commit to multiple films', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3e5993c0-0ee2-419b-b405-b06aeb9ec920'), 'First 007 movie in which Bond doesn''t smoke. Interestingly though, a large papier-mache Marlboro box can be spotted on the right side of the screen during a festival', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1386d783-8c09-4f24-9536-00b3e5854cca'), 'There was originally a scene in the Bahamas with Bond meeting Paula for the first time, set in a beach bar, she was to spell out "007" in the sand as a recognition sign', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('abac100b-3eb8-425f-8870-8390a393eda8'), 'First appearance in the James Bond film franchise of a shark-infested swimming pool, used to execute a disloyal subordinate, which became the basis for Dr. Evil''s "sharks with frickin'' laser beams" in Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery (1997)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Thunderball'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('39efc541-5892-43b2-a9ee-ef55a5ee2186'), 'While scouting locations in Japan, the chief production team narrowly escaped death. On 5 March 1966, producers Albert R. Broccoli and Harry Saltzman, director Lewis Gilbert, cinematographer Freddie Young, and production designer Sir Ken Adam were booked to leave Japan on BOAC flight 911, departing Tokyo for Hong Kong and London. Two hours before their Boeing 707 flight departed, the team was invited to an unexpected ninja demonstration, and so missed their plane. Their flight took off as scheduled, and 25 minutes after take-off, the plane encountered severe turbulence and disintegrated over Mt. Fuji, killing all aboard', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8eaebd42-c298-4f3c-91a1-f2cad42247ef'), 'The volcano set cost almost as much as Dr. No (1962)''s entire budget. It was so large, it could be seen from three miles away', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc74823d-b129-4cea-9ce5-9e9c1851cfbf'), 'The henchman that Bond fights in Osato''s office was played by Samoan pro wrestler Peter Fanene Maivia, known by his ring name "The High Chief". Maivia also served as the film''s fight choreographer, and is the grandfather of wrestler Dwayne Johnson', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('abe48607-3818-4f8f-952e-0598f0986597'), 'The relationship between Sir Sean Connery and the producers deteriorated to the point where he refused to act if they were on-set', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c6f7aafa-d499-452a-beaf-590f797a3a1b'), 'As this was anticipated to be Sir Sean Connery''s last appearance as James Bond, publicity material released in advance of the movie announced Bond would be killed, married, and become Japanese. While these events were portrayed in this movie, they were actually ruses as part of Bond''s undercover activities', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('618fe01b-e651-4fff-810e-dfe6516b6919'), 'During the filming of his scenes, Donald Pleasence claimed that the white cat which was selected for his character kept dirtying his trousers when frightened', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3c917b2b-facf-4a67-9748-b88c25ec5176'), 'Aerial unit cameraman John Jordan lost his foot during the filming of the helicopter stunt sequence. He was shooting from the camera helicopter while sitting on the floor with his legs dangling out, when one of the other choppers flew too close below, and caused a major downdraft. Jordan''s helicopter dropped down towards the rotor blades of the chopper below, which sliced through his leg and the landing struts of the camera helicopter. Doctors managed to re-attach his leg, but it eventually turned gangrenous, so it had to be amputated. He died three years later during the filming of Catch-22 (1970), after he had refused to wear a harness while filming a bomber scene. While sitting in the tail gunner position of the camera plane and giving a hand signal to another airplane, he lost his grip and fell 4,000 feet to his death', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fb1dee56-bbae-46c8-87c3-6b3c7eb8ee29'), 'Reportedly, the noise made during the shooting of the grand finale on the volcano set scared "Blofeld''s" white cat and it ran away. It wasn''t found for several days, and it was eventually discovered hiding in some of the set''s rafters. Footage of the scared cat wound up in the finished movie when "Blofeld''s" security shutters are closed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('019f433b-384d-489e-adc6-486cde7c7d04'), 'First movie to show James Bond in his Royal Navy uniform and to clearly indicate that he holds the rank of Commander', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ba34752d-2f2a-4c4e-b7c5-a1ff0a0ebedf'), 'The rocket pistol and cigarette rocket were real-life weapons that were featured after the manufacturer paid for the product placement. It was hoped they would become standard military and intelligence equipment. However, they proved to be too expensive (ammunition cost three times as much as normal ammo), clumsy (useless at any distance over 15 yards), and unreliable (horribly inaccurate and tended to start fires), and ceased production in 1969', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0b3598a0-3664-48e5-ae50-546005f85ecb'), 'While in Japan, Sir Sean Connery and his then-wife Diane Cilento were hounded by the international press. During news conferences, the press insisted on referring to Connery as James Bond. Local newsmen attempted to photograph him in a rest room. Thirty extra private security guards were hired to combat the excess noise and hindrance, but even the guards started to take photos. Connery was allegedly photographed on a toilet and the picture published in a Tokyo newspaper. Halfway through filming, Connery announced he would not be returning as James Bond. To ease the tension, the producers removed his contractual obligation to do one more 007 movie, despite offering him $1 million. After this movie wrapped, Connery was reportedly asked whether he found Japanese women attractive, to which he allegedly replied no, causing many Japanese people to call him bad names. This faux pas turned out to be based on a mistranslation, on a day when Connery was exhausted after an intensive day''s filming. Connery didn''t go out of his way to be too personable with the interviewer who was aghast that the actor showed up in a casual t-shirt with baggy trousers and sandals, and not wearing a toupée. "Is this how James Bond dresses?" he asked, to which Connery replied tersely "I''m not James Bond, I''m Sean Connery, a man who likes to dress comfortably."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4f776ae2-e2e9-47e8-ba62-1970f5053084'), 'Last Bond movie to make extensive use of voice dubbing. In this movie, and most of those made previously, many of Bond''s leading ladies and villains were dubbed by other actors and actresses. This practice rarely occurred in future Bond movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('28d4c208-d3c2-41ce-9aaf-3b6dee652e5d'), 'One hundred of the four hundred inhabitants of the southern village of Akime appeared as extras in the Ama fishing village scenes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('50576557-643d-4951-aee5-7d740529e63c'), 'The atmosphere during the production was reportedly chilly. Sir Sean Connery had grown bored with the Bond role and frustrated with the public fascination with the franchise. The movie posters declaring that "Sean Connery IS James Bond" didn''t help. Furthermore, Bernard Lee and Lois Maxwell were appearing in the James Bond knock-off Operation Kid Brother (1967) with Neil Connery, Sean''s younger brother, and the elder Connery let them know he was not happy about it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7ca1ffdf-930d-4738-9cd5-a4eff05f96e4'), 'Tsai Chin, who played Bond''s playmate in the opening pre-credit sequence, returned to the Bond film franchise in a cameo appearance in Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a317e1a-7749-4af0-a7ee-306e15577a08'), '"Blofeld" Donald Pleasence never blinks when speaking', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8ec482ce-9933-4bde-9f64-34b8738eed5f'), 'This is the only EON Productions'' "James Bond" movie to date in which James Bond does not get behind the wheel of an automobile', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e2ff633a-2f89-46c3-a365-881e6b6b3694'), 'Out of simple courtesy on Bond''s part, this is the only movie in which he accepts a martini (from Henderson) that is stirred, not shaken. This is an intentional joke by the producers, not a mistake in the script', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('945cb537-f8a9-45f6-97a9-fcbd4558c653'), 'The Little Nellie gyrocopter was based on the real-life Wallis Autogyro. Its inventor, Wing Commander K.H. Wallis, actually flew Little Nellie in this movie. The machine was incorporated into the plot after production designer Sir Ken Adam heard Wallis in a radio interview discussing his invention. Wallis had to log 85 flights in total to film the sequence. It was filmed in the Japanese mountains, except for one scene. The scene where the rockets were fired was filmed outside of Japan, because Japanese law forbade the firing of rockets in the air', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('494f91a7-382e-48d4-b45e-3f659d181411'), 'In order to gain some measure of authenticity for the team of stuntmen who would double as ninjas in the climactic battle in the volcano, the producers enlisted the help of Japan''s only practicing ninja master, 34-year-old Masaaki Hatsumi, who had inherited the tradition from his then-retired teacher Toshitsugu Takamatsu. Takamatsu and Hatsumi had advised during the production of the first two of the Japanese "Shinobi No Mono" Ninja Assassins series of movies produced in Japan between 1962 and 1966, and not only did this movie provide an opportunity for Hatsumi to give more credibility to the ninja characters, but also allowed him a few brief moments of screen-time aboard Tiger Tanaka''s private train, as he interrupts Bond and Tanaka''s sake discussion to announce that the photographs are ready for viewing', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9aa0eba9-b56a-491c-9efa-0ef343e7c176'), 'Much of the story structure of this movie was re-used extensively in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), Moonraker (1979), and Tomorrow Never Dies (1997)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80d35cee-179e-4fed-8d56-1fc7c002bbbb'), 'Donald Pleasence''s ideas for "Blofeld''s" appearance included a hump, a limp, a beard, and a lame hand, before he settled on the scar. He found it uncomfortable, though, because of the glue that attached it to his eye', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3d3099ef-1bf0-4c5a-9e79-f9b41e5adaa2'), 'Terence Stamp was considered by producer Harry Saltzman as a replacement for Sir Sean Connery. He suggested to Saltzman that he play the role disguised as a Japanese warrior, revealing his identity at the end. Saltzman was not impressed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e1c448e7-45a2-4ade-a058-880b73882727'), 'The Toyota 2000GTs used in this movie were not convertibles; they had no roofs at all. Sir Sean Connery would not have fit into any 2000GT with the roof up, so the roofs were removed entirely, and not replaced with soft tops', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b4e71d07-8676-4734-be23-825230034a27'), 'Nancy Sinatra was the first non-British singer to perform a theme song for a James Bond movie. In The Nation''s Favourite Bond Song (2015), shown in Britain, it was revealed that she was so nervous about doing it that it took 25 takes, and the final song used in the film was made up of the best parts from each recording', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a0389b42-67c8-4df7-b042-303f9370d080'), 'Director Lewis Gilbert''s regular editor, Thelma Connell, was originally hired to edit this movie. However, after her initial, almost-three-hour cut received a terrible response from test audiences, Peter R. Hunt was asked to re-edit the movie. Hunt''s cut proved to be a much greater success, and he was awarded the director''s chair on the next movie as a result', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6e8a84e9-4c2d-4f32-a357-fb0f83732822'), 'The face of "Ernst Stavro Blofeld" is shown for the first time in a movie. Of all the many actors who have played "Blofeld", it is the interpretation by Donald Pleasence in this movie which is the source for the Mike Myers parody of the character as "Dr. Evil" in the Austin Powers film franchise. "Blofeld" appeared in later Bond movies, played by a different actor each time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0f76b338-1a4e-4e9e-89fe-5a3cf6247aab'), 'Tiger Tanaka''s voice was dubbed by series regular Robert Rietty, but one line remains in his own voice: when he speaks Japanese to the girls bathing him and Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('07bb3ca1-51a1-499b-8126-6a8b300defe6'), 'In the novel, Ian Fleming describes "Blofeld''s" hide-out as being a castle on the coast. Sir Ken Adam discovered that this could never be constructed: the Japanese never built their castles directly on the coast for fear of typhoons, hence, the creation of the elaborate volcano set', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('576f7823-0627-4b85-9979-e4fd21ab2037'), 'The reason why this movie is so different from the book is that Roald Dahl hated the book. He called it Ian Fleming''s worst book, comparing it to a travelogue. On creating the plot, Dahl said he "didn''t know what the hell Bond was going to do" despite having to deliver the first draft in six weeks, and decided to do a basic plot similar to Dr. No (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3708788e-5f7d-40b8-9868-890ca6e0564a'), 'Sir Ken Adam''s volcano set was constructed at Pinewood Studios and consisted of a movable helicopter platform, a working monorail system, a launch pad, and a full-scale rocket mock-up that could simulate lift-off. Seven hundred metric tons of structural steel and 200 miles of tubular steel were used. Adam once said that the set used more steel than was used for the London Hilton Hotel. The set also used 200 metric tons of plaster, 500,000 tubular couplings, 8,000 railway ties for the monorail, and over 250,000 square yards of canvas to protect the set from the weather, were all employed in the construction of the set, which cost just over $1 million. It was visible from three miles away', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('403a588f-ddbd-4631-9163-33c9ef87fc05'), 'This marks the fifth and final on-screen appearance together of Sir Sean Connery and Lois Maxwell. In Diamonds Are Forever (1971), the scene where the disguised Moneypenny gives Bond his travel documents at the port of Dover, Maxwell and Connery filmed their lines separately, and were not present together for the short scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a68f19c2-8fb9-47bb-bab6-c62d8ccd3a66'), 'Screenwriter Roald Dahl later said that of all the filmed adaptations of his written works, this one was the only one where he liked the filmed results', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fa175a5e-de0e-459f-8248-1e325bda7c6f'), 'The novel was the last Ian Fleming James Bond novel published during his lifetime. Released on 16 March 1964, it was the 12th novel in the series. For the first time in the James Bond film franchise, the screenplay bore little resemblance to the source novel. Some characters and the Japanese setting remain intact, as do several minor details (the oubliette, and the man wearing a face mask, et cetera), but the two stories are radically different', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1a6e85f6-d979-4565-afa1-1236b30cfc8b'), 'This was the second highest-grossing movie of 1967 after The Dirty Dozen (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3528ede0-5fc9-45fa-ad1f-b0ccc2b5ed5c'), 'Before the title sequence, there is an outdoor shot of a Russian radar station where U.S. and Soviet leaders are having a crisis meeting. This was filmed at Mågerø in the Oslo fjord in Norway to add a Nordic winter feel to the footage. The dome-shaped radar station is still in operation today, run by the Norwegian military', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87f379c9-7ab1-4282-8b63-c732add93ebd'), 'Nancy Sinatra was asked to perform the title song after her father Frank passed on the opportunity', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a8f170cf-be49-484f-9e07-4caf11e95b69'), 'Despite being a major character in this movie, Kissy Suzuki''s name is never mentioned once on-screen, nor do we learn Aki''s last name. Both situations are unique amongst major Bond movie characters', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('adcd3654-6dae-4f4c-a466-9cc7421e09b2'), 'After it was discovered that Mie Hama (Kissy Suzuki) couldn''t swim, Sir Sean Connery''s then-wife, actress Diane Cilento, doubled for her in her swimming scenes wearing a black wig. Some reports claims that Hama could not do them because of stomach cramps', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('92c84db4-9af1-4e64-894c-d67edcf62aeb'), 'Donald Pleasence worked on the film for three weeks', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e0cfcded-8e0f-41e9-bc8a-e63a53ab6a28'), 'The volcano base was the result of 379 conceptual drawings', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9b33de9d-e106-4627-8dfd-6590c182c2db'), 'The Little Nellie gyrocopter shown being assembled is not the one that is shown flying. The "kit" machine was a mock-up made strictly for the assembly sequence. The WA-118 gyrocopter was flown by its owner, Wing Commander K.H. Wallis, during all the action sequences', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0ef9260f-6c61-463a-bdfa-79edd127c1c4'), 'Bond producer Barbara Broccoli grew up in the behind-the-scenes world of James Bond, and as a child during location shooting in Japan for this movie, she caught a fever from the Japanese custom of sleeping on the floor. Sir Sean Connery''s star status provided him with a comfortable bed, and he generously relinquished it so she could properly fight her illness', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d7db25b-ab4c-47c8-abf9-0dbe6c65c067'), 'Several actors were asked to play "Blofeld" before Donald Pleasence, but all had stage or television commitments which made them unable to accept the role. Producer Harry Saltzman, who had an eccentric choice for actors to play villains, had originally hired Jan Werich to play "Blofeld". Werich was the personification of sophisticated intellectual humor in Czech theater and movies, and was known as the "Wise Clown". Casting a clown as a demonic villain backfired during production. It was felt that Werich looked too much like Father Christmas (Santa Claus) to be menacing, and he was released after a week''s shooting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('af0e06ac-5ae8-4578-af40-7155edbe42ea'), 'The ship from which 007 was "buried" at sea was the Royal Navy ship H.M.S. Tenby (F65). The scene was filmed in the winter, which didn''t go over too well with the crew, who had to wear tropical gear for the scene. It was shot several times as the "body" didn''t sink the first time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98df8027-7b9f-46a6-8064-9d902a12b7ee'), 'Burt Kwouk (SPECTRE Number 3) was dubbed. Kwouk had previously played Mr. Ling in Goldfinger (1964)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c548ac6d-a4a7-4a80-9215-e9570ddb3fec'), 'Only Bond movie in which 007 refers to Miss Moneypenny by the nickname "Penny". This nickname was also used, on occasion, in the original Ian Fleming novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('43002af0-5d3f-4e7b-9727-d26e5f9d570c'), 'The first Bond movie in which 007 does not visit Britain at all. Because of this plot point, M and Miss Moneypenny are given portable offices, a gimmick re-used in The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), and Moonraker (1979)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('edf61989-660f-45fc-a732-106e655eb8ef'), 'Actor and stuntman Joe Robinson instructed Sir Sean Connery in the art of judo for the scene where Bond has to fight with "Blofeld''s" giant bodyguard "Hans" near the end of the movie. Robinson also doubled Ronald Rich, who portrayed "Hans". He appeared as diamond smuggler "Peter Franks" in Diamonds Are Forever (1971)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('16df0a35-f579-4b8b-bb52-664c48df375e'), 'In the fall of 1967, Eva Renzi told the Newark Evening News that she declined the Helga Brandt part because "Bond pictures are good for pretty girls, but not for actresses. I would rather sell shoes."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('feed1e97-2047-47fb-8877-050422f10bba'), 'This movie was released two months after Casino Royale (1967). This was the first of two times that two James Bond movies were released in the same year. It occurred again 16 years later with Octopussy (1983) and Never Say Never Again (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('056a06b2-13e5-4fd9-87fc-b9f72dbc0ce5'), 'William Sylvester has a brief uncredited role, involved in the second launch of U.S. astronauts. Sylvester''s next role was as Dr. Heywood Floyd in 2001: A Space Odyssey (1968)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'You Only Live Twice'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('cc52b629-98cb-4dd6-a344-0bb3c7dd6cea'), 'Sir Sean Connery was originally meant to appear in this film, but opted out due to the studio refusing to pay his $1,250,000 fee. Connery was replaced by George Lazenby. However, Connery was able to renegotiate with the studio, and return in the next Bond film, Diamonds Are Forever (1971)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('11282da8-1169-4f5e-98d2-47df4d615df8'), 'During filming at Piz Gloria, the cast and crew received their per diems in cash. Upon seeing George Lazenby with a suitcase stuffed full of cash, Telly Savalas invited him to a late-night poker game that he regularly held with crew members, and promptly relieved Lazenby of having to carry so much extra weight. Upon hearing of this, producer Harry Saltzman visited the location, joined the game over Savalas'' protests, and won back Lazenby''s money. He then informed Savalas in no uncertain terms that he was not to victimize his "boy" (Lazenby) again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b96d0fa5-10d7-4f36-84d9-ba11408c44cd'), '"Blofeld''s" headquarters was a partially completed restaurant on top of Mount Schilthorn. The owners allowed filming on condition EON Productions paid $125,000 and made the interior sets as permanent fixtures and construct a helicopter pad. This involved 500 tons of concrete being taken up by helicopter at a cost of $125,000. When the restaurant opened, it was given the name Piz Gloria used in the movie. The only public access to the restaurant is by cable car (from Mürren or Stechelberg). The Piz Gloria was the first established revolving mountain restaurant in the world', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40238551-6afe-4fa4-8fd6-6c44b41d2560'), 'Having secured a suit ordered but uncollected by Sir Sean Connery and getting a Rolex and haircut like him, George Lazenby talked his way into meeting producer Albert R. Broccoli, producer Harry Saltzman, and director Peter R. Hunt. After bluffing his way through the meeting and falsely claiming he had wide acting credits, he secured a screentest. Lazenby then confessed to Hunt that he had made it all up and that he wasn''t an actor. Hunt laughed and told him, "You just strolled in here and managed to fool two of the most ruthless bastards in the business. You''re an actor."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('009abf7d-3fa0-45a3-893c-8bbef6efcbfb'), 'George Lazenby suggested a scene where Bond skis off a cliff and opens a parachute. This was scrapped, as the filmmakers lacked the resources to pull it off. It was used as the opening for The Spy Who Loved Me (1977)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9f4bc7e1-f9b8-4748-a581-a2c3375aae60'), 'The producers originally intended to explain the change of lead actors in this movie by saying that Bond had undergone plastic surgery because his "old" face was now too well-known by foreign spies and terrorists for him to go undercover. But they then decided not to refer to the change at all, and thus hopefully minimize the public attention being paid to George Lazenby''s replacing Sir Sean Connery. However, after the opening action sequence, right before the titles, Bond says directly to the camera, "This never happened to the other fellow", an intentionally comedic reference to the change in actors', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1dc40ff3-199d-4509-8785-38cadb549583'), 'There are many reasons why George Lazenby only made one appearance as James Bond. According to the DVD documentary, and the 2012 documentary "007: Everything Or Nothing", the reasons given were:Lazenby''s youthful cockiness rankled producer Albert R. Broccoli''s nerves. One incident mentioned is Lazenby skiing down the slopes on his own (resulting in the broken arm) and a moment of arrogance on Lazenby''s part that spoiled a cast and crew party; The notoriously harsh British tabloids writing up unfavorable stories about Lazenby and how he failed to measure up to Sean Connery, thereby swaying public opinion against the movie before it was released. One incident cited by Lazenby was during an interview with a reporter in the commissary in which Dame Diana Rigg jokingly yelled from across the room "I''m having garlic for lunch, darling! I hope you are too!" This lead to an article in which Rigg supposedly hated Lazenby so much that "She eats garlic before love scenes"; Lazenby arrived at the premiere with longer hair and a beard (much in the late -1960s counter-culture style of young people at the time, but totally at odds with the Bond persona). The producers were none too pleased with Lazenby becoming more and more of a liability and, despite the fact he had reportedly been offered a seven-movie deal, they opted to secure Connery''s return for the next film; Another deciding factor was the lower box office take of this film. While it was still a hit, recouping more than ten times its cost and becoming the second highest grossing movie of the year at the worldwide box office, it failed to match the grosses of the Sean Connery Bond films, suggesting that the public did not accept Lazenby in the way they had Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('047e8b07-26fe-49f9-a3a6-20b82829bb9f'), 'Ilse Steppat''s only English-language role was as "Irma Bunt" in this movie. She was not able to enjoy her new success. She died of a heart attack less than a week after the release of this movie, making it her final film role. The character of "Irma Bunt" was intended to return in the next James Bond movie, Diamonds Are Forever (1971). But because of her death, the character did not return', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('49f9c52d-2336-4d97-be95-b3da825e9164'), 'Sir Sean Connery later said that he would have preferred to do a Bond movie like this one, as opposed to You Only Live Twice (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('caf562b6-c24c-49e9-baa1-9c6fe6b03550'), 'George Lazenby is the only actor to get a Golden Globe nomination for playing James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8dd8ab8b-a59e-4088-9a4a-cb8aa26c355d'), 'According to George Lazenby, he and a crew member played a prank on Angela Scoular (Ruby), the Bond Girl who writes her room number on the inside of James Bond''s bare thigh. The crew member warmed a sausage, and they put it under Bond''s kilt. When Scoular puts her hand under the kilt, she is ever the professional and hardly reacts', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5691f933-8146-4426-a4f5-902dc4e81f2f'), 'For the opening sequence, railroad ties were buried under the sand to allow Bond''s Aston Martin to drive on the beach', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ca46b0fc-aa64-443d-9a1e-106bb34a17ee'), 'The theme "We Have All the Time in the World" was the last thing that Louis Armstrong ever recorded. He died two years later. It is also the first theme song in the film franchise not to include the movie''s title as part of the lyrics', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4136dd8b-aaf3-4a81-b3d9-bdc2b10c5832'), 'This is Sir Christopher Nolan''s favorite Bond movie, and many references can be found in Inception (2010). He said, "What I liked about it, that we''ve tried to emulate in this film, is there''s a tremendous balance in that movie of action and scale and romanticism and tragedy and emotion."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e70275da-7e40-4565-91a3-3815dca532e3'), 'This is the last time that John Barry''s original Dr. No (1962) arrangement of the James Bond Theme would be used on-screen. It would however, continue to be used in trailers, et cetera as late as Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('958d45ad-0279-48c9-aed3-89696b93c003'), 'George Lazenby wanted to do most of his own stunts, but the studio wouldn''t allow him. During the shooting of one of the stunt scenes, Lazenby broke his arm, thereby delaying the filming of many of his later scenes. When James Bond is taken to "Ernst Stavro Blofeld''s" Telly Savalas lab at Piz Gloria, Lazenby''s broken arm in its cast is hidden by his coat, which was draped over his arm. "Blofeld''s" guard removes it from him as Lazenby was unable to do so. The guard removing the jacket was played by Yuri Borienko, who ironically had had his nose broken by Lazenby in the screen-test fight scene that the actor had done to land the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('244b42c5-6e5f-4ff1-9fc3-ee6f4995d8f4'), 'The only Bond film which was entirely set and filmed in Europe', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('10c6d1f3-fbd1-457a-9872-f24c1e501116'), 'Willy Bogner performed some spectacular skiing feats for the filming of chase sequences for this movie. These included skiing backwards downhill with a hand-held camera, sometimes placing it between his legs and being towed behind a bobsleigh along the bobsled course', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('12612369-2185-45f2-97ff-ce7043db7510'), 'As James Bond passes a janitor in "Marc-Ange Draco''s" headquarters, the man can be heard whistling the Goldfinger (1964) theme', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d2d504c4-8fcf-4b43-865f-586df1d608bb'), 'Many Olympic ski competitors, as well as other ski experts, contributed as body doubles, extras, and supporting roles for performing the necessary skiing sequences in the movie. The principal actors were not allowed to ski in the movie, due to insurance regulations', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4cd46bfe-7d0e-4027-ba0d-48bd128bb1c5'), 'This movie performed admirably, out-grossing its nearest competitor almost two to one at the U.S. box office where, according to Variety, it was the most popular movie in the country for four solid weeks. It generated enough rentals at the box office to claim ninth position on the box office chart for 1970. The persistent belief that it was a flop arises from its earnings in comparison to the previous three Sir Sean Connery Bond movies, all of which made more than $100 million worldwide, whereas this movie grossed $87 million worldwide', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('84322f3b-9e7f-49b3-b869-30bfc31e5869'), 'Featured the only signature gun barrel sequence of all James Bond movies in which Bond drops down on one knee while shooting at the audience. It''s also the only version of the sequence where the descending blood completely erases Bond''s image, leaving only the red circle', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('888b2e4e-b6e1-4a85-b46e-c62a54202d1d'), 'Certain filming techniques appeared in the James Bond film franchise for the first time in this movie: slow-motion (when Bond is knocked out in his bedroom), flashback (Bond remembering Tracy being captured), and "breaking the fourth wall" (George Lazenby looking into the camera briefly, immediately after his line "This never happened to the other fella"). Though it seems to be a self referential remark (Lazenby replaced Sir Sean Connery as Bond), it also has a meaning in the context of the story', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6d8e9697-2150-4958-aad0-2b3e60b450c9'), 'In the novel, the casino where James Bond and Teresa "Tracy" Draco play baccarat is the Casino Royale, where Bond makes annual visits to the grave of his old flame Vesper Lynd nearby', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('71e91dae-7f93-48cc-a988-19221162acc1'), 'First Bond movie since From Russia with Love (1963) to use an instrumental theme over the opening titles. The decision to forgo the usual song was prompted by the conclusion that any lyric composition that attempted to include the full title of this movie would be awkward, and at best, sound like a humorous Gilbert and Sullivan song, which would be inappropriate for the film franchise. As of 2015, no other movie in the franchise since has done so', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1cc74fd0-6712-4454-9b79-af1a67f661b6'), 'The picture of "Tracy''s" mother was a photograph of Dame Diana Rigg''s own mother', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cbb7c27c-3934-4f76-aa9c-b5dc0e77495b'), 'Whereas ads for You Only Live Twice (1967) loudly touted "Sean Connery IS James Bond", the marketing for this movie downplayed the name of the replacement actor completely. This is the last time that the name of the actor playing Bond appears below the title, and in several of the ads for the movie, there is an image of a faceless Bond. Since George Lazenby was a virtual unknown when he was cast as Bond, initial teaser advertising for the movie emphasized the Bond character rather than the actor playing him. United Artists would later say that this marketing strategy was a mistake, which hurt the movie''s performance at the box office', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a4de5180-1d8a-44aa-ba3b-abc03776863b'), 'While cracking open a safe in a Swiss lawyer''s office, Bond finds a copy of Playboy, referencing the original story on which the film is based, as it first appeared in the magazine. On Her Majesty''s Secret Service was the first of Ian Fleming''s Bond novels serialised in Playboy, featured in the May 1963 issue. It was followed by a shortened version of You Only Live Twice in April 1964. The film includes the February 1969 issue with centrefold Lorrie Menconi', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('beac30e6-c065-48ff-9d47-a715a16a21fc'), 'Timothy Dalton was offered the part of James Bond, but turned it down feeling that, at twenty-two, he was too young and relatively inexperienced to take the role. Dalton played Bond in The Living Daylights (1987) and Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ac55da74-52c0-4a72-bc2c-2d19f9399239'), 'George Lazenby said he experienced difficulties during shooting, not receiving any coaching despite his lack of acting experience, and with director Peter R. Hunt never addressing him directly, only through his assistant. Lazenby also declared that Hunt also asked the rest of the crew to keep a distance from him, as "Peter thought the more I was alone, the better I would be as James Bond."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('05abe934-dce4-48ee-b856-dc658289ccc1'), 'The sequence where James Bond finds Teresa "Tracy" Draco waiting for him in his hotel suite has since been used as an audition scene for actors trying for the role of James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('364d9b89-3410-435c-b6f6-3191cf3740b0'), 'Donald Pleasence was replaced as "Ernst Stavro Blofeld" because producer Albert R. Broccoli and director Peter R. Hunt felt he was unsuited to the more physical side of the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2e67c77f-a79d-40a7-8e41-b820cb4d0fe9'), 'Bond''s line to the Saint Bernard about going to get the brandy was improvised by George Lazenby', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('051c0bde-7ee6-4e2a-9bf9-175adc9ce7a1'), 'This was originally going to be the fourth Bond movie. However, Thunderball (1965) was filmed instead after the on-going rights dispute over the novel were settled between Ian Fleming and Kevin McClory. It was due to follow that, but problems with a warm Swiss winter and inadequate snow cover led to the producers postponing the movie again, favoring production of You Only Live Twice (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('388bef4f-d528-4b3a-853b-db390688c065'), 'Every year, the Swiss army dynamites mountainsides to prevent avalanches. For a film scene, the crew collaborated with the army to find a location, but a natural avalanche occurred before filming. They ended up using stock footage, special effects, and close-ups for the scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab3c3d82-9f61-4e85-913e-762073bfafd6'), 'The title was a corruption of a very familiar phrase known to most British people. For many decades, all correspondence sent from Government departments (the Tax Office, Social Services, et cetera), arrived in envelopes which did not have a stamp, but had the words, "On Her ("His" when there was a male monarch) Majesty''s Service" printed on the envelope. Such correspondence was usually referred to as "OHMS"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2094f898-bc2a-45a9-8d80-0d58056ce6a2'), 'The motto, "Orbis non sufficit", given to Bond when he researches his own coat of arms before impersonating "Sir Hilary Bray", is Latin for "The World Is Not Enough", which was used as a Bond movie title in The World Is Not Enough (1999)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6536b848-08c1-49d3-a249-c15895c4a8c9'), 'Between the resignation of Sir Sean Connery at the beginning of filming You Only Live Twice (1967) and its release, producer Harry Saltzman had planned to adapt "The Man with the Golden Gun" in Cambodia and use Sir Roger Moore as the next Bond, but political instability meant the location was ruled out and Moore signed up for another season of The Saint (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3584e885-e81a-4644-a993-d96d055a9709'), 'Dame Diana Rigg said one of the reasons for accepting the role of "Tracy" was that she always wanted to be in an epic movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dfe65ee1-7db0-4692-a366-cd8a63c13160'), 'Bond''s sliding along the ice while firing a machine gun in the attack on Piz Gloria was a spur-of-the-moment idea from director Peter R. Hunt', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('69c3976e-c82a-409b-bbe9-d1d885e6af9d'), 'Final time until For Your Eyes Only (1981) that James Bond would be seen tossing his hat. He does it twice in this movie: the ritualistic one in "Miss Moneypenny''s" office, and again at the wedding ceremony', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80440961-b053-4448-b0e3-38709b80a687'), 'Camera operator John Jordan had also filmed the helicopter sequences for the previous Bond movie, You Only Live Twice (1967), and lost his foot when his helicopter suddenly dropped down, and the rotor blades of another chopper below sliced through his leg. Doctors initially managed to re-attach his leg, but it eventually turned gangrenous so it had to be amputated. Jordan nevertheless returned for this film, and filmed scenes while suspended eighteen feet under a jet helicopter as the pilot flew around mountain peaks and glaciers. The following year, Jordan was tragically killed on a similar job for Catch-22 (1970), when he fell out of the plane he was filming from, after refusing to wear a harness', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5b287708-1c4e-4fff-adb3-c5cca73912de'), 'This was once the longest Bond film made (142 min). Even so, two scenes were deleted from the final print: "Irma Bunt" spying on Bond as he buys a wedding ring for "Tracy", and a chase over London rooftops and into the Royal Mail underground rail system after Bond''s conversation with "Sir Hilary Bray" was overheard. It was only recently exceeded by Casino Royale (2006) (144 min), Spectre (2015) (148 min), and No Time to Die (2021) (163 min). Prior to this film, Thunderball (1965) was the longest at 130 minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2219677b-4c1f-4ebb-a164-7225d5fd9622'), 'Kevin McClory considered casting George Lazenby as James Bond in Never Say Never Again (1983), but Lazenby was dropped from consideration when Sir Sean Connery confirmed that he wanted the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b34eb79a-4bc9-476d-93a1-7bd536453559'), 'James Bond tells "Marc-Ange Draco", regarding Teresa ''Tracy'' Draco, "Her price is far above rubies, or even your million pounds." The first six words are from Proverbs 31:10, which describes a worthy woman', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fa5ced59-7a0b-4578-890e-e53f92c31185'), 'No Time to Die (2021) drew heavily from this film in its plot, themes, and tone. It also featured the 1969 Aston Martin DBS and Louis Armstrong''s song "We Have All the Time in the World"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80e83b53-882f-42c8-9d5b-57737f477434'), 'George Lazenby attended the premiere after growing a full beard and shoulder length hair. This was seen by some as a protest against the producers, while trying to intentionally sabotage his future in the film franchise. Despite his contract for future Bond movies, Lazanby was having second thoughts, as he had difficulty keeping up with the rigors and demands of making and promoting the movie. At the same time, Lazenby''s agents had him convinced that the Bond film franchise would soon lose its audience. Lazenby''s relationship with producers Albert R. Broccoli and Harry Saltzman had already started to become strained over the course of production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d9d0ceae-80fe-4927-b53b-9f93887dd2d1'), 'George Baker provided the voice of Bond when 007 is pretending to be "Sir Hilary Bray"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6bd51e27-9e41-4378-b109-d9dfe32f0b10'), 'The motto on the coat of arms that "Ernst Stavro Blofeld" seeks to claim as his own, "Arae et foci", can be translated "For hearth and home"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3514582d-6706-48ad-b225-148383dc6b43'), 'The John Barry score for this movie was the first in the EON Productions franchise to extensively use synthesizers and electric guitars', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1b8f7028-586d-42d7-9711-56ca25ad0411'), 'During filming, George Lazenby (James Bond) was fooling around on horseback and caused Bernard Lee (M) to fall into a fence and tear his leg open. As no doctor was available, the local vet stitched up the gash', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('131a38a5-4051-42a7-a61c-b430c1b1a651'), 'This is the favorite bond movie of Steven Soderbergh who said "For me there''s no question that cinematically On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) is the best Bond film and the only one worth watching repeatedly for reasons other than pure entertainment (certainly it''s the only Bond film I look at and think: I''m stealing that shit)."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('96b5d0fa-fd25-48f8-8964-dcb99ace3214'), 'It has been alleged that George Lazenby and Dame Diana Rigg didn''t get along. However, according to director Peter R. Hunt, these rumors are untrue and there were no such difficulties, or else they were minor, and may have started with Rigg joking to Lazenby before filming a love scene "Hey George, I''m having garlic for lunch. I hope you are!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f42d42ea-76c6-4e7e-b846-fff3763277ed'), 'Born in Australia, George Lazenby is one of two James Bond actors who was born outside the United Kingdom. The other actor is Pierce Brosnan, who was born in Ireland', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b67d0767-f5b7-4df3-bf97-97830ea1f6ae'), 'For the scene where Bond and Tracy crash into a car race while being pursued, an ice rink was constructed over an unused airplane track, with water and snow sprayed on it constantly. George Lazenby and Dame Diana Rigg did most of the driving due to the high number of close-ups', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('08053643-1572-47aa-aa37-2a268cf16e96'), 'This is the only James Bond movie in which Bond goes to Portugal, where Ian Fleming was inspired by Casino do Estoril to create "Casino Royale", the first Bond novel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3a65a066-236d-45b8-b22d-36a99975eebc'), '"Nymphalis polychloris", the species of butterfly that James Bond detects at M''s home, is a fictional taxon', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0366ae88-5d56-4c2d-a1b6-e05e7ba24b03'), 'Gabriele Ferzetti was only 13 years older than Dame Diana Rigg, who played his daughter', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d501d8ae-7581-41fc-874c-e1fcf5603a9b'), 'The bobsledding chase was also filmed with the help of Swiss Olympic athletes, and was re-written to incorporate the accidents the stuntmen suffered during shooting, such as the scene where Bond falls from the sled', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c2aa632f-e1e9-46bc-a3c1-b4873e98ca25'), 'The first of two times James Bond is shown in his MI6 office. The other being Die Another Day (2002)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ae5c41ff-1163-46a2-a391-d54ca4bed5c0'), 'First time "M''s" house (called Quarterdeck in the film) is seen in a Bond film. Casino Royale (2006) was the second. "M''s" house is also seen in the unofficial Casino Royale (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4459c2a1-1962-42e5-809b-e9d2d617fcd5'), 'An earlier version of the script had Gert Fröbe come back as "Goldfinger''s" twin brother. This was when the Spectre legal rights were still being decided. Another version had "Goldfinger" and "Blofeld" as brothers themselves', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0fdc7ba1-7ede-4292-afa5-044dd69d02d7'), 'Director Peter R. Hunt was reported to always enter the set carrying an annotated copy of the novel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d1bf472b-cbcb-4bc6-b224-ef8b44594239'), 'The pre credit scenes of 007 racing a car down the beach to rescue "Tracy" were shot day for night at Guincho Beach outside Estoril', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('f655d0be-4271-48fe-a14f-907764cbb7b5'), 'During a late 1990s airing of the movie on TBS'' "Dinner and A Movie", Bruce Glover recalled that while filming their scenes together, he and Putter Smith had Sir Sean Connery convinced that the two were actually openly homosexual. Glover added that a few years later, while on an airline flight, he was flirting with a stewardess when he suddenly heard a male Scottish-accented voice saying, "You son of a bitch". Glover turned around and saw that the man was Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('15f10d99-e61a-4054-aa09-82473c06ced5'), 'Because of Sir Sean Connery''s high fee, the special effects budget was significantly scaled back. Connery was reportedly paid $1,250,000 to return as James Bond, a figure unheard of in those days', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7388caaa-cc29-40b5-b84d-00d1a2c66c24'), 'Instant mashed potatoes were used to replicate the consistency of the brown substance mud bath featured in the opening teaser. What the producers failed to take into account was that after twenty-four hours, and under all the hot lights, mashed potatoes emit an almost unbearable smell', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('095daddd-5328-4ede-a5fb-194f58570922'), 'Sir Sean Connery made the most of his time on-location in Las Vegas: "I didn''t get any sleep at all. We shot every night, I caught all the shows and played golf all day. On the weekend I collapsed, boy, did I collapse. Like a skull with legs." He also played the slot machines, and once delayed a scene because he was collecting his winnings', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7cda28e-55ed-495e-a891-3c3ccd0831be'), 'During Bond''s briefing with "M" and "Sir Donald Munger" at the beginning, "Munger" refers to Bond having just been on holiday, and "M" later quips how the Service had managed well during Bond''s absence. These were inside jokes referring to Sir Sean Connery''s absence in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f5a31780-3a46-460c-bf6d-620dc1027354'), 'Reportedly, the final scene Sir Sean Connery filmed as Bond (at least in the official film franchise) was the one in which an unconscious Bond is loaded into a coffin at the funeral home. So, Connery''s last day of playing James Bond for EON Productions was Friday, August 13, 1971', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e629961-8252-4538-bec3-d93960efae77'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli hated the line "Alimentary, Dr. Leiter", which Bond says when asked the location of the diamonds concealed in a corpse. He thought no one would understand it referred to digestion. At the premiere, two people in the front row burst out laughing at the line, and Broccoli quipped, "Big deal, they''re doctors."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('38a473bf-6736-4c64-8a9c-c85c52a044cb'), 'Director Guy Hamilton didn''t like big American cars, and took particular delight in trashing them in the movie''s numerous car chase scenes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0bba1795-1bdd-43c4-b9cf-ea18b70798bd'), 'Bond''s escape through a moon landing "movie set" refers to the popular conspiracy theory of the time that the real moon landings were faked. The scene was filmed in a Johns-Manville gypsum plant located just outside of Las Vegas, Nevada. During filming, the moon buggy''s wheels kept falling off. In one scene where a car turns over, you can see one of the wheels that had broken off the buggy rolling in the foreground. The moon buggy was discovered rotting in a farmer''s field in Kent in the early 1990s, and completely restored in 1993 by the James Bond International Fan Club. In 2004, it was auctioned at Christie''s and purchased by Planet Hollywood Las Vegas for $44,000', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1d640775-4041-4385-b7f9-ce9cdbc997cc'), 'George Lazenby was asked to make a second Bond movie but declined, due to a lengthy and restrictive potential contract. Burt Reynolds was the original choice to replace him but was unavailable. John Gavin was signed to play Bond in this movie, and had recently played the French Spy OSS 117 in the Eurospy flick OSS 117 Murder for Sale (1968). Adam West turned down the role because he felt that James Bond should be a British actor (coincidentally, West was first cast as Batman after the producers saw him play a Bond-like character in a Nestlé Quik commercial). Michael Gambon turned down the role because he was "in terrible shape" and "had tits like a woman." At the last minute, Sir Sean Connery agreed to return as Bond for the sixth time in a two-picture deal, at an astronomical salary for the time. Albert R. Broccoli insisted that Gavin be paid the full salary, for which his contract called', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4e4245ea-d043-43c4-b99a-988e63b3823d'), 'The original plot had Gert Fröbe returning as "Auric Goldfinger''s" twin from Goldfinger (1964) seeking revenge for the death of his brother. This character was a Swedish billionaire with a laser mounted on a supertanker', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ee5ba2e-7986-4cb3-b827-b0212835af70'), 'Jill St. John and Lana Wood have been involved in a decades-long feud that began during the filming of this movie, throughout the spring of 1971, when both women were dating Sean Connery at the same time. In February 1982, less than three months after the mysterious drowning of Lana''s sister Natalie Wood, St. John started a romance with Robert Wagner, Natalie''s widower and Lana''s ex-brother-in-law, and eventually married him. At a Bond girl photo shoot reunion in September 1999 for Vanity Fair magazine, an altercation occurred between St. John and Wood when photographer Annie Leibovitz asked for a picture of them together. Reportedly, St. John was so adamantly opposed to the idea that it reduced Wood to tears. Family publicist Alan Nierob, however, said it was he who vetoed the photo because Mr. Wagner would prefer his present wife not be shot with his former sister-in-law. In February 2016, Wood crashed a benefit honoring St. John in Palm Springs and publicly confronted Wagner in front of cameramen over Natalie''s death. (The case has been reopened since November 2011, initiated by yacht skipper Dennis Davern''s admission that he originally lied to police.) Following the confrontation, Wood claimed she received a threatening phone call from an anonymous woman who told her to "lay off" Wagner "or something serious could happen to you." She reported the threat to authorities. "My first instinct was it might be Jill, trying to scare me off, and protect him. But I''d recognize Jill''s voice. It wasn''t her," Wood told RadarOnline in July 2016. Wagner was officially named a Person of Interest in Natalie Wood''s death in February 2018. St. John reportedly slammed the door in LACSD homicide detectives Kevin Lowe and Ralph Hernandez''s faces when they tried to question Wagner at the house she shares with him in Colorado. On July 25, 2018, Lana Wood appeared on Megyn Kelly Today (2017) and when asked by Kelly if she thinks Wagner "murdered" her sister, Lana said, "Yes." Despite this, Lt. Hugo Reynaga announced in May 2022 that the sheriff''s department has cleared Wagner in its investigation into Wood''s death and that the case remains cold', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2bc65326-2bca-4854-8fa0-e0e403b05763'), 'This is the second of three James Bond title songs sung by Dame Shirley Bassey, the others being Goldfinger (1964) and Moonraker (1979). She also sang a version of the "Mr. Kiss Kiss Bang Bang" song for Thunderball (1965), which was not used. To date, Bassey is the only singer to have performed a Bond title song more than once', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4841e40c-665c-450d-bc89-befdaf73643c'), 'Final Bond movie in which he is seen wearing a hat during the gun-barrel sequence. When Sir Roger Moore took over the role in Live and Let Die (1973), the sequence was filmed with Moore without wearing a hat, a tradition that continued with every subsequent Bond movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c4f3c6ad-c549-49aa-9234-c4db4c402faf'), 'When Lana Wood was cast as "Plenty O''Toole", she was told early on that the scene where she is thrown out of Bond''s hotel room and lands in the pool required the stunt team to throw her into the pool "basically naked", but she was assured that no one outside of the crew would see her undressed in public, because the scene would be shot at night. Unfortunately for her, the scene was shot in Las Vegas, and as she noted, most of the people in Vegas were up at night, so contrary to what the filmmakers had promised her, she had to endure countless people watching her from their hotel rooms as she emerged from the pool soaking wet, clad in nothing but flimsy see-through underwear and high heels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f845b5ba-d7e9-40b3-ae1d-8eb41ed0034a'), 'Instead of building their own oil rig, the production team hired a semi-portable one for forty thousand dollars a day, customized it, and then towed it to a location off the Southern California coast', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fbe393af-d9c8-4424-a37a-f3fa85d0d626'), 'Sir Sean Connery dated Jill St. John and Lana Wood during production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ea95bac6-bb54-4fe2-a02b-b937fcd2fd05'), 'Since the car chase in Las Vegas would have many crashes, the filmmakers had an arrangement with Ford to use their vehicles. Ford''s only demand was that Sir Sean Connery had to drive the 1971 Mustang Mach 1 that served as "Tiffany Case''s" car', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('63f5df82-353a-4718-8a1f-20f14652e852'), 'Producers Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli cast Lana Wood as "Plenty O''Toole" after seeing her in Playboy Magazine. Her voice was dubbed in the movie, and she is standing on a box for some of her scenes with Sir Sean Connery because even in high heels, she was too small to fit into the frame with him. In the scene in Bond''s hotel room she was unaware that her derrière would be visible through her pink panties', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80a65af5-7f8f-47bf-a6b4-f61dfeae220b'), 'When director Guy Hamilton couldn''t remember a name he would call it "Hergerscheimer". Hence, the appearance of a doctor named "Hergerscheimer" in this movie is an in-joke from screenwriter Tom Mankiewicz', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7dd06a07-c5e1-4578-8c2e-a5968b755247'), '"Willard Whyte" was based on Howard Hughes. Amongst the similarities; Whyte owned the Whyte House in this movie, Howard Hughes owned a real life Las Vegas Hotel, the Desert Inn. At the time of the movie, Jimmy Dean, who played Whyte, was an employee of Hughes at the Desert Inn. Dean confessed to being largely uneasy portraying a fictional version of his real-life boss', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('521af717-bc58-45a7-a913-95ba6ba26927'), 'Lois Maxwell "Miss Moneypenny" wears a hat in her only scene to hide the fact that she had dyed her hair', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('939bd436-2698-40f3-a6ea-78e8c2727056'), 'Desmond Llewelyn confessed that the RPM controller that "Q" uses to cheat at slot machines was the one 007 gadget he wished actually worked', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6bef4974-547c-4ab4-8afd-6f498b3a386a'), 'Charles Gray "Ernst Stavro Blofeld" played a Bond ally called "Henderson" in You Only Live Twice (1967). David Bauer "Morton Slumber" previously appeared uncredited as an American diplomat in You Only Live Twice (1967). Ed Bishop "Klaus Hergersheimer" also appeared uncredited as "Hawaii CapCom" in "You Only Live Twice" (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('deafff0b-648f-4f5d-b3f6-4c2d34bc98f3'), '"Tiffany''s" house belonged to Kirk Douglas', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('336d4e5b-1ea0-43a1-8d09-a7cf9c4227f9'), '"Miss Moneypenny" was almost re-cast for this movie, as Lois Maxwell''s agent held out for more money. Maxwell was disgruntled that several days working on each Bond movie disrupted her career', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4344414d-5f93-43a9-9291-8369a5260575'), '"Tiffany Case" was blonde in the novel. In this movie, she''s a redhead. This is addressed when Bond meets her "Weren''t you a blonde when I came in?"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f9c92de-05ef-429e-8b29-8a7bd5c67136'), 'For the deleted scene where "Plenty O''Toole", soaking wet and wearing a white towel, returns to Bond''s hotel room after being tossed in the pool in the hopes of retrieving her clothes, and to see if Bond is alright, Lana Wood was not wearing anything under the towel and she was genuinely cold', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d5459597-9ff5-4dd8-9a5d-e3043c4723a1'), 'Upon release, this movie broke Hollywood''s three-day gross record', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('230dbc31-fbae-4a14-b0de-a9f2a8064a45'), 'Lois Maxwell dyed her hair black for Endless Night (1972). As a result, she wears a hat as part of her disguise as a customs officer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8c171cbc-1278-4ee7-a507-24067efb7b9b'), 'The "Willard Whyte" kidnapping plot was based on a dream of producer Albert R. Broccoli. He had known Howard Hughes in Hollywood, and dreamt he was going to meet his old friend in Las Vegas, but when he entered Hughes'' room, it was occupied by an impostor. Hughes was flattered and allowed EON Productions to film inside his casinos, and at his other properties. His fee was reputed to be one 16mm print of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2b872a3d-f88d-4f8c-99ce-b623a75ee44f'), 'Sir Paul McCartney was the first choice to write the title song for this Bond movie, but this did not happen until the next installment, Live and Let Die (1973)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7daba70b-e057-4cf1-bce3-c7bdff904fae'), 'Sir Roger Moore was offered the role of James Bond here, but he was unavailable due to his commitment to The Persuaders! (1971)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c1a6621-8eeb-4361-8fb2-fa1b4997c408'), 'The alleyway car roll sequence was filmed in two locations. The entrance was at the car park at Universal Studios, and the exit was at Fremont Street, Las Vegas. It was filmed over a three-day period. The car chase includes one of the most famous Bond gags ever, in that it enters the narrow alley balanced on the right pair of wheels and emerges while balanced on the left pair of wheels. A shot was inserted of Bond and "Tiffany Case" rolling 90 degrees to the right in an attempt to correct the goof, but this doesn''t explain how Bond was able to flip the car on its other side, as the alley should be too narrow for that', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('129f28d3-ed07-482a-986b-aa69de66041c'), 'Until Spectre (2015), this was the last James Bond movie made by EON Productions to officially use the S.P.E.C.T.R.E. criminal organization or the villain character "Ernst Stavro Blofeld". The name S.P.E.C.T.R.E. is not mentioned at all in this movie, as "Blofeld" is apparently operating sans S.P.E.C.T.R.E. After this movie, writer Kevin McClory''s legal claim against the Ian Fleming estate that he, and not Fleming, had created the organization for the novel "Thunderball" (1961) was upheld by the courts. "Blofeld" is seen, but not identified in For Your Eyes Only (1981), as EON''s arrangements with the Ian Fleming estate at the time did not permit them to use McClory''s works. The McClory-penned unofficial Bond movie Never Say Never Again (1983) made use of "Blofeld" and S.P.E.C.T.R.E., as it was a remake of Thunderball (1965)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0d6973cd-45d5-4488-bed8-03a00012d1cc'), 'Actresses considered for the role of lTiffany Case" included Raquel Welch, Jane Fonda and Faye Dunaway. Jill St. John had originally been offered the part of "Plenty O''Toole", but landed the lead after impressing Director Guy Hamilton during screentests. She became the first American Bond Girl', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6259b807-7b57-4f31-8e31-9447fb7e0fad'), 'Due to the height difference, Lana Wood had to stand on a box for most of her scenes with Sir Sean Connery. This proved to be problematic for the scene where Connery had to strip Lana out of her dress, and down to her underwear, because a body double would not have worked for obvious reasons. Ultimately, Lana was given extra high heels to wear in that scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('340f9d0e-d3aa-4d0b-a4d4-9f058a36108b'), 'The outdoor elevator scenes were shot at the (now demolished) Landmark casino. This building, with its UFO-like penthouse, was replicated in the sci-fi spoof, Mars Attacks! (1996)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f2d6d6ee-2ff6-4c32-a77a-ef5c504fb22c'), 'There is a jewelery shop in London named after lWint" and "Kidd"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('32ba6fd0-c95a-4c77-b6a9-0bc7c6513bc7'), 'The machine that Bond encounters in the oil pipeline looks like a robotic torture device is a Smart PIG (Pipeline Inspection Gauge) and is actually used to check the integrity of pipelines and also that they are free of blockages', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('63965785-4e1e-46c5-9444-fece9d0efaed'), '"Tiffany", being the first American Bond Girl, is argumentative, abrasive, loud, and brash when compared to previous Bond girls who were more demure. She is likely meant to be a commentary on American women', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2e26201d-e97c-4c2d-9636-f2d07632287e'), 'The laser satellite''s reflector is actually the collapsible reflector from an old-fashioned camera flash-bulb attachment', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6cb05521-3075-4e5c-a4cb-e9c34939bca1'), 'Musician Paul Williams was originally cast as "Mr. Wint". However, when he couldn''t agree with the producers on money concerns, Bruce Glover replaced him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('76f200e6-1ab3-4878-9709-98a758d25478'), 'Ilse Steppat was supposed to reprise her role as "Irma Buntl from On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), but she died after that movie was completed. Presumably, Bond would kill her in revenge for "Tracy''s" death', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('701e86b2-560f-4e1c-b4c4-7b78b7b6ed8b'), 'During location filming, Sir Ken Adam visited several funeral homes in the Las Vegas area. The inspiration behind the gaudy design of the Slumber mortuary (the use of tasteless Art Deco furniture and Tiffany lamps) came from these experiences', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('72f15125-a1da-4f5a-827b-86a4230d7e14'), 'Despite being the main henchmen of the movie, "Mr. Wint" and "Mr. Kidd" never share a scene with "Blofeld"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35e9c87e-a7c0-4011-b390-0d42b06e314a'), '"Mr. Wint" originally killed "Dr. Tynan" by shoving the scorpion into his mouth', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('106e5c1f-49c3-4bd3-b8ec-d4141e96abdf'), 'A deleted scene shows how "Mr. Wint" and "Mr. Kidd" killed "Shady Tree", with a water pistol that turns out to be real', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1dee40d7-4389-4dd4-a72c-d5843a260a62'), 'Bond is correct when he describes Mouton Rothschild as a claret. It was officially elevated to that status in 1970, the year before this movie was released. A real sommelier would have known; the fact that "Mr. Wint" didn''t exposed him to Bond as a fraud', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ebd9cf1-def6-4275-887c-4cdd81953308'), 'Jazz musician Putter Smith was invited by producer Harry Saltzman to play "Mr. Kidd" after a Thelonious Monk Band show', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5c14f49c-e23f-4205-8cb3-948b5341b862'), 'Given all of the business with caskets, cremation, et cetera, it''s interesting to note that producer Albert R. Broccoli once worked as a salesman and manager for the Long Island Casket Company, and Sir Sean Connery once worked for an undertaker', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4af65248-4cec-4259-a8e1-6dd78d2f1678'), 'Mr. Wint in fact makes two slip-ups which raise James Bond''s suspicions. A claret is a red Bordeaux wine, something a real sommelier (wine steward) would know, of course. But before that, he also makes a minor character error in serving the wine to Bond. The small silver saucer on the chain is a tastevin, which the sommelier uses to check the wine after opening the bottle and before serving it. This practice has started dying out in fine establishments since this was released in 1971', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0972fbd8-39d0-45f0-b3c7-b63091018343'), 'When this movie aired on ABC, the network had the scene where Lana Wood walked around wearing nothing but a flimsy pair of see-through pink panties artificially altered, to make it appear as though she was wearing a black bra with black panties', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98fab404-c04c-426b-9422-c2a4a425fe52'), 'First Bond movie to not use the villains from the novel of the same name, which was largely because the movies were filmed in a drastically different order than the books had been released, and often altered from their source material. This movie sees the return of "Ernst Stavro Blofeld" as the villain, after he was featured in From Russia with Love (1963), Thunderball (1965), You Only Live Twice (1967) and On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), whereas the book''s villains were the Spang Brothers (although "Wint" and "Kidd" were in both the novel and movie). "Blofeld" was briefly introduced in "Thunderball" Ian Fleming''s 9th Bond novel, after which he altered his appearance and killed Bond''s wife in "On Her Majesty''s Secret Service" (11th novel); Bond finally tracks down and kills him in "You Only Live Twice" (12th novel). "Diamonds are Forever" was the 4th novel but adapted as the 7th official movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('04eb2e26-48f3-4994-bc81-8c066ce15dd8'), 'Bruce Glover said he was surprised at having been cast, because at first the producers said he was too normal, and that they wanted a deformed, Peter Lorre-like actor', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f511fa12-32b4-4397-a3d1-a9ffe7c16229'), 'Some dialogue between "Mr. Wint" and "Mr. Kidd" at the funeral parlor was cut from the script. As Bond passed them, they were arranging flowers. "Mr. Wint" said, "Mother loved Azaleas, but they always made her sneeze." "Mr. Kidd" replied, "Now she can really enjoy them." After "Mr. Wint" knocks Bond out with the urn, he quipped, "Mother was always such a help."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d9ef91a7-b0a6-4879-a1c1-c6d3868acce6'), 'This was the last official appearance by Sir Sean Connery as James Bond. Though it was made later in the film franchise, "Diamonds Are Forever" was only the fourth novel published, making it the first of the six Bond novels adapted with Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4c23a45e-cd1e-4ca2-a633-7cb82e251ab9'), 'This movie is the fourth most watched movie to be broadcast on British television when it was shown on ITV on March 15, 1981. It attracted 22.15 million viewers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('10cd3a35-5693-40a3-b3b7-31833cbd2dc9'), 'The two fighting girls in charge of watching "Willard Whyte"are named "Bambi" and "Thumper". These characters were not in the novel, but were made up for this movie. Stuntwoman Donna Garrett was originally signed to play the character of "Bambi". However, the last one (Trina Parks) had the name of her character changed in the Spanish-dubbed version, for uncertain reasons, to "Pluto". "Bambi" and "Thumper" are two of the lead characters in the Disney animated classic Bambi (1942)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56442db5-8d10-4a13-92de-4dc80515fcf5'), 'This is the only Bond film in which Sean Connery''s eyebrows weren''t trimmed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('718a416c-ad37-459e-a966-9aeef38c1dd3'), 'In this movie, "Plenty O''Toole" tries and fails to sleep with James Bond, only to end up losing her clothes and being thrown out of a window wearing nothing but her underwear and high heels for her trouble. In real life, Lana Wood, who played "Plenty", claims to have had an affair with Sir Sean Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Diamonds Are Forever'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('d44a780f-ddee-4ab9-bccb-fad1318bcc15'), 'It took crocodile wrangler and stuntman Ross Kananga (the villain in the movie was named after him) six takes to complete the scene were he doubles for Sir Roger Moore when Bond flees the bad guys by running across the backs of three crocodiles in a swamp. Kananga received $60,000 for the stunt, filmed at Swamp Safaris, his 350 acres of mangrove swamp on Jamaica''s north coast, where he kept a herd of over 1000 crocodiles. In a 1973 interview, he explained; "something like that is almost impossible to do. So, I had to do it six times before I got it right. I fell five times. The film company kept sending to London for more clothes. The crocs were chewing off everything when I hit the water, including shoes. I received one hundred ninety-three stitches on my leg and face."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('53864fe5-bb22-42c3-8c51-ca1bc5df3e4e'), 'Sir Sean Connery turned down the then astronomical sum of $5.5 million (close to $32 million in 2019 dollars) to play James Bond for a seventh time. Connery gave Sir Roger Moore his personal seal of approval for inheriting his role, calling him "an ideal Bond"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ea91d97d-40d6-40e9-8973-8864ae7ae10d'), 'Sir Roger Moore was 45 when he made his debut as 007, making him the oldest actor to portray the iconic character. The youngest was George Lazenby, who was 29 in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('af2b2530-476e-461d-9287-9ea0a8f6cdea'), 'The boat chase through the bayous was originally written in the script as just "Scene 156 - The most terrific boat chase you''ve ever seen". Bond''s speedboat jump made it into the Guinness Book of World Records for its distance of one hundred ten feet (thirty-three and a half meters), a record that stood for three years. Clifton James'' spontaneous reaction in that scene was kept in the final print. Bond''s stunt boat used to make the high jump over Sheriff Pepper''s car was specially designed with redistributed weight so it would fly through the air with more stability. The second boat was not scripted to collide with the police car, but after this happened while shooting the stunt, the script was changed to accommodate it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('831289ce-aa23-4157-92db-fe2e4492554e'), 'The part on the bridge of the crocodile farm was extremely dangerous to film, since crocodiles are able to jump up from the water and attack, which the crew found out relatively shortly before filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0c1de1a4-b7f8-41b1-b5e5-fbed729145a1'), 'The producers offered Clint Eastwood the role of James Bond, fresh from his success with Dirty Harry (1971). He was flattered, but declined, saying Bond should be portrayed by an English actor. Ironically at this point, James Bond had never been played by an English actor. Sir Sean Connery being Scottish and George Lazenby being Australian. The first Englishman to play Bond was Sir Roger Moore', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7fedf1ef-95c4-4240-97c7-159cd0f6d856'), 'The producers made a conscious decision to make Sir Roger Moore''s Bond significantly different from Sir Sean Connery''s. In this film, Bond never orders a vodka martini, but drinks bourbon whiskey, "neat" (no ice or water) instead. The mission briefing occurs in his flat, not the office (only the second time Bond''s apartment is featured in the movies after an appearance in Dr. No (1962)). Bond does not wear a hat. He smokes cigars instead of cigarettes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6acfb323-5dbe-4f9e-8f9c-f41716f4f3d6'), 'Sir Roger Moore suffered an injury during the boat chase. The engine cut out, and the momentum carried him into a boathouse. He cracked some of his front teeth, and twisted his knee. He had to walk on a cane for several days afterward, but was still able to complete the scene, because all he had to do was sit in the boat', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d15d368-b7b3-4ef3-914f-dc36e9083780'), 'Geoffrey Holder hated working with snakes. As he was playing "Baron Samedi", he was called upon to handle a lot of them. He was particularly against having to play the scene where his character falls into a coffin full of them. However, he was obligated to perform the scene without raising too much of a complaint, because Princess Alexandra was visiting the set the day the scene was being filmed, and he didn''t want to lose face in front of royalty', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('06c11223-a182-43df-b4d2-28e98e21ab96'), 'Only James Bond movie with Sir Roger Moore in which "Felix Leiter" appears. David Hedison, who played "Felix", played the role again in Licence to Kill (1989), becoming the first actor to reprise the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0b60342f-a120-4e86-9ab1-a36d906f9e5b'), 'Madeline Smith "Miss Caruso" said additional awkwardness of the bedroom scene was created by Sir Roger Moore''s overprotective wife, who was on the set during filming. In order to establish the effect of Bond unzipping "Miss Caruso''s" blue dress with his magnetic watch, a thin wire was attached to the zipper from the watch. A stagehand lay on the floor underneath Smith''s body to pull the wire down, while Moore pretended to unzip the dress with his watch. According to Moore, it took twenty-nine takes to get it right', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('95929413-defa-44a1-894a-80ed7e5269cc'), 'According to Sir Paul McCartney, after producer Albert R. Broccoli ''Cubby'' heard the title song in its final release form, he said, "Yeah, that''s good for a demo, but when are you going to do the real record?" McCartney curtly replied, "That''s it, Cub."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cc368b69-6639-4c3c-bb3b-a23bb495d385'), 'Sir Roger Moore had a fear of snakes, just like his co-star Geoffrey Holder, who had to fall into a coffin full of them. As a result, they hated shooting that scene. In addition, the script supervisor was so afraid, she refused to be on-set with them, an actor fainted while filming a scene where he''s killed by a snake, and Jane Seymour became terrified as a reptile got closer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3c8ad10c-b9e7-4d0c-94d7-07ac883f2b7b'), 'The attempted assassination by a snake while Bond is bathing was filmed in an unheated London set in mid-winter. The temperature was near 10ºC (50ºF), chilly enough to keep the snake sluggish. At a tropical temperature, the snake would''ve moved too swiftly for easy filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56468b56-8144-4073-8644-615add2ef557'), 'On his DVD audio commentary, Sir Roger Moore considered Live And Let Die (1973) to be his second best Bond movie after The Spy Who Loved Me (1977)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4d35ed11-9a5c-4708-84cc-67f73a22cb16'), 'The first Bond film in which 007 has a liaison with a black woman, Rosie Carver (Gloria Hendry). When this movie was released in South Africa, all of Hendry''s love scenes were removed, due to the Apartheid policies of the government', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2e21b7ef-c192-4aa5-8922-07be15581f1d'), 'According to Yaphet Kotto, he was not allowed to do any press for this movie, nor was he allowed to attend the premiere. Kotto states the producers told him they were afraid of the public''s reaction to the villain being black', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('51d61df4-8d0b-4d9f-8732-7dca56a6dfe5'), 'Maurice Patchett, the stunt driver who drove the double-decker bus (doubling for Sir Roger Moore as James Bond) in the sequence where the upper level of the bus is sheared off by a low bridge, was a London bus driver in real life. Double-decker bus drivers in London go through a rigorous training program, where they''re required to swerve the bus on wet ground and keep it upright, much like is shown in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cc30b18b-a1bf-4fac-af22-6d9a8083e740'), 'According to Sir Roger Moore, Yaphet Kotto was difficult to work with. However, Kotto denied this and maintained that though he may have been quiet, he was courteous to everyone in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d85bdd1a-fc34-4b47-9416-f7e7bbf47ccc'), 'Early in the production, Sir Roger Moore was hospitalized with kidney stones. Later, Moore and Jane Seymour caught dysentery while shooting in Jamaica', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cf614802-5523-4387-acc1-20287b81a313'), 'The first Bond movie to be set in a fictional country. The next one to do this would be Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ad57f26a-8c3c-4f4a-af25-5abf9fa959f8'), 'Sir Roger Moore wrote a production diary during filming, which was simply titled Roger Moore as James Bond 007: Live and Let Die (1973). It was published as a paperback by Pan in 1973 and features a complete dossier of filming from the first to last day. Accompanying it are several pages of colour stills, many taken by Moore''s then-wife Luisa Mattioli. The book was never re-issued, and is today quite rare. In the book, Moore uses the same self-deprecating humor, for which he became famous, and details numerous otherwise-unknown incidents, squabbles, milestones, and production notes. It was re-released in June 2018', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ce7db779-12c2-44b2-8e3d-9d52cb291be8'), 'Speaking on what it was like to work with Sir Roger Moore, Jane Seymour said: "Roger was fantastic to me. When I was in New Orleans or in Jamaica, he made sure every night that I was OK and safe, checked to see whom I was with, he''d include me in any social thing that happened."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('41f3a174-6e31-4f90-9b36-cfc887c8eb24'), 'When 007 is held captive in a chair by "Tee Hee", Sir Roger Moore''s quip "Butterhook" was improvised', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('85e91470-6c09-4a9c-9331-0f3b1ff259b1'), 'Sir Roger Moore was actively discouraged from raising his eyebrow, as that was a trademark of his previous successful character, "Simon Templar" of The Saint (1962) fame', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('46f99dfa-1ed9-49fe-98e8-aeff434f6d30'), 'Screenwriter Tom Mankiewicz dabbled with tarot cards to familiarize himself with the art. He took them to a party and performed tarot readings on the guests. At that party, Michael Caine and his then-girlfriend attended, and he used his tarot cards to predict the two would be married. The two married and Mankiewicz said in his autobiography that for years afterwards, Michael''s wife, Shakira Caine, was convinced he had special powers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fdeaed69-e138-476a-9cd4-98c64b96af8d'), 'Jamaica, part-time home of James Bond creator Ian Fleming, was used as the filming location for the fictitious country of San Monique. It was not called Jamaica, as that country had already been used as a setting for Dr. No (1962). Jamaica is also a setting in the James Bond novel "The Man With the Golden Gun", and the short stories "For Your Eyes Only" and "Octopussy"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fc3b371a-c0bb-459a-8579-24ec21faf690'), 'Sir Paul McCartney''s iconic theme song for this movie almost wasn''t used. After McCartney submitted the song, producer Harry Saltzman said he liked it but wanted it to be sung by someone else, preferably a black female artist. McCartney told producers he''d only sell the song for the film if he and his band were allowed to perform it for the film. Saltzman had passed on producing A Hard Day''s Night (1964) and came to quip that he didn''t want to turn down McCartney a second time. However, Saltzman would subsequently say he much preferred Brenda Arnau''s version of the song, also heard during the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ad8bc04b-7d71-47bb-b989-9561586b404a'), 'Desmond Llewelyn didn''t appear in this movie as "Q", because Llewellyn was appearing on the television show Follyfoot (1971). The producers also decided not to include the character, feeling that "too much was being made of the films'' gadgets", and decided to downplay this aspect, much to Llewelyn''s annoyance', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d011ba89-1dd5-4f8c-91f5-ef7d9b9658df'), 'Tom Mankiewicz originally wrote the main Bond girl to be black (with an eye on Diana Ross for the part) but one of the producers told him it couldn''t be done, on account of some of their markets (primarily Japan and South Africa) banning all movies with interracial romances. It was years until another 007 photoplay, Die Another Day (2002), featured the lead Bond girl as black', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bc086330-b6b8-4eb8-885f-8ae83632c59f'), 'This movie holds the record for the most watched movie to be broadcast on British television when it was shown on ITV on January 20, 1980. It attracted twenty-three and a half million viewers. There were only three television channels in the U.K. in 1980, and no home computers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6bc6f6c6-a784-43e3-b3cd-91ada12d7ded'), '"Solitaire" is the only character to ever beat James Bond in a card game', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c692049-6a83-4c45-8053-61bf22594753'), 'Sir Roger Moore wrote in his autobiography that he played a prank on Jane Seymour. During lunch, she had a habit of asking people nearby to pass the ketchup, then the salt, then another sauce, repeatedly. One day, Moore and the rest of the crew got and up left when Seymour sat down, causing her to burst into tears, causing Moore to regret the joke', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('805b909c-7f70-45fd-8661-67d8fb57e22a'), 'Bond''s apartment is shown for the second time in the franchise. The setting is not used again until Spectre (2015). Among the fixtures is a machine for making coffee that is treated as a gadget. Today''s audiences will recognize it as an espresso machine, a La Pavoni Europiccola to be exact. Bond does not use it correctly. The coffee grinder is a Gaggia Sirio', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('678ffd33-bb71-4286-8412-95cdfe7b2c0b'), 'This is the first time in the Bond series that a rock song was used as a main title song. The Sir Paul McCartney and Linda McCartney song charted in the U.S. on July 7, 1973, and peaked at the number two spot, where it stayed for three weeks. In the U.K., it debuted on July 9, 1973, and went to number nine. McCartney paid for the orchestra used for the song from his own pocket. Rolling Stone Magazine accused McCartney of selling out to the establishment when it was announced that he would be providing the theme song to this film. As it transpired, McCartney became the first artist to be nominated for a Best Song Academy Award for a James Bond title track. The soundtrack album charted in the U.S. on July 28, 1973, and topped at number seventeen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('282b6c80-9b3a-4bc9-b3e6-6617138ea333'), 'According to Sir Roger Moore in his autobiography, his relationship with producer Harry Saltzman changed while making this movie. Whereas previously they had been good friends, they were now employer and employee. When David Hedison checked into Moore''s hotel, Saltzman had him moved. Moore also noted that Saltzman''s relationship with producer Albert R. Broccoli was becoming more strained', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('52304129-6ed5-4aa7-a24e-53ffba959bb4'), 'Jane Seymour arrived on-set with a note from Richard Attenborough, who requested sympathetic treatment for his tired old daughter-in-law: "She may well need a shoulder to lean on."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4011a935-b2d5-46b6-9cc0-8a69b7e3cebb'), 'Sir Roger Moore''s mother was a great fan of silent star Richard Dix. Moore was able to get Dix''s son a small part in this movie. Robert Dix played the agent who was murdered at his own New Orleans funeral in the pre-credits teaser. His voice was dubbed by Shane Rimmer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('447c2c8e-b8bf-44be-ac61-bd06c3c27065'), 'Lois Maxwell had only been included in Diamonds Are Forever (1971) during filming as a late addition, as she had asked for a pay increase. For this movie, she returned for the same fee, but due to a technical error, the filming of her scenes in Bond''s house at the start of the movie extended to two days, costing the production more than if they''d paid the increase she requested. Sir Roger Moore later wrote that Maxwell celebrated the double-pay-day by purchasing a fur coat', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ea5c2a9f-68f6-4d48-9192-3e6fb0d09049'), 'Sir Roger Moore became the first actor to perform the gun-barrel sequence without a hat', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7b125784-db05-4796-a748-6660485cd9b9'), 'Bernard Lee was very ill during filming, causing the producers to consider replacing him as "M" with Kenneth More', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('23cfda1d-5a19-4727-a2bf-cee2a470d91e'), '"Dr. Kananga" (Mr. Big) is at least partially based on Dr. Francois ''Papa Doc'' Duvalier, dictator of Haiti, who used Voodoo as the basis of his personality cult, and even claimed that he was "Baron Samedi"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3cd2705e-40e0-43f6-9dfd-6b0e2fd3daa3'), 'It was Sir Roger Moore''s idea for Ross Kananga to wear crocodile shoes for his big stunt', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('38d0ab44-cea2-4e9a-a74f-270319fef978'), 'The characters of "Baron Samedi" and "Dambala"are named after two powerful Loa spirits in the Voodoo religion', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('38a7e2f0-7c47-4df3-8190-c8d63e571833'), 'Ian Fleming based the Bond girl "Solitaire''s" name on the Jamaican Solitaire bird known as the Jamaican Rufous-Throated Colitaire Bird. Her full name in the novel is "Simone Latrelle", but this is never mentioned in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bdc50334-ff4b-43aa-b256-7cc0e8f84a93'), 'Some exterior shots of Harlem were in fact filmed in Manhattan''s Upper East Side. This was because as filming in Harlem took place, the producers were reportedly required to pay protection money to a local gang to ensure the crew''s safety. When the cash ran out, they were "encouraged" to leave', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9132e4b7-20fa-4795-a891-0fc5ec8d714d'), 'During the scenes in New York early on in the film, you can catch glimpses of the partially incomplete World Trade Center. The top few floors are still being fitted out with cladding', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7cc440e3-63fe-4a75-ba59-41e7dc9f8a61'), 'Though this is the first movie in which "Q" does not appear, the book was actually the first in the series to make reference to "Q" branch. The book follows directly from Casino Royale, in which Bond''s hand is knife-scarred with a Russian character identifying him as a spy. "Q" (or Q branch) performs surgery on the hand to conceal the scars', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1a95d48f-b643-4b07-8f94-1703fa17b2d5'), 'After this movie, the "Felix Leiter" character did not appear again in the Eon Productions official series until The Living Daylights (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ad7ae6cb-ef50-4f8a-aeff-fb94cbaa65a6'), 'The character of "Quarrel, Jr." is a direct reference to the first Bond movie, Dr. No (1962) which also featured a character named "Quarrel". The original novel takes place before "Dr. No" (in which, as in the movie version, "Quarrel" is killed) and features the first appearance of the character. At one stage, the Bond girl character of "Honey Rider" from "Dr. No" was considered returning in this movie, but this idea was withdrawn', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6bcf44ef-b794-4dfd-86f3-488a05f7f95a'), 'Since director Guy Hamilton was a jazz fan, screenwriter Tom Mankiewicz suggested to him to film in New Orleans, Louisiana. Hamilton did not want to use Mardi Gras, since Thunderball (1965) featured Junkanoo, a similar festivity, so after more discussions with the writer, and location scouting with helicopters, he decided to use two well-known features of the city, the jazz funerals and the canals', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d8055f83-1ba8-4b4d-ad09-0870884e9658'), 'On the set, one of the crocodiles at the Crocodile Farm was called "Old Albert", named after producer Albert R. Broccoli', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('942adadc-272a-40b5-997e-cd819b086af7'), 'The first Bond film which does not feature "Q", the head of Special Ordnance Branch. The character appeared in Dr. No (1962), but under his real name of "Major Boothroyd" (he wasn''t played by Desmond Llewelyn in that movie either). Fans demanded Llewelyn''s return, and he appeared in eleven more Bond movies from 1974 to 1999', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('322274da-5ebf-4184-8a8d-b028a5b56563'), 'This is the only James Bond movie to have a supernatural theme', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('75f203cd-b87f-4038-ba46-7a6e384172b9'), 'Whilst filming Diamonds Are Forever (1971), this was chosen as the next novel to be adapted because Tom Mankiewicz thought it would be daring to use black villains, as the Black Panthers and other racial movements were active during this era. This was inclusive with the box office success of the early Blaxploitation movies like Shaft (1971), Super Fly (1972), and Across 110th Street (1972) (which United Artists released when this movie was filming)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('46fb5043-0066-41ce-9d50-c718e71f38d9'), 'The tarot cards used by "Solitaire" are the "Tarot of the Witches" deck and was created specifically for this movie by Fergus Hall. Their reverse side, which has the 007 numbering on a red background, cannot be seen in the "James Bond 007 Tarot Book". The tarot card "The High Priestess" was in the likeness of Jane Seymour, who played "Solitaire"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e9095aaf-bc9b-4d34-9dfd-322b6ab21241'), 'Twenty-six boats were built by the Glastron boat company for this movie. Seventeen were destroyed during rehearsals', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('82496643-3482-405f-8d30-159388a5aed9'), 'A running theme in the official trailers was whenever a new Bond is introduced, the trailers for their first Bond-movie includes music from their predecessors first movie. Music from On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) can be heard in the trailers for this movie, and music from this movie (most notably Sir George Martin''s distinctive arrangement of the James Bond Theme) can be heard in the trailers for The Living Daylights (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3cfb8659-1699-49c1-9c24-1e10ce838802'), 'While "Solitaire" was supposed to be black, Rosie Carver was supposed to be white', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6c4f2215-bf74-4d2d-875e-1cabf3b9c601'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli considered Goldie Hawn and Dame Helen Mirren for "Solitaire"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d26205bf-153c-40d1-8764-780ecd39700b'), 'Regular Bond voice artist Nikki Van der Zyl dubbed much of Jane Seymour''s dialogue', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('19da40e9-d629-4782-8b62-9ce79acaa109'), 'Sir Roger Moore is the only James Bond actor who was older than his predecessor. He was three years older than Sir Sean Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8bf7c7c1-a24b-4d43-a8fa-41ee225802af'), '"Live And Let Die" was the second James Bond novel written by Ian Fleming. It was first published in 1954. Its working title was "The Undertaker''s Wind" which also provided the name of the seventeenth chapter. Story elements from the novel have also been used for the James Bond movies For Your Eyes Only (1981) and Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40454617-9cad-41bf-8c54-ee74eb82d215'), 'This movie is only partially based on Ian Fleming''s original novel. The characters, locations, sequence of some events, and even clothes in the book are present in the movie. Many major plot elements were left out of this movie, only to be recycled in later movies. The novel''s climax involved Bond and "Solitaire" being dragged behind a speeding boat, as bait for sharks and Baracudas. This was used in For Your Eyes Only (1981). The novel also included a scene where "Felix Leiter" is wounded by a shark, and Bond goes to fight in a warehouse as a result. This was used in Licence to Kill (1989). Appropriately, David Hedison, who played "Leiter" in this movie, became the first actor to ever return to the role, essentially playing out his character''s original fate from this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('de7836b0-e138-4760-bceb-eab387d62f4b'), 'The white "pimpmobile" is actually a Chevrolet Corvette fitted with the fiberglass molding of a Cadillac Eldorado. The vehicle was marketed as the "Corvorado" by Dunham Coach of Boonton, New Jersey. Other Dunham conversions featured in this movie included a Cadillac Fleetwood and Eldorado (seen parked in front of the Fillet of Soul restaurant), along with two Lincoln Continentals (a 1969 Mark III and 1973 Mark IV, with the Dunham conversion, down to the custom wire hubcaps). Les Dunham stated that he kept possession of the Corvorado after this movie was completed. It has been modified several times for appearances in other movies and/or car shows. He claimed that the car was used in Super Fly (1972)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7fb70023-d0a4-444d-a64d-0e1ddfa44f4c'), 'When "Dr. Kananga" says to "Solitaire", "these growing signs of impertinence are beginning to disturb me, even as they did with your mother before you. She had the power, and lost it, and became useless to me.", which suggests that the character of "Kananga" was older than the actor portraying him. Yaphet Kotto was 33 at the time of filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8ba5835c-5027-4dc4-b9a9-805c2a7d8018'), '"The James Bond 007 Tarot Book" was released to coincide with the film. They were illustrated based upon Fergus Hall''s unique paintings', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6e22854a-d567-4425-a54d-f946d9a12cb4'), 'Around the time Sir Roger Moore got the part of James Bond, his home telephone number allegedly ended in the digits 007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5b42742f-ba88-4e6c-aef5-0e8a29ce2a78'), 'Special security was added for the shooting of the scenes in Harlem, New York', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('797bfb28-58b0-4602-b38b-908056605838'), 'The production drawings of "Tee Hee''s" mechanical arm sold for £1,292', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('82ef386b-7725-466d-bbd7-41239e8e0590'), 'In the novel, the real name of "Mr. Big" was "Buonaparte Ignace Gallia". In this movie, the real name of "Mr. Big" was changed to "Dr. Kananga" after the film''s stuntman Ross Kananga. Both Dr. No (1962) and this movie filmed in Jamaica. Both pictures actually therefore had villains with the title of "Dr." - Dr. No and Dr. Kananga respectively', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4324035-3760-4ba8-9e9c-0003c643a0f1'), 'This was the first James Bond movie that was seen by Daniel Craig, the sixth actor to play Bond in the official series', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0466b025-90c3-4784-b6d1-a2b8401e56fa'), 'Sir Roger Moore recommended Madeline Smith for the part of "Miss Caruso", having worked with her on The Long Goodbye (1971)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1d990f66-f338-4086-a602-8fe2e9b0aaa1'), 'Sir Roger Moore had to undertake a crash course in bus driving, so as to be able to drive a double-decker bus for the motorbike and bus chase sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b7392242-d2e7-4d96-a991-9510caacf75a'), 'First of two times that James Bond has been seen hang gliding (a popular new activity in the 1970s) in the Eon Productions official James Bond franchise. Sir Roger Moore is the only actor to play James Bond hang gliding. The second time was in Moonraker (1979)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Live And Let Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('86eb1878-0de8-43a4-8e35-d6a8abcd60cd'), 'The island used as the filming location for the Scaramanga''s beach house (Phang Nga Bay, Thailand) is known as "James Bond Island". The first map used to show Bond its location based on the tracker signal shows it to be approximately 200 miles due north of Taiwan where it is said to be. The second more detailed map, although being labelled as "China," does in fact show Phang Nga Bay and the island''s true filming location is marked correctly', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a579678-33c1-4558-b619-103863ebc789'), 'While on-location in Thailand, Sir Roger Moore found a cave full of bats. He couldn''t resist seeking out Sir Christopher Lee, telling him what he had found and joking "Master, they are yours to command!" Lee appreciated the joke', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f0f3dd3b-2056-4d28-8504-96db3dc1d34d'), 'One of the lowest grossing Bond movies. That fact, combined with behind-the-scenes problems, nearly made this the final Bond movie, and delayed production of the next entry in the franchise, The Spy Who Loved Me (1977)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f126baf9-13a7-44b3-b5c5-61ee105b0d77'), 'In his autobiography, Sir Roger Moore said that when they were filming the boat chase on the klongs, he fell in twice. The first was on purpose (because they told him not to do it), and the second time was by accident. On the second fall, Moore made the mistake of opening his eyes underwater, and saw what the local undertakers did with the bodies of the less fortunate. Conversely, this is the only Sir Roger Moore Bond movie where the Bond character is not drenched in water in some way', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('76917d83-9c2d-436a-9aa9-ef8465e0af49'), 'Prior to this movie, Hervé Villechaize was so poor that he was living out of his car in Los Angeles, California', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('63de4a79-ee8a-491b-b27d-17c46d323118'), 'Before acting, Sir Christopher Lee had a brief career in the British Secret Service, in which he studied several languages. One of these languages was Swedish. Off-set, he spoke Swedish with Britt Ekland and Maud Adams. His wife, Gitte Lee (née Krøncke), is Danish', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b5567179-a60c-42d1-99c9-e74545c3b36f'), 'According to Sir Roger Moore, director Guy Hamilton wanted to toughen Bond up more, in order to be closer to Ian Fleming''s original intent for the character. One of the ways was by having Bond twist the arm of "Andrea Anders" behind her back, and threaten to break it unless she told him what he wanted to know. Moore didn''t enjoy filming the scene, feeling that Bond would have instead charmed the information out of her. Another scene Moore didn''t enjoy was pushing the boy into the water during the boat chase', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7fa2bc18-e7d7-4f00-a4f2-f94fc375e793'), 'Originally, this movie was to follow On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), with George Lazenby playing Bond. Lazenby even briefly reported that it would be his follow-up in the media, before changing his mind, and quitting the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da953406-9e44-4245-a849-bad36fbb5021'), 'While doing the title sequence, title designer Maurice Binder ran into a problem with one of the nude models. Her pubic hair was sticking up when they needed it flat. After a few minutes of her trying and failing to get it right, Binder smeared her pubic hair with Vaseline. She gave Binder the brush and told him to fix the hair to how he needed it. The whole thing was seen by Sir Roger Moore and producer Harry Saltzman, causing Moore to turn to Saltzman and quip, "If you''re the producer of this film, you''re not getting the perks!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3770439b-7386-46b1-95c0-a8edde3c9cc6'), 'The source of the name "Scaramanga" originates in the name of a man that Ian Fleming knew, called "Pandia Scaramanga". He had met him, and stayed at his house on the island of Hydra, in the Greek isles. Reportedly, Fleming sought permission from him to use his surname, indicating that he would be James Bond''s adversary in "The Man With The Golden Gun". The real Scaramanga apparently responded: "I certainly do not mind you using my name, but please do not kill me."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ca907f33-f078-415f-88bc-d51a40c7148b'), 'Travelling to Los Angeles for The Tonight Show Starring Johnny Carson (1962) to promote this movie, Sir Christopher Lee had his golden gun confiscated by U.S. Customs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d756f9b-e7aa-4a0d-8e59-435947d2dd68'), 'Sir Christopher Lee named "Francisco Scaramanga" as one of his favorite roles', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2a38c7f3-6aee-4202-b684-b9be98faa7c1'), 'Score composer John Barry admitted that he added the slide whistle to the car roll because he didn''t think audiences would take such a stunt seriously. He has since regretted this', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1802ce09-b9e8-4fa8-b09d-f2d0b96a2515'), 'Britt Ekland admitted to being terrified when filming the scene where she and Sir Roger Moore escape from Scaramanga''s island. In his autobiography, Moore pointed out one particular shot, right before the second explosion goes off, when Ekland falls to the floor; according to Ekland, that wasn''t acting. Moore came back, picked her up, and helped her go on. His arm was around her back as the second explosion went off, and he felt the tiny hairs on her skin get singed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ab08aea-fe44-46f9-9e08-89e543014960'), 'The title role was originally offered to Jack Palance, before it eventually went to Sir Christopher Lee, the cousin of Ian Fleming who was known as the Man with the Golden Pen (Fleming had previously wanted Lee in the title role in Dr. No (1962))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b4346715-4d98-462b-83dc-bd07b0737704'), 'Though James Bond and "Francisco Scaramanga" are enemies in this movie, Sir Roger Moore and Sir Christopher Lee were close friends, dating back to the early days of their respective professional acting careers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('becdd576-c29a-466a-97d5-7f06f3eec81a'), '"Scaramanga''s" island hideout has since become a tourist attraction. During filming, the island was deserted', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4b0099a8-437a-4725-bee7-9c942c2a7f83'), 'Three golden guns props were made; a solid piece, one that could be fired with a cap, and one that could be assembled and disassembled, although Sir Christopher Lee said that the process "was extremely difficult"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('254b81f4-73a5-424c-ba6e-64b16ba5f110'), 'This movie marked the first time Sir Roger Moore fired his Walther PPK in the Bond film franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0f92df1-2f60-46e9-ba7d-e6e620610ba5'), 'First James Bond movie to be shown at the Kremlin. According to Sir Roger Moore in his audio commentary, apparently when the movie had finished, one Russian official turned around and said "We didn''t train him (Scaramanga) very well." In the movie, it is explained that Scaramanga was recruited by and acted as a hitman for the K.G.B.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('900d7bea-4f3e-40f7-b9ac-cdefc7df0cf5'), 'The Republic RC-3 SeaBee seaplane, which Bond uses to fly to the "Scaramanga''s" lair, was donated by a wealthy American James Bond fan (though only on the condition he fly it himself. Which he did, all the way from the United States to Thailand)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f410f48f-fcef-47cd-9679-2f995f1103c6'), 'The corkscrew car jump was apparently conceived several years before this movie went into production. Researchers at Cornell University (Calspan in Buffalo, NY) were studying rollover collisions for the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, and they did a computer simulation of the barrel roll stunt used in this movie. Race car driver W.J. Milligan Jr., who was the promoter of the American Thrill Show during the 1960s and 1970s, with the sponsorship of the American Motors Corporation, performed the barrel roll stunt, known as the Astro Spiral Jump, and it debuted on January 12, 1972, at the Houston Astrodome, using an AMC Javelin. Milligan was contacted by producer Albert R. Broccoli during an American Thrill Show performance in Hershey, Pennsylvania, where he wanted the stunt performed in a James Bond movie. Producers Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli allegedly took out patents and copyrights on the stunt, as they did not wish it to appear in another movie before they had used it. The three hundred sixty-degree car-spiralling jump over a canal was performed in just one take by uncredited British stuntman ''Bumps'' Williard as eight cameras simultaneously captured the spectacle. So potentially hazardous was the nature of the stunt, divers, ambulances, and cranes were on standby alert, in case of any catastrophic consequences. The stunt was so rapid that the film is shown in slow motion. Williard was given a large bonus for completing the jump on the first take. Jay Milligan performed the driving stunts with the AMC Hornet used in this movie. AMC provided fifteen vehicles used in this movie (some of them where AMC Matador police cars). There were two AMC Hornets used for the spiral jump stunt, and one of them is owned by Jay Milligan, which is the back-up vehicle, while the other one is in a museum. The jump is also credited with being the first stunt ever to be calculated by computer modeling and was first tested at the CALSPAN campus in Buffalo', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f5a511fb-6704-40ed-a9b8-a5c7adcf209e'), '"The Man with the Golden Gun" was the thirteenth and final complete James Bond novel written by Ian Fleming. It was the first and only one of his full James Bond novels to be published posthumously. Some sources claim that it was unfinished at the time of his death, whereas other experts, such as Andrew Lycett and John Cork, maintain that Fleming had completed it before he died. It is of controversial debate as to whether Fleming wrote the novel completely himself or whether other(s) were involved. Fleming''s own personal correspondence from the period indicates that he had completed the novel and submitted it to his publisher before his death. The correspondence also indicates that Fleming was not pleased with the novel, and had considered retiring from writing Bond novels, because he feared he had lost his edge', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3b0ddbc6-68b1-47f0-96a8-917d78c7eab2'), 'The martial arts scenes were added to the script because the genre was becoming popular at the time of filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('15c1fba5-c770-4832-a4cc-22a66e7578a9'), 'Harry Saltzman sold his 50% share of the Bond franchise to United Artists to alleviate the very large financial difficulties he had incurred', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b6370a8d-3847-4bb9-baa0-e576cb78f968'), 'The "Bottoms Up" strip club kept the same interior used in this movie, until it closed in 2004', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1d1b443-7b42-4e22-aafd-3a662217af6e'), 'Sir Christopher Lee wore full body make-up, to give the appearance of having a tan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5543c0c1-eab7-4a5b-8891-9591e0ae3ac9'), 'Producer Harry Saltzman wanted an elephant stampede in the movie, so Bond and "Scaramanga" could chase each other on elephant back. The rest of the creative team balked at the idea, but Saltzman went to see an elephant trainer. It turns out that elephants need a special shoe on their feet to protect them from rough surfaces when they work. A few months later, while filming in Thailand, producer Albert R. Broccoli got a call saying his elephant shoes were ready. Saltzman had ordered about 2,600 pairs of them. The sequence was not in the movie, but the man who made the shoes had not been paid. As of 1990, Eon Productions still owed him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7892a472-3efb-4626-a6b4-a350836dfabe'), 'While shooting in Thailand, the cast and crew were unwittingly housed in a bordello', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('623d3165-5187-41fb-b56c-1863c1f11179'), 'As a joke on Desmond Llewelyn, Sir Roger Moore wrote fake dialogue for "Q", and then gave it to the script girl to give to Llewelyn after he had spent a whole month learning his lines and was about to come on-set', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f34affde-c9f1-4ade-963c-cdefeb27077a'), 'In the dinner scene with "Scaramanga", Bond says, "There''s a useful four-letter word, and you''re full of it." Essentially the same quip is used again by Bond, this time played by Timothy Dalton, in The Living Daylights (1987). "Koskoff", who has betrayed him, says, "For you I have great affection, but we have an old saying: duty has no sweethearts." Bond replies, "We have an old saying too, Georgi, and you''re full of it."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('695a3e25-83cd-4c51-8c5c-9f271d6e4c3b'), 'In his 2008 autobiography ''My Word is My Bond'', Roger Moore states that Hervé Villechaize was something of a sex pest to the women on the set of this film and frequently visited strip clubs during Thailand shoot and paid for the services of local prostitutes. Moore states that he himself found Villechaize to be a creepy individual and never warmed to him (unlike Christopher Lee, an actor that Moore had nothing but respect and admiration for)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e5d0f09-a620-4966-b356-202ac4156ba3'), 'This is the only Bond film where Roger Moore actually runs (as he does after the karate scene). Moore made it clear to producers that he didn''t want to be filmed running as it made him look awkward', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a7b00428-2ab5-4294-ab57-cec298f2d4ca'), 'Sir Roger Moore and Lois Maxwell "Miss Moneypenny" are former classmates at RADA, the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d62f2865-6b92-4965-8219-51a8c0cd7ff8'), 'According to production designer Peter Murton, the sequence where "Scaramanga''s" car transforms into a light airplane was accomplished in the editing room. Wings were attached to the car, and a stuntman drove the carplane to the runway. At this point, the editor simply cut to a radio-controlled model built by John Stears', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('500bfc40-4a7c-4c84-9d1d-ab3953ec61cb'), 'The secret headquarters for MI6 in Hong Kong Harbor was the wreck of the R.M.S. Queen Elizabeth. The vessel had been renamed before the time of filming, and was known as the Seawise University', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('43111b06-c4b4-4dd0-86fb-8ff6783348a2'), 'The golden gun was manufactured by special effects wizard John Stears from several tobacco and men''s accessories, such as a cigarette case, fountain pen, and cigarette lighter. During the 1950s, KGB agents were issued with miniature, one-shot, .22 caliber guns, compacted in cigarette cases', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a3f6f00e-789a-4818-a880-a0e1137b16f5'), 'Hervé Villechaize lamented to Sir Roger Moore that whenever he stayed at a hotel, he could never get a room above the first floor. When Moore asked him why, he said it was because he couldn''t reach the buttons in the elevator', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('afabc796-bdd3-4215-9fd5-2da1e713f108'), 'The second unit, still shooting in Bangkok, was forced to return to England a few days early when political unrest erupted in the city', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40227935-9b8c-4db4-8d13-08f5594994a9'), 'This movie bears virtually no relation to the book other than the name of "Scaramanga", his third nipple, his golden gun, his occupation as an assassin, and a brief monologue about the shooting of an elephant when he was younger. Even the locale was shifted from Jamaica, as that location had already been used for Dr. No (1962) and Live and Let Die (1973). "Scaramanga" was changed from an American hood into a more urbane methodical assassin, more akin to Bond. the book also had "Mary Goodnight"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ba792317-ac12-497e-ba58-3c66b62991ba'), 'The final entry in the series where Bond would wear a business suit in the gun barrel opening. All subsequent entries would see Bond in the tuxedo and bow tie. The version of Roger Moore in the business suit however, would feature in all of Moore''s subsequent trailers until the end of his tenure as Bond as the aspect ratio of 1.85:1 it was shot in was the standard for trailers during this period (the new tuxedo version was shot in 2.35:1 so would have had to have been re-formatted for trailers). Daniel Craig''s Bond wears a business suit in all but his last one, "No Time to Die" (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5846bea1-4136-4827-8f02-5be727d76f3f'), 'This is the James Bond movie on which the partnership between Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli is said to have deteriorated. Sir Roger Moore stated in his DVD audio commentary that this predominantly occurred behind closed doors', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('00230a87-d615-47eb-ba83-43acc8108de1'), 'Filming began on November 6, 1973, with a double filling in for Sir Roger Moore, who wasn''t scheduled to begin shooting until April 1974', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('13b272a1-2e35-427a-a836-61cd5f695527'), 'Marc Lawrence played "Rodney", the gangster who was shot by "Scaramanga" at the beginning of the movie. He also played a Las Vegas hood who worked for Slumber, Inc. in Diamonds Are Forever (1971). It is not clear whether or not they were intended to be the same character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b7cc4caa-c21f-4c58-b79d-2a28a25536e7'), 'The novel reveals "M''s" name for the first time, "Miles Messervy". In The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), "Gogol" addresses him as "Miles", but his last name is never revealed in any of the movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3c1b08d0-a192-470f-90f5-0ba15c781f2f'), 'The last scene filmed was Bond trying to steal the golden bullet from the belly dancer''s navel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80dded3b-9538-479e-8776-5a66b0344ebf'), '"Scaramanga''s" solar gun fires an invisible laser beam because the special effects team didn''t have the money to make the "golden beam of laser light" for which the script required', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('36a2c642-05eb-40f0-ae52-2aa67d72978e'), 'When first meeting Bond in the car, "Lieutenant Hip''s" nieces greet him in two different languages. Niece number two says "Sawadee ka" (Thai for "Hello" and "Goodbye") and niece number one says "Ni hao ma" (Mandarin for "How are you?"). Also, in their second meeting, niece number two says "He is handsome" in Thai, and niece number one replies in Mandarin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9c994f1b-dc1b-40c3-bfa4-00a27c66b4a7'), 'On October 10, 2008, it was discovered that one of the golden guns used in this movie, which is estimated to be worth around £80,000, was missing (suspected stolen) from Elstree Props, a company based at Hertfordshire studios', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('95e23441-2483-4389-a3fd-7cdbceddc0e3'), 'Last James Bond movie to be directed by Guy Hamilton', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('06e1a7cf-9af3-439d-a9b1-4d188b4bdc54'), 'In the fight in the dancer''s dressing room, Sir Roger Moore sprays one of the villains in the face with an aerosol can of Brut 33, a nod to the Fabergé company, with which Moore was associated', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Man With The Golden Gun'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('6066c08a-0863-4649-9193-bfa45a38fed8'), 'A representative from the Egyptian government was on-set throughout the shoot in Cairo and Giza, to make sure that the country was not portrayed in an unflattering light. For that reason, when the scaffolding collapses on Jaws, and Bond quips "Egyptian builders", Sir Roger Moore merely mouthed the line, dubbing it in later. It went unnoticed by the official Egyptian minder, and ironically, got a great laugh from Egyptian audiences', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('39040a73-bfdc-415b-b20f-1a657b20a2bb'), 'The closing credits say, "James Bond will return in For Your Eyes Only (1981)" but, because of the successes of Star Wars: Episode IV - A New Hope (1977) and Close Encounters of the Third Kind (1977), Moonraker (1979) was chosen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d949511f-e2d5-4374-b0ca-9f45b05a85f1'), 'The eyesight of cinematographer Claude Renoir was failing at the time of this movie, and he could not see to the end of the massive supertanker set. As a result, he could not supervise the lighting. Sir Ken Adam turned to his friend Stanley Kubrick, who, under the condition of complete secrecy, supervised the lighting. He suggested the use of floodlights. In addition Katharina Kubrick (Kubrick''s stepdaughter) designed the dentures that Richard Kiel (Jaws) wore in this movie and "Moonraker" (1979)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2365f661-6a63-4c0d-a12e-f3af1ec3936a'), 'The stunt driver was having problems making the Lotus Esprit look sufficiently exciting in the chase scenes, because it held the road too well, and had to be driven dangerously fast to make it slide impressively on corners. One scene in Sardinia required the car to drive up a hill on a mountain pass and round a sharp bend. The normal stunt driver was not available, and the crew who were waiting at the top asked Lotus employee Roger Becker to drive the car up. He thrashed the car, skidding dramatically around the corners and making a dramatic one hundred eighty-degree turn on a gravel area as he stopped at the top. "Would you mind doing that again?" they asked him. "And this time we''ll have the cameras rolling." From that time on, Roger became the stunt driver for shots involving the Lotus', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c68b37a8-1b05-4783-a4fc-a023d7e3cb5a'), 'By the time this movie was made, the James Bond films were the most lucrative in the world, and many manufacturers wanted their products featured. There was great competition for the company that would supply Bond''s car. Don McLaughlin, Public Relations Manager of Lotus, realized that the best way to win this coveted position was to make the producers chase after him, rather than going begging to them. One day he turned up at Pinewood driving a brand new unreleased Lotus Esprit, with all identifying names covered up. He parked it outside the Bond set, knowing that the producers would see it when they broke for lunch. Once the car had attracted a crowd, all clamoring to know what the car was, McLaughlin nonchalantly got in the car and drove away without answering any questions. As he had expected, the producers were desperate to discover what the car was, and producer Albert R. Broccoli later chose it for this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('234e54a2-4d05-4bc5-bca3-be900699c048'), 'In the scene where "Major Amasova" couldn''t drive a manual transmission car, Barbara Bach couldn''t actually drive one in real life either. Sir Roger Moore''s responses were unscripted', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('61d90257-faeb-4839-ae6c-e65e4c97a4c3'), 'Rick Sylvester''s opening ski stunt was shot from the top of Asgard Peak on Baffin Island in Canada. The summit was only accessible by helicopter. A small crew, including Sylvester and second unit director John Glen, travelled there in July 1976, a month before principal photography began. They stayed in the neighboring village of Pangnirtung for ten days, awaiting the right weather conditions. Numerous cameras were positioned around the site to capture the moment. All the camera operators felt that they lost sight of the skier as he went sailing off the cliff, all except one camera, which stayed with him throughout the stunt. The scene was all uncut. Sylvester''s pay was $30,000. Sylvester was supposedly given an additional bonus when he successfully completed the shot', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8a8f568a-0dd5-470b-ba71-be0c800da92a'), 'Richard Kiel "Jaws" could only keep the metal teeth in his mouth for about half a minute at a time, due to the excessive pain and discomfort. He often had to show comic expressions, which was quite contradictory to the way he was feeling, wearing the extremely uncomfortable braces. Kiel, 7''2'''', played an almost identical part in Silver Streak (1976). The chain through which Jaws bites was made of licorice. In order to simulate the character''s metal teeth, Kiel''s stunt double Martin Grace used pieces of orange peel wrapped in aluminum foil', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e973af4-94d2-4f26-8a1a-171ea822f733'), 'When James Bond drives the Wet Nellie up onto the beach, a small boy points to the car in the water. This is Richard George Kiel, son of Richard Kiel "Jaws"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0eb08103-2b82-42f6-ba63-0e20d400c726'), 'Prior to the introduction of "Naomi", Caroline Munro accidentally sat on a bee and was stung hard on the behind. Despite the resulting pain, she was pushed on by the filmmakers to complete the scene. When shown boating in and greeting Sir Roger Moore and Barbara Bach, the stern look on her face wasn''t due only to the character of the henchwoman she was playing, but the pain from the sting she was feeling', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dfeb3d19-86bc-4589-a1ac-2ce3b1fecbdb'), 'After this movie''s release, demand for white Lotus Esprit cars surged to the point that new customers had to be placed on a three-year waiting list', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fbd08de2-7804-4abd-ba1e-1404bcaf433c'), 'Ian Fleming was so disappointed with the "Spy Who Loved Me" novel that he would not allow the publisher to print the book in paperback. It was not until Fleming''s death that the book became widely available', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('95dd1f75-1dbc-4ad9-8e85-38d5d400363e'), 'The famous Union Jack parachute ski jump stunt during the pre-title sequence was originally suggested by George Lazenby to be used in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), but the necessary equipment to film it was not available then. The Bond producers thought it was a great idea, and later added the Union Jack to the parachute and used it in this movie. It has been noted with that scene''s climax, James Bond''s status with the people of Britain changed from being simply a popular character who happened to be British to an iconic British hero on par with King Arthur, Robin Hood, and Sherlock Holmes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('57a1db34-fdf2-45c3-8d83-ecefea491834'), 'This movie introduced to the world a spy sea scooter known as a "wetbike" (better known now as a jet ski), sparking a new water-activity industry. This gadget was commonly referred to as the "motorbike that rides on water"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1df33409-b743-4ce5-aafb-b10d1b51891e'), 'First Bond movie to make significant references to Bond''s past, including his recruitment to the British Secret Service from the Royal Navy, his "many lady friends", and his marriage to "Tracy" in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8123b15e-fee6-4ff4-8f3f-dbbf0f37a005'), 'The character of "Major Boothroyd" is addressed as such by Barbara Bach for one of the rare times in the film franchise. "Boothroyd" (played by Desmond Llewelyn) is the head of Q branch, but the name "Q" stuck to the character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9741e440-f9c3-4562-a79f-993959c96c71'), '$1 million of the $13.5 million budget was spent by production designer Sir Ken Adam on building the largest soundstage in the world: 336''x139''x44''. The set was used for the interior shots of "Stromberg''s" supertanker. The tank had a capacity of 1.2 million gallons. In honour of this the stage was named the "007 Stage"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('68185fc1-3a2c-45ce-95f9-d8b6e9e17d31'), 'Elvis Presley saw this movie on Wednesday, August 10, 1977 during a special viewing at the General Cinema in Whitehaven, Tennessee. It was the last movie he saw, as he died six days later on Tuesday, August 16, 1977, at the age of forty-two', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a283aad3-5223-4705-bdf9-47b0b21bdb1a'), 'The metal teeth worn by Jaws are on display at the Spy Museum in Washington, D.C.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b6ffe663-443b-4007-bd54-6e6e4d30d421'), 'Karl Stromberg (Curd Jürgens) has webbed hands. However, they often go unnoticed by viewers on video and DVD compared to when the movie was released in cinemas. A bigger image on a theater screen makes them more noticeable. In one of the later scenes, you can clearly see this in a side view of his right hand', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('91537a56-d335-4831-b4e1-4ce5a8d837f9'), 'Barbara Bach was cast only four days before principal photography began, and auditioned hoping to secure just a role in this movie, not the female lead', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('41e9481c-b208-4adb-87ed-b119fbe2aa8c'), 'With this movie, director Lewis Gilbert also decided to fix what he felt the previous Sir Roger Moore movies were doing wrong, which was writing the Bond character too much the way Sir Sean Connery played him, and instead portray Bond closer to the books, "very English, very smooth, good sense of humor."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f5b47076-e1dd-41ec-b4c4-9de60422e19e'), 'To pay tribute to the death of Sir Roger Moore, two James Bond movies, this movie and For Your Eyes Only (1981), Moore''s two favorite of his Bond movies, as well as the two he considered his best, were re-released on selected dates in selected territories around the world, within a few weeks of his passing, with fifty percent of the proceeds going to Moore''s beloved charity, U.N.I.C.E.F., for which he was a Goodwill Ambassador', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('aa08c1b4-cc78-4b5b-a55d-618735caadb9'), 'The crew was upset because of the horrible food in Egypt, so producer Albert R. Broccoli had a refrigerated truck with food brought from England. However, someone forgot to turn on the freezer, so all the food was inedible upon arrival. Broccoli jumped into action, taking a Jeep and some crew into town to grab items like tomatoes and pots and pans. Pasta was flown in from Cairo. Well-known as an amateur chef at home, Broccoli cooked up a feast for the cast and crew, served by him and Sir Roger Moore. The crew applauded the meal, and a sign was painted in the messroom with "Trattoria Broccoli" written on it, "Trattoria" being the Italian word for simplest restaurant. Broccoli''s Italian parents are largely credited for his culinary skills', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('65f10ebe-9f59-4527-a0a8-329599634fa9'), 'Sir Roger Moore decided last minute it would be much more dramatic if he was sitting in the chair, instead of standing behind it when the gun underneath the dining table was fired. The special effects team had only reinforced the back of the chair for the original planned shot, which meant Moore risked serious injury if he didn''t leap away in time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('02f4cae5-b2c5-4acb-88d7-b3be6410e50b'), 'The scene where James Bond is watching a light show that illuminates the Sphinx and Pyramids is an actual show called "The Sound and Light" show, which would continue to be shown for many years afterwards', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1f6c9a49-5284-4206-ac19-e0c1d7db040f'), 'Despite the disappointing box-office performance of "The Man with the Golden Gun (1974)," Albert R. Broccoli nevertheless invested $13.5 million on the production of this movie, the most expensive Bond movie yet produced', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e510aaee-713d-49b7-aab0-beb6a816f625'), 'According to production designer Sir Ken Adam, that was a look of real panic on Barbara Bach''s face in the scene where the tunnels of Atlantis are flooding, because she didn''t expect such a powerful deluge of water', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f0485a9d-6253-462f-a9ca-ee702a0923f3'), 'First Bond movie to use an original villain, and not one based on a villain from the novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f751699c-cbf4-4d42-b50f-b265ef950d0e'), 'In his audio commentary, Sir Roger Moore comments on the opening parachute ski jump that could have gone horribly wrong for stuntman Rick Sylvester. After the jump, a disengaged ski clipped the unopened chute as it was falling. The ski could easily have prevented the chute from opening. It can still be seen in the final footage when the ski clips the about-to-open parachute', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('09264520-aa63-4400-9b20-4340ae35bffd'), 'The title song "Nobody Does It Better" was sung by Carly Simon, with music by Marvin Hamlisch, and lyrics by Carole Bayer Sager. It is the second Bond theme song to be titled differently from the name of the movie that is played on the main titles, although the phrase "the spy who loved me" is included in the lyrics. The first differently named theme is "All The Time In The World" from the movie "On Her Majesty''s Secret Service"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fe9bf9f9-aa2f-405b-adfc-0bcfea7ebf86'), 'One of the first directors to be considered was Steven Spielberg. There was some worry about his inexperience, as he was caught up on an extremely lengthy pre-production schedule for a little movie he was making at the time called Jaws (1975), which provided inspiration for a major character in this movie. Spielberg always wanted to direct a Bond movie, and ended up making his own Bond-like franchise, Indiana Jones', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a3f9ea4f-ecd0-4e82-9260-a95b84f60570'), 'Richard Kiel recounted how Jaws'' survival at the end was met with giant applause at several screenings', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('49acf224-f4e0-4114-8f07-bcdfbd01da64'), 'The novelization by Christopher Wood gives Jaws a backstory. His real name is Zbigniew Krycsiwiki. He was born in Poland, the product of a union between the strong man of a travelling circus and the Chief Wardress at the Women''s Prison in Kraców. The relationship and subsequent marriage had been a stormy one, and, when it broke up, the young Zbigniew stayed with his mother and attended school, and subsequently university in Kraców. He grew to a prodigious height, but in temperament, he followed his father, and was surly and uncooperative, given to sudden outbreaks of violent temper. Because of his size, he commanded a place on the university basketball team, but he was sluggish of reaction, and his lack of speed was constantly exposed by more skillful but less physically endowed players. After a failed attempt at a basketball career, Krycsiwiki was arrested by the secret police for having taken part in the "1972 bread riots." While he was imprisoned, the police "beat him with hollow steel clubs encased in thick leather" until they thought he was dead, leaving his jaw broken beyond repair. Krycsiwiki later escaped, and stowed aboard one of Stromberg''s vessels. Eventually he was caught, but instead of turning him in, Stromberg hired a prestigious doctor to create an artificial jaw. After fourteen operations, Krycsiwiki''s jaw was restored using steel components that created two rows of terrifying razor-sharp teeth, although Jaws was left mute', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5bc65236-4ac8-4eef-9464-103d90a07955'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli named this movie, along with "From Russia with Love (1963)" and "Goldfinger (1964)," as his three favorite James Bond movies, according to an interview with the Hollywood Reporter''s Robert Osborne on April 12, 1982', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4c1bcfc1-94f5-4fb5-9bbe-a5d7915502f6'), 'Though not credited, Charles Gray has an off screen cameo, as the narrator heard in the pyramid scene. This makes Gray''s third participation in an official Bond movie, with his first appearance as Henderson in You Only Live Twice, and more noticeable as Bond''s arch nemesis Ernst Stavro Blofeld in Diamonds are Forever', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b02dd238-330f-49d2-8ac7-4cf9b7bd3bc1'), 'The ambient sound effects on the train to Sardinia were the same ones used in From Russia with Love (1963)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e3a8988e-334e-4c0c-bc98-12fa1c751345'), 'The first James Bond movie produced solely by Albert R. Broccoli. All previous Bond movies had been co-produced with Harry Saltzman, or other producers. Saltzman left the series during pre-production of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a3d615ca-b835-4f2d-933f-031d441a73ba'), 'The only James Bond movie in which M''s (Bernard Lee) first name (Miles) is said. His name was said to be Admiral Sir Miles Messervy in the novel "The Man with the Golden Gun". It is only the second time in the film franchise that M calls Bond by his first name James, and not 007 or Bond (the first was On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)). Q is referred to by his real name (Major Boothroyd) in Dr. No (1962), From Russia with Love (1963), and this film by Anya Amasova', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8a16811e-c515-4515-ad4e-51f90b9ff40d'), 'The movie received three Academy Award nominations, the most ever received by a James Bond movie until Skyfall (2012). These were for Best Art Direction-Set Decoration, Best Score, and Best Song, "Nobody Does It Better". It was the first Bond movie to receive multiple Oscar nominations', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('10af0f76-0a9d-4a01-b422-b1ffd4a017c7'), 'Last Bond movie (to date) of Shane Rimmer. He played the commander of the U.S.S. Wayne here, and had previously played a N.A.S.A. technician in "You Only Live Twice (1967)," and the head of Willard White''s aerospace division in "Diamonds Are Forever (1971)." He also provided the voice for the American Agent at the beginning of "Live and Let Die (1973)."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b0a3ae16-3084-43d0-983d-5cdf51e342d3'), 'The Lotus submarine car was code-named Esther Williams in an early draft of the script, and was also nicknamed by the crew as "Wet Nellie" (after the mini-helicopter in You Only Live Twice (1967)), which is the name used in the novelization. This car was an empty shell of a car that was propelled off of a pier, and into the sea by a compressed air cannon. Designed to operate while filled with water, it was driven by two divers in full scuba gear, but overheated while idling in between takes. The chase sequence involving Wet Nellie runs for seven minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7e76beff-af4c-452a-b2da-142079f750e4'), 'Richard Kiel credited stunt coordinator Bob Simmons with suggesting to producer Albert R. Broccoli that Jaws be allowed to survive at the end of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d2d01056-480e-46d8-b047-155527e595a7'), 'A total of four "Wet Nellie" diving cars were built for the underwater scenes. All but the last one were hollow shells. One was shot off the pier by an air cannon and had retractable wheels, one had panels that covered the wheel wells, one that had diving planes that extended from the wheel wells, and one that was actually able to move underwater. The last one was operated by scuba divers, since the car was filled with water. One of the fiberglass "Wet Nellie" shells was found on a scrap heap. It was restored on Bond Ambition (2014). The final restoration has one wheel down and one wheel in the process of retracting on the passenger side, and the dive fins in place on the driver''s side. It also has the window shields, periscope, missile, propellers, and rudders as seen in the film. It is on display at a James Bond Museum in Florida', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c2533aed-4da2-4fa0-ac4c-123063a00e06'), 'The Liparus oil tanker in this movie is a model of the real one owned by Royal Dutch Shell, which was constructed in 1975 and commissioned a year later as an L-class tanker. She could hold 275,000 to 315,000 tons of crude oil. Shell sold off the tanker in 1983, when it was renamed the "Paradise" and went through several owners. It was scrapped in China in 2003. A miniature tanker had to be built for this movie, even though one of Albert R. Broccoli''s friends offered the production a real one. They had to turn the offer down as the insurance premiums on tankers were prohibitively expensive, clocking in at 50,000 pounds a day. The tanker model of the Liparus was sixty feet long, with the Stromberg shipping logo used in place of the Shell Oil Company livery (including the stern, where the "London" registry was painted over), powered by a Evinrude outboard motor', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ee40735c-3434-4f00-9fe5-fe81350df198'), 'This was the first James Bond movie to be composed by an American (Marvin Hamlisch). A piece of music composed by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart inspired the title song "Nobody Does It Better", composed by Hamlisch. This movie includes in its score a few pieces of classical music by such composers as Johann Sebastian Bach (Air in Orchestral Suite No. 3, BWV 1068 aka Air on the G String), Frédéric Chopin (Nocturne No. 8 in D-Flat, Op. 27 No. 2), Camille Saint-Saëns (The Aquarium from The Carnival of the Animals) and Mozart''s Andante second movement of Piano Concerto No. 21. "Elvira Madigan" plays when Atlantis arises from the sea. After the van breaks down, the theme from Lawrence of Arabia (1962) plays when Bond and XXX walk across the desert. One young assistant in the cutting-room put it in as a joke, and it brought laughs to the team and they kept it in the final cut. As such, this was the first James Bond movie to use a score from another movie. Also, Anya''s music box-transmitter plays "Lara''s Theme" from Doctor Zhivago (1965). All of these pieces of music, however, are not included on the movie''s soundtrack album, as they are merely excerpted in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('44325371-b7cd-434c-918e-d301bc6b6a23'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli wanted Lois Chiles to play the part of Russian agent Anya Amasova. Upon talking to her agent, it was discovered that Chiles had retired temporarily, upset by criticism she had received, and was taking acting lessons. Chiles became the next Bond Girl in Moonraker (1979) after sharing a seat next to director Lewis Gilbert', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8a42dc34-8bd6-4a38-82ea-0a5e18dac45e'), 'James Mason was considered for the part of villain Karl Stromberg. His famous role as Jules Verne''s Captain Nemo in Walt Disney''s 20,000 Leagues Under the Sea (1954) was a major element in his consideration. He would also be considered as main villain Hugo Drax in the next Bond movie Moonraker (1979). Coincidentally, James Bond creator Ian Fleming based the villain Drax on the Jules Verne''s character Robur from the "Clipper Of The Clouds", "Master of the World" and "Robur, The Conqueror" stories. Sadly, Mason never got into any Bond movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('04e3510a-1480-4e1f-8caa-181a6ccf5af0'), 'According to the sleeve notes of the CD soundtrack, composer John Barry allegedly could not return to the U.K. for taxation purposes, and so did not compose the score for this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b9bdfc6c-4b15-49c4-ad46-416f5f5f2edd'), 'The evening dinner suit worn by Roger Moore sold for £5,112', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('acabca10-160e-4736-a319-0d14733e3206'), 'Michael Billington (Sergei Barsov, Anya''s lover in the K.G.B.) was under consideration for 007, and played him during the casting of the leading ladies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab598fc3-1550-49c3-904f-23a85e2b6594'), 'The Union Jack parachute Bond uses in the opening sequence is an incorrect design. The red Cross of Saint Patrick is swapped with the white Cross of Saint Andrew in one corner. Prince Charles obviously did not notice this during the movie''s premiere, when he stood in honor of the flag', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('85ac60d4-9b86-400b-95a9-fb3244a5d406'), 'The last sub leaving, before the tanker sinks, has a Hull number of 593. S.S.N.-593 was the U.S.S. Thresher, which is on Eternal Patrol. Eternal Patrol is a designation for a submarine lost at sea', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c44596b2-5bb1-4fe3-9851-9b38c7a27701'), 'When Jaws'' car crashes into an old man''s hut in Sardinia, he says in Italian: "Mamma mia che è successo? Oddio, tutto distrutto!", which roughly translates to: "Oh my, what happened? Oh my god, it''s all destroyed!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('76bf84e9-32ac-4d5b-8212-6f9a168b28ae'), 'The first appearance of recurring character Defence Minister Frederick Gray (Geoffrey Keen). While walking along the docks, Bond addresses him as "Freddy" for the only time in the franchise (in all subsequent movies, he uses the more formal address "Minister")', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3ffcb9c9-864c-4bef-9170-036bbc08c9f1'), 'The Lotus Esprit, capable of transforming from car to submarine in the movie, was purchased for £616,000 at a London auction in October 2013 by Elon Musk, who plans to rebuild the vehicle as an actual dual-purpose car', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Spy Who Loved Me'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('08281b79-b723-49d0-9df0-a5ceeb6e3108'), 'Except for a few brief close-ups, the entire sequence of Bond, Jaws and the pilot falling from the plane, with Bond and the pilot fighting for a single parachute, was shot in free fall. The seven-pound camera for these sequences was mounted on the helmet of another skydiver, and a few shots are of the cameraman''s own arms and legs. Stuntmen Jake Lombard and B.J. Worth wore parachutes concealed within their suits. The "parachute" over which they fight is actually a dummy chute, which had to be removed before the stuntman could use the real parachute underneath. Stuntman Jake Lombard would don and remove the dummy chute up to three times in a single jump. The actual parachutes used by the stuntmen had a main and reserve chute concealed within the suit-coats. A breakaway seam ran down the back, which allowed the parachute to be opened without the need to remove the coat. There were only 60 to 70 seconds of free fall time, between when the stunt performers exited the aircraft and when they had to activate their chutes. After factoring in the time needed to get the performers and cameraman into position after leaving their plane, only a few seconds of film could be shot per jump. Therefore, the entire sequence required 88 jumps, and five weeks to film, just to produce the two minutes of footage in the final movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8b66031e-951b-4b9f-9045-898bc74d015d'), 'The cable that Jaws bites is actually made of licorice', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8bd63315-a127-47c2-8960-d67cbf003930'), 'The scene in which the gondola converts into a hovercraft, and elevates out of the water, succeeded with the fifth attempt. During the first four takes, the vehicle was so unstable that Sir Roger Moore fell into the water, and he needed to have his silk suit replaced for each take. It was fortunate that the stunt worked during the fifth take, because he was wearing the last available silk suit', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('de3990db-950c-4ee5-bd99-258f774fe75d'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli complained that Maurice Binder''s title sequence cost more than the entire budget of Dr. No (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3e93e39f-c821-44f4-809e-d04cc7423a64'), 'During the cable car stunt, high above Rio de Janeiro, a real cliffhanger moment occurred when stuntman Richard Graydon slipped, and was hanging on for dear life. The rest of the crew, including Sir Ken Adam, were petrified while the camera was rolling, and they were watching from a vantage point', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7ab26355-90ba-4840-9657-5ced02ea1394'), 'The cost for this movie was $30 million, nearly as much as the first eight films combined, without taking into account inflation', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8dfd025d-03d3-4d17-9f04-2f584eec654c'), 'For the fight between James Bond and Chang, this movie had the largest amount of break-away sugar glass used in a single scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c922a025-e9a3-4dd4-891a-927365d2c9f4'), 'Bernard Lee''s final appearance as M. The actor died in January 1981 when For Your Eyes Only (1981) was in pre-production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7c8d58f6-0f47-42c2-aad7-115524664fd0'), 'Despite the previous movie telling us that James Bond will return in For Your Eyes Only, producer Albert R. Broccoli chose this movie as the next installment, after the success of Star Wars: Episode IV - A New Hope (1977)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f94d2bac-828f-4c07-8067-a74a514ffa78'), 'Jaws was supposed to be Bond''s archnemesis in this movie, until director Lewis Gilbert started paying attention to some of the fan mail he was getting from small children, asking why he couldn''t be a goodie instead of a baddie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('574c89c5-75d1-46f8-b3f8-52d603e811bf'), 'Producer Albert R. Broccoli called Steven Spielberg, requesting permission to use the indelible five-note leitmotif from Close Encounters of the Third Kind (1977). Broccoli wanted to use it as the entry code for an electronic laboratory door lock in a scene in this movie. Several years later, Spielberg called Broccoli requesting permission to use the 007 theme music for a scene in a movie he was producing, titled The Goonies (1985). Broccoli pointed out that there were more than five notes in the 007 theme music. Spielberg suspected the producer''s tongue was firmly planted in his cheek, as he continued to banter. He was right. The Steven Spielberg and Albert R. Broccoli connection has another twist: Spielberg expressed an interest in directing a Bond movie while in negotiations with Broccoli, until George Lucas offered him the script for Raiders of the Lost Ark (1981)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f4d3260a-d198-41f9-af8c-6da2502f8250'), 'This was the highest-grossing Bond film for 16 years, until surpassed by GoldenEye (1995), longer than any other film in the franchise. The second-longest is Skyfall (2012), which has remained the highest-grossing as of 2025, 13 years. The third-longest is Thunderball (1965), which was the highest-grossing for eight years, until surpassed by Live and Let Die (1973)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0cafb472-e19e-4f99-962d-d43e8335c248'), 'Sir Roger Moore arrived a few days late for the shoot in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, due to a kidney stone attack in France. Moore had also had a renal colic attack while filming Live and Let Die (1973). Once he arrived in Rio de Janeiro, he literally walked off the plane, went into make-up and hair, got fitted out, went back onto the plane, and was then filmed arriving in Rio de Janeiro as James Bond for this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('57eae127-c6aa-43af-9fa7-0ce2b8ca4e2a'), 'During the scenes set in Venice, Pope John Paul I died. Filming was then suspended for the day, partly because the bells ringing in Venice mourning his death were so loud, it made it impossible to work', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ffc0d0df-636c-4f03-8404-b5c5a1f1f20e'), 'The title song was sung by Dame Shirley Bassey, the last time she did so in the Bond film franchise. The other two were Goldfinger (1964) and Diamonds Are Forever (1971). She also sang a version of the "Mr. Kiss Kiss Bang Bang" song for Thunderball (1965), which was not used. To date, Bassey is the only singer to have performed a Bond title song more than once', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('09c1d824-873d-4d77-8b2b-86968ce68ba7'), 'In the novel, Ian Fleming stated that when Bond reaches age 45, he will be "automatically taken off the ''00'' list and given a staff job at Headquarters." Sir Roger Moore was forty-five when he portrayed James Bond in Live and Let Die (1973)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('246c26e0-e122-4203-80b5-6b5a6d7c71fc'), 'Sir Roger Moore enjoyed filming in Paris, because production didn''t start until noon, and the hours were shorter. Eight hours a day on a movie is the limit one can work in France', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('36ecb07c-1176-4d30-8225-55f69d761aaa'), 'It was the first movie to feature the modern space shuttle in a movie. This movie''s release was supposed to coincide with the first launch of the space shuttle, but this unfortunately didn''t occur until April 12, 1981, just before the release of the next James Bond movie, For Your Eyes Only (1981), and exactly 20 years after Yuri Gagarin was the first man in space (April 12, 1961)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35d7b1e9-a69f-4182-acae-35f8bbd4d4be'), 'Sir Roger Moore''s distaste at the shooting scene is quite genuine. In his autobiography, Moore expressed an extreme dislike for bloodsports, and a reticence about guns', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db9e942b-0410-4da3-930f-78119a800113'), 'The only time Bond fires a gun in this movie is when he shoots the sniper out of the tree with Drax''s (Michael Lonsdale) shotgun', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('124ce91b-9e6b-46f1-95c5-4fa1d7f2acac'), 'Richard Kiel is the only henchman to appear in two Bond films', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1847a5d8-aff6-4075-9963-b33caa0096f0'), 'This movie became the focus of a real-life adventure story, when mercenary John Miller used it as cover, in his attempt to kidnap fugitive Great Train Robber Ronnie Biggs from Rio De Janeiro, Brazil, and return him to Britain for trial. Miller and his team posed as members of this movie''s production team, offering a cameo in the movie to Biggs, intending to lure him onto a yacht for the proposed scene to be filmed, and once in international waters, sail it to a Commonwealth country, from where he could be extradited. The scheme became unstuck when a member of the press, who''d heard rumors of the operation, telephoned Biggs'' house, thinking he had already been snatched', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e9075af-3696-406a-b08e-82b2b3cbb861'), 'Because of all the wild stunts they were allowed to shoot in Venice, producer Albert R. Broccoli donated money to the Save Venice Fund', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('86da3a5d-1b90-481d-a3f1-44f69f914f5b'), 'While certainly not the movie of which he was most ashamed, Sir Roger Moore often made fun of himself, and this movie, for the absurdity of the plot', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7dbb5419-3e8c-4455-b9e7-b03b31af7da7'), 'Lois Chiles had originally been offered the role of Anya in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), but turned down the part when she decided to take temporary retirement. She got the role of Holly Goodhead by chance when she was given the seat next to director Lewis Gilbert on a flight', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('368715d7-4836-457f-b472-4f89b87bd9ee'), 'The first time in the series where M shares a scene with the main antagonist', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a8fa8b4-36e7-4db2-876f-d2b8896ac4ae'), 'A "moonraker" has two dictionary definitions. It is a synonym for a moonsail, which is the highest sail of a ship. It is also a term from a Wiltshire folk story, where smugglers, trying to hide contraband, pretend to rake the water in a pond, so as to catch the reflection of the moon. It is sometimes used to refer to a man of extreme ambition, which could apply to either Bond or Drax', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('13dc6ab2-8b04-485d-8102-76491eba4782'), 'Barbara Bach was originally scheduled to make a brief appearance as Anya, the character she played in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), but the idea was dropped only a few weeks before filming began. According to the book, "The Bond Files", her character was going to be the woman shown in bed with General Gogol, in the scene where he moans to his British counterpart that he''s having trouble sleeping', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2172e761-a7fb-4081-860b-0a2dd4f40c26'), 'Real lasers were used in assisting with the creation of the special effects in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dbc9de46-6430-4dc0-80b9-09c165a560ea'), 'The Concorde jetliner shown when James Bond arrives in Rio de Janeiro is not, as some people erroneously believe, the one that was destroyed in the July 2000 crash in Paris, which resulted in all Concordes being permanently removed from service. This aircraft is production number 205, registration F-BVFA, and upon its retirement it was sent to the Smithsonian Air and Space museum in Washington, D.C., where it still can be seen today', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('becb451c-9259-4b3f-80ec-0bd667340a9f'), 'Final James Bond movie (to date) to feature John Barry''s second signature James Bond theme, "The 007 Theme", and the only Sir Roger Moore Bond movie in which it is heard', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('94b41b90-210b-40f3-943a-8be2b8c29278'), 'Stunt double and veteran skydiver Jake Lombard bore a strong resemblance to Roger Moore (that is, after he was persuaded to cut his long hair, and shave off his equally long beard). This allowed many relative close-up facial shots of Bond in free fall. As for the role of the pilot, skydiver B.J. Worth was chosen first, with Jean-Pierre Castaldi being chosen later for studio scenes, due to his resemblance to Mr. Worth', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ffa62fa-e78a-4659-ad0d-37a104ca6bc5'), 'In addition to being offered the chance to perform the title song, Frank Sinatra was offered the role of Hugo Drax', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('31468b88-cece-4368-87c9-0d53c513d049'), 'When the Minister of Defence and M arrive in Venice, the Minister mentions that he plays bridge with Drax. This is a reference to the original novel, in which the character of Drax is introduced as a card cheat, who constantly wins while playing bridge at M''s favorite club', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d9938107-3644-40bc-a3bb-7745e9888369'), 'This is the only James Bond movie where the signature pistol of Bond is not seen, be it the Walther PPK or the Walther P99', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e0a26761-3513-405b-ac47-087033b31af0'), 'To build the gigantic three-level Space Station set interiors at France''s Epinay Studios, the production utilized two tons of nails, 100 tons of metal, 220 technicians, and 10,000 feet of set construction woodwork', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8bd4aae-a10c-420f-8cb6-eccef9417dc0'), 'This movie utilized the largest set ever built in France', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('360c911b-21ed-4a00-8cd8-6c6543178af3'), 'When shooting moved to Rio de Janeiro, the Brazilian authorities wanted more money. As a result, the cable car scene was almost cut from the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c656a506-4796-4484-9d11-8e33fe6b380d'), 'When work on the film began, N.A.S.A. had not yet officially finalized the design of the Space Shuttle. At the time of filming, the Approach and Landing Test with the Enterprise (OV-101) was completed in October 1977, while Columbia (OV-102) was under construction. Fortunately for the production designers, there were subsequently no visible changes made to the shuttle''s design, making their rendering of it accurate. This also included the Shuttle Carrier Aircraft (N.A.S.A. 905, which is a former Boeing 747-123 aircraft originally sold to American Airlines), the opening sequence featured the S.C.A. with the Drax Enterprises Logo on the vertical stabilizer, but retaining the American Airlines livery. The real Shuttle Carrier Aircraft (N.A.S.A. 905) has been retired after ferrying Endeavour in late 2012, where it has become a museum display at Space Center Houston, with the Space Shuttle Explorer mounted on top, in 2015', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3d42caf5-2f0c-4648-8552-fcca2629646e'), 'Adapting to the different work ethics in France, production designer Sir Ken Adam was informed by the union leader that the crew will not work overtime. Adam could not recall even one Bond movie he designed which did not include overtime on the part of the construction crew to complete the interiors. Ultimately, the crew saw his designs, and they decided that it was indeed worthwhile to work overtime. In fact, he recalled that on Sundays, they brought their whole families', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e9d2da54-600c-4f56-a420-bde569ee1f17'), 'Vaux le Vicomte, a mini Versailles outside Paris. In the film it''s located in the Mojave Desert in California having been moved stone by stone by Hugo Drax', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dfb1acea-8435-41a0-8d4b-299ddaebbabd'), 'The majority of the women, seen as part of Drax''s master race, were Paris models, with the exception of Anne Lonnberg (who was a musician and actress prior to taking the role of the museum tour guide). The receptionist seen at the Venini Glass gallery (Irka Bochenko) became a musician (using the pseudonym Iren Bo). She recorded a hit single (Happy Birthday Mr. Bond) for the 50th anniversary of the James Bond film franchise (with Sir Roger Moore providing background vocals)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9bd272de-975b-4b8f-88ad-acfbc8111a70'), 'All of the space center scenes were shot at the Kennedy Space Center in Florida', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77b9edf8-1172-42c7-a8c3-1bd2c707d6ed'), 'Sir Roger Moore is believed to have conducted approximately 390 interviews for the promotion of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f27a6d63-5cfb-4ba5-b451-97852bab8c83'), 'In his original novel, Ian Fleming described Drax as "a Lonsdale figure". Twenty-four years later, after James Mason, Stewart Granger, and Louis Jourdan were rejected for the part, Drax was portrayed in this movie by Michael Lonsdale. Jourdan played Kamal Khan in Octopussy (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d743b939-6d55-46d0-a75c-84951fae9712'), 'During shooting, Lois Chiles'' brother Clay was diagnosed with Hodgkin''s disease. After filming wrapped, she returned to her native Houston to donate platelets to him every ten days. Sadly, her brother did not survive', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Moonraker'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('646c89ad-d0ac-473c-b56a-c34979341b83'), 'Only Bond movie to date in the official franchise not to feature "M". It was the first Bond movie not to feature Bernard Lee as "M", who had played the role in the previous eleven movies in the franchise. Lee died of stomach cancer on January 16, 1981, after the filming of this movie had started, but before his scenes were shot. Although Bernard Lee was dying of stomach cancer, he did try to film at least one scene in the movie, but in the end, it was too much for him, and he had to bow out. He died not long afterward. As a result, "Q''s" role in this movie was slightly expanded to fill the gap. As such, several scenes, originally intended to include "M", were re-written with "Q", (for example, the confessional scene). As a mark of respect, producer Albert R. Broccoli refused to re-cast the role, changing the script to say that "M" was on leave', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f61bae4c-33b6-4af0-b786-90d0933f060b'), 'In this movie''s conclusion, Bond uses his shoelaces to create a Prusik knot, attaching himself to his climbing rope so he can ascend a mountain. This technique, which is indeed possible to do with shoelaces, was invented by Austrian mountaineer Karl Prusik, and is common amongst climbers. The Prusik knot celebrated its 50th anniversary the year this movie was released, having first appeared in an Austrian mountaineering manual for rope ascending in 1931', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c6be63d4-e063-485e-aec3-4e8ffa2717be'), '23-year-old stuntman Paolo Rigoni died during the filming of the bobsled chase. This was due to a poorly designed track. Rigoni was not the only one to lose his life there, however. During an actual competition another bobsledder was killed at the same exact spot. The track was later modified for a less severe turn', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a57a66e5-6847-428a-98fe-5c4e79ef89a3'), 'A line of dialogue had to be cut from the opening helicopter sequence for legal reasons. The bald man could not be called "Blofeld", as Kevin McClory had won a court case several years previous, and owned the rights to the use of "S.P.E.C.T.R.E.", and "Ernst Stavro Blofeld". Unofficially disposing of Blofeld so early in this movie was Albert R. Broccoli''s way of telling McClory that the success of 007 did not depend on him, and he got rid of Blofeld (supposedly) once and for all. McClory produced and released the unofficial Bond movie, Never Say Never Again (1983), in which Blofeld was played by Max von Sydow. Blofeld did not appear in an EON produced Bond movie again until Spectre (2015), after the rights matter was finally settled in 2013', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f7688975-e6a8-4cca-9fa3-5ddfcf4bf51a'), 'The stunt of Bond falling off the cliff was dangerous, since the sudden rope jerk at the bottom could be fatal. Derek Meddings developed a system that would dampen the stop, but Rick Sylvester recalled that his nerves nearly got the better of him: "From where we were, you could see the local cemetery; and the box (to stop my fall) looked like a casket. You didn''t need to be an English major to connect the dots." The stunt went off without a problem', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('45f411fb-f46d-4e23-8db7-52420e583421'), 'Begging Bond to spare his life, "Ernst Blofeld" baffles viewers with the cryptic line "I''ll buy you a delicatessen, in stainless steel!" It is reported that the phrase is attributable to producer Albert R. Broccoli, who recalled accounts of 1930s New York mafia gangsters offering full-service delis as a bribe to cohorts, complete with stainless steel countertops', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e2247dad-511b-462f-9f31-bb72018836bc'), 'Sir Roger Moore hated the final scene with Margaret Thatcher. He felt it didn''t suit the serious tone of the rest of the film. He also didn''t like getting a clue about the A.T.A.C. from a parrot. Moore thought it represented the type of silliness his Bond films were usually criticized for', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('55013145-6d77-4fb9-acb3-e991e77dbae6'), 'To enter the identigraph booth, "Q" enters five digits of a seven digit code. Those five digits were the first five notes to the chorus of "Nobody Does It Better", the theme to The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). James Bond responds by entering the final two notes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('981447d3-caec-43e7-9902-c3bd434e0406'), 'To pay tribute to the death of Sir Roger Moore, two James Bond movies, The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) and this movie, Moore''s two favorite of his Bond movies, as well as the two he considered his best, were re-released on selected dates in selected territories around the world within a few weeks of his passing, with fifty percent of the proceeds going to Moore''s beloved charity, U.N.I.C.E.F., for which he was a Goodwill Ambassador', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e03664d7-20c8-4db1-ada1-559cd89fd989'), 'The reason the underwater close-ups of Carole Bouquet had to be faked was that she had sinus trouble that made it impossible for her to dive or remain underwater', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0c484215-e2f1-45cc-9586-510be4ac45b9'), 'The epitaph in the opening scene of Bond''s wife''s tombstone is, "we have all the time in the world", his last words to her in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), and title song. Forty years later in the film that would see the death of Bond, No Time to Die (2021), he would say these words once again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('13e4c89a-24d7-4ca4-abf6-8f6301e16204'), 'Sir Roger Moore''s vertigo made the rock face climax especially hard to do. Moore has said that he took a small amount of Valium, and drank a tall glass of beer before some of the scary climbing sequences, which helped him through the close-up shots. Stuntman Rick Sylvester performed most of the work. Moore only had to dangle over a four-foot drop, while Sylvester dangled over a twenty-foot drop', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('219551ce-ec90-43fc-897a-d1ac96a24f9d'), 'When Bond and Melina are dragged along by the boat, the camera was operating at a reported speed of 72 to 84 frames per second, and then played back at 24 frames per second, to simulate underwater inertia. The bubbles were added in close-up by simply adding Alka-Seltzer, which were then imposed over the negatives, when Bond and Melina opened their mouths', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eeb8056c-9a63-4bf2-9d0a-70582125fafc'), 'The assassination of "Melina Havelock''s" parents was first intended as part of the opening credits sequence. The reaction shot of the murder was intended to cut to a close-up on her face, whereby the look of anger and revenge in her eyes would then segue into the main titles', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9c391f76-71d6-4306-a486-7524a12fffd0'), 'Carole Bouquet was dubbed. However, she dubbed herself in the French version', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7e6571a6-632c-421c-b87d-42c177e0cf8f'), 'This movie saved United Artists from financial ruin. At the time of this movie''s release, the studio was still reeling from Michael Cimino''s Heaven''s Gate (1980), a notorious $40 million bomb that was about to force United Artists to file for bankruptcy. When this movie took in a worldwide gross of $195 million, the studio was saved, and afterwards turned its focus toward blockbusters and less on personal movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('33559168-f1a0-45a6-afaf-a314225b8c5e'), 'Moonraker (1979) was a huge financial success, but critics commented that the film franchise had become too focused on wild gadgets, outlandish plots, over-the-top villains, and screwball comedy. As a result, producers decided to return to a more realistic storyline in this movie, using From Russia with Love (1963) and On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) as models. Therefore, this movie contains many story elements similar to those movies; the A.T.A.C. is similar to the Lektor, Kriegler is similar to Grant, Columbo is similar to Kerim Bey, and the winter activities sequences are similar to those in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6e8d417b-6fe7-45eb-8043-045c4b4a8dec'), 'A major problem occurred during production which threatened to stop the filmmakers filming. The monks who lived in the monastery on top of the Meteora Mountain placed sheets and plastic on top of the roofs and external infrastructure so as to halt filming. They allegedly did not like the violence associated with James Bond. Reportedly, Sir Roger Moore told them that he had once been a Saint (a reference to The Saint (1962)). A special hearing of the Greek Supreme Court was convened, where a panel of judges decreed that the monks only had rights over the interiors of the mountain-top monastery, but the exteriors were the domain of the people and the local government. The movie crew was eventually able to film at the location, which included a gigantic fall by Stuntman Rick Sylvester. They did not film inside the monastery (known as St. Cyril''s in this movie), but built a set on top of a neighboring rock for some of the hideout''s exteriors. The interiors were filmed back at Pinewood Studios on a set designed by Peter Lamont', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('30051e9f-c7be-434d-8d88-8db941f56d34'), 'The closing scene with British Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher, marked the first time a real-life head of government was portrayed on-screen in a James Bond movie. She was portrayed by Janet Brown, who was well known in the UK for her impersonation of Thatcher', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0ee172ac-714d-4dbe-a455-775ef909931f'), 'It was during this production that Cassandra Harris introduced her husband, Pierce Brosnan, to producer Albert R. Broccoli', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('14ed9a7e-7f27-486c-a05d-1666a921b965'), 'Maurice Binder decided to include Sheena Easton in the title sequence because he thought she looked striking. After meeting her in person, he told producer Albert R. Broccoli, "I must have that face!" However, shooting Easton in the title sequence proved to be a problem, since Binder was using soft-light focus, and a very high resolution film stock. On extreme close-ups of Easton''s face, the smallest, most imperceptible head wobble would blur her image on the film. Binder finally had to resort to putting Easton''s head in a steel clamp, which kept her head perfectly still. The tongs of the clamp were hidden in her hair, with the support hidden behind her back. "It was the most painful thing I''ve ever worn," Easton later recalled. "But he got my face, in 70 millimeter."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('330b61e1-4177-4130-a3ea-86e55389e7ce'), 'Cassandra Harris "Countess Lisl" was, at the time of filming, married to future Bond actor Pierce Brosnan. Brosnan was offered the part five years later, but he was unable to appear as Bond in The Living Daylights (1987) due to Remington Steele (1982) commitments', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('07f08a07-e005-4966-9365-b62a6f7e2b2e'), 'For the first time since On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), we see Bond toss his trilby onto the stand to announce himself to Moneypenny. Roger Moore was never seen wearing it during his time in the role, despite repeating the procedure in the next two entries', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e77241b6-1e36-4ea8-bd2a-e064e04abfd5'), 'In the opening sequence, James Bond visits his deceased wife''s grave at Stoke Poges Church, adjacent to Gert Fröbe''s golf course, from Goldfinger (1964). The scene was written when Sir Roger Moore was considering retirement from the franchise, to provide story continuity between different Bond actors. Ironically, the teaser scene has absolutely nothing to do with the plot of the movie that follows, leaving it more connected to earlier Bond movies, than to the one it opens', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3bc2a9de-2ec0-493a-aadb-98e7d5eac9c2'), 'In the movie, James Bond rejects "Bibi''s" Lynn-Holly Johnson''s advances, presumably due to her being too young for him. Bond later has a relationship with "Melina" Carole Bouquet. Melina is presumably older than Bibi in the movie. In reality, the two actresses are only a year apart in age', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('aa9c53e3-d82a-4bbf-9fc5-8ee47a08adc6'), 'According to Julian Glover, he was in such dire financial straits before being cast in this film he was considering selling his car and house. Playing a Bond villain significantly boosted his fortunes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('76ecb113-f9ea-42ab-b786-927a42161e00'), 'Sir Roger Moore has stated that, of all of the cars he drove in the franchise, the Citroen 2CV was his favorite', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d41f0617-1e2c-425b-b993-538df8c2333f'), 'Bond mentions a Chinese saying: "Before setting out for revenge, you first dig two graves". That particular quote is indeed Chinese and attributed to the Chinese philosopher Confucius', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8643c3b-2534-4a2c-a9de-883b96be6d25'), 'Director John Glen stated that there had been some discussion of bringing back the "Jaws" character for a third time, but eventually the idea was rejected, as they felt he did not fit the movie''s more serious tone', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c2da1a36-c22d-4166-938e-bc6d83257fef'), 'Since flying a helicopter through a warehouse was thought to be too dangerous, the scene was shot using forced perspective. A smaller mock-up was built by Derek Meddings'' team closer to the camera that the stunt pilot Marc Wolff flew behind, and this made it seem as if the helicopter was entering the warehouse. The footage inside the building was shot on-location, though with a life-sized helicopter model, which stood over a rail. Stuntman Martin Grace stood in as Bond, when the Agent is dangling outside the flying helicopter, while Sir Roger Moore was used in the scenes inside the model', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('011397c1-8889-4a73-89bc-352ad989a938'), 'Steven Spielberg had been very much interested in directing a James Bond movie in his earlier years and had talked with producer Albert R. Broccoli about directing one, but Broccoli told him he only wanted British directors to helm the film franchise. Shortly afterwards, George Lucas offered Spielberg an iconic hero of his own, in the form of Indiana Jones, in Raiders of the Lost Ark (1981)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d551c6cc-7d6d-4ff2-a5db-88bf39f90b0f'), 'The exploding Lotus at the start of this movie was a tacit acknowledgment that Bond would not be relying on fancy gadgets in this movie as he had done in the last few entries in the franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('83af08f1-5f82-4de4-abc8-8fa552a2f784'), 'The close-ups of Carole Bouquet and Sir Roger Moore for the underwater scenes were filmed in slow motion a studio with a wind fan to produce the effect of floating hair. The bubbles were added in later', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c2510563-fac9-4c03-ae7b-9cc62d73e816'), 'Charles Dance''s feature-film debut as the thug "Claus" in this movie. He played James Bond author Ian Fleming in Goldeneye (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5b283251-4c04-409e-bb9e-5a4af4801363'), 'Jeremy Bulloch (Smithers, the guy testing Q''s gadget with a fake cast on his arm) appeared in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), as an H.M.S. Ranger crewman. He returned as Smithers in Octopussy (1983). He also played Boba Fett in Star Wars: Episode V - The Empire Strikes Back (1980) and Star Wars: Episode VI - Return of the Jedi (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4d6e5c00-c547-40e1-9b83-ace942cfc154'), 'Julian Glover "Aristotle Kristatos" was a candidate to play James Bond in the sixties, and was on the short list, as a possible replacement for Sir Sean Connery and George Lazenby, prior to the role going to Sir Roger Moore', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('63083d12-38ae-4e0f-b9a9-66da0493f084'), 'This was the first Bond movie to be based on one of Ian Fleming''s short stories (instead of one of his novels). Interestingly, there are several scenes in this movie lifted from other Fleming tales. Examples: The assault on the smugglers'' boat and warehouse was lifted intact from a short story titled "Risico", and the sequence featuring Bond and Melina being dragged through the coral was lifted from the climax from the book, "Live and Let Die". The Identigraph appeared in a slightly different form in the book, "Goldfinger"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e1bdf09e-319d-4689-a31a-079390ebf5d7'), 'The helicopter sequence in the pre-credits sequence involves Beckton Gas Works, which Stanley Kubrick converted to the Vietnamese city of Hue in 1987 for Full Metal Jacket (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d1541a62-222a-4a6b-b926-6d14c07c588a'), 'The story involving the sinking of the ship named the St. Georges off the Albanian coast was inspired by an international incident on April 11, 1968, when a Soviet submarine was blown up, and sank in the Pacific Ocean. Seventy personnel died, and the U.S. Navy located the wreck using the nautical Glomar Explorer under Project Azorian: The Raising of the K-129 (2010), a mission funded secretly by the CIA through Howard Hughes'' corporations, on whom the Willard Whyte character in Diamonds Are Forever (1971) was based', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d8cf30c-919e-4529-8139-d8cdf702941f'), 'When Bibi (Lynn-Holly Johnson) flirts with Bond (Sir Roger Moore), she states that Aristotle Kristatos (Julian Glover) is much older than Bond. While Bibi pursues Bond, she later tells Kristatos that he''s "too old for her". Glover was born in 1935, and is actually eight years younger than Moore', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('75188dab-0ef6-4517-afa9-162fc7124b8b'), 'Sir Roger Moore wasn''t sure if audiences would accept his more serious portrayal of Bond in this film; for instance, in one scene, he coldly disposes of a bad guy off a cliff. But in the end, critics wound up giving Moore some of the best reviews in his career', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fba6978d-d446-4a25-a33e-eff565e779b6'), 'The title song is the first in the James Bond film franchise in which we see the person who is singing, in this case, Sheena Easton. The song was a Top 10 hit on both the U.K. charts (number eight) and U.S. charts (number four, July 25, 1981). It received an Academy Award nomination for Best Song, and was featured in a song and dance number at the Oscars on March 29, 1982. It featured dancers dressed as villains and henchman, such as "Dr. No" and "Ernst Stavro Blofeld", as well as the real Harold Sakata and real Richard Kiel, reprising their roles as "Oddjob" and "Jaws", respectively. A dancer played James Bond, and at the end of the sequence, he took off in a rocket with Sheena Easton, who had been singing the title song live. This was just one of a medley of five song and dance numbers for each Best Song nominee on the night, and it also acted as a preamble to the presentation by Sir Roger Moore of the Irving Thalberg Honorary Award to Albert R. Broccoli in honor of the James Bond film franchise. Starting with this movie, and the rise of the MTV Generation, all Bond movies have had music video tie-ins', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1a7ff3a3-e6d7-45bb-bdc2-557cd6039067'), 'The opening scene, where Bond visits his wife Tracy''s grave, was written as a way to introduce the new Bond actor, thus linking the new actor to elements from previous Bond movies. Namely, Timothy Dalton, who was approached to take over as Bond in this movie. Dalton declined, as he disliked the direction the franchise was taking at the time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4217817b-7cb2-4396-b347-214f202c4b4c'), 'After viewing Flash Gordon (1980), the producers at one time wanted to cast not just Topol "Zarkov" in this movie, but also Timothy Dalton "Prince Barin" as Bond, and Ornella Muti "Princess Aura" as Melina, even writing the part specifically for her. Dalton eventually became Bond in 1986, after Sir Roger Moore retired from the franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e430fa32-b121-48f6-afe3-65d6b9f9871d'), 'When shooting the still for the movie''s main poster, photographer Morgan Kane allegedly asked his model to put the swimsuit on backwards, as it hung too low over her legs. After the poster had been released, some newspaper editors felt that there was too much buttock shown in the poster. To show less skin, the swimsuit was extended, or shorts were added to the hips in the posters. The original poster caused outrage among various groups, causing Saskatchewan to rate this movie "Special X", despite being rated PG or equivalent virtually everywhere else. That rating was later lowered. Apparently, the model''s identity was not known for some time. More than one model alleged that she was the owner of the legs, but it was finally revealed they belonged to 22-year-old New York City model Joyce Bartle', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('28271cdd-12d2-45d6-b7d6-62811f4d7f49'), 'Although an accomplished cross-country skier, Sir Roger Moore wasn''t insured to do any downhill skiing. Willy Bogner handled all the skiing for him. Any close-ups with Moore were done with him strapped to a sled pulled downhill, while Bognor skied backwards while looking into the camera. Moore tried to learn downhill skiing in Gstaad. His children had school afternoons there, and were embarrassed that he kept falling over. But he eventually became quite reasonable at it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4a4ebd9-3558-4aa5-9bee-70a295bc2d95'), 'When "Ferrara" introduces Bond to "Kristatos", he invites them to join him in some glühwein. This is an Austrian-German type of spiced wine served heated, often after ski runs. It means "glow wine", said to make one glow with warmth, and can be seen in a hotpot carafe on Kristatos'' table', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('104d1695-8768-41a3-af53-b9daa019b04d'), 'Because no snow had fallen in Cortina d''Ampezzo for several weeks when filming moved there on 1 January 1981, there was little on the ground so some 25 truck loads were brought in from outlying districts to spread around the streets where filming was to take place', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c0ba9317-c60f-4529-977c-697e6921df3c'), 'Four Citroën 2CVs were used, with modifications for the stunts. All had more powerful flat-four engines, and one received a special revolving plate on its roof, so it could get turned upside down', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('55fcb43b-60b2-4912-b9ec-3d3359f3a1b8'), 'This movie draws its inspiration from three real-life events. First, the disappearance of the British trawler "Gaul" during a storm in the Barents Sea in 1974. Rumors abounded that, like the St. Georges, it was actually a spy ship monitoring Soviet forces, and was lost as a result of an espionage mission gone wrong (over forty years later, the wreck was discovered, and proven to have sunk purely as a result of bad weather). Second, the crippling of two British destroyers in 1946, by sea mines laid by the Albanian Communist regime in international waters. Last, the recovery of codebooks and components of the Enigma cypher machine from the sinking German armed trawler "Krebs" during World War II, which proved to be invaluable in deciphering secret German communications', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4b12e7b4-9fbe-473b-b40f-25faa7f115f3'), 'The stunt double for Cassandra Harris "Lisl" was injured when hit by the dune buggy in the beach scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6cda223a-e237-4a0d-b3cb-04ed8e7478db'), 'This was the first James Bond script to be written by regular James Bond writing duo team Richard Maibaum and Michael G. Wilson. This writing partnership continued until Licence to Kill (1989). It was also the first James Bond movie directed by John Glen, whose first Bond movie he worked on was On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), as second unit director. He directed four more movies in the franchise, ending with Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'For Your Eyes Only'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('adb0474f-bdbd-4093-91d6-0ae7796c82a7'), 'According to Sir Roger Moore''s commentary in the DVD during the dinner scene, the eyeball in the stuffed sheep''s head that Louis Jourdan eats is made out of marzipan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0171977e-2751-4c9d-b243-50b679233f8c'), 'Released in the same year as the rival "Warner Brothers" James Bond production "Never Say Never Again (1983)," which showcased the return of Sir Sean Connery to the role. This movie earned $187 million worldwide. "Never Say Never Again" (1983) earned $160 million', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('279155c2-d6b7-4ac3-a452-46285902de50'), 'Stuntman Martin Grace had a serious accident while filming on the train. Hanging on the side of it, the train went into a non-assessed area of the track and he rammed into a pylon, seriously damaging his leg and hip and hospitalizing him for several months. He made a full recovery. In a similar vein, the actor who uses the buzz saw yo-yo broke his arm when he fell over the balcony onto Octopussy''s bed. Despite his injury and having to wear a cast, he insisted on completing the rest of his scenes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c9abd4c9-ccad-45b0-a3ed-030924b7bd80'), 'The blue-ringed octopus is highly venomous. It produces Tetrodotoxin, which it uses in self-defense. Tetrodotoxin is also found in puffer fish. One milligram of the toxin can kill a person, and there is no known antidote', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9ec36a8d-a28b-4691-aa6b-b58a63bcd603'), 'It was not a planned part of the Indian cabbie chase sequence when a cyclist rode in between the two battling vehicles, but it -by chance - fortunately provided added suspense', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a6ce0a37-096a-43e9-84c0-23b516cecdad'), 'Barbara Carrera turned down the role of Octopussy in order to appear in "Never Say Never Again (1983)" because she wanted to work with Sir Sean Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7a018dee-4743-4e5a-a015-d0b04f848fb9'), 'Robert Brown appears as "M" for the first time, replacing Bernard Lee, who died between "Moonraker (1979)" (Lee''s final appearance as M) and "For Your Eyes Only (1981)," which left M out entirely', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3c1df711-bcf0-4956-8250-0cc8bd6b79b8'), 'In his book, "As You Wish: Inconceivable Tales from the Making of The Princess Bride," Cary Elwes states that before he was an actor, he worked as a production assistant on this movie, with his job being to drive Sir Roger Moore to the set every morning. Elwes further goes on to say that he was "a nervous wreck" being constantly afraid of getting in a car accident and accidentally killing the Bond actor, so he drove very, very slowly. On one occasion, Mr. Moore noticed how scared Elwes was while driving and calmed him down by complimenting his driving, saying, "You can speed up a little if you want to."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cbec6f82-3079-42b8-8a1e-f2bc1cc9b317'), 'Last Bond movie to reveal the name of the next Bond movie during the end credits, namely "From A View To A Kill," which later dropped the "from" out of the title', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('97b16dac-573d-46a1-b05a-3485aff190a0'), 'In the train / flying car stunt, when the car landed, one of the stuntmen dressed as a fisherman only just made it out of the row boat in the lake where the car was landing. This footage can be seen in the finished movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5b450fd0-042e-491f-bd51-d96008ba8fcc'), 'During filming, Sir Roger Moore was misdiagnosed with heart problems. When he got home, Maud Adams had her boyfriend, who was a doctor, give him a second opinion. He pronounced him medically fit', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0f599033-048b-489f-9b4f-a672135bb985'), 'The quip at the end of the opening sequence, "Fill ''er up, please!", was initially removed by director John Glen. It was only when he went to his local cinema and caught the trailer (which included the line), and saw how well it went down with the audiences, that he reinstated it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a3823b8c-de4e-4866-b7af-7d5838be7eec'), 'Vijay Amritraj played a snake charmer. In reality, Amritraj is terrified of snakes, and was virtually unable to take part in any of the action. His character mentions this while disposing of the cobra in the basket, by telling Bond, "This was the wrong cover. I hate snakes."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b5dba0c5-fcbf-4fb1-b1e9-aca63a732e7b'), 'Kristina Wayborn (Magda) says a romantic "au revoir" to James Bond, by way of an elegant elegiac window exit. She performed this stunt herself, swirling down to the ground, her dress acting as her support, and being unwound as she alighted safely to the ground. Weyborn''s departure was filmed in two different locations: her fall from the balcony was filmed at Pinewood Studios in England, and her landing was filmed on-location in India', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b079820b-514f-45ba-a9b3-59c4dd643854'), 'Permission to shoot in the region of Udaipur had to be sought and granted from the reigning Royal Maharana Bagwat Singh. He would frequently entertain the A-list of the cast and crew at dinners during production, where they would be served specially made Rose Wine', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c06af9e-817e-4f4a-9965-b4c949ae5955'), 'Octopussy is the daughter of Major Dexter Smythe, who was allowed by James Bond to commit suicide, rather than be captured, when his crimes of embezzlement and murder were discovered. This is the only reference to Ian Fleming''s original short story "Octopussy" in the movie. The Sotheby''s auction scene comes from the Ian Fleming story "Property of a Lady". The scene of 009 trying to escape East Germany, is an allusion to Fleming''s "The Living Daylights". The line "Spend the money quickly, Mr. Bond", spoken by a villain, who loses to Bond at a gambling table, is paraphrased from the novel "Moonraker".', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4547e829-bb19-4129-99aa-42a19d70e8c7'), 'Q appears as an active participant in a mission for the first time, as opposed to being behind the scenes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5043419e-e894-4aa2-8b98-92655e89d511'), 'Kristina Wayborn broke several toes while shooting the attack on the Monsoon Palace by Octopussy''s Circus. A bazooka, she was to kick out of a thug''s arms, was supposed to be replaced with a plastic model, but the stuntman was holding a metal one by accident', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77ddb63f-8d7c-4b08-874a-478a95cfee1d'), '1983 saw all three actors who played James Bond reprise their role. Moore & Connery led their own features. But what is lesser known is that George Lazenby had a cameo as the character "JB" in the TV Movie "The Return of the Man from Uncle". Lazenby is only referred to by the initials "JB" and he even drives a Aston Martin to help Napoleon Solo in a car chase. All nods to his previous time as James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f3d59d2c-c3b9-428d-a00e-88a6ae6de2c9'), 'This movie was released four months before Never Say Never Again (1983). This was the second time that two James Bond movies were released in the same year. It previously occurred with Casino Royale (1967) and You Only Live Twice (1967)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a8ed6e39-dca0-4790-ac6f-65a4c9ee4884'), 'The Fabergé Egg, as seen in the movie, was based on the Imperial Coronation Egg designed by Peter Carl Fabergé. It was made in 1897 to commemorate the 1896 Coronation of Czar Nicholas II. The jewelled egg contains a model of a Coronation Coach; a guilloché field of starbursts with a translucent lime yellow enamelling on the exterior surface; trellised greenish gold laurel leave bands have mounted at each intersection point an opaque black enamelled Imperial gold double-headed eagle with a rose diamond on their chest; on the top is a large portrait diamond with a cluster of ten smaller diamonds; and a smaller portrait diamond is set within a cluster of rose diamonds at the reverse end. The actual Coronation Egg was yellow in color. The egg reappeared in Ocean''s Twelve (2004)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6a2958af-5805-446e-ac2f-4a8220b8ea81'), 'During casting, James Brolin was almost given the role of James Bond, when at the last minute, Sir Roger Moore agreed to play Bond again. Brolin''s screentests can be seen on the DVD. Moore had gone out of contract after Moonraker (1979), and had agreed to return to the role one more time in For Your Eyes Only (1981). The production went with Moore, because this movie would be competing with Never Say Never Again (1983), starring original and former James Bond actor, Sir Sean Connery. The uncertainty in using an American actor in the role, having to introduce a new actor, and going-up against Connery were the reasons. In the meantime, Oliver Tobias, Michael Billington, Timothy Dalton, and Ian Ogilvy had also been considered for James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6ffed9ff-e6e6-4f39-8a7a-810c12ba0711'), 'Many production and story ideas and elements, not used in "Moonraker (1979)," ended up being utilized for this movie. These included the knife throwing twins, the casting of Louis Jourdan as the villain, and the Acrostar Bede jet sequence. The backgammon game was originally intended to take place in Max Kalba''s club in "The Spy Who Loved Me (1977)."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7547fe71-9326-4296-ab5b-0ebc00f332e1'), 'In one scene, a Soviet Chairman (played by Paul Hardwick) is seen and appears to be a caricature of Soviet leader Leonid Brehznev. The real-life Brehznev died in November 1982 after the scene was filmed and before the film''s release. In post-production, the filmmakers felt like deleting the scene (due to Brehnev''s passing), but since the scene was needful to the plot and the film doesn''t specify what year/time it''s set in, it was decided to be left in the film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('86f9197c-7a57-41d4-9501-2e28d9c32c9f'), 'The short story was published in Playboy Magazine, being serialized two years after Fleming''s death, in the March and April 1966 editions. It was also the final James Bond short story written by Ian Fleming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40aa447c-ed47-4732-932e-ed3097a63cdf'), 'The first acting role for Vijay Amritraj, a professional tennis player attempting to transition into an acting career. Parts of his role as Vijay involved inside jokes relating to his tennis career', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f9edce7a-0f22-459b-9658-fb35cca7bbf7'), 'Even though Maud Adams played the title role, the audience doesn''t see her face until one hour and nine minutes into the movie. That would explain why she was nominated in the Best Supporting Actress category at the Saturn Awards, instead of in the Best Actress category. She lost the award to Candy Clark in Blue Thunder (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('46678c2f-e166-4c44-bd67-7999c6cffd6b'), 'The "company" taxi used to pick up 007 was specially constructed at Pinewood Studios, and capable of speeds in excess of seventy miles (one hundred thirteen kilometers) per hour', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a7580594-3280-4822-b759-58b3d0f72fa1'), 'General Orlov''s line "but tomorrow I shall be the hero of the Soviet Union" was removed in Finland', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('efc936e8-f8ff-4ad1-b12a-e96bc053863f'), 'While travelling between England and India in August 1982, production designer Peter Lamont was on a plane that was hijacked', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e712dc3-69b9-46a1-9734-d97befc080ed'), 'With the re-casting of M in this movie, it was Sir Roger Moore who recommended Robert Brown for the part. Moore had known Brown since the two worked together on the television series Ivanhoe (1958)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f41c5130-bd09-4ba9-a754-73ef107dafa3'), 'Because of the hotel''s involvement with this movie, Udaipur''s Lake Palace Hotel is now nicknamed "The Octopussy Hotel"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98f1fd33-8c70-4906-8c14-afa44028b365'), 'The black and white Octopus insignia was a symbol of S.P.E.C.T.R.E., the criminal spy organisation seen in other James Bond movies. However, in the short story and this movie, it has no connection to either story. Even if the producers had wanted to resurrect the Octopus symbol for this movie, the legal settlement with Kevin McClory gave him all of the rights to the use of "S.P.E.C.T.R.E.", and as such, the black-and-white octopus insignia could not have been used in this movie. The type of octopus seen on the Octopussy girls'' bodies was different. It was a blue-ringed octopus. In this movie, this symbol was a sign of an old secret order of female bandits and smugglers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('45424f8e-0a4c-46a8-8be8-f70199c9140b'), 'The elephant hunt sequence had its origins in the The Man with the Golden Gun (1974). Producer Harry Saltzman had wanted an elephant stampede in the movie, so Bond and Scaramanga could chase each other on elephant back. The rest of the creative team balked at the idea, but Saltzman went to see an elephant trainer. It turns out, that elephants need special shoes on their feet to protect them from rough surfaces when they work. A few months later, while filming in Thailand, producer Albert R. Broccoli got a call saying his elephant shoes were ready. Saltzman had ordered about twenty-six hundred pairs of them. The sequence did not end up being in "The Man with the Golden Gun", and the man who made the shoes did not get paid. As of 1990, EON Productions allegedly still owed him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('74c9c715-76b1-4646-b5fd-f007d22d1255'), 'Kabir Bedi remains the only established Bollywood actor to appear in a James Bond movie. Zaheera, who appeared in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service, had a short-lived career in the Bollywood industry in the 70s and early 80s', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('23de91ca-1ae3-4837-bdd9-18176b12e079'), 'Steven Berkoff agreed to play Orlov when the director''s first choice, Rutger Hauer, turned down the role. This move paid off well on Berkoff''s part as his short but fierce performance as the ruthless general was a hit with American audiences, leading to him being cast as villain roles in Beverly Hills Cop (1984) and Rambo: First Blood Part II (1985)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eac7da15-a388-4537-ba34-bfe5b3479f6c'), 'During the parade leading to the circus, a performer is wearing the Silver Shamrock skeleton mask from Halloween III Season of the Witch', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6ccff648-a6e4-4e8f-81d9-89950df9654a'), 'Feldstadt is a fictitious German city created for this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('38644a66-6498-4382-a205-2e75a0c6e820'), 'Octopussy''s bed was designed in the shape of an octopus by Peter Lamont', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40e36efa-0a93-47f6-be86-72a0dc5c3c11'), '"Octopussy and The Living Daylights" was the fourteenth and final Ian Fleming James Bond book published in 1966. Sometimes released as just "Octopussy", it was the second posthumous book in the series after "The Man with the Golden Gun". Before he died, Fleming had intended to produce a second book of James Bond short stories like the "For Your Eyes Only" collection', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0c5a839-656c-48f9-a717-5a7da0981ae1'), 'Though an Indian location had been previously touted for Live and Let Die (1973), India only really became a choice when location scouts came across the city of Udaipur and its local leader allowed full co-operation and access to its architecturally stunning palaces', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('53e40986-b34c-4725-b774-65631cc4877d'), 'The character of Penelope Smallbone was named after one of the models who appeared in the opening credits to The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). At one point, Lois Maxwell flubbed a line and called her Penelope Smallbush, so that Sir Roger Moore replied "We know where your mind has been, Moneypenny!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1ae19686-6b5d-417e-ba6e-0a9301918a77'), 'Writer Ramon Sanchez spoke to producer Michael G. Wilson in the 1980s. Wilson related his concern that it could be the end of the James Bond film franchise, pointing out that Sir Sean Connery was returning as James Bond in another movie not made by EON Productions. He was careful not to reveal copyrighted material, so to help him, a concept was needed, that would beat anything, with which the opposing movie studio could come up. Sanchez gave Wilson a concept that eventually made its way to the movie: a female villain with a female criminal organization, running a circus as a front with a train. Wilson approved, and then asked Sanchez how to resolve a hitch, a small problem in the story, and a big problem in the screenplay. He explained that the Ian Fleming story was a short story of gold embezzlement and murder by a government man that James Bond cornered. That story was too short for a movie, and he could not justify calling this movie "Octopussy" if the concept for the movie was not remotely close to the short story. He had to link the two stories together, make the result longer, and squeeze it for all it had. Sanchez suggested that the woman lead be made not such an evil villain, but the daughter of the man in the story, Major Dexter Smythe, allowed by Bond to commit suicide, rather than be captured, and that her father''s pet name for her was Octopussy, tying in to the Octopussy title nicely. Make her Bond''s love interest, and the leading Bond Girl, and he had his story', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('550c119f-51d4-48ad-b9c7-ae486f9e5527'), 'Roger Moore had become an executive board member at The House of Fabergé in 1970', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ecf8cd5a-a8ab-41b8-a3cd-2d1e834ca80a'), 'Most of the crew, as well as Sir Roger Moore, had food poisining problems while shooting in India. Apparently Moore was rarely out of the toilet on the flight home', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('206632f6-540c-4cc0-b3b9-ecb6313679b4'), 'The "Sit!" command (with the emphasis on the "t") Bond uses to stop the tiger, is a nod to then-popular Barbara Woodhouse, a dog trainer who was famous for her polite and firm tone when commanding dogs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('70926339-f451-477a-b67a-ed547a129e00'), 'Former British Olympic gymnast Suzanne Dando supervised the stunts performed by the gymnastic team in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('95d96202-d08a-4751-9e7b-8ef4e9b993b0'), 'First James Bond movie to be released with the MGM lion logo at the beginning. MGM merged with United Artists in 1982, the year before the release of this movie, and this is the first Bond movie distributed by the new company, MGM/UA Distribution Company, Inc', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6894b0b1-bd9f-4ecc-9722-b4e83b99de09'), 'The two primary gadgets Bond receives from Q (a pen containing acid, and a watch with video capability) are similar to two gadgets given to Evelyn Trimble, a.k.a. James Bond, in Casino Royale (1967). Bond even repeats the same "poison pen letter" joke that invited eyerolls in the earlier movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c8d6a2d2-e60d-4075-b904-2d00271d64c5'), '"Be at least twenty miles away when it goes off", warns the Soviet officer who instructs Gobinda about the atomic bomb. While that is certainly good advice, the surface detonation of a one hundred kiloton nuclear weapon would be easily survivable already at one third of that distance, and even closer if you knew of it in advance, and took minor precautions. For a weapon that size, the five-PSI air blast radius, where most residential buildings would be blown apart, "only" goes out to a radius of some twenty-four hundred meters (one and a half miles). The thermal radius, where you''d get third degree burns, if caught in the open, is about four thousand meters (two and a half miles). On the other hand, you had better stay upwind. This being a surface burst, you could get severely irradiated even around seventy-two kilometers (forty-five miles) away after a few hours, if caught in the main plume', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3edb87a9-0e1e-4bee-ace0-a2b9222edfba'), 'Thirteenth James Bond movie in the Eon Productions franchise, and the sixth to star Sir Roger Moore as Bond. With this movie, Moore equalled the number of Bond movies that Sir Sean Connery had made in the official franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('550575ac-ffd2-4970-8013-d487d3258c5a'), 'Another actor was hired in addition to Vijay Amritraj when there was a dispute with Actor''s Equity because Armitraj was not a member of the actor''s union. However, producer Albert R. Broccoli asked his friend Leonard Goldberg to arrange a guest appearance for Vijay on Fantasy Island (1977) in order to receive Screen Actors Guild membership and subsequent Equity approval', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c8f27806-7f15-474b-a392-666bdb37a656'), 'Although set in Argentina, due to the Falklands War, RAF Northholt, just up the road from Pinewood Studios was used for the pre-title sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6912a91c-811a-49b3-bd94-d910d60de623'), 'Richard Maibaum wanted Gert Fröbe to come back as Goldfinger''s twin brother. This is the last time he would try to use this idea, as Gert Fröbe died in 1988', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2d0de0ac-5cc6-44ce-881d-431c9f182da1'), 'The exterior of the Monsoon Palace was used for shooting. However, the interior of the palace is not inhabited. The interior shots were all done in a studio', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('045d0156-3855-46fb-8279-193d38afc86d'), 'The pre-title sequence has a scene where Bond flies a nimble homebuilt Bede BD-5J aircraft through an open hangar. Hollywood stunt pilot, and aerial coordinator, J.W. "Corkey" Fornof, who piloted the aircraft at more than one hundred fifty miles (two hundred forty-one kilometers) per hour, has said, "Today, few directors would consider such a stunt. They''d just whip it up in a computer lab." Having collapsible wings, the plane was shown hidden in a horse trailer. However, a dummy was used for this shot. Filming inside the hangar was achieved by attaching the aircraft to an old Jaguar with a steel pole, driving with the roof removed. The second unit was able to add enough obstacles, including people and objects inside the hangar, to hide the car and the pole, and make it look as though Sir Roger Moore was flying inside the base. For the explosion after the mini jet escapes, however, a miniature of the hangar was constructed and filmed up close. The exploding pieces of the hangar were only four inches in length', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a2bff8b5-ba3b-47e1-8af5-f241d31135f2'), 'As of 2026, this is the only movie in the official James Bond franchise to feature a woman''s name, or nickname, as the title of the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('de0cbf64-d33a-40cc-980d-b4c8e8d63273'), 'In the fight in Octopussy''s bedroom a henchman is thrown into the aquarium and a Blue Ringed Octopus attaches itself to the man''s face. This octopus is almost the same size as his head when this species of octopus is about the size of a golf ball', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0324efc9-da73-45a6-bc2c-7079a1cc98cd'), 'Kamal''s cheating at backgammon is taken from the novel "Moonraker", where Hugo Drax cheats at bridge, until Bond beats him at his own game. The line "Spend the money quickly, Mr. Bond", appears in the novel as well. It is also similar to the golf game in Goldfinger (1964)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ceb43538-6ae3-4132-8bde-20118b9ed486'), 'This is the only James Bond movie in the EON Productions official franchise that featured the famous West Berlin and East Berlin Cold War crossing point, "Checkpoint Charlie"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('004797da-909e-4d66-ba33-6bd54e0df549'), 'Footage of Sir Roger Moore and Kristina Wayborn in bed was shown in one of the trailers, but is not included in the final cut', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5591daab-27b8-4902-9ba9-9ca13e9d7060'), 'The wristwatch with a television monitor is known as the "Liquid Crystal TV Seiko," model T001-5019. Two physical watches were supplied to the production. The screen on the retail version available to consumers was black and white only', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('421d36c6-ce61-43e2-9b11-ee2ab2d85d61'), 'Graffitti written in green by an unknown person or Agent(s) on the Berlin Wall, seen after production wrapped, read: "007 WAS HERE OCTOPUSSY"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cb5ad8ec-51cc-4dd3-9f65-725edeac07a7'), 'Barbara Broccoli, producer Albert R. Broccoli''s daughter, was credited as executive assistant. She took over production of the EON James Bond film franchise after her father''s death, associated with executive producer Michael G. Wilson', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f78b1c2d-a38a-40e7-a0b5-578f2406d7cf'), 'A hand with a pair of eights in the card game Texas Hold ''Em is called an "Octopussy". A hand with a pair of eights is seen in Casino Royale (2006), in which this card game is a major feature', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Octopussy'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('b0aee8a4-4c4b-4376-ac3c-ed9c7cff0a71'), 'Sir Roger Moore was 57 at the time of this film''s release, making him the oldest actor to play James Bond, tied with David Niven in Casino Royale (1967). Moore was also the second-oldest, as he was 55 when Octopussy (1983) was released. The third-oldest are Moore, Sir Sean Connery, and Daniel Craig, who were all 53 when For Your Eyes Only (1981), Never Say Never Again (1983), and No Time to Die (2021) were released, respectively', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('10da833e-7749-47e4-a79a-7b58f4d1e2c1'), 'At the time of this movie''s release, Sir Sean Connery told the press, "Bond should be played by an actor 35, 33 years old. I''m too old. Roger''s too old, too!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('67281956-89aa-47d4-a564-db2504f59d86'), 'Although only appearing briefly, this movie is Dolph Lundgren''s first on-screen role, playing General Gogol''s KGB bodyguard Venz. He landed the position because he was dating Grace Jones at the time of filming, and was conveniently on-set when director John Glen realized he quickly needed someone to fill in as a simple gun-wielding bodyguard', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0f7e3b0-f9ba-4706-82dc-475779670227'), 'This film was Lois Maxwell''s final appearance as Miss Moneypenny. Apparently, after she was told that she would be retiring from the role, she thought she could become M as a promotion. Producer Albert R. Broccoli believed that audiences wouldn''t accept James Bond being given orders by a woman. M became a woman when Dame Judi Dench took on the role in GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d408fbb-285f-4bc1-8970-aa7a50d0f25e'), 'When Stacey comes out of the shack in Silicon Valley wearing a pair of coveralls, Bond comments "Pity you couldn''t find one that fits", and Stacey gives him a dirty look. Sir Roger Moore ad-libbed the line, and Tanya Roberts'' reaction was genuine. Roberts had refused to film the scene until the wardrobe department made her a pair of custom-fitted coveralls that would look flattering on her. Because she was so difficult to work with, director John Glen decided to leave it in', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1b67a38b-c939-4788-b9fe-c236b08cc08e'), 'The title song was written by John Barry and Duran Duran, and was sung by Duran Duran. It has been the only James Bond song to reach number one in the U.S. It stayed at the top position for two weeks out of its 17-week run on the charts. It entered the U.K. and U.S. charts on May 18, 1985, and it peaked at number two on the U.K. charts. The soundtrack album charted in the U.K. on June 22, 1985, where it went to number 81. In the U.S., the soundtrack album entered the charts on June 29, 1985, peaking at 38', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e7e9cbd-0c5a-4e27-a601-988f6459d89f'), 'In his DVD commentary, Sir Roger Moore said that of the seven Bond films in which he starred, this is his least favorite. He didn''t like the increased violence, and he felt he was getting too old for the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9560feaf-7576-4e60-8f38-dc9b7c2e4b37'), 'According to former CIA agent Tony Mendez (the subject of the spy movie Argo (2012)), after watching this movie, his superior at the CIA asked him if they have any facial recognition technology as depicted in this movie. When Mendez told him they did not, he ordered them to develop it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3efd04c8-6b82-4ce2-8347-1f6bfcc3a27c'), 'When Grace Jones (May Day) screams during the mine sequence, as sparks fly around her, her screams are for real. She did not know that electric cables around her would go off as a special effect for the scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('058cc670-0a23-40ab-b631-d104cac505d1'), 'Dianne Feinstein was the mayor of San Francisco at the time of filming. Because Sir Roger Moore was her favorite of the first three actors to play Bond, she granted all of the necessary permits to film in the city', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('be2eaec9-9aa8-4aba-9698-db866cb7464a'), 'Duran Duran was chosen to do the song after bassist John Taylor (a lifelong Bond fan) approached producer Albert R. Broccoli at a party, and somewhat drunkenly asked "When are you going to get someone decent to do one of your theme songs?"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6f0eaa96-b846-4877-9850-b50fdc1aabe7'), 'The Remy-Julienne stunt team from France did many of the stunts in this movie, but in the San Francisco segment, a scene in which Sir Roger Moore was supposed to be driving a fire truck, the stunt driver was too short to reach the pedals and properly operate the truck. There wasn''t much time to "rig" the truck, so Moore volunteered to drive it, quite expertly as noted by the local San Francisco Teamsters. Moore claims he was a lorry driver, among other things, before his acting paid the bills', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db7ae71a-a2dc-49b2-8c94-3f7882aa16f7'), 'Reportedly, Grace Jones had a black dildo with her during the bed scene between May Day and James Bond, according to Sir Roger Moore''s biography', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35290a99-d975-4c4d-ac70-94da36cc131a'), 'As it turns out, the age difference between Sir Roger Moore and his female co-stars was not as great as previously thought. Grace Jones and Tanya Roberts had long pegged their ages to 1952 and 1955 birthdates, respectively, but Jones and Roberts were actually born in 1948 and 1949 respectively', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2234a17e-d84e-4a7a-bf87-0190e605efbc'), 'In his memoir, Sir Roger Moore remembered that Grace Jones would play loud music in her dressing room, which meant he couldn''t get his afternoon nap. Moore admitted that after unsuccessfully asking Jones to turn the music down, he got so annoyed he threw a chair at the dressing room wall. As he dryly observed, this did not help set the mood for their yet-to-be-shot sex scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('84493617-fa4c-407d-b230-8fb48742f2f6'), 'This movie was intensely disliked by Sir Roger Moore, who was barely on speaking terms with Grace Jones during filming. He did not consider this to be a real 007 movie. Moore said, "I was horrified on the last Bond I did. Whole slews of sequences where Christopher Walken was machine-gunning hundreds of people. I said, ''That wasn''t Bond, those weren''t Bond films.'' It stopped being what they were all about. You didn''t dwell on the blood and the brains spewing all over the place."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('17342fd1-ae03-4ee0-b8dd-d99536f05320'), 'Christopher Walken became the first Academy Award-winning actor to star in a Bond movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('344ba425-42d2-435e-a543-9286d0aa9179'), 'With this being Lois Maxwell''s final appearance as Miss Moneypenny, it brings her total screen time across a 23-year span of James Bond movies to just one hour. She also delivered fewer than two hundred words', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b99fc698-75f1-41ee-96ce-9b5af5f05dfe'), 'When Bond is trapped underwater, he opened a tire valve, and breathes the air from the tire. MythBusters (2003) did a James Bond Special, and tried repeatedly to reproduce this action. It proved to be impossible to do. This act was also performed by either Jennifer Garner or a stunt double in Q & A (2002). Another report says it is possible though car tyres contain iron reinforcement strips which will oxidise over time, so there may be less oxygen in the car tyre than expected', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7859ad94-b1b9-4af7-8c01-6460bb9e5319'), 'The disclaimer, "Neither the name Zorin, nor any other name or character in this film, is meant to portray a real company or actual person" was added, after producers discovered a real company known as Zoran Ladicorbic Ltd. Their industry was fashion design', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8f4a809f-e4c1-4016-8733-d29d4f5150c3'), 'In a December 2007 interview, Sir Roger Moore said regarding this movie, "I was only about four hundred years too old for the part."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7fa4a9a8-c82a-43b4-b766-062e9165fa29'), 'After producer Albert R. Broccoli told Lois Maxwell (Miss Moneypenny) that she would not return for the next Bond movie, he commented that they were the only two people from Dr. No (1962) who were still working on the franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f6bacb49-4c9d-4123-b8f8-996c778667ed'), 'The selection of Duran Duran to perform the theme song was seen as an attempt to help market this movie (and potential future James Bond movies) towards a younger audience, specifically the "MTV generation"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f03de0b3-be84-4a8f-bb30-a73bbf67a051'), 'David Bowie was offered the part of Max Zorin. He turned down the role, in favor of one in Labyrinth (1986). Bowie later explained that he thought this movie''s script was too "terrible" and "workmanlike" to spend much time working on, and he told the producers what he thought of it. He also said that his directness wasn''t received very well by them. In 2003, he admitted that he didn''t like the Bond movies, and hadn''t seen one since the Connery era', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab779d6f-012f-41b7-99f7-723b758b191e'), 'At "A Night with Sir Roger Moore" in Dublin, Ireland on November 20, 2016, Sir Roger Moore was asked who would win in a fight with Grace Jones. Moore paused and remained silent for several seconds before saying, "My mother once said if you have nothing good to say about someone, then say nothing at all." Jones, on the other hand, recalled working with Moore as enjoyable and that he was one of her favorite co-stars. She claimed their lack of rapport was due to her desire to ''stay in character,'' as she was meant to hate Bond. In her book, "I''ll Never Write My Memoirs" [2015], she explains she deliberately stayed in character, which ''creeped'' Moore, but that he was helpful to her throughout', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('715d2a4f-6e82-4300-a70a-3cddefb246f8'), 'Lois Maxwell suggested that Miss Moneypenny be killed off', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('30b9d340-e3ca-4659-b1b1-556e75f5099b'), 'The effect of splitting the Renault in half was achieved by disabling an electromagnet used to hold the front and rear sections of the car together. The car was equipped with a small fuel tank in the front section. Because the "half car" did not have a muffler, it was quite loud', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e9fe905-635e-4dd2-ad34-d6a987d40697'), 'The role of Russian Agent Pola Ivanova was originally meant to be the character Anya Amasova, the female lead from The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). When Barbara Bach declined to reprise her role, the new character of Pola Ivanova was created, and was cast with Fiona Fullerton', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('172ad4b9-b7ff-41cc-9557-94b5ded0f911'), 'This movie is often credited with helping to spark the interest in snowboarding, due to its use in the pre-credits opening action snow sequence. The snowboarding stunts were performed by Thomas Sims, American inventor of the snowboard. A cover version of The Beach Boys song "California Girls" (performed by Beach Boys associate Adrian Baker) can be briefly heard as an in-joke, when James Bond snowboards. The song does not feature on the soundtrack album', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0498028c-0bcc-4052-a2f7-cf4d0422f6e1'), 'Aside from using a shotgun loaded with rock salt, James Bond doesn''t actually shoot anyone in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('843e69dc-366f-4435-a872-b725d018229a'), 'Because of the unprecedented level of cooperation from the San Francisco authorities, producer Albert R. Broccoli insisted that the premiere take place in the city. It was held at the Palace of Fine Arts, and was the franchise''s first world premiere to be in the U.S', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1d54f75a-b8b8-47b2-a9fa-0e1e5ba8eb0c'), 'In the opening sequence in Siberia, when the Russian soldier is left dangling from a precipice, amongst his garbled words, can be heard "Roger Moore!"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1750a206-2065-41b5-9619-aafcd8bf08c0'), 'Tanya Roberts had high hopes that this would be her big break, telling reporters at the time: "Kim Basinger got The Natural (1984) after making a James Bond movie. The same kind of thing could happen to me." Unfortunately, despite the global attention that comes with every Bond release, it did nothing to boost her career, and she did not appear in a widely released theatrical motion picture ever again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2d1f261f-454b-4db3-805c-22978555b40a'), 'First theatrical movie of Alison Doody, who turned eighteen during filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0730f5f2-f018-4594-ad6f-809cb0ed0774'), 'Barbara Broccoli had to collect Grace Jones every morning, because Jones didn''t enjoy early morning starts. She learned to be very diplomatic with Jones in the car ride to the studio', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('af362606-f1a8-49c3-85c1-00156bb28a0e'), 'There was much criticism that Sir Roger Moore''s stunt doubles were too obvious in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b3ee3568-10f5-4429-9a43-6f94daf210a6'), 'In his 2008 autobiography "My Word Is My Bond", Sir Roger Moore admitted he felt at the time that he was too old to play James Bond in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a538f5f-619e-46c4-a82e-6b204cfb2f28'), 'The opening sequence of this movie was the first time James Bond was depicted on a mission inside Russia. Specifically, it was the snow-capped region of Siberia (which was filmed in Iceland)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d9c91545-4d15-46a0-9527-bd72d3058a4a'), 'Sir Roger Moore had some cosmetic surgery before filming began', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('33ae8a02-fa1d-44de-8bbc-82403afd385c'), 'Timothy Dalton was considered to step in as James Bond, if Sir Roger Moore decided not to return. He ended up being cast as Bond in the next two films: The Living Daylights (1987) and Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('faf1842a-830a-4798-bb6d-1cf3b3480403'), 'This is the only James Bond movie to have the title from an Ian Fleming work be amended or changed in some way. The source title which is from the "For Your Eyes Only" collection of short stories was called "From a View to a Kill". This was also this movie''s working title, as seen in the end credits of Octopussy (1983), but the word "From" was dropped before filming began in May 1984', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d15c6191-b1ce-4a0d-ad2d-0ab5e1d11aae'), 'Dr. Carl Mortner, a.k.a. Hans Glaub (Willoughby Gray), was modelled after Josef Mengele, the infamous Nazi doctor who performed unethical and sadistic experiments on Jewish prisoners in Auschwitz during World War II', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2a2fe1ed-ec97-4167-a6cb-829292bbc0d5'), 'Just before the jump off the Eiffel Tower stunt was to be undertaken, two thrill-seeking members of the public made an unauthorized jump off Paris''s famous landmark. It has long been a dare, lark and thrill for people to jump off famous structures without permission. The first of this movie''s jumps was so successful that the second jump was cancelled, thereby eliminating any further risk, cost or time. However, as mentioned in Inside ''A View to a Kill'' (2000), two of the crew, including Don "Tweet" Caltvedt, allegedly went and made an unauthorized jump, as they were apparently very disappointed that they didn''t get to jump off the Eiffel Tower. The unauthorized stunt jump cost them their jobs, as it jeopardized the remaining filming of the shoot in the French capital', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3cde8eac-3384-43f4-8c44-44c13ce0a0d6'), 'Filming was delayed when the "007 Stage" at Pinewood Studios burned down on June 27, 1984, during production of Legend (1985). It was completely rebuilt in less than four months, and renamed "The Albert R. Broccoli 007 Stage". Coincidentally, the title song of the movie contained the lyric "Dance into the fire". The stage burned down again in July 2006 just after filming had been completed on Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b18fadfa-da01-478a-81c1-2b89f6e2dada'), 'The description of Max Zorin in the script was based on Sting, and written with David Bowie in mind, but he turned this movie down', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9369f923-627d-4d3c-877f-1d5d612e6e85'), 'Tanya Roberts was not only the last leading Bond woman of the Moore era but was also the first to pass away. Roberts died on 4 January 2021 at age 71', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7aa8d0c8-008a-485d-8f95-cf353c70e42b'), 'The role of Max Zorin was offered to Rutger Hauer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('20062fb1-aaaa-4169-a7d7-b2c082c0d285'), 'This is the last movie in the franchise on which long-time stuntman Bob Simmons worked and his next-to-last project ever. He died in 1987', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3a5f4ed5-06d9-4386-8b7d-ff48fafbd798'), 'Bond beds four women in this movie, which is a tie for the most (at time of release) with Never Say Never Again (1983)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b7759bcd-3b2a-4acf-bd43-b34bd5cd1892'), 'None of the principal cast ever went to Iceland for this movie, not even Sir Roger Moore', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2dedf7b3-2f1c-484a-bd9e-abc535199144'), 'The idea to set the story in California''s Silicon Valley was a concept conceived by producer and co-writer Michael G. Wilson. In the first draft, Zorin wanted to destroy Silicon Valley by changing the course of Halley''s Comet, but it was later decided that this plot was not believable', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('970ddf09-4c24-49ec-b85f-da3f5fb51d1d'), 'Grace Jones recalled in her autobiography that while looping the dialogue in post-production, her clothes kept making rustling noises. So she stripped off, and carried on while naked', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0e099590-21f8-4161-a46f-6eb3778d0b06'), 'Patrick Macnee had spoken very critically about the James Bond film franchise. He said he had preferred Ian Fleming''s original James Bond novels compared to the movies. Macnee took his part largely as an opportunity to work again with Sir Roger Moore, who was a good friend of his. The pair worked on "The Sea Wolves (1980)" and "Sherlock Holmes in New York (1976)."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bb640971-5a24-4d0c-a290-70e61dda1c41'), 'Maryam d''Abo screentested for the role of Pola Ivanova, but was ultimately rejected, because she was too young for the part. She appeared briefly in White Nights (1985), where she played the French girlfriend of Mikhail Baryshnikov. She earned a major place in the James Bond universe, when she starred as 007''s main love interest in The Living Daylights (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('59935217-f926-441a-af52-b97b7acd9326'), 'As reported by "Variety" on November 26, 1985, while this movie was still in release in some territories, Sir Roger Moore officially had advised producer Albert R. Broccoli that he would be retiring from the role of James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6adc4136-785b-4608-8c31-59a17cfb8641'), 'Sir Roger Moore became good friends with San Francisco Mayor Dianne Feinstein and her husband after their support in helping to make this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a14669d4-3733-4b75-98d8-547c43775561'), 'This is the only James Bond movie where the famous spy genre catchphrase "Nobody ever leaves the K.G.B." is heard. It is said by General Gogol (Walter Gotell)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5a8d45ed-9446-4bf4-8780-d99ad7f213cf'), 'Of the five films in the series he personally directed, John Glen pronounced A View to a Kill (1985) as the one with the most beautiful Bond girl - Tanya Roberts (Stacey Sutton)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1014b09-7c90-41f5-b6ed-05318db5f2c6'), 'The 1962 silver Rolls-Royce Silver Cloud II seen in this movie was owned by producer Albert R. Broccoli, who lent it to the production. Its license plate number in this movie was 354 HYK. A duplicate model without an engine was used when Zorin and May Day push it into the lake', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d38c37f2-7912-4b58-ac9d-fac05b075d43'), 'The story is considered a re-working of much of the story structure of the earlier James Bond movie Goldfinger (1964). The two movies share many story elements', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('956150e3-feaf-4859-9635-faa829a99069'), 'According to the James Bond encyclopedia by John Cork and Collin Stutz, Felix Leiter was originally going to be Bond''s contact in San Francisco. However, owing to Chinatown being such a prominent part of the city, David Yip was cast as Chuck Lee instead', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f3d31bd3-da8d-4069-b3d4-9fe38b399cf2'), 'Third official Bond movie to not state the title of the next Bond movie during the ending credits. Neither Dr. No (1962) nor Thunderball (1965) stated the next movie at the end of their credits either', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4a8c6235-73eb-4593-bb79-3bb97d78d7fb'), 'The San Francisco cable cars seen in this movie are road vehicles. At the time of filming, the entire system was being overhauled, meaning the bus-like vehicles had to be used instead. (This is evident during the fire truck chase, where the vehicles have been placed over the rails to give the real effect, but clearly have tires, and larger wheels). The cable cars, unlike in this movie, do not run to Fisherman''s Wharf', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('38c4339f-8754-436a-a7fe-5073144b7489'), 'Stacy Sutton''s villa mansion, Whitewood House, was played by Oakland California''s Dunsmuir House', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'A View To A Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('db7658e8-82ef-4754-8519-b97e70bd92de'), 'Timothy Dalton was originally considered for the role of James Bond in the late 1960s, after Sean Connery left the role, following You Only Live Twice (1967). Dalton was screen-tested by Albert R. Broccoli for On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), but he turned down the part, as he thought he was too young. He was also considered for Diamonds Are Forever (1971), but turned it down again, still feeling he was too young. He was considered again for the role in For Your Eyes Only (1981), when for a while, it was unclear whether Roger Moore would return. However, Dalton declined at that time, as there was no script. Dalton was offered the role again in 1983 for Octopussy (1983), and yet again in 1985 for A View to a Kill (1985), but had to decline the role both times due to previous commitments. Dalton was not even the first choice to play Bond in this film, as Pierce Brosnan was originally slated to star in early development before being let go by the producers at the last minute to finish his television commitments. With Brosnan temporarily out of the picture, Dalton was once again offered the role and this time he accepted', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6a5f76b2-ffa3-4aaa-9db7-43be62a40fa3'), 'The casting of Frederick Warder and Glyn Baker as 004 and 002 was intentional, due to their resemblance to George Lazenby and Roger Moore, respectively. For the movie''s opening scene, the writers wanted to toy with the audience''s expectations of which of the 00 agents was Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('70d39f8c-5318-43a5-959f-3173e04e3c58'), 'This was the last Bond film to be scored by John Barry', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d12262d-efc7-44fd-b3a9-a06e97d9672f'), 'Timothy Dalton was originally unavailable to play Bond, and Pierce Brosnan was then chosen to play 007 in 1986, and was given the script to this movie. Although he was contracted to Remington Steele (1982) for seven seasons, NBC decided to cancel the show at the end of the fourth season, which meant that Brosnan was free to play James Bond in this movie the following year. However, shortly after the end of the fourth season, NBC had second thoughts about cancelling "Remington Steele", and subsequently approached the Bond producers directly in an attempt to strike a deal that would allow Brosnan to play James Bond and Remington Steele the following year. NBC also offered to completely reschedule the shooting of Remington Steele to ensure that there were no scheduling conflicts. But eventually, Albert R. Broccoli famously told NBC that "James Bond will not be Remington Steele, and Remington Steele will not be James Bond." Accordingly, Brosnan would only play Bond if the show remained cancelled. NBC had a sixty day deadline to revoke their decision to cancel the series, and at 6:30 p.m. on the sixtieth day of the deadline, Brosnan learned that NBC decided to make a fifth season. The Bond producers subsequently prevented Brosnan from becoming the next James Bond. Subsequently, the role went to Timothy Dalton, who was now finally available. NBC went on to make only six episodes of the fifth season of Remington Steele before finally cancelling the show for good', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d14cfe03-d6ba-450c-b634-721bdb68e12e'), 'A stuntman was originally going to play the role of 004, the man whose rope is cut by the Russian assassin in Gibraltar at the beginning, but after watching rushes, director John Glen decided that they needed a real actor for the part, and it was given to another actor. At the time, this actor was out of work and staying home taking care of his baby while his wife was away on business. Upon getting the call, he left the baby with a neighbor, left his wife a note telling her he''d gone to be in a James Bond movie, and caught the next plane to Gibraltar to start filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7833e0a6-5597-41af-9ff9-dd5969c21ee9'), 'At one point, the film was intended to be a prequel. The film would end with Bond being given his mission for Dr. No (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('03f37307-4033-44e1-b47a-1e570d32428f'), 'This was the last James Bond film to use an original Ian Fleming title until Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c4750649-0b89-44dc-98fe-66c54356875a'), 'The macaw in the safe house kitchen is the same one from For Your Eyes Only (1981)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('96d2ff9a-7511-43a3-b579-2e36e5cdcb4e'), 'The rocket fired from the ghetto blaster in Q''s lab in the movie was actually a special effect activated off-screen by King Charles III (then Prince Charles) who was touring the studio at the time of filming with then wife Princess Diana. The effects crew offered to allow His Royal Highness to activate the rocket that was used in the final cut of the film. The Royal visit also instigated the famous footage and photograph of the Princess of Wales hitting her husband over the head with a breakaway bottle, apparently instigated by Jeroen Krabbé', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a63a402-4842-4d55-ab72-c0e32ad783f8'), 'This was the first official James Bond film not to feature Lois Maxwell as Miss Moneypenny, being the first film in the franchise to feature another actress, Caroline Bliss, in this role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e22c667-9b10-4874-80bb-91c42d1e08e3'), 'The cello case chase sequence down the snow took three days to shoot. The case was specially made of fibreglass, and fitted with control handles on the sides and skis underneath. Firecrackers were set in the snow to simulate gunfire and during filming, the case would tend to topple over as Timothy Dalton was heavier than Maryam d''Abo. The sequence was the brainchild of John Glen who had to convince colleagues Richard Maibaum, Michael G. Wilson, and Albert R. Broccoli. He did this by hopping into an actual orchestral cello case himself', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('62d7d506-03c1-4d39-ac16-1059e79e9509'), 'The name of the gas pipeline which crossed from Czechslovakia to Austria was the Trans Siberian Pipeline. The gas pipeline vehicle used for Koskov''s defection escape is an actual piece of equipment known as a Scouring Pig. It is used to check and clean the natural gas pipeline between Western Europe and Russia. The apparatus was adapted though for the movie so as to be able to carry a person', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3c35aa52-2cb8-473f-9ce9-9628d6d3b944'), 'Brad Whitaker''s personal war museum included busts and statues of himself dressed up as the following leaders of military history: Alexander the Great, Genghis Khan, Attila the Hun, Adolf Hitler, Napoléon Bonaparte, the Duke of Wellington, Oliver Cromwell and Julius Caesar', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6cf82081-a4a3-484a-a355-5b3d36e4a601'), 'Sam Neill auditioned for James Bond. Michael G. Wilson, John Glen, Dana Broccoli, and Barbara Broccoli were all impressed with his screentest, but Albert R. Broccoli wasn''t sold on him. Neill was the second New Zealander considered to play Bond, after David Warbeck for For Your Eyes Only (1981). Neill later revealed that he hated the audition and was relieved he didn''t get the role, explaining in his memoir that later he met Roger Moore who told him, "You should have been Bond!" to which Neill respectfully disagreed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eea17a96-a8a6-47fc-8f66-3cda8e0e0047'), 'Morten Harket, the lead singer of pop group a-ha (who performed the title song), was offered a small role as a bad guy in the movie. He turned down the offer, due to extensive touring in Japan. He also felt that they wanted to cast him, due to his popularity, rather than his acting. He is also the only person to perform lead vocals on a Bond theme song who is neither American or British', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8942b66-1824-4013-9e0b-ce9b065fa089'), 'The first time James Bond drives an Aston Martin since On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fd4547a7-8e9c-4076-8102-78ddcb100948'), 'Features the only deliberate nude scenes in the James Bond film franchise, outside of opening titles. They are when two men have their shower facility torn out from over them in Afghanistan, and when Pushkin''s girlfriend''s top is torn off in a hotel room', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('602cbba9-720e-4a0d-96eb-5ca61275723e'), 'The medevac helicopter, a Bell UH-1 Huey (registration G-HUEY), was originally used by the Argentine Army. It was captured by the British during the Falkland Islands War, and used as a support aircraft until being sold to the private sector', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4f19e710-27d2-469c-afca-1d8090cefeb9'), 'This was the first Bond film to feature a different song over the closing credits. It was called "If There Was a Man" and was performed by The Pretenders who sang two songs for the movie, the other being "Where Has Everybody Gone?". The group were originally considered for the title song but, following the huge success of Duran Duran''s song A View to a Kill (1985), it was decided to go with a trendier group. Chrissie Hynde of the The Pretenders also has sung a cover version of the Bond song Live and Let Die (1973) which can be heard on the David Arnold Bond song compilation album, "Shaken and Stirred: the David Arnold James Bond Project"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('196d6ec5-0e6d-447b-9a1a-09c5b28c9a76'), 'Sean Bean was considered to take over as James Bond. He would later play the villain Alec Trevelyan in GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c1b1e963-4f23-4907-bbf6-2a8f11688561'), 'This was originally proposed as a restart the Bond franchise, but the idea was dropped. It was taken up again with Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9300ddf0-5dde-4c31-a6e1-6cb1102beff0'), 'A-ha and John Barry did not collaborate well, resulting in two versions of the theme song. Barry''s film mix is heard on the soundtrack (and on a-ha''s later greatest hits album Headlines and Deadlines). The version preferred by the band can be heard on the 1988 a-ha album Stay on These Roads. However, in 2006, a-ha complimented Barry''s contributions: "I loved the stuff he added to the track, I mean it gave it this really cool string arrangement. That''s when, for me, it started to sound like a Bond thing."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e1b54993-e9e8-480e-888a-35d080c49eb0'), 'Walter Gotell''s last Bond film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cd02d2eb-fd7e-48a7-95eb-c49d37b28edb'), 'Contrary to popular belief, the film was never written with Roger Moore in mind. At first, screenwriters Richard Maibaum and Michael G. Wilson wrote several treatments, in which a twenty-something James Bond teams up with a senior agent named Burton Trevor on a mission to infiltrate the jungle compound of a Chinese warlord named Kwang. Trevor would die helping Bond escape, Bond would hunt down and kill Kwang, and subsequently be promoted to the Double-0 section, taking Trevor''s old number "007". After two full-length treatments, producer Albert R. Broccoli vetoed the idea, arguing that audiences were more interested in who James Bond is rather than who he was. The Bond origin idea was (partially) resurrected for Casino Royale (2006), in which Bond is shown shortly after being promoted to Double-0', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('baff7f45-eae2-4ee8-95cf-167121c78bae'), 'The character of Pushkin was originally to have been General Gogol, a recurring character from The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). Pushkin is chief of the KGB, the same position Gogol held in previous appearances. A new character was created after Walter Gotell fell ill, and Albert R. Broccoli could not get him insured. Gotell has said Broccoli even offered to pay an extensive sum personally, but still could not get coverage. Pushkin''s girlfriend was likewise supposed to be the secretary seen romancing Gogol in several films. Gotell was able to film a cameo as Gogol (now a member of the Soviet foreign office) for the end of the movie, marking that character''s final appearance', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cdca6d39-23a3-452c-b731-d7b04d381545'), 'This is the first time James Bond had been seen smoking since The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), this time smoking cigarettes for the first time since On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d97b021f-710d-4034-9c7f-26b96a630859'), 'For a while, General Pushkin (John Rhys-Davies) was intended to return in Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b5373d88-0683-43ec-abb7-00e12ce9eee9'), 'An ending, similar to the one that featured a parody of Margaret Thatcher and Denis Thatcher in For Your Eyes Only (1981), was originally intended for the movie. It was to include, instead, a parody of King Charles III and Princess Diana. However, the idea was scrapped', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('88b2b7f7-9057-4b16-bca0-a46b83d74939'), 'The ferris wheel on which Bond takes Kara is the same one from The Third Man (1949). John Glen''s first job was on the film, in the visual and sound editorial department. Fellow 007 director Guy Hamilton also worked on the film as an assistant director, and Bernard Lee, Robert Brown, and Geoffrey Keen had parts in the film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('221f1aee-45f1-4bb6-8c03-b0cfcdf3f324'), 'A Hercules is unable to taxi with its ramp lowered to the ground. During the escape scene in Afganistan, the production team built the rear end of a Hercules on the back of a large furniture truck, hence the different ramp design, and narrower fuselage when Kara drives in. It was not a C-123 in these scenes, as previously suspected', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0945d0a5-5df1-4af1-ac8e-1004b904393b'), 'Maryam d''Abo had previously screen-tested for the role of Pola Ivanova in A View to a Kill (1985). She didn''t get the part but director John Glen saw something in her. Maryam went for another test before the production with Albert R. Broccoli and Glen watching. After shooting an unproduced film in Germany, her scenes were sent to United Artists who recommended her to the Broccoli family. She had cut her hair and encountered Barbara Broccoli in a health club who was surprised with her new look. On Barbara''s recommendation, the United Artists office and John Glen wanting to her her again, she returned to Pinewood and received the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9604a184-6024-4b04-b409-f9f3262e1219'), 'For a brief time, when it was presumed Roger Moore would return for one more film, one of the main ideas floated around by the screenwriters was to have Bond battle an evil villainess, to be played by Bette Davis. This idea was quickly scrapped when the screenwriters learned Moore would not return for another Bond film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a1874a02-1d1e-4fa0-ace7-5cff56c46568'), 'During World War II, SMERSH (Smiert Spionam, death to spies) was a branch of the NKVD (later KGB), the Soviet Secret Police. The Bond movies, seeking to improve Anglo-Russian relations, eliminate all references to SMERSH, except for a one-liner in From Russia with Love (1963), and the subplot of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('46e1f43c-94f8-495b-a6f4-e1e6d0eeb20b'), 'Kara Milovy (Maryam d''Abo) is the last "main" Bond girl to be blonde until Spectre (2015). All leading Bond girls in the other films in the interim were brunettes or redheads', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3dc1e92d-79e7-40d8-a31b-836b59c7c3b0'), 'Maryam d''Abo posed nude for Playboy magazine in September 1987 to promote the film, but later regretted it because she felt the poses were too "pedestrian."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4e9fbb98-1da8-40ef-ad27-aa605ec6a6f2'), 'The "Living Daylights" short story, the third short story in Ian Fleming''s "Octopussy and the Living Daylights" collection is briefly referenced at the start of Octopussy (1983). This is when a British agent is seen trying to escape from East to West Germany. The equivalent sequence in this movie is set in Czechoslovakia and Austria', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a6a8bc75-8137-408f-bdc9-f96013c434d9'), 'Was released in the 25th anniversary year of the James Bond films. To mark the occasion, a television special Happy Anniversary 007: 25 Years of James Bond (1987) was produced as part of the promotional campaign for this film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('10f623da-c76e-4d4e-ab65-475f65d69ea1'), 'With this film, the James Bond franchise broke $2 billion at the global box office. It was the first film series to reach the milestone', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('05be0e19-66c5-45a1-b744-d2fd2f67862b'), 'Was the first James Bond film since Moonraker (1979) not to have its title announced during the closing end credits of the previous film. That was A View to a Kill (1985) and no Bond film has done so since', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('50f78d24-7cc0-4ff1-a6e3-fa43121c1dea'), 'The Red Cross organization in the USA, UK, and Canada protested against the use of the Red Cross emblem and symbol in the movie. It can be seen on a helicopter during the escape from the Blayden House siege, and later in the film on sacks containing opium. They maintained that its use in the film was inappropriate, and unauthorized. Interestingly, helicopters showing a Red Cross logo can be seen in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('32959bbb-1390-4255-bb2d-713d2820f593'), 'Nadim Sawalha (Tangier Chief of Police) played Aziz Fekkesh in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). Peter Porteous (Gasworks Supervisor) was the jewel forger Lenkin in Octopussy (1983). Joe Don Baker (Brad Whitaker) later played helpful CIA agent Jack Wade in GoldenEye (1995) and Tomorrow Never Dies (1997)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6025c6e0-cb12-4fc3-a349-d3df5ed47d0f'), 'The four-engine Lockheed Hercules C-130 plane was played by the smaller two-engine C-123 Provider plane. This was because it was more cost-efficient to rent the smaller plane. A model of the C-130 was used by special effects expert John Richardson for flying shots, while close-ups of actors, such as the net fight, utilized the C-123, where one can actually see that it had two engines, and not four', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eb7b5233-e282-492f-adae-43c7f39aa9e1'), 'The Land Rover in the opening sequence was driven by an RAF Fitter who was based at the radar installation at the top of the rock. He volunteered to drive after the stunt driver refused to drive the tight roads on the Ministry of Defence owned roads. The Fitter drove the roads several times a day and was very comfortable driving them at speed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9f039fca-39ac-4d80-a2a9-4a2bcf937456'), 'Maryam d''Abo mimed the pieces of music that she played on the cello, learning from composer John Barry. The strings were coated with with dry soap so that the sound couldn''t be heard. Maryam also took horseback riding lessons for the Afghanistan scenes. Filming the cello case scenes down the mountain took much control since Timothy Dalton was heavier than her', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ca58404c-0500-45af-a617-d5e36387e79b'), 'Originally, the Pet Shop Boys were asked to compose the soundtrack, but backed down when they learned that they would not provide a complete soundtrack, but merely the opening theme song', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5ca19c22-735a-429e-a498-e927a208a9fc'), 'Maryam d''Abo was originally hired only to appear in screen tests opposite actors testing for the role of James Bond. When she was cast, Pierce Brosnan was still set to be the new James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('42e752e0-f61f-4e07-9669-ebfcf22add4e'), 'General Gogol is credited in the closing credits as "General Anatol Gogol", even though in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), M called him by his first name, "Alexis"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a5e822ee-7238-4789-a0fe-4d2a51fc472d'), 'General Pushkin''s surname is a nod to the Russian poet and novelist Aleksandr Pushkin, just as General Gogol''s name was a nod to the Ukrainian novelist Nikolay Gogol', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80601ce3-eff2-41a6-9995-208bab35fee1'), 'As a "thank you" for supporting the production by loaning cars, Aston Martin chairman Victor Gauntlett was offered a small role as a KGB colonel, but did not have the time to play the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('538e757b-91f4-4ed8-954f-8dc19666ddaf'), 'At the start of the film, a Land Rover flies off the cliff edge in Gibraltar. The point at which the Land Rover flies off the cliff was filmed on Beachy Head, near the town of Eastbourne, England', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7e21f5da-836c-4004-ad30-ce73c5b02d63'), 'Two different Aston Martin models were used for filming, a V8 Volante convertible, and later for the Czechoslovakia scenes, a hard-top non-Volante V8 Saloon, badged to look like the Volante', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8cacd2fe-cbce-4cab-83ad-d5ec17e85af4'), 'Aerial stuntmen B.J. Worth and Jake Lombard performed the pre-credits parachute jump. The terrain and wind were unfavorable. Consideration was given to the stunt being done using cranes, but Worth stuck to skydiving, and completed the scenes in a day', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bbad48e3-520b-42da-a350-21e5614baffd'), 'The woman who appeared in a white negligee in one of the movie''s main posters was American model Kathy Karges. She was allegedly paid $600 for this modelling job. This poster caused some controversy, because it seemed to evoke violence against women, as the poster girl appeared at the end of a gun barrel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2d5ad7b2-d363-4e54-b2c0-a60d3c3f8427'), 'Some unedited footage was stolen, and videos were sold as if they were the completed movie. Albert R. Broccoli and the other producers then released a poster explaining that this copy of the movie was unfinished, and had no soundtrack or special effects at all, saying that the only way to see the real movie was going to the cinema', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bbc5c261-ad47-4557-9d24-860f136ed9ff'), 'Naturally, with a movie that features orchestras and cellos, this Bond film features numerous pieces of classical music: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart''s 40th Symphony in G minor (1st movement) is heard being played at the Bratislava Conservatoire during the defection sequence. Aleksandr Borodin''s String Quartet No. 2 in D major (3rd movement) is heard the second time James Bond is in the audience hearing Kara perform at the Bratislava Conservatoire. When Bond and Kara arrive in Vienna, they hear Johann Strauss''s Wine, Women, and Song Waltz. The opera they hear in Vienna is Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart''s Il Nozze di Figaro (act 2). Kara practices Antonín Dvorák''s Cello Concerto as Bond returns to the hotel room. At the film''s end, Kara is playing Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky''s Rococo Variations', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('018ec90e-3230-4316-b9e9-2a963e72e423'), 'Timothy Dalton was officially announced as the new James Bond, and to appear in this movie, on August 7th, 1986', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a6b84add-c740-4991-adbe-ab4dc0657adf'), 'In 1986, Madonna reportedly declined a one million dollar deal to sing the theme song of this movie. She would eventually sing the theme song to Die Another Day (2002)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f09f279f-680c-40ad-af0e-8de2029b675f'), 'Timothy Dalton says the famous "Bond. James Bond" during the pre-title sequence, This is the third time Bond has done this before the opening titles, after On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) and Diamonds Are Forever (1971)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('124ce325-28ab-42f7-b999-1bccdbc399c8'), 'Robert Bathurst auditioned for the role of James Bond after being persuaded by a casting director. He later admitted in an interview that his "ludicrous audition" was an "arm-twisting exercise", as the producers still wanted Timothy Dalton', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('06d40bbc-7511-42f7-a660-6df1f55a4030'), 'Trial runs of the stunt with the Land Rover, during which Bond escapes by parachute from the tumbling vehicle, were filmed in the Mojave Desert, although the final cut of the film uses a shot achieved using a dummy', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d67fda4a-5c74-43bf-9a4d-cad2eebc7492'), 'The plot relating to the embezzlement of Soviet funds by Soviet official General Georgi Koskov contains story elements used by Ian Fleming in the James Bond novel and film versions of "Casino Royale"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('44e366ea-e838-4b06-86cf-d572f31adb66'), 'In the opening scene in Gibraltar, real military installations were used. These included a Ministry of Defence road not open to the public', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('50b67083-08f1-4b83-985a-916b1dc1dbb4'), 'The roller coaster Kara and James ride is a Pinifari Zyklon Z47 named Hochbahn. It operated at Prater Park from 1979 to 2006', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dbb6890a-b10e-4b8f-862a-dcccea5cd9e2'), 'During the three days it took to film their fight sequence, Bill Weston fractured a finger, and Andreas Wisniewski knocked him out once', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('84a9eb19-f46f-4f1f-b8c3-25e23db6cd82'), 'Lee Van Cleef was considered for the role of Brad Whitaker', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('798bd0d8-4f0d-4d01-bfb8-f8b57302bef5'), 'Eight years before he was cast as Bond, Timothy Dalton played a millionaire playboy named Damien Roth in Fallen Angel (1979). His character was described by John Bosley (David Doyle) as being "almost James Bond-ian."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e64a670-f3aa-4b96-af4d-956153c8b828'), 'This was the first of Timothy Dalton''s two appearances as James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b34e97b8-933d-43d8-badb-8afd97a62adf'), 'Timothy Dalton and Walter Gotell would work together again on an episode of Tales from the Crypt (1989) some years later. Maryam d''Abo would also appear on the series, but in an unrelated episode', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6d7689c3-5cfd-427c-be7b-d1bc2960caf9'), 'Necros is the Greek word for death', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The Living Daylights'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('22101068-f1b0-4126-819b-ea90d1a977a0'), 'In an interview during filming in September 1988, Timothy Dalton denied media claims that his Bond was not allowed to have as much sex due to the AIDS epidemic being a major concern at the time. However, in a 2007 interview, he admitted that this was true', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f74e045-e361-471f-813e-4ba950421c0b'), 'Desmond Llewelyn later noted that this was the first time that he''d made any real money out of the Bond films', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c811b2d9-8723-483c-af09-cdd567b8e37e'), 'In an interview, Timothy Dalton stated that his Bond was a much darker, grittier incarnation than the ones before him because he wanted to go back to the Ian Fleming novels, and capture the essence and the spirit of that character. In contrast to the movies, which typically depicted Bond as suave, charming, witty and relying on gadgets, the books described him as much less glamorous and often employing brutal force to obtain his goals. Although reception of the change was mixed at the time, when the series successfully repeated the concept for Daniel Craig''s Bond movies, it retrospectively led to a bit more appreciation for Dalton''s style of Bond as well', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7cd56b18-7135-42a5-b3da-06ec785659ab'), 'Robert Davi was taken by several thugs, while on vacation in South America, to an actual drug lord. The man enjoyed his portrayal of a drug lord', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bfa75f5d-9611-4136-a3c4-e0166d486147'), 'Of all of the Bond films, this one has the largest role for Desmond Llewelyn as Q', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a8015a8d-7ac8-43d5-a35e-1f1a84b2b0f5'), 'It is widely and incorrectly rumored that this was Timothy Dalton''s last James Bond film due it being financially disappointing. In reality, Dalton was to star in a third James Bond film after this one, titled "Property of a Lady", written by Michael G. Wilson and Alfonse Ruggiero Jr. and set to start shooting in 1990, with pre-production work having begun in May of that year. However legal issues with MGM beginning that year created long delays which eventually led Dalton to announce his retirement from the role in 1994, a year after his initial contract expired, paving the way for Pierce Brosnan''s casting in GoldenEye (1995). Had the film been made, it would have been set in Scotland, Tokyo, and Hong Kong, and would have involved nanotechnology. While no director was ever officially attached, John Landis, Ted Kotcheff and John Byrum were all under consideration', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('06e4987d-0d91-41f7-8d17-e5f1fc5761f5'), 'At 21 years old, Benicio Del Toro is the youngest actor to play a villain in a James Bond film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b32d9167-421e-4bac-ad72-b9dda390e28d'), 'Budget restraints were imposed, as the producers were still paying interest on the overspending of Moonraker (1979)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('88e354b2-d8a7-4098-85ab-a51d968a9823'), 'Last James Bond film for six years. In August 1990, director John Glen left EON Productions. Thirteen-time Bond screenwriter Richard Maibaum died on January 4, 1991. Some called this a "bloodless coup". Legal wrangling over the ownership of the James Bond character, coupled by these departures, delayed the release of the next film. In the interim, producer Albert R. Broccoli retired, and Timothy Dalton decided not to play the role a third time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c10745d8-6602-4cc8-bc65-7493c691ed39'), 'Long-time James Bond franchise producer Albert R. Broccoli fell sick during the production of this movie. The thinness of the air in Mexico affected his lungs and breathing, and he left the location accompanied by wife Dana and daughter Barbara. He was unable to return, and this was the last James Bond movie in which he was on the set', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e246af33-7b82-48d0-8014-a028d7cf8f69'), 'According to the DVD commentary, Timothy Dalton was unavailable for Talisa Soto''s screentest, so Robert Davi filled the role of Bond, and proved to be rather good in the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('edcd65d6-a1c0-4cd9-a183-53d0548cbdba'), 'In 2018, Timothy Dalton admitted that after thinking of not doing a third Bond movie, he finally decided that he wanted to do a final one, until Albert R. Broccoli told him that after the five year gap it would not be possible to do just one. Dalton then quit, since he had no intention to play Bond "for the rest of his life"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bb44420f-92be-46a4-a99b-84ac478c1c9d'), 'The Broccolis (Albert and his daughter Barbara) arranged for a medical team to fly down from Washington with the sole purpose of attending to the crew, a lot of whom were having trouble adjusting to the pollution and high altitude of Mexico City', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1d410726-508a-422c-b85f-9b6f2fb00c2a'), 'Despite being one of the least commercially successful Bond movies in the United States, it was considered by director John Glen to be his best "007". This opinion is shared by some fans and critics, who praise the realism of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80178571-b069-4407-9e4a-5adff49b9618'), 'Bond makes a quip when introducing Q to Pam. "Pam, this is Q, my uncle. This is Pam, my cousin." In the real-life S.I.S., "cousins" is a term for the C.I.A', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('13bd4325-8b47-4946-9cdc-066e2e96d55b'), 'According to Robert Davi, he wrote his line "Loyalty is more important to me than money."', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('06ac6d32-5d49-4cc3-95b5-b9f314590759'), 'Bond''s controversial betrayal of M was, in part, a way to sidestep the fact that the British have no jurisdiction over a Latin American drug cartel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4b000543-cea1-45db-a7bf-6392a2a9afa9'), 'Pam Bouvier (Carey Lowell) is the first Bond Girl to ever drink one of Bond''s signature vodka-martini cocktails', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f25a7edb-3ca3-43ec-a5f7-5d808aba0f83'), 'Making their final appearances with the James Bond franchise: Richard Maibaum (writer), John Glen (director), Maurice Binder (title design), Robert Brown as M, Caroline Bliss as Miss Moneypenny, and Timothy Dalton as James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('50e7ff6a-d187-4783-8f51-2c2beacf7644'), 'The last film of the franchise produced and released during the Cold War. At that time, Soviet Communism was already being viewed as less of a threat, and any new possible foreign adversaries were not yet clearly recognized. Producers felt that a Central American dictator and drug lord would give the movie a topical story line', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3de7296d-8a1b-49d5-8f0e-511ca3d3bb67'), 'When Truman-Lodge (Anthony Starke) says that the set-up cost them $32 million, that is an inside joke, a reference to the film''s $32 million budget', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9bd81ac3-b8a1-49b7-9fa6-49258d2dd0e8'), 'According to the book "The Making of Licence to Kill" by Sally Hibbin (published 1989), Carey Lowell handled herself so well during her fight scenes that members of the stunt team gave her the nickname "Pambo"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('62b508b9-8892-430b-89d9-8ffca3f988b6'), 'Director John Glen said the production had a tough time pulling off the action, stunts and huge set-pieces, because the budgets of the Bond films had not changed since Octopussy (1983). This was mostly due to MGM''s constant financial woes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5b1181d2-f482-4933-a40a-46f54824af4a'), 'Wayne Newton got the role of Professor Joe Butcher after sending a letter to the producers expressing interest in a cameo, because he always wanted to be in a Bond film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fc1bddf1-ba8a-43ab-a4a2-47197556a24e'), 'In AMC''s Bond Girls Are Forever (2002), Carey Lowell said that she shut her eyes and flinched every time she fired the gun, and had to be trained to fire with her eyes open, because a CIA operative would not flinch. However, she still winces a bit whenever she fires the handgun', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9b3b7f8a-d82d-4b3a-aa49-8a630e6b0999'), 'Milton Krest''s death used a prostethic head, which was created by John Richardson''s team, based on a mold of Anthony Zerbe''s face. The result was so gruesome that it was shortened and toned down to avoid censorship problems', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('aacf02b0-a9c0-4b96-a885-687b8f1248e8'), 'Bond poses as someone looking to buy a Great White Shark, presumably for an aquarium. In fact no aquarium has ever been able to keep a Great White. Marine biologists believe that because aquariums are unable to create a suitable artificial environment for great whites in captivity it causes them to become depressed. They aren''t at all happy with their new environment. A common behavior among great whites in captivity is to ram their heads into the walls of their tanks', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bf07cd00-3322-4ed3-ae99-bae3819f32d9'), 'Marked the last filmed appearance of Felix Leiter until "Casino Royale (2006)". David Hedison remains the only actor to play Felix Leiter opposite two different Bonds, Timothy Dalton in "Licence to Kill (1989)", and Sir Roger Moore in "Live and Let Die (1973)"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('37d1610a-d449-4535-92d4-72ed63933eca'), 'During one of the takes of Bond and Leiter''s parachute jump, a malfunction of the harness equipment caused David Hedison to fall on the pavement. The injury made him limp for the remainder of filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0d111bef-e4cb-4dbf-add5-3532b2eff468'), 'Pam Bouvier''s alias as Ms. Kennedy is a reference to Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis, whose maiden name was Bouvier. Her weapon was a .25 caliber Beretta 950 automatic', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eba4fd1c-6e8f-4fcf-8dc3-a82080e3f3ab'), 'While Carey Lowell wore a wig for the scenes set in the United States, a scene where Bouvier cuts her hair was added so Lowell''s natural short hair could be used', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab992f29-04ef-4866-aedf-86b976c20894'), 'John Rhys-Davies was offered a cameo role as General Pushkin, but declined the offer, as he was filming Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade (1989); ironically, his co-star was the original James Bond, Sean Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('42608db7-3773-4006-a197-817a0a400f49'), 'Sea-Air Service, a sea plane company located in Louisiana, leased their sea plane for the scene where Bond takes over the plane full of cash. When the plane was returned after filming, errant movie cash was found while cleaning the cabin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bf043f11-961c-45df-ab55-6ca4edd309ed'), 'The closing credits song "If You Asked Me To", sung by Patti LaBelle, was featured on the B-side of the main title song''s 45 rpm single, and became an unexpected minor hit. The LaBelle song charted in a Rhythm and Blues Top Ten, and was later sung in a cover version by Céline Dion, where it became an even bigger hit', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0651a359-e35f-4361-b747-632cd9b19d0e'), 'Extras during the wedding scene include Doug Redenius, a postman from Chicago, Illinois, who owns one of the largest collections of Bond memorabilia, Sandi Sentell, a gym teacher from Atlanta, Georgia, who won an MTV/VH1 competition to appear in the film (in the film, a bystander is seen wearing a VH1 t-shirt with the late 1980s logo design), and still photographer Keith Hamshere as the wedding photographer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('94830e68-fc97-4337-82ce-51153bbd1c2d'), 'The film was originally to be set in China, but production difficulties became insurmountable. Screenwriters Richard Maibaum and Michael G. Wilson wrote two treatments set around drugs in the Golden Triangle, with the villain being a drug warlord of the region. Ideas for the film included a motorcycle chase along the Great Wall of China, and a fight sequence in the recently discovered museum of ancient terracotta statues at Xian. When the Chinese government made several restrictive demands, such as veto rights over the script, the viability of the location fell through. Also, John Glen felt that The Last Emperor (1987) had removed some of the novelty from filming in China', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b695739e-2e87-4292-a3ed-852e6ff542e0'), 'The mini sub seen in this film is an updated version of the one used in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), called the Shark Hunter II', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('34896a72-3124-4e27-a53c-ddcb8fc076a3'), 'Sanchez is from Isthmus City, a fictional city that references the country of Panama which lies on an isthmus, and its corrupt dictator Manuel Noriega, whom the C.I.A. were working very hard to oust at the time. He was eventually deposed by U.S. troops in the same year this film was released. Sanchez seems to be an on-screen representation of Colombian drug lord Pablo Escobar, who was terrorizing his country with bomb attacks and selective killing of Presidential candidates at the time of the movie''s release', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('78bb0e33-91ec-4d51-915c-ef026e63edb9'), 'Due to the Writers'' Guild of America strike in 1988, long-time James Bond screenwriter Richard Maibaum was unable to continue working on the screenplay. A long time member of the Guild, Maibaum felt he could not betray his membership and ghost-write the script. Co-writer Michael G. Wilson had to complete the screenplay on his own. This was to be the fifth and final pairing for the Maibaum-Wilson writing team, which had started with For Your Eyes Only (1981)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9c0c76c8-34ff-49a4-9f64-128a4c546751'), 'This film marked the retirement of John Barry from composing scores and songs for the franchise. Michael Kamen took over composing duties on the film, as John Barry was undergoing throat surgery at the time. Creative differences with the band A-ha on The Living Daylights (1987) allegedly also contributed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c53a6e7e-9013-401a-91a1-3d5d98d5aa9d'), 'Gladys Knight''s title song is the longest of all the Bond songs. In the UK, it peaked at the number six position on the charts. As a Christian soul singer, Knight apparently objected to having to sing a song with the word "kill" in it, but eventually, she conceded. The song is apparently based on the "horn line" from the Goldfinger (1964) title song and consequently royalty payments were allegedly made to relevant personnel. The music video of this song was directed by Daniel Kleinman, who succeeded Maurice Binder as title designer on GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('edb5efe4-e295-406d-a725-5531816c3081'), 'While in production, various newspapers reported that this would be the most violent Bond film yet, and would trying to keep up with the mega violence of such recent, popular action fare as "Lethal Weapon (1987)" and "Die Hard (1988)." This was the first Bond film to score a PG-13 rating, due to its violent content', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bf35642e-bbe6-4c59-a8fb-79c51fdb231b'), 'This is the third James Bond movie to use story elements from Ian Fleming''s James Bond novel "Live And Let Die" (1954), the others being "Live and Let Die (1973)" and "For Your Eyes Only (1981)"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cf6c2c22-8454-459e-8722-34bd144cafd2'), 'This is the only James Bond film not to mention the name of the song or its artist in the opening credits sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f0aed951-daff-40c1-aac4-45464f1ab722'), 'First James Bond movie to include tobacco warnings in its closing credits. This was in the form of a United States Surgeon General warning. Smoking of tobacco, cigarettes, and cigars occurs in numerous Bond movies, and this is the only one of them to include a health warning. The film featured product placement of the Philip Morris Company''s Lark cigarettes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35691b89-e444-4604-b32d-50dcfbd17d4f'), 'The aquatic battle between Bond and the henchmen required two separate units, a surface one led by Arthur Wooster, which used Timothy Dalton, and an underwater one, which involved experienced divers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('21853c48-ca27-407a-a01d-4a5cd9bb3723'), 'Carey Lowell had described becoming a Bond girl as "huge shoes to fill", as she did not see herself as a "glamor girl", even coming to audition in jeans and a leather jacket. When refused on a Friday, she spent the weekend going to a Contempo Casual shop buying a halter dress. She shown up again at the audition and got the role. the opposite of what she thought a CIA operative would look like', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('42e9f75d-19f2-4ccb-93c4-003c2bc2457f'), 'At one point, Lea Thompson was considered for the role of Pam Bouvier, but she turned down in order to allow her to star in Back to the Future Part II (1989) and Back to the Future Part III (1990)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('65749a2b-b584-492d-8629-f9c3f47c4d3a'), 'While on the set of "Scarlett (1994)," Timothy Dalton officially announced his resignation from the role of James Bond on April 11, 1994', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff3a735e-221c-4b91-8356-afe413a0b22d'), 'John Glen was reluctant to cast 61-year-old David Hedison, since the role had a scene parachuting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('be398153-be7b-48bc-b563-9b72a7657c6d'), 'To portray Sanchez, Robert Davi researched on the Colombian drug cartels, and how to do a Colombian accent, and since he was method acting, he would stay in character off-set. After Davi read "Casino Royale" for preparation, he decided to turn Sanchez into a "mirror image" of James Bond, based on Ian Fleming''s descriptions of Le Chiffre', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('628d8d32-982d-4f89-b260-8842a343c7c5'), 'According to Robert Davi, the tearaway dress that Carey Lowell wears in the casino scene was inspired by a similar dress that Talisa Soto wore during her audition', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fde879f5-c552-44a2-8c5e-5d20407e3e33'), 'Timothy Dalton got homesick while filming in Mexico. He said that he really missed a good pint of bitter', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7c55ecc6-3269-4cb8-9d64-b1f4c84f06a1'), 'Re-united Robert Davi and Grand L. Bush, one year after they played FBI Agents Big Johnson and Little Johnson, respectively, in Die Hard (1988). As well as for composer Michael Kamen, who scored Die Hard (1988) and this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e423d7d-6a27-47d7-9bad-02bc1699eb57'), 'A good portion of Bond''s plan to get close to Sanchez comes from the novel "Goldfinger", when Bond recounts to himself his exploits in breaking up a Central American drug ring', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'License To Kill'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('c8f47cb7-6487-4a31-a703-047eb291ff96'), 'The previous Bond movie, Licence to Kill (1989), used a contest advertising campaign to help generate interest for the next movie, and the winner of the contest was promised a cameo role in it. Unfortunately, due to many production issues, work on Goldeneye did not begin for many years. Nevertheless, the contest winner was given a scene after the long delay. She does not have a speaking part, but you can see her in a lovely gold and black evening dress looking over Xenia Onatopp''s (Famke Janssen''s) shoulder as she plays Baccarat against Bond (Pierce Brosnan)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c78108cc-dd6b-416b-8d4a-2244b1777716'), 'Famke Janssen broke a rib during the sauna fight scene, according to her interview for Everything or Nothing (2012). Before filming the sequence, Janssen encouraged Pierce Brosnan to run her into the wall as hard as he could, and actually insisted he do it, citing that the walls were padded', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d13dd7dd-68ed-46ca-8adc-ea44fd26c885'), 'Features the highest bungee jump from a structure in a movie. The drop was over seven hundred twenty-two feet. The man who did the jump has a cameo as the black-haired Tiger helicopter pilot shot by Xenia Onatopp', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dbbf4c1f-d91e-437d-b4f3-6bf875c0b16c'), 'Computer graphics were used to create the famous "gun barrel" opening, making this movie the first James Bond film to use CGI. The image of the barrel is the same as the traditional one but altered to emphasize shade and light. The falling blood resembles the original but is slightly different. This gun barrel with slight changes would be used for the rest of Brosnan''s tenure in the role and was completely changed in image and concept for 2006''s Casino Royale when Daniel Craig took over the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8dc0e292-6a2c-4270-85ea-cd271bee625b'), 'Agent 007 killed 47 people in this movie, making this the highest amount of people James Bond killed in a single movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5ee9791f-f538-467e-9ad0-eba5fc9f1ebf'), 'This film is the first in the series with an original story not based on any of Ian Fleming''s novels or short stories. Previous films with original plots, including The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) and Licence to Kill (1989), still used titles or adapted elements from Fleming''s written work', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1b97ae46-f7a3-4b8a-913e-b29b26bbf7c3'), 'An East German architect and a Russian civil engineer were present during the construction of the Russian sites and interior sets. They refused to have their names credited', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6cd32c9d-1aa5-40d0-ad67-9f7bac10089a'), 'Minnie Driver earned just $5,000 for her role as an inept singer who performs "Stand by Your Man" in Robbie Coltrane''s club', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('588566e0-294c-4dcb-b833-8f418d586747'), 'Ralph Fiennes auditioned for James Bond. He replaced Dame Judi Dench as M in Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bfed271a-9a85-4b90-9d1b-be2838d3a6e2'), 'In the opening car chase between Bond''s Aston Martin and Onatopp''s Ferrari, Famke Janssen performed some of her own driving stunts. She confirmed this in an interview with Jay Leno in 1995', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d25b225-8ac4-4f39-a4e7-cd125a304cbc'), 'The first James Bond film produced following the dissolution of the Soviet Union and the end of the Cold War. This provided the background for the film''s plot, which was the first in the series not based on any of Ian Fleming''s stories. The production was the first to film in Russia, with some scenes shot on location in St. Petersburg. However, to reduce expenses and security concerns, many scenes intended to be in Russia were filmed in the United Kingdom. Epsom Downs Racecourse in Surrey stood in for the St. Petersburg airport. The tank chase sequence combined filming on location in St. Petersburg with extensive work at Leavesden Studios, a former Rolls-Royce aircraft factory in Hertfordshire. This was the first film to shoot at Leavesden, which later became a world-famous studio. A Russian T-54/55 tank was modified for the sequence, with its steel tracks replaced by rubber-shoed tracks from a British Chieftain tank to avoid damaging the streets of St. Petersburg', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('307698a8-89fd-4dd2-b556-9b520e88601f'), 'This was the first time a German sports car, in this case the BMW Z3, was used as the primary James Bond vehicle. The product placement of the BMW Z3 Roadster has been considered to be one of the most successful in movie history, according to "The Hollywood Reporter" and the book "Product Placements" by L. Kinney and B Sapolsky. It reportedly cost $3 million, but recouped the company $240 million in advance sales, partially due to exposure in the media. A limited edition "007 Model" of the BMW Z3 was sold out in a day of it going on to the market. This movie represented the first of a three-movie deal with BMW to promote their cars', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eae0acfc-d0d9-4aa0-a184-d14fae0d22de'), 'Dame Judi Dench''s glass of bourbon is really apple juice with two lumps of light glass passing for ice cubes. Pierce Brosnan drank iced water instead of the famous vodka martini', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98d33b5a-6d93-4bd5-aac6-d55892a5ab66'), 'At the time the script was being written, the producers were under the assumption that Timothy Dalton would be renewing the role of Bond. It was written to match Dalton''s darker, more realistic portrayal of 007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8ec3644b-30c7-4937-951b-7b6ca68df842'), 'This was the first time a Bond film was shot in Russia - the same country that had banned the general release of all the previous Bond films -but it involved miles of red tape and almost 150 permits from every utility and commission in the city. Even then filming came to a halt one day when a local paper reported the company was destroying the city. It took almost a day to convince the authorities that the only things being destroyed were pieces of fabricated scenery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7d6cbf6-3e93-4cb9-87d0-cbad04abd9f5'), 'Nails had to be attached to the tires of the Ferrari F355 for the skid in the car chase with James Bond''s Aston Martin. This Ferrari was rented and, after colliding with 007''s car, had to be repaired overnight, at a cost of $80,000', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c1d5563a-2dca-4291-95ab-d4aac966de5a'), 'Michael France authored the original screenplay for the production in 1993 and 1994. Screenwriters Jeffrey Caine and Bruce Feirstein later performed extensive rewrites to the script. Industry rumors suggested these revisions were necessary because the original plot shared significant similarities with True Lies (1994) (1994). Verified production accounts indicate the script changes were primarily motivated by a desire to modernize the series for a post-Cold War era and to accommodate the casting transition from Timothy Dalton to Pierce Brosnan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('33887da0-e69c-4c28-a573-2c4ce5faa6e8'), 'The villain, Alec Trevelyan, was named in tongue-in-cheek homage to John Trevelyan, who was the British movie censor during the sixties when the "golden age" of James Bond movies were made. Trevelyan took a dim view to Bond movies, particularly Bond''s penchant for pun one-liner jokes after killing someone. Indeed, Trevelyan felt so strongly about what he saw as "callous sadism" in Bond''s character, he wrote about his antipathy towards the Bond films in his autobiography "What the Censor Saw". To date, he is the only British movie censor in the BBFC''s one hundred year history to have written an autobiography. He was head censor from 1959 to 1970, retiring when he felt that movies were becoming too mindlessly violent. This, he felt, was due to the collapse of the production code in the U.S. Ironically, upon his retirement, he campaigned for an end for movie censorship for adults', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3f37eb16-592b-40e8-b7b1-e155cf35683a'), 'The film''s title refers to "Goldeneye", the name of author Ian Fleming''s winter home in Jamaica. Fleming purchased the property in 1946 and wrote all of his James Bond novels and short stories there. The estate''s name originates from Operation Goldeneye, a World War II contingency plan Fleming devised while serving in the British Naval Intelligence Division. The operation''s objective was to monitor Spain and undertake sabotage operations in the event of a Spanish alliance with the Axis powers, ensuring British communication with Gibraltar', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7783ea17-4963-4c3d-8ba6-f533b87e56d4'), 'Sir Roger Moore paid a visit to the set to see his son, Christian Moore, who was working as a third assistant director. He quipped that early tests of Pierce Brosnan hadn''t worked out, so he was brought back', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bab5fda4-6b0e-4eda-b9a1-14057a54e17a'), 'Agent 006, Alec Trevelyan (Sean Bean), was originally named "Augustus Trevelyan", and written as a much older character, and a former mentor of James Bond. The producers were keen to hire Sir Anthony Hopkins for the part, but he turned it down. Alan Rickman also turned down the role, stating that he was tired of playing villains. Finally, Sean Bean was cast after the part was re-written, but elements of the original idea survive in the finished version, though, instead of the character remembering the 1940s, his parents managed to escape execution, but committed suicide some time later, when Alec was a small child', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a34b061d-cc3d-40b5-938e-8bd262f013b8'), 'A six-year gap separated the theatrical releases of Licence to Kill (1989) and GoldenEye (1995), a delay caused by legal disputes involving production company Danjaq and studio MGM. This hiatus marked the longest period between James Bond films in the series'' history up to that point. The record was later nearly matched by the six-year gap between Spectre (2015) and No Time to Die (2021), the latter of which was postponed multiple times due to the COVID-19 pandemic. While the gap between Licence to Kill and Goldeneye was approximately six years and four months, the gap between Spectre and No Time to Die was slightly shorter at five years and five months', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('18aac40a-6d31-409d-8c04-4b6d66f3a891'), 'The film''s climactic sequence, set in Cuba, used the Arecibo Observatory in Puerto Rico as the location for the antagonist''s satellite dish. The 305-meter radio telescope also appears in the film Contact (1997). The Arecibo Observatory operated for 57 years. An auxiliary support cable failed on August 10, 2020, followed by a main cable failure on November 6, 2020. The National Science Foundation (NSF) determined the structure was no longer stable and announced the telescope''s decommissioning. The 900-ton instrument platform collapsed into the reflector dish on December 1, 2020, before controlled demolition could be performed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('500c5778-61c5-4f2d-afbe-84f6b0253c84'), 'First 007 film to feature a woman, Dame Judi Dench, in the role of "M," head of the U.K.''s security agency MI6 (Foreign Intelligence). Dench''s character was reportedly inspired by the career of Stella Rimington, former Director-General of the U.K.''s MI5 (Domestic Intelligence) and first woman to head that organization. However, Dench denied this, explaining, "But the script was actually written before she had her job. I have never met her but I have recently had a message from her children who say it is staggering how alike we are. We have the same gestures and speech patterns, apparently. It is a terrific part to play because I get to keep Bond in order"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('934a2198-9573-4cca-be9b-8a42dd2acb9a'), 'The only Bond movie where James Bond, M, and Miss Moneypenny were all re-cast with a different actor and actresses. The only holdover was Desmond Llewelyn as Q', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('943cbe82-e27a-4ba3-84dc-3fa3d262214c'), 'Pierce Brosnan hurt his hand in his bathroom at his house in Malibu before shooting began, so in several shots, his hands were doubled by his 22-year-old son Christopher Brosnan, who was the third assistant trainee on the second unit. These include: pulling on a hand-brake in the Aston Martin DB5, flipping open the glove compartment to reveal a bottle of chilled Bollinger champagne, using the laser in the opening bungee jump, and cutting through the floor of the train with the laser in his wristwatch', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4c4e958a-4bb1-47a4-8ed6-221b9ff1c16d'), 'The most successful James Bond movie since Moonraker (1979)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('84587498-8dd6-4cd4-b1ca-f9cd3362a53b'), 'The reason Bond''s Z3 Roadster isn''t seen deploying any of its gadgets (apart from the radar) is because the deal with BMW came very late in production. The car used was a prototype, meaning that it couldn''t be damaged in any way, or used in any action scenes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2db2fd38-9588-49b7-ac53-9501b86872f0'), 'First of two appearances by Joe Don Baker as James Bond''s CIA counterpart Jack Wade, who also appeared in Tomorrow Never Dies (1997). Wade was created as a replacement for Felix Leiter, who had lost his leg (and presumably retired from field work as a result) in Licence to Kill (1989). However, Baker wasn''t new in the Bond movies. He previously played Brad Whitaker, one of the villains of The Living Daylights (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e1a70509-1725-492d-b431-f212cd3e9ead'), 'In the first draft of this movie, Xenia''s preferred method of killing was the use of her hands to induce heart attacks instead of using her thighs to suffocate her victims. The latter method was mentioned in The Living Daylights (1987), when Q described a female K.G.B. assassin who strangles men with her hands or thighs. Miss Moneypenny commented: "Why James, she''s just your type!" The scene where Xenia kills Admiral Farrell with her thighs during sex marks the first explicit sex scene in a Bond movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f17dfe85-2eb0-4759-8655-a7286b48b2ae'), 'The 1995 book "The Making of GoldenEye" by Garth Pearce reveals that Desmond Llewelyn arrived on set to film his scenes on 10 February 1995 wearing a crumpled green suit. He proceeded to explain that he had worn it non-stop for the previous two weeks to achieve an uncared for appearance', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('163f97e3-75fd-40d3-b57e-e227a66aa1d7'), 'Xenia Onatopp displays a Baccarat hand totaling seven during the casino sequence when James Bond first observes her play. The hand consists of two face cards and a seven. In Baccarat rules, face cards hold a value of zero, resulting in a numerical representation of 007. James Bond plays a final Baccarat hand against Xenia Onatopp consisting of two face cards and a six. This combination creates a numerical representation of 006. The hand functions as a reference to Janus syndicate leader Alec Trevelyan, formerly Agent 006, whom Bond believes deceased at this point in the production time-line', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('25d418d5-26a0-498e-92d9-1b6ababf40c6'), 'Final James Bond movie viewed by Albert R. Broccoli', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8f572ee5-2c34-49f9-bea6-6c220bb72d03'), 'The new arrangement of the James Bond theme, used in the opening, was disliked by many fans, and was replaced by a more traditional version in future movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c4ac55cf-904a-48b1-abe3-551f3f080354'), 'Production of the tank chase sequence required approximately six weeks of principal photography. The second unit, led by director Ian Sharp, filmed on location in Saint Petersburg, Russia, for approximately one week beginning April 11, 1995. The crew completed the remaining five weeks of the schedule on a two acre back-lot set at Leavesden Studios in Hertfordshire, England.Production Designer Peter Lamont oversaw the construction of the Saint Petersburg exterior set, which featured a two block recreation of Russian streets supported by 62 miles of scaffolding. The construction phase for the set spanned approximately seven weeks', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c64d347c-c5d3-4f30-a798-52e4b2016e91'), 'John Woo turned down the chance to direct. He said he was honored by the offer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('18ec9966-da20-412b-9b51-5f5b19f9051c'), 'Visual effects supervisor Derek Meddings died of natural causes in June 1995, following the completion of principal photography. The end credits contain a formal dedication to his memory. Meddings oversaw the miniature effects and large scale model photography for the production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fe76cdd0-1047-42e1-8756-01fbd6a9f72e'), 'Sean Bean previously auditioned for the role of James Bond in The Living Daylights (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('978a7eb6-80b5-4944-bd9c-9d9363e9cac1'), 'The first of the James Bond movies to be released on DVD', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('90cad652-31bb-49c5-9695-29b0965199ce'), 'The sets that included the Soviet Arkangel chemical facility, the satellite base, and the interior of the armored Soviet train were all built on a soundstage in London. The facility set in particular was the most complex out of all, since the engineers put so much detail into the architecture, that they even had working outlets and light switches, as well as working cookware in the cafeteria into which James Bond looks. During breaks on-set while shooting on that location, cast members and crew who chose to remain on-set for lunch, would actually eat in the cafeteria built for the scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5a221db8-99c3-47e2-a093-5bf80254494d'), 'Production documents and the original screenplay by Michael France identify the character of M, portrayed by Judi Dench, as Barbara Mawdsley. This specific name later appeared in the 1997 James Bond novel "Zero Minus Ten" by Raymond Benson and the official film novelization by John Gardner. While the name remains absent from the final theatrical cut, the production utilized this identity to distinguish the character from previous incarnations', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b15ed34a-d698-4ae9-a522-6e02645d5867'), 'Due to his fear of heights, Pierce Brosnan was not able to go to the Gregorian Dome and other parts of the Arecibo Observatory in Puerto Rico; a stunt double was used', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('11343f11-58a8-4b40-b270-be69b6d89b4e'), '90,000 cans of Perrier water were used in the collision between the tank and the Perrier truck', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2d6f397c-4e25-4c64-a6a2-f6ebd99f44b1'), 'Part of the St. Petersburg tank chase was filmed at Leavesden Studios. They faked all of the relevant statues and treasures, and smashed replicas on a U.K. backlot, but that didn''t stop a few breathless "They''re destroying our art!" newscasts in Russia', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('317553fe-4663-4b50-89bf-5b92cca8fbc3'), 'Film features the most extensive use of model and miniature work in the history of the James Bond film series. Miniature effects supervisor Derek Meddings, to whom the film is dedicated, oversaw the creation of key miniatures including the Severnaya radar complex, the armored train, and the Arecibo Observatory satellite dish. The production was the last in the series to rely heavily on practical miniature effects prior to the wider adoption of computer-generated imagery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9c982c30-377a-4e7c-8b37-59da87023c52'), 'The opening weekend box-office gross was slightly altered to $26,205,007. The same last three digits were used in the reports for the opening weekends of the next two James Bond movies as well', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a0c59e88-b034-4191-9b25-71330dede139'), 'One of the theatrical trailers spoiled Alec Trevelyan being revealed as the villain', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6134700d-b255-4d58-887c-c5502dc1220a'), 'In 2018, Timothy Dalton admitted that after thinking of not doing a third James Bond movie, he finally decided that he wanted to do a final one until Albert R. Broccoli told him that after the five year gap, it would not be possible to do just one. Dalton then quit, since he had no intentions to do Bond "for the rest of his life"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fdb43d87-32e9-42a3-9977-5cf20ca2b697'), 'Paul McGann was the original choice for the role of Bond after Liam Neeson turned down the role. He would have been cast in the role had Pierce Brosnan turned down the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7b6cc48a-649e-4b20-842a-7cae6ff2f3ac'), 'Alec Trevelyan is a descendant of Lienz Cossacks, who were repatriated to the Soviet Union by the British after World War II, after assurances they would be treated as Allied POWs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('16abf82b-7236-4d56-b5e6-42b81dd4e878'), 'The first draft of the script contained scrapped action sequences that ended up in future James Bond movies. Bond and Marina''s (later renamed Natalya) escape from a underground nuclear explosion and a chase sequence involving helicopters equipped with giant buzzsaws ended up in The World Is Not Enough (1999). The U.S. government''s and MI6''s collaborative effort to destroy the space-based weapon "Tempest", later renamed "GoldenEye", was resurrected and used in Die Another Day (2002) as the attempt to destroy Icarus. Lastly, the free fall sequence ended up in Quantum of Solace (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2e08f8f5-5459-4977-9349-310df8acd5c0'), 'Director Martin Campbell''s personal dislike of smoking meant that James Bond was to give the habit up again. 007 had started smoking again when Timothy Dalton arrived on the scene, but EON was clearly uneasy about the image this presented, as they placed a "smoking can kill" warning during the end credits of Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('58f23c9f-5251-4a22-9582-b746bbdab922'), 'The new M being a woman was in fact Lois Maxwell''s idea (the original Miss Moneypenny). Maxwell had wanted to be the new M, and that in the movie, Miss Moneypenny is promoted and is revealed as the new M. Which would have tied in nicely with M being her character''s initial. But she was disappointed when Dame Judi Dench was cast in the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e6dc117c-4794-407f-8d2b-580eae91368a'), 'Alec Trevelyan''s black locomotive in the movie was nicknamed on the set as "Darth Train"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8ca6e09d-786b-4b24-9294-4efb1fc21dea'), 'The actual MI6 Headquarters was used for external views of M''s office', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('65de897d-5f92-4965-9927-7913d2a16ee3'), 'A Russian T-54/55 tank, on loan from the East England Military Museum, was modified with the addition of fake explosive reactive armour panels. In order to avoid destroying the pavement on the city streets of St. Petersburg, the steel off-road tracks of the T-54/55 were replaced with the rubber-shoed tracks from a British Chieftain tank. The T-55 Tank is now on permanent display at Old Buckenham Airport, where the East England Military Museum is based', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c9b5e62a-ec08-4b1f-b860-f9f698abe3c9'), 'The title song did not chart in the U.S., but in the U.K., it went to the number seven spot on the charts. The song was written by Bono and The Edge of U2, and performed by Tina Turner. All three were neighbors to each other, living in the south of France. One day, the U2 members went over to Turner''s place, whereupon The Edge played the song on Turner''s piano. Bono''s inspiration for writing the song was his honeymoon stay with his wife at Ian Fleming''s Jamaican beach house "Goldeneye", which is also the name of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f156d209-56de-49bd-aeb6-96b048616f2e'), 'Pierce Brosnan and George Lazenby are the only 007 actors born outside the United Kingdom. Lazenby was born in Australia, Brosnan in Ireland. Unlike Lazenby, Brosnan moved to the U.K. when fairly young', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ac51680f-60a9-4c8e-a379-92e4713047d7'), 'When M gives James Bond the GoldenEye mission, she tells him not to go off on a personal vendetta and avenge Alec Trevelyan. In the narrative, M referred to the events of Licence to Kill (1989), in which 007 got his revenge upon drug lord Franz Sanchez for torturing Felix Leiter and murdering Leiter''s bride, Della Churchill', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('41f4eb7c-363b-419b-932b-8363c7d4b4a9'), 'The band Ace of Base submitted a demo for the title song. Their record label, Arista Records, withdrew the song from consideration, concerned that the film''s potential failure would damage the band''s commercial success. The song was later reworked with different lyrics and released as "The Juvenile" on their 2002 album "Da Capo"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('836ebacb-4c8b-4564-b7e2-37b3ddebd44b'), 'The French Navy provided full use of the frigate F.S. La Fayette, and their newest helicopter, the Eurocopter Tiger, to the production team. The French government also allowed the use of Navy logos as part of the promotional campaign for this movie. However, the producers had a dispute with the French Ministry of Defence over Pierce Brosnan''s opposition to French nuclear weapons testing, and his involvement with Greenpeace. As a result, the French premiere of this movie was cancelled', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2fed9ed5-eeb1-4db5-bab9-9c9fdc44d5a0'), 'In April of 1995, during post-production, the K.G.B. was renamed the "Federal Security Bureau", making this the final James Bond movie that was made during the K.G.B.''s existence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d8c166e-98ca-46a4-8567-a711052e6cf2'), 'Pierce Brosnan was officially introduced to the press as the new James Bond on June 8, 1994, at the Regent Hotel in London. He was sporting a full beard, as he was about to start production on Robinson Crusoe (1997) the next day', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7222145-10d2-4a1b-b426-8e59517cfc29'), 'None of the principal cast members portraying Russians or former Soviet citizens are Russians. Izabella Scorupco (Natalya) is Polish/Swedish, Famke Janssen (Xenia) is Dutch, Gottfried John (Ourumov) is German, Tchéky Karyo (Mishkin) is French, and Robbie Coltrane (Valentin) and Alan Cumming (Boris) are Scottish. Also, Actor Pierce Brosnan was born in Ireland. The closest to an actual Russian is that Izabella Scorupco is Polish and Poland is a Slavic country as is Russia', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('92915673-615b-4d2e-b889-b725b397e2c9'), 'For the scenes in which Xenia Onatopp is seen flying the Tiger helicopter, a male pilot had to be made up to look like Famke Janssen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('76f195c6-85ff-43ca-b0ca-7e32f6f14f0d'), 'Following Licence to Kill (1989), Michael G. Wilson and Alfonse Ruggiero Jr. wrote a script treatment for a seventeenth James Bond film. The production, intended for a 1991 release, carried the working title "The Property of a Lady" from an Ian Fleming short story. The plot involved nanotechnology and locations in Scotland, Tokyo, and Hong Kong. Timothy Dalton was contracted to return as James Bond for a third film. Production stalled for several years due to legal disputes regarding the ownership of the James Bond character rights. After the extended delay, Dalton announced his retirement from the role, which subsequently went to Pierce Brosnan. During the film''s extended pre-production phase, potential directors considered for the project included John Landis, Ted Kotcheff, and John Byrum. The death of longtime screenwriter Richard Maibaum and the box office performance of Licence to Kill (1989) also contributed to development delays and extensive script revisions that evolved the initial concept into the final film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b338c918-44f9-403d-975c-49536a73e06a'), 'The pre-title sequence takes place nine years before the main part of the film. This would make it 1986. Coincidentally, that was the year Pierce Brosnan was first offered the part of James Bond, but had to give it up when his the producers of Remington Steele (1982) decided to renew his contract', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab82f362-f6eb-4f2e-b41d-e171676dfac4'), 'Natalya Simonova is unique within the Bond Leading Lady pantheon because she is introduced early in the story and survives numerous ordeals before she ever crosses paths with Bond. She finally meets him just over an hour into the film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f4c63278-621b-4f31-82b6-8455d595a77b'), 'Michael G. Wilson, the extra with the glasses and dark hair on the Russian security council, is a familiar face to Bond fans. He served as an extra in 16 Bond films, going all the way back to Goldfinger (1964). He also wrote the screen plays for 5 of them plus the cartoon series James Bond Jr. (1991), and served as producer / executive producer for 15 of the films, including No Time to Die (2021). In all, his involvement in Bond films spans an amazing 59 years', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8908038e-b3d1-4125-9b2c-ce0a0fc11eea'), 'The production could not use its traditional home at Pinewood Studios. The studio was already booked for the production of First Knight (1995), which starred the original James Bond actor, Sir Sean Connery. Producers converted a former Rolls-Royce aircraft engine factory and aerodrome at Leavesden, Hertfordshire, into a new production facility. The production nicknamed the new studio "Cubbywood," an homage to longtime Bond producer Albert R. Broccoli. This was the first film to shoot at the new facility, subsequently named Leavesden Studios. The studio later hosted productions including Sleepy Hollow (1999) and Star Wars: Episode I - The Phantom Menace (1999)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d5f01f6-0176-4de9-b135-651f1f84ab1a'), 'Pierce Brosnan is the last actor to play James Bond in the EON Productions films who was cast by founding producer Albert R. Broccoli', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8901cc88-eae9-4ede-b44a-98e8f2c0f40f'), 'Producers considered Australian actress Elle Macpherson for the role of Natalya Simonova. Actresses Paulina Porizkova and Eva Herzigova were both offered the role of Natalya Simonova, but each declined. Elizabeth Hurley was rumored to be in consideration for a Bond girl role during the production period', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0efa1c54-10ca-45c3-877c-a5bf0592836b'), 'This is the only James Bond movie starring Pierce Brosnan where Bond is not lying on top of the female lead in the final shot of the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e9b77339-dd40-4b0f-a1a7-fd16800d0a1e'), 'Liam Neeson turned down playing James Bond in the movie as he didn''t want to be in an action film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0ae947c5-23a6-4b12-bb8a-3c8e3e38a53a'), 'The archives breakout scene took approximately two weeks to shoot, five hundred blanks were fired during that time, and much of the cast and crew wore ear plugs or headphones, due to the sound it created when shooting indoors, since all of the weapons were real', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7ce09e06-a795-402e-b313-cd2b5529a9e9'), 'Chris Columbus is a big James Bond fan, and he was crushed when Pierce Brosnan didn''t get cast when he was offered the part during Remington Steele (1982), but they wouldn''t release him from his contract, and he thought Brosnan a phenomenal actor. When the two worked together on Mrs. Doubtfire (1993), Columbus told Brosnan he''d make a great James Bond, even though Brosnan thought that ship had sailed. In 1994, MGM called Columbus telling him they''re looking for the new James Bond, and Brosnan was one of the choices, so Columbus recommended him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c0ea7b8d-3808-49cf-bba7-ab6de2d39bb3'), 'Three genuine T-55s were used for the tank chase (the exception is the scene where James Bond chases Russian utility vehicles; the tank here was a dummy built around a Saladin armored car). An extra hatch was cut in each to provide Pierce Brosnan with a fake driving position (the true driver sat on the left). According to stuntman Jim Dowdall, the tank skids were assisted by spreading several gallons of washing-up liquid on the road. He also states that there was one minor accident when the tank ran over a camera worth two hundred thousand pounds sterling', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0e17c5a6-29d4-44c7-9271-51f6a718bd5b'), 'Visual effects supervisor Derek Meddings revealed in an interview that he utilized more miniatures for this movie than any film he worked on before', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('223a5f45-6ab2-4651-9cd5-944d962dabe0'), 'The second appearance in a James Bond movie of Joe Don Baker, after playing a villain in The Living Daylights (1987). In this movie and Tomorrow Never Dies (1997), he played the role of CIA agent Jack Wade, a Bond ally. Precedents were Walter Gotell, who played villain Morzeny in From Russia with Love (1963), and ally General Gogol in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) and other movies; and Charles Gray, who played ally Dikko Henderson in You Only Live Twice (1967), and villain Ernst Stavro Blofeld in Diamonds Are Forever (1971)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b2c1bc07-5245-4da0-8dc7-3b178edaabca'), 'Instead of Miss Moneypenny, Loelia Ponsonby, James Bond''s secretary in the early Fleming novels, was in the first draft of this movie. Presumably, Ponsonby was going to replace Moneypenny as a recurring character. Ultimately, tradition prevailed, and Moneypenny ended up in the final draft, and Ponsonby was scrapped', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d606618-abb8-424d-bf81-6ab03e4aac2d'), 'Swedish pop music group Ace of Base was originally slated to perform the title theme song. They recorded the song, written by the band''s own Jonas Berggren, but it was pulled out of the project by their record label at the time. Ace of Base later re-wrote the lyrics to the song, renaming it "The Juvenile", and put it on their album, "Da Capo", released in Europe in late 2002. The song was released as a single off of that album in Germany, in December 2002. With the lyrics, the words ''The Juvenile" replaced "The Goldeneye", both having the same number of syllables, while the lyrics "Tomorrow''s foe is now a friend" clearly refers to Alec Trevelyan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('990052a9-171b-4858-9365-47eab371bbc2'), 'Sir Sean Connery recommended Mel Gibson as a candidate to take over as James Bond. Working on Braveheart (1995) at the time, he turned it down. Gibson had been approached to play the role as far back as The Year of Living Dangerously (1982). He later told Michael Parkinson during his interview on Parkinson (1971) that he had not been interested in playing Bond because he did not believe he could outdo Connery. He also mentioned at the end of the interview that some journalists had suggested he was too short to play Bond, standing at under 5''10''''', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('885a8333-904d-42f3-a805-9ddae213fbf6'), 'Whilst on the set of Scarlett (1994), Timothy Dalton officially announced his resignation from the role of James Bond on April 11, 1994. The script for this movie was originally earmarked for Dalton in the role of James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1886c8e-9973-45cd-bed2-626224c219a1'), 'First James Bond movie produced by Barbara Broccoli (with Michael G. Wilson) as a fully fledged main producer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5daef017-8de7-41e2-bc76-7e9d65b55c6f'), 'C.I.A. Agent Jack Wade and the Marines arriving after Trevelyan''s defeat was a nod to Dr. No (1962). In that first James Bond adventure, C.I.A. Agent Felix Leiter and the Marines are too late to join the battle against the main villain, Dr. No', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('28d2de54-ed40-4a8e-921d-79630107aa57'), 'At one point, Courteney Cox was considered for the role of Xenia Onatopp, but she was turned down due to scheduling conflicts with Friends (1994) and Famke Janssen was cast instead', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f6eccc5-b5a2-41d5-90b7-38cbb39ae218'), 'Several actors were considered for the role of James Bond before the producers cast Pierce Brosnan. The list of actors included Liam Neeson, Sam Neill, and Mel Gibson. Sam Neill declined after his wife, Natasha Richardson, gave him an ultimatum that she would not marry him if he took the role. Hugh Grant was also approached by the producers to discuss the role. Lambert Wilson auditioned and was the studio''s second choice for the part if Pierce Brosnan had declined', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('aff226f9-b2b9-4f76-abb4-4dc35cd67df2'), 'Michelle Eldridge provided the singing voice for Minnie Driver''s character Irina, even though Driver is a trained and successful singer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e73402df-897d-43b1-b4da-aef948d835c8'), 'The Earth viewed from space is the same model as used in Moonraker', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a1787502-c784-42bd-b970-c8edf3ef66ef'), 'The ending of the pre-credits sequence with James Bond jumping after the airplane featured Jacques "Zoo" Malnuit riding the motorcycle to the edge and jumping and B.J. Worth diving after the plane, which was a working aircraft, with Worth adding that part of the difficulty of the stunt was the kerosene flying in his face', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4ba3aac-df9b-4058-8859-11711be7d537'), 'For the confrontation between James Bond and Alec Trevelyan inside the antenna cradle, Martin Campbell decided to take inspiration from Bond''s fight with Red Grant in From Russia with Love (1963). Pierce Brosnan and Sean Bean did all of the stunts themselves, except for one take where one is thrown against the wall. Brosnan injured his hand while filming the extending ladder sequence, making producers delay his scenes and film the ones in Severnaya earlier', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7514dd7f-351b-4735-91b4-50fc12297f32'), 'In a curious move on the marketing, Dame Judi Dench''s name does not appear on any of the posters or in any of the trailers. This despite it being announced that she''d be taking over the role of ''M'' from the late Robert Brown before the marketing campaign began, as well as her prominence in the film''s theatrical trailer. Instead Joe Don Baker, who portrays CIA Agent Jack Wade in this film, receives the "and" billing on the poster and in the Ads. This would not be the case for the future, as Judi Dench''s name would appear in all the marketing of her next three Pierce Brosnan adventures, and three of Daniel Craig''s tenure', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('52d7ebe1-9f75-468a-852c-39539f3c2f9d'), 'As the producers did not collaborate with Bono or The Edge, the score did not incorporate any of the theme song''s melodies, as was the case in previous James Bond movies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('15d7298e-e3eb-45dd-b298-6c65aaf0f3f9'), 'This is technically the first James Bond film in which a character is audibly heard using the expletive "f--k," albeit in Russian rather than English. Xenia Onatopp says "Blyat''" (which literally translates to "w--re" but is more often used colloquially as "f--k") twice, after losing to Bond at Baccarat and after the fight in the steam room', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('33cc471a-459d-45bc-ae46-11956d95a000'), 'GoldenEye (1995) marks the reintroduction of MI6 Chief of Staff Bill Tanner, a character whose previous appearance was in For Your Eyes Only (1981). Michael Kitchen portrays Tanner in this film and reprised the role in The World Is Not Enough (1999). The character was included in early script drafts for Tomorrow Never Dies (1997), but Michael Kitchen was unavailable for filming, leading to the creation of a new character, Charles Robinson, to fill a similar function', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('96ad6beb-2219-41d4-b71f-1763ce3d9a32'), 'General Leonid Pushkin, James Bond''s ally in The Living Daylights (1987), was in the first draft of this movie. Just like in The Living Daylights (1987), Pushkin was going to be used as a pawn in the major villain''s scheme. His character was replaced with Dimitri Mishkin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Goldeneye'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('7facdacb-aede-403f-9dea-af28a48ab17c'), 'For the fight scene in the bicycle shop, the producers had to call in Jackie Chan''s stunt team because none of the stuntmen wanted to do the scene with Michelle Yeoh due to her full contact stunt fighting style, which she perfected in Hong Kong action films', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('54b97e70-b7c3-4f9e-8502-68ed3740f4bb'), 'Sir Anthony Hopkins was cast as Elliot Carver, and joined the production, but walked after three days because it was so chaotic, and there was no completed shooting script; due to the pressure on EON Productions to finish the movie on time, new pages of the screenplay were being delivered every morning. He opted to appear in The Mask of Zorro (1998) instead', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c70bcf0e-d53c-4384-ad41-1c0830331f66'), 'Just before shooting the scene where James Bond and Wai Lin get on the motorcycle, director Roger Spottiswoode took Pierce Brosnan and Michelle Yeoh aside, each without the other''s knowledge, and told each of them not to let the other get in the driver''s seat. The result is in the final movie: Bond and Wai Lin fight over who gets to drive before getting on the bike', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b98c1161-830e-43a7-b5f4-16960023f180'), 'This movie made particularly heavy use of gadgetry, because some fans thought there was too little of it in GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a7930bb7-b326-4d20-bcc2-14ffcae04e49'), 'When they had to re-shoot the car park scene, it was too expensive to go back to Germany, so it was done at Brent Cross Shopping Centre in London. Posters around the stores told shoppers that the explosions were nothing to worry about. It took ten days to shoot this car park scene, and seventeen BMWs were used', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3678a679-144e-4295-85e2-48f23a1375c7'), 'When Götz Otto was called in for casting, he was given twenty seconds to introduce himself. He simply said, "I''m big, I''m bad, I''m bald, I''m German. Five seconds, keep the rest"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1059a4c-c0a4-489e-8854-471b1a836b5a'), 'Ricky Jay (Henry Gupta) is also an acclaimed magician, who holds a world record for the fastest throwing playing cards. The producers initially wanted a scene where he threw playing cards at James Bond (Pierce Brosnan). They set up the scene to block, Ricky was fifty or seventy-five feet away, and was asked to hit Brosnan in the face. Ricky warned them it wasn''t a good idea, safety wise. After they convinced him to do it, he agreed, and hit Pierce right above the eyes. To his disappointment, for some reason, they never asked him to repeat it on film. Gupta is shown throwing cards in the DVD deleted scenes. Jay would also be employed by the CIA in real life to teach their agents sleight of hand (how to pick pockets, pass objects between them unobserved etc)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fbe21aba-0717-4312-99f2-f5c46a00c3c2'), 'According to the book "The Bond Legacy", a farewell scene for Q was written for this movie, on the assumption that Desmond Llewelyn would soon retire from the role. The idea was dropped, only to be revived for The World Is Not Enough (1999)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a1005a47-d8e7-48f5-8e62-1df31937eb37'), 'Michelle Yeoh got along well with Pierce Brosnan during filming, saying afterwards that Brosnan was "a gentleman"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f33e241e-cfbd-4c22-9c5d-14df1e4691e6'), 'As of 2019, Elliot Carver (Jonathan Pryce) has the distinction of being the only James Bond villain with a spouse', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98386a5c-e062-4aca-8b58-a2b2696c4a31'), 'Dedicated to the memory of long-time James Bond producer Albert R. Broccoli', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('adaf0957-ead7-469a-b821-99b86dcdf9bd'), 'Pierce Brosnan was injured during one of the fight scenes, a stuntman''s helmet hit him in the face. Brosnan required eight stitches down one side of his face, leaving the crew no choice but to film many of his scenes from one side only', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b76700fa-b065-45ab-9c43-a18254228938'), 'The stealth ship is not a fictional invention. Lockheed secretly constructed and demonstrated one in the early 1980s, but the U.S. Navy finally decided they didn''t want any. The prototype, called the Sea Shadow, was 160 feet long, and the movie''s ship closely resembles it in shape', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('73925c32-df33-48f4-888c-98956fdb032c'), 'James Bond gets a new gun in this movie, the Walther P99, because Walther wanted to debut its new firearm in a Bond movie, which had been one of its most visible endorsers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dbd3a5ac-67a9-413e-8668-60f6edb511f6'), 'Michelle Yeoh reportedly wanted to perform all of her own stunts, but was prevented because director Roger Spottiswoode ruled it too dangerous, and prohibited by insurance restrictions', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6ec2b124-d6b6-4488-92bd-da59ffae5399'), 'Pierce Brosnan and Teri Hatcher feuded briefly during filming, due to her arriving late onto the set one day. The matter was quickly resolved, though, and Brosnan apologized after realizing she was pregnant, and was late for that reason', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6c08273a-6d7f-4af3-8534-0692ff5d65fa'), 'Monica Bellucci read for the role of Paris Carver. According to Pierce Brosnan, "The fools said no". She was cast in Spectre (2015)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('773b398a-a2e4-43ba-9fbd-3f2c7f01bc74'), 'Since director Roger Spottiswoode felt that after the tank chase in GoldenEye (1995), he could not use a bigger vehicle, the motorcycle chase was devised', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9020e25e-a5d0-4443-abd8-9cc2ebf1fce1'), 'Pierce Brosnan later said that production of this movie was "like pulling teeth"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bf82a4d0-ff20-4a5c-b288-cba173539b01'), 'Fifteen BMW 750s were destroyed in the making of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc17b638-fad6-4a4b-8213-b2fa9e2c429c'), 'When James Bond is at Oxford University to "brush up on a little danish", Pierce Brosnan says "Det er en fornøjelse at lære en ny tunge, professor" which can translate to "It''s a pleasure to learn a new tongue, professor". Inga Bergström, played by the danish actress Cecilie Thomsen, then replies. "Jeg vil våge at påstå, at de er et rent naturtalent", which translates to "One might say, that you have a natural talent"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('34693095-924f-4267-97c2-1140f55c1bdd'), 'As shooting began on April 1, 1997, neither Sir Jonathan Pryce nor Teri Hatcher had been cast', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6156631c-678a-43f0-aa98-3bea90bbd47f'), 'In the original drafts of the script, Stamper (Götz Otto) was to have suffered a brain injury that caused pleasure to be registered as pain (and vice versa). The idea was dropped, but a version of it made it into The World Is Not Enough (1999), where the villain Renard is unable to feel pain', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d0a561e-8f0c-4692-b171-349fc8332394'), 'The third and final film in the franchise to show James Bond in his Royal Navy Commander uniform', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('57f4511a-b52f-48e6-a0e4-f8f3779d6f94'), 'H.A.L.O. stands for "High Altitude Low Opening" Jump. Stuntman B.J. Worth had to make eighty jumps out of a plane in order to film the H.A.L.O. jump sequence, eight jumps fewer than the eighty-eight required for Moonraker (1979)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0fc13228-2a84-43d2-bfaa-de550aa68822'), 'Because the second half of this movie was set in Vietnam, the production negotiated for a while for permission to film there. Although it appeared close, the Vietnamese Ministry of Culture and Information eventually refused to allow it. The production decided to use Thailand as Vietnam, with Bangkok substituting for Saigon. At one point during filming, a helicopter mistakenly hovered over the American Embassy to Thailand, causing fears that it was spying', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('64e24726-0708-4812-9087-b07b6727d1e0'), 'Screenwriter Bruce Feirstein''s nine-word pitch to the producers was: "Words are the new weapons; satellites, the new artillery"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('361c056c-e844-4845-80d8-ec580b264e2e'), 'The interiors of James Bond''s Hamburg hotel room were filmed in part of the redecorated ballroom at the Stoke Park golf course where the golf scenes from Goldfinger (1964) had been filmed years earlier. To commemorate the occasion, the management added a photograph of Pierce Brosnan to the golf course next to one they already had of Sean Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77b5d466-3073-48f0-a05a-8c44aaa97abe'), 'In GoldenEye (1995), M (Dame Judi Dench) said: "Unlike the American government, we prefer not to get our bad news from CNN". Ironically in this movie, she gets her intelligence from Elliot Carver''s newspaper "Tomorrow"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff55e93c-1e13-48ed-b552-56f43fbe407c'), 'A young Gerard Butler makes an appearance as "Leading Seaman - H.M.S. Devonshire." He was later considered to star as James Bond in Casino Royale (2006), but turned it down, due to fears of typecasting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4899417a-fe7a-4941-85d8-20aaafc0749c'), 'Product placements, brand integrations, promotional tie-ins, and sponsorships for this movie include: BMW in their second movie in a three-movie promotional deal; L''Oréal cosmetics; Heineken beer; Dunhill; Ericsson cellular phones; Omega watches, James Bond wears an Omega Seamaster watch; Smirnoff Red label vodka; Brioni clothing; Bollinger champagne; Avis Rental Car; and Electronic Arts'' tie-in video game, Tomorrow Never Dies (1999). This is the first movie in film history to have its entire budget be covered in product placement campaigns. Various companies each chipped in enough in endorsements to allow for the $100 million budget', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('933772aa-c31b-4118-b31c-cc6d5f640617'), 'Scenes that take place off the coast of Vietnam were filmed near Thailand instead, near the so-called ''James Bond Island'' that was featured in The Man with the Golden Gun (1974)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3f2fb680-4b11-4790-8b3a-82521dd9e47e'), 'Teri Hatcher said that she accepted her role in this movie to fulfill her then husband''s life-long dream of being married to a Bond Girl. As it turned out, her scenes had to be filmed quickly because of an unexpected pregnancy. She later expressed her dissatisfaction with the part, saying it was "an artificial kind of character to be playing that you don''t get any special satisfaction from it"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('01b742d0-84d1-4f4c-8d68-4a7d06181d54'), 'Though it has long been part of the James Bond character''s reputation in story and dialogue, this is the first instance in the EON Productions official franchise where James Bond has an on-screen relationship with a leading Bond Girl who is known to be married to another man', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da78c393-1541-4fe9-a03c-60d551391a88'), 'Seventeen 750iL Aspen Grey BMWs were used for the car chase. Four were adapted to be "hidden driver" cars, in which a concealed driver would sit in the back using a small steering wheel. Video monitors were attached to cameras hidden in the wing mirrors, and on top of the windshield. Three more BMWs were used as back-up for the hidden drivers. One car was equipped with the sliding glove compartment, revealing a safe, and only used for this one scene. Another, dubbed the "cannon", was specially prepared to be propelled off the roof. It was stripped of as much weight as possible, in order to be fired from a special rig. The remaining seven pristine cars were used only for back-up and exterior shots, including one that was being kept in Hamburg for shooting there', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fe7a42c4-918c-4d6e-a005-5b79bbba13d1'), 'A love scene between 007 and Paris Carver was dropped from this movie, as Teri Hatcher was pregnant at the time. The scene was replaced with the scene in which Elliot Carver watches recorded footage of Paris asking James Bond if he still sleeps with a gun under his pillow, confirming Gupta''s discovery that Bond is a government agent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1867581d-82f4-4559-b975-b8459570666b'), 'This is the fourth of nine movies in which James Bond drives his Aston Martin DB5. The other eight are Goldfinger (1964), Thunderball (1965), GoldenEye (1995), The World Is Not Enough (1999) (on the thermal camera and in a deleted scene), Casino Royale (2006), Skyfall (2012), Spectre (2015), and No Time to Die (2021). The DB5 has appeared with four different license plates: BMT 216A - Goldfinger (1964), Thunderball (1965), Skyfall (2012), and Spectre (2015); BMT 214A - GoldenEye (1995), Tomorrow Never Dies (1997), and The World Is Not Enough (1999); 56526 - Casino Royale (2006), which featured the only left-hand drive DB5 Bond; A 4269 00 - No Time to Die (2021); Therefore, with nine movies, the DB5 car has appeared in more Bond movies than any actor who has played Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5fe028e8-96d5-483d-b811-23ea1c796cd4'), 'James Bond switched from a Walther PPK to a Walther P99 in this movie. The Walther P99 was used until Quantum of Solace (2008), where they went back to the iconic Walther PPK', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0eb69af-88b7-4f07-8e35-ef9b646e3f5e'), 'Teri Hatcher filmed the scene where she is stripped down to her black underwear out of her black dress while she was pregnant', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('24f04048-d970-4133-82dd-48bcf67355ce'), 'The location into which James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) drives his DB5 near the start of this movie also doubled for St. Petersburg in GoldenEye (1995), in the scene where Jack Wade''s (Joe Don Baker''s) car breaks down', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f378a0ba-9c3f-4246-9aa6-85bb9e1e1588'), 'Paris Carver being a woman from 007''s past, whom he once loved, was suggested by Pierce Brosnan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9540603e-0d11-4cd2-8a06-9add1d7da3d7'), 'The sledgehammers used by the actors to try to break into Bond''s BMW car were specially designed props made of balsa wood and foam rubber to avoid actually breaking the glass', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a816193a-1a55-4d85-89c5-19664d59d873'), 'The headline, "The Empire will Strike Back", so admired by Elliot Carver when reviewing media reaction to the impending British attack, mirrors a real headline run by Newsweek during the Falklands War in 1982, picturing H.M.S. Hermes, and the headline "The Empire Strikes Back"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7531d781-5d06-4573-8485-c96bbbb08f4f'), 'The title was inspired by The Beatles song "Tomorrow Never Knows"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('804b4b6f-5536-438f-85e9-9f26ebdcc297'), 'Because snow was an essential ingredient for the opening action sequence, and the existing snow was already melting, the art directors had to truck in loads of extra snow just to meet production requirements. This sequence alone took two weeks to complete', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('14ac6751-5a7e-4228-a4f1-ad2cc1d5d598'), 'Producers considered starting a film franchise based on Wai Lin (Michelle Yeoh), but this never materialized', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6a7426f0-9172-49ee-844b-1112f3db7800'), 'Stunt coordinator Vic Armstrong''s wife stood in for Michelle Yeoh in the motorcycle chase. It was rehearsed over a period of two weeks', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c85eaf47-d27d-4314-907c-072069667f61'), 'The original script had a reappearance from Valentin Zukovsky from GoldenEye (1995). He appeared in The World Is Not Enough (1999)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('05e82011-6bd9-46cf-b3d8-1e68011791f6'), 'MGM exerted a lot of pressure on the producers to come up with a follow-up to GoldenEye (1995) that was as successful. This was mainly at the urgings of billionaire Kirk Kerkorian, who had recently bought the company, and wanted the release to coincide with MGM''s public stock offering', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4f328438-e410-4bb8-b70b-e41ba8123440'), 'David Arnold was chosen to compose the score on the personal recommendation of John Barry', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1a8f36dd-cac5-4464-8c4f-e1132646c57e'), 'The first draft of the script was set during the July 1997 transfer of Hong Kong from British to Chinese rule, with Carver a zealot bent on destroying Hong Kong, rather than hand it over to the Chinese. According to director Roger Spottiswoode, this plot was dropped when former U.S. Secretary of State Henry Kissinger, who was acting as a consultant on the production, warned that, if something actually did occur during the handover in real life, this movie would look ridiculous. Furthermore, this would have instantly dated a movie that was due to open in November, so in January 1997, when production was kicking off, a frantic re-write of the script was taking place. With all of the actors and actresses on board and ready to film, the new script also had to tally with their visions of their characters. Sir Jonathan Pryce and Teri Hatcher were unhappy with the route their characters were taking in the new script, prompting even more re-writes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bba8f5f4-0dc6-4459-ad3f-ed7d3352afcc'), 'Martin Campbell declined the chance to direct again, not wanting to make two James Bond movies in a row. He opted to direct The Mask of Zorro (1998) instead', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b3932544-ed20-4da4-a3e4-61a0ffcc2dfe'), 'This is the first James Bond movie in the official franchise to have a running time under two hours since Diamonds Are Forever (1971). The next movie to run under two hours was Quantum of Solace (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b30078cd-cfc3-4efd-b462-d893378254ff'), 'In the novelization, James Bond revealed that Natalya Simonova from GoldenEye (1995) married a hockey player. This happened to Izabella Scorupco in real life', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fdf08178-9faa-4a94-9174-c2c6ce2bad98'), 'The ships used in this movie are Type-23 Duke Class Anti-Submarine frigates. The interior shots were all filmed at the H.M.S. Dryad ship simulator, and most of the personnel in the background were real Royal Navy personnel. Most of the dialogue and commands are very accurate, though some has been modified so the viewing public can understand it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d927fe1e-6b2b-4020-b4ff-23e3b68ea719'), 'Elliott Carver''s newspaper factory is the printing presses of London''s Daily Telegraph and Evening Standard', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ef1fb199-d37f-42f0-aed4-7d96e2187509'), 'This movie cost $52 million more than GoldenEye (1995), the largest increase in budget between two James Bond movies, as of 2015', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b1306d31-0416-4296-b587-5aa33b89803b'), 'Vic Armstrong was under serious consideration to direct, and would have been next to be offered the job if Roger Spottiswoode had not accepted. Spottiswoode called Armstrong to tell him this and to apologize, saying "I''ve just taken your movie." He then asked Armstrong if he wanted to direct the second unit', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d9f67380-2cd3-4a24-811f-cc20b1be2842'), 'Stunt performers Mark Southworth and Wendy Leech performed the skyscraper jump on May 21, 1997, in Bangkok, with temperatures reaching as high as 110 degrees Fahrenheit (43 degrees Celsius). Wendy also doubled for Michelle Yeoh during the motorcycle chase with Jean-Pierre Goy riding the BMW R1200C cruiser. A dummy was strapped to Goy''s back, as he performed the rooftop jump over the helicopter on the same bike on July 24th. The helicopters blades had been removed to be added digitally in post-production. On that same day, Pierce Brosnan and Michelle Yeoh were filming their close-ups hanging thirty feet up at the side of a five-story building, to complete the Carver building stunt', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a8e6f927-6a08-4e53-88c1-061360a9a7e0'), 'The novelization, and the deleted scenes, give Elliot Carver''s backstory. He is the illegitimate son of media mogul Lord Roverman, whom Carver drove to bankruptcy, and blackmails into suicide, later taking over his business', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c87bbe96-56be-4a45-93a3-a11417c79dc0'), 'The opening arms bazaar sequence was originally intended to appear in The Living Daylights (1987). The weapons being sold at the arms bazaar were described as a Chinese Long March Scud rockets, and on the jet aircraft were Soviet SP-5 torpedoes. Neither of these weapon systems actually exist, however. The Long March program was a Chinese program designed to launch missiles into space, and the "SP-5" nuclear torpedo simply doesn''t exist in Russian, or the former Soviet arsenal', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b2e6b3b8-f943-4f41-99fe-2c921105200d'), 'Even though this was the 18th film in Eon Productions'' James Bond series, released 35 years after Dr. No, this is the first film in the series in which Bond is not rendered unconscious in some way either by being knocked-out, drugged, gassed, hit by a tranquilizer gun, etc. In some movies, such as Goldfinger, this happens to him as many as three times', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b0b0dbd1-0ac3-4cc7-88a5-fdc16152b48e'), 'The title song tune was chosen by way of a competition. There were about twelve entries, including songs from Emil Jørgensen, Pulp, Saint Etienne, Marc Almond, Sheryl Crow, and David Arnold. The first choice was written and performed by Swan Lee, but they were turned down, because they were not famous enough. It was suggested that another artist sing the song instead, but Swan Lee rejected this idea. Pulp wrote a theme song, which later appeared on the B-side to the group''s single "Help the Aged", following a title change to "Tomorrow Never Lies", the same name as the working title for this movie. Sheryl Crow''s song, which won out, did not chart in the U.S., but charted at the number eleven spot in the U.K.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a1a7155c-6712-4031-ab8c-2f0e838fc748'), 'Not counting the regular characters of James Bond, Q, M, and Miss Moneypenny, this is the first Bond movie to contain absolutely no Ian Fleming references (GoldenEye (1995) was named for Fleming''s estate, and Licence to Kill (1989) used elements from several Fleming stories)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b8e08431-4f93-4631-94a0-ba9e14c4567a'), 'The Walther P99 gun that Bond uses in the film sold for £9,987', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8f5e6b3d-fec9-408c-a771-7b2451a50b09'), 'The Daily Mail reported that director Roger Spottiswoode and screenwriter Bruce Feirstein were no longer on speaking terms, and that crew members had threatened to resign, with one saying "All the happiness and teamwork, which is the hallmark of Bond has disappeared completely." This was denied by Pierce Brosnan, who claimed, "It was nothing more than good old creative argy-bargy", with Spottiswoode saying, "It has all been made up. Nothing important really went wrong"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fa3e4fdb-bd9b-49a2-96cf-8e57d99e7814'), 'In Don''t Tug on Superman''s Cape (1995), Teri Hatcher''s character Lois Lane has a dream in which she is the Bond Girl Miss Goodbottom in the movie "The Spy Who Left Me", a reference to The Spy Who Loved Me (1977)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2a168239-3ea4-4803-9a33-b6d1cc6f2f4d'), 'A lot of the model work and underwater sequences were filmed in the "Titanic" tank at Twentieth Century Fox''s Baja Studios in Mexico, just a few days after Titanic (1997) had completed filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f4de03cf-4203-4e63-bed1-38273960ba85'), 'Sales of real and toy replica Walther P99 pistols went through the roof after this movie was released', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('88a1b955-3e35-47d6-9342-af9122d2eabf'), 'Because the producers had already secured a release date, the production couldn''t find studio space. They ended up shooting much of the interiors in a converted Asda (the British branch of Walmart) warehouse', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff024ec5-e5a9-4ca3-a2aa-d1ba619e3787'), 'Natasha Henstridge was in the running to play Paris Carver at one point', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('29bd0d60-4c3e-4f58-8aa7-05d5a09973b2'), 'The BMW 750i that James Bond uses in this movie is the first Q-Branch car in the franchise that has four doors', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('757f16cd-769a-429b-802e-8f604f506b9a'), 'The DVD release contains a music track where people can watch the movie without dialogue and with the score and background music only', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a288dab-8a9a-47a5-b057-1d6808feaeb4'), 'Sir Jonathan Pryce (Elliot Carver) played James Bond creator Ian Fleming in Ian Fleming: Where Bond Began (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ae1b733a-bc31-43aa-be9e-a19364533390'), 'Five hundred extras were used for Elliot Carver''s launch party where James Bond reconnects with Paris', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f7330380-d666-4fb3-8f6b-867af9178043'), 'The character of Henry Gupta (Ricky Jay) was originally written as a young man from India', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d8e51bc-23b6-420f-9d2e-3a006141470e'), 'The first James Bond film that failed to open at #1 at the domestic box office since Licence to Kill (1989). It came in second after Titanic (1997), which opened the same weekend. This is Pierce Brosnan''s only Bond film that failed to open at #1', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da78a19b-5b0c-46ef-88a8-84c3d83ce9cf'), 'This was the first of three James Bond movies to be adapted into books by then-current Bond novelist Raymond Benson. Benson''s version of Bruce Feirstein''s screenplay is suitably expanded, and includes some nods to past Bond movies, including the suggestion that Bond was lying when he said he had taken a course in Oriental languages in You Only Live Twice (1967). The book is styled more after Fleming''s novels, as opposed to this movie, with detailed backstories given to characters such as Elliot Carver, Stamper, and Paris Carver, missing from the movie, which gave the characters more depth. Wai Lin''s activities in China tracking General Chang before she travels to Hamburg (omitted from the movie) are also included. Differences from this movie: Carver suffers from Temporomandibular joint dysfunction (TMJ disorder) due to stress, and takes regular painkillers as a result. General Chang''s fate is revealed, stating he was found by the Police in Beijing hiding inside a stall in a women''s restroom', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e0c39ef-fa64-4f45-b1b2-262ef8dcb497'), 'Felix Leiter is mentioned in the novelization, where it is revealed that he now works for Pinkerton''s. This happened to him in the novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ffe28392-ca53-47bf-ba18-23ee7f25b1a4'), 'Chief of Staff Bill Tanner was intended to return in this movie after appearing in GoldenEye (1995), but Michael Kitchen was unavailable. He returned for The World Is Not Enough (1999)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('26824459-1981-4fdb-9a60-f4f433486ded'), 'The alleged "Atlantic Hotel" car park rooftop belongs to an electronics department store. This car park is located on Steintorwall/Steinstraße in Hamburg, but not in the neighborhood of the real "Hotel Atlantic". Bond''s car is then propelled from the top of yet another building, a clothing retailer on Mönckebergstrasse/Lange Mühren, which has no parking facilities of its own, let alone its own roof', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Tomorrow Never Dies'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('953f3dc1-fce4-4812-896f-ab8d670ae409'), 'When the real MI6 learned that this movie would shoot a scene around their Headquarters, they moved to prohibit it, citing a security risk. However, Foreign Secretary Robin Cook, at the urging of Member of Parliament Janet Anderson, moved to overrule them and allow the shoot, stating, "After all Bond has done for Britain, it was the least we could do for Bond"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f5433815-1a72-4bc5-a774-d6487d3972ff'), 'Desmond Llewelyn (Q) died in an car accident soon after this movie was released. Llewellyn said just before his death that he was planning to appear in the next Bond movie. The video release was dedicated to Llewelyn, and featured a tribute montage of his appearances in seventeen Bond movies over thirty-six years. Not only was this his final Bond movie, it was the last James Bond movie of the second millennium', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0e3453b2-c4ff-4322-bbe1-561bf611ce39'), 'The adjusting of the tie underwater by James Bond in the opening boat chase was an idea conceived by Pierce Brosnan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6e447026-056c-4d65-b33d-da5a9c3480ef'), 'In the warehouse that Zukovsky (Robbie Coltrane) has turned into an operations room, the girlie pictures seen on the walls are of former Bond Girls', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4f0ad1a8-bf2c-4d98-8703-f2bb150df521'), 'The scene in which James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) grabs the cables on the Millennium Dome required extraordinarily difficult stunt work. Director Michael Apted intentionally left a shot of one of the stuntmen missing a cable he was attempting to grab in the final cut. Apted included the miscue in order to highlight how difficult the scene had been to film, and as an honor to the stunt performers who worked on the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff52c7a5-969a-4c3f-af5d-8a7f424f561a'), 'To create the effect when Bond looks through his X-ray glasses, the actors were first filmed in their regular costumes, then again this time wearing special costumes that revealed the shapes of guns and knives underneath translucent clothing. The two were then matted together', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1fd557b-1220-4aa7-b23c-38c625b8565a'), 'In the Scottish Headquarters castle, a portrait of Bernard Lee (the original M) hangs behind the current M''s (Dame Judi Dench''s) desk', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98e0e064-7e6c-4b27-83d9-d44721789e38'), 'When Q (Desmond Llewelyn) introduces James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) to his successor, played by John Cleese, Bond jokingly asks "Does that make him R?" The character''s name is never mentioned in this movie, but is credited as "R"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f5388a77-a284-46e1-b4ca-58902aecdc80'), 'During one day of filming, Sir Sean Connery stopped by the movie set to witness Pierce Brosnan doing the stunt where he escapes a massive fireball while hanging on some wires. Afterwards, when Brosnan was packing up Connery spoke to him and said "Are they paying you enough money?"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d33fc793-0412-45ec-aa43-bc5ddb679abb'), 'Denise Richards was attracted to the role of Dr. Christmas Jones, as she found the part to be "brainy", "athletic", and had "depth of character", a change in direction from previous Bond Girls. Audiences did not agree, and often consider Christmas to be the worst Bond Girl ever. This was the first Bond movie to win a Razzie (in the category of Worst Supporting Actress), for the same reason', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1dbaf0b0-5c7f-45e0-9b1a-f1bc1be51e1c'), 'The title is the translation of the Latin motto, "Orbis non sufficit", given to George Lazenby''s Bond, when he researches his own coat of arms, in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969). The motto also appears in the original Ian Fleming novels. It was the motto of the Spanish King Felipe II', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('488c8bfb-9782-4ac8-bd34-5323d58671ef'), 'Much of Robbie Coltrane''s lines were derived from cut scenes from the GoldenEye (1995) script', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('66f75249-0b8f-4bab-ab72-37542e63124d'), 'Before the shoot even began, a set was being built in Turkey, and was almost finished. One day when director Michael Apted was touring around Istanbul, a bombing took place. Therefore, shots that included the cast were never shot in Istanbul, according to Apted, due to security reasons. Not a single cast member went to Istanbul. The shots of Robert Carlyle and his men getting off the boat on the jetty at Elektra''s (Sophie Marceau''s) palace were shot in the tank at Pinewood against a bluescreen or greenscreen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('95acc49b-18c5-4cd4-ba75-87c097ca96ce'), 'The boat chase took seven weeks to shoot, as the river Thames'' nine-mile-per-hour boat speed limit had to be factored in. The filming of the boat chase sequence was broadcast live over the Internet, via webcams set up at specific points over the Thames. The scene was not originally intended to be part of the opening sequence, until test audiences said that the jump-from-the-window opener was anti-climactic. As such, it was brought forward, and had to be shortened. As it is now, this fourteen to fifteen minute opener, is one of the longest pre-credits sequence in a James Bond movie. After being the longest for about twenty-two years, it now places second to the pre-titles sequence in No Time to Die (2021), which runs for about twenty minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0eeb198e-9be7-423e-85b2-2a8ce8c8275e'), 'The writers modelled Q''s goodbye scene on Merlin''s farewell to King Arthur', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0dbab599-698a-4370-a1a1-c5bf951b979a'), 'When the producers visited BMW''s plant, the company''s representatives were left speechless at being apprised of how their brand new Z8 would be used', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7eff75a4-c34a-461b-b5b5-1cf650a64d41'), 'The highest grossing of all of the James Bond movies released in the twentieth century', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9b1e33f3-b609-4548-a23a-64c1ccfd097f'), 'Serena Scott Thomas did her love scene with Bond herself, turning down the offer of letting a body double do it for her', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('309db3e1-5bbb-4fd2-ac8c-3ce295885c77'), 'Director Michael Apted stated that casting the right actress to play Elektra King was critical since the character was the center of the story. He wanted a European actress with great range and an enigmatic quality - but preferably not a British actress. For Dr. Christmas Jones, he wanted a young, vibrant Gen-X American actress in her twenties who could bring sassy flair and tomboy attitude to contrast against the character''s beauty (which she is often ogled over - much to her irritation). Roger Ebert agreed with Apted''s casting choices: in his review of The World is Not Enough, he called Sophie Marceau and Denise Richards "first rate" as Elektra and Christmas', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec28c609-1cc5-48a0-935c-169cb914e690'), 'All of the pipes representing Elektra''s pipeline were made of cardboard', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6d661ce5-7fa0-4fa8-b853-bca56b1c2c3a'), 'The five-bladed buzzsaw was originally intended to be in GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a11689bc-9588-43e6-8d31-fd67f01d5667'), 'This was the first movie to feature the newly constructed Millennium Dome, built for London''s New Year''s celebration of 1999/2000 (even though the new millennium didn''t begin until January 1, 2001). Supposedly, the original script contained a line for M (Dame Judi Dench) at the end of the opening sequence which read, "Well, at least the Millennium Dome has some use." That line was cut', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab0197c4-e951-426e-a049-714cc58663ba'), 'The opening pre-title sequence is so long that, in theaters, the titles and opening song didn''t occur until one minute into reel two', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1092421-b578-42e5-a38b-ee3b24e1a657'), 'The Scottish castle used as MI6''s secret headquarters is the same castle used in Highlander (1986). It''s called "Eilean Donan Castle", and is located near the Isle of Skye, West Scotland', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a640098e-74ee-4960-8ca8-5699bce63942'), 'Maria Grazia Cucinotta originally auditioned for the part of Elektra King, but director Michael Apted didn''t think her English was good enough to play her convincingly. Cucinotta gladly accepted the smaller role of the Cigar Girl, as she really wanted to be in a Bond movie. MGM preferred Sharon Stone for the role of Elektra', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('97462865-ddb4-42c7-8e2a-d98cd1f1dbb0'), 'Sophie Marceau''s breast can be seen in her bed scene between Elektra King and James Bond. This happens just after Bond says "Enough ice for one night". Apparently, the glimpse had been airbrushed out, so it cannot be seen in the trailer, and remains only in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cdf92892-ac15-4448-8d8c-14ed74b9314b'), 'After Neal Purvis and Robert Wade finished their version of the script, director Michael Apted wanted the character of Elektra King to be further developed. The studio suggested that Apted''s then wife, screenwriter Dana Stevens, do an uncredited polish. Stevens worked on the script for three weeks, increasing the importance of both Elektra and M but this version pushed 007 into the background. Bruce Feirstein was asked to deliver a final rewrite, making sure that James Bond remained the focal point of the film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('31f63399-6669-48ba-a6d2-ba0b2f16e361'), 'According to a 1999 article in Entertainment Weekly at the time of this film''s release, studio executives were worried the Bond franchise was not drawing a younger crowd despite a reasonably successful revamp with Pierce Brosnan in 1995. Hence, they pushed for Denise Richards to be cast as Dr. Christmas Jones. This film went on to gross a then-record first weekend opening for a Bond film of $35.5 million. This was about $10 million more than the previous two Brosnan Bond films'' respective opening weekends. Box office analysts at the time credited the inclusion of Richards in the cast as the likely reason for the increase in opening weekend ticket sales. She was highly recognizable to the younger crowd the studio was after', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1ecc9e12-f521-4320-ace6-f835d71cb155'), 'The method by which the parahawk pilot survives his fall in the ski-chase scene (deploying a parachute after Bond lures him off a cliff) is highly reminiscent of the opening of The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). The method by which Bond downs him (collapsing his canopy by slicing it with the sharp edge of his ski) is the same way stuntman Rick Sylvester was almost killed while filming the sequence, one of his skis detaching, and nearly clipping the edge of the parachute', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d81718a4-576b-4aaa-a416-e54e48eb8c3c'), 'Elektra''s villa in Baku is, in reality, Kücuksu Kasri, an Ottoman summer residence built in the nineteenth century, and located in Istanbul, Turkey', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('313d2331-b434-49e3-90b1-b8e5ed2c7e44'), 'Elektra King''s oil pumping facility, with the oil pipeline on its roof, was the Motorola building in North Swindon, England. The building, which was clearly visible from the A417/A419 dual carriageway, had a distinctive heat exchanger on its roof in the form of a long cylinder. The production team used CGI to extend this cylinder and form the pipeline', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('92ddcacf-663c-41a1-b08f-5e0c1ef266ab'), 'This movie''s story was inspired by a segment in the November 13, 1997 episode of ABC News Nightline (1979) featuring Daniel Yergin. It was seen by producer Barbara Broccoli on a plane in November 1997. The episode reported the last great oil discovery on the planet was in the region of Eastern Europe. It covered pipelines in the area, and discussed the grand reservoirs of oil that exist below the Caspian Sea. It told of the rise of small towns in the region that have grown into centers of grand affluence, which has included the building of numerous casinos. The episode showed how this oil reserve was now an opportunity for the western world to capitalize, as it was no longer a Russian jurisdiction, and as such, major oil companies now had interests there. Broccoli hypothesized how a James Bond villain might want to create a monopoly by removing all competitors and owning the only pipeline in the region', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fb98b4b2-377b-496e-ab36-7073dbf0c01a'), 'At a press conference in Hong Kong on December 2, 1999 not long after this film''s release, Pierce Brosnan defended Denise Richards performance as Dr. Christmas Jones. He stated the criticism leveled at her was misguided and missed the point. This is because Christmas Jones was meant to be a very specific, vividly unconventional scientist who is not anyone''s idea of a typical nuclear physicist - and consequently has a chip on her shoulder because of the treatment she gets - especially from men. Roger Ebert clearly got this, and called Richards "first rate" as Jones. The Hong Kong press conference wherein Brosnan defends Richards can be found in the Special Features area of this film''s Blu Ray release', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('554a1434-45be-4c56-882c-7a7251b7fa56'), 'Sarah Donohue, a British model with several years of powerboat racing experience, was the stunt double for Maria Grazia Cucinotta in the boat chase scene. Immediately prior to this job, she had recovered from serious injuries sustained in a powerboat racing accident. Being a blonde meant that she had to wear a wig', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ebb2e37a-a07f-4dd1-b791-550bd12c49ab'), 'The first James Bond movie to be shot in Pinewood Studios since The Living Daylights (1987)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db36d2f2-23b0-4079-9dba-d6384ab6ca01'), 'Thirty-five boats were used to create the chase down the Thames', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b61ac5e9-0a33-45a6-bc68-6cf4f3550dba'), 'Two shooting locations had to be postponed, and filming had to be switched to Spain. The skiing locale was changed due to avalanches in the French Alps, and filming in Turkey was halted due to political unrest. However, a secret filming unit, comprised of twelve crew, did film in Istanbul, under the fake cover movie title "Destiny"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c9cf9bc9-5e4f-4f4b-9de5-100d88bda362'), 'Producer Barbara Broccoli was a big fan of Sir Peter Jackson''s Heavenly Creatures (1994), and was interested in Jackson directing this movie. However, when she saw Jackson''s The Frighteners (1996), she was put off by his style. Joe Dante was another director possibility. Had Jackson been hired, he would''ve been one of three New Zealanders to direct a Bond film, the other two being Martin Campbell (GoldenEye (1995) and Casino Royale (2006)) and Lee Tamahori (Die Another Day (2002))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('32ff097c-5588-462f-befe-84d165b7f7f8'), 'The Caucasus skiing chase sequence was filmed in and around Chamonix, France. Filming was delayed due to an avalanche, but the crew assisted with the rescue operations', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('824b7d02-20c1-44b5-83bf-2c97a5cd86cc'), 'The line "There''s no point in living if you can''t feel alive" is quoted three times in this movie. It''s also a line in the title song by the band Garbage. However, it is not heard during the title sequence, as the song, like many over the years, is edited for time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e906bbbd-4535-4fb3-bb01-2f474a81a577'), 'Roger Spottiswoode was asked to direct, but he turned it down, feeling tired after the chaotic production of Tomorrow Never Dies (1997)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b129da8b-053c-4e23-9c20-40aa75ba1269'), 'At the time of release, this movie and Sleepy Hollow (1999) were the only two movies in U.S. history to open on the same day and each gross $30 million in their opening weekends', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('001b648e-b670-4f3b-b4f8-f91ce4dec4ec'), 'Dr. Christmas Jones (Denise Richards) wearing a green tank top and shorts was written as a nod to video game icon Lara Croft. James Bond was an influence behind Lara Croft and Daniel Craig, who succeeded Pierce Brosnan in the role of James Bond in Casino Royale (2006), appeared opposite Angelina Jolie in Lara Croft: Tomb Raider (2001). Jolie was strongly considered for the role of Vesper Lynd in Casino Royale (2006), which went to Eva Green', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5dcaac31-7bac-466c-8f66-794e9c3467fb'), 'In For Your Eyes Only (1981), Melina Havelock (Carole Bouquet) explains to Bond that "Greek women, like Elektra, always avenge their loved ones." Elektra King also has a line in this movie about James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) losing loved ones, which the writers intended as a reference to Paris Carver''s (Teri Hatcher''s) death in Tomorrow Never Dies (1997)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1ccef479-fd52-4081-8e9e-75f9508ac427'), 'Robbie Coltrane''s appearance as Russian mobster Zukovsky marks him as one of the few supporting characters to appear in more than one movie. (He previously appeared in GoldenEye (1995).) Other characters to have been in a Bond movie more than once are Clifton James'' Sheriff J.W. Pepper, who was in Live and Let Die (1973) and The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), and "Jaws", played by Richard Kiel, who appeared in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) and Moonraker (1979). Also, Sylvia Trench, played by Eunice Gayson, who appeared in Dr. No (1962) and From Russia with Love (1963). David Hedison also appeared in two films (Live and Let Die (1973) and Licence to Kill (1989))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('89d56d92-2dc2-4b5a-825c-9e56c4c1ce26'), 'When he arrives in Azerbaijan, James Bond introduces himself as being from Universal Exports. In the Ian Fleming novels, "Universal Exports" is a cover identity for the Secret Intelligence Service (MI6), which wasn''t officially recognized as existing until 1994', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('819a9735-8a9d-495e-9267-ac5909ed9b48'), 'The destruction of Valentin''s factory operations took approximately five months to complete', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fcefe3b3-7bb4-402f-ab98-e5d9829eae7a'), 'With the release of this movie, this makes Pierce Brosnan one of two James Bonds who own a whole decade to himself. In the 60s, Sir Sean Connery had to share with George Lazenby. In the 70s, Connery shared with Sir Roger Moore. Moore shared the 80s with Timothy Dalton. Pierce Brosnan shared the 2000s with Daniel Craig, and Craig owns the 2010s. Even though Dalton didn''t resign from the role until 1994, all of the Bond movies from the 90s starred Pierce as Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('17b9b15a-eb73-4469-b34f-8eb18cba76d5'), 'Sir Robert King''s funeral is set in Scotland, but was filmed just outside of London. Dame Judi Dench was appearing in a play in the West End at the time, and wasn''t able to fly to Scotland', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bc95b60a-a841-45ee-b3b5-6fafa5f1b1f9'), 'The opening banker sequence was originally set in Havana, Cuba (it includes the Cigar Girl) then was moved to Geneva, Switzerland (the Swiss Bank thing), but was finally set in Bilbao, Spain', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bdc02989-f180-44f0-ac68-bf205c6dc028'), 'In the script, it is explained that Sir Robert King (David Calder) inherited the oil fortune from his wife''s family. Her father had no male heirs, so he left the property to his son-in-law', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3ed7c629-436b-4be4-8669-fdbb9438aafa'), 'Due to his background with dramas and thrillers rather than action movies, director Michael Apted was reportedly chosen to direct this film because of its character-driven script. Also, Apted''s experience directing movies like Nell, Coal Miner''s Daughter, Gorillas In The Mist, Gorky Park, and Agatha, which all had strong, complex female characters, was also another factor. This is evident in the final film, with Elektra and M getting more shading than usual. Even the supporting role of Christmas Jones gets some humanity and complexity when she tells Bond she is avoiding personal questions after he asks her why she of all people is in Kazakhstan', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f70ae57b-7575-43ae-8a1f-afdb894de7d4'), 'Before Robbie Coltrane''s character is reintroduced into the franchise, a neon profile of his face can be spotted above the entrance to his casino in Baku', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e1d1940-e7cb-4658-b120-7bb63e76fee0'), 'Sharon Stone, Catherine Zeta-Jones, Monica Bellucci, Maria Grazia Cucinotta, Milla Jovovich, Elizabeth Hurley, and Vera Farmiga were considered to play Elektra King, and Natasha Henstridge, Tiffani Thiessen, and Geri Halliwell-Horner were considered to play Christmas Jones. Cucinotta was instead cast as an unnamed "cigar girl," and Bellucci was later cast as Lucia Sciarra in Spectre (2015)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8f82cc3a-b130-4122-bfc6-af15b868ac92'), 'The BMW Z8 driven by James Bond in this movie was the final part of a three-movie product placement deal with BMW, but due to filming preceding the release of the Z8 by a few months, several working mock-ups and models were manufactured for filming purposes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('549f3789-59be-4820-8d4f-4e7e006716fd'), 'The ski-parahawk attack scene was inspired by the ski chase in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969). Filmmakers wanted to connect this movie with that one, from which its title is derived', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e52e5a8-6b36-4430-be16-bab8bbc10d4e'), 'To help promote this movie, skywriters were hired to write "007" in the sky across the U.S.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f6da7a9b-9953-4f1a-8254-2bda76704fbe'), 'Second James Bond movie to use Turkey as a location; From Russia with Love (1963) was the first. A big car chase through the old town of Istanbul was ultimately eliminated, but the idea was reused for the opening scene in Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d96339a0-e585-4a13-ba08-8ddba2741973'), 'The title song, "The World is Not Enough", sung by Garbage did not chart in the U.S., while in the U.K., it peaked at the number eleven spot on the charts. The soundtrack album went to the number one hundred six spot on the U.K. charts. There are two versions of the soundtrack, the second one differs in that it includes a twentieth track, titled "Sweetest Coma Again", sung by Luna Sea with DJ Krush. This track is only included on the Japanese album release, as this song played during the closing credits of the Japanese release of the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('acde0f74-ce83-459f-85f1-0d772970b130'), 'Denise Richards has been widely-criticized as being too young for her role as Dr. Christmas Jones. However, Roger Ebert praised her in his review of this film and called both Richards and Sophie Marceau "first rate." Ebert clearly recognized that Dr. Christmas Jones was meant to be a young, twenty something, snarky Generation X with attitude American sidekick to contrast sharply against Elektra''s cooler and more mysterious European enigma. And at the age of 28 during filming, Richards was the right age for a rising nuclear physicist toiling in a pay-your-dues job dismantling abandoned nukes and decommissioning mothballed test sites in the middle of Kazakhstan. Richards plays the role just fine in this context', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('47c24566-2e31-4ec5-aac2-ccee16b86a67'), 'It was rumored this movie originally had a different plot, and that it was going to be dark like Licence to Kill (1989) and GoldenEye (1995), and that it was going to focus on James Bond''s offspring (the main villain) and it would be revealed Bond had fathered a child he never knew existed, and that the child was given up for adoption, hence the title "The World is Not Enough", which is Bond''s family motto, and that the original plot was rejected', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec205708-eb26-47f5-a007-22bb41bae765'), 'Until the release of Die Another Day (2002), this was the highest grossing James Bond movie of all time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9a370db7-9396-47cc-b688-94c567722bb4'), 'In its opening weekend, this movie competed with Sleepy Hollow (1999). However, both survived the fierce competition, each collecting over $30 million, and ended up being big box-office successes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('45249453-3c25-4e79-96ef-c892e21b6dc0'), 'Zukovsky has a gun concealed in a cane. A similar weapon appeared in the novel "Casino Royale"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('734c32a3-3069-4527-bd8d-85b74fc5ec9e'), 'The title originates from the epitaph of Alexander the Great', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bf2e5a7c-849e-4747-9047-dacf864334d1'), 'Published newspaper reports during production of this movie indicated that, as the last James Bond movie of the millennium, this would feature cameos by virtually every surviving previous Bond girl. Ursula Andress, Dame Diana Rigg, Famke Janssen, and Barbara Bach were mentioned by name as amongst those slated to appear. Sadly, this idea, if it was ever more than a media rumor, never came to fruition', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab7438f4-c45b-4dd3-9af3-40d514ed357e'), 'Out of all the principal roles in The World is Not Enough, the character of Christmas Jones is the one who changed the most from initial treatment to final shooting script/actual film. She started out as a French Polynesian insurance agent from Lloyds of London. Her profession was changed because of similarities with the insurance agent female lead of The Thomas Crown Affair remake that Pierce Brosnan was filming at the time. She briefly became a bounty hunter, before making her a nuclear physicist who is more pivotal to the plot. As a final change, Christmas Jones'' nationality switched from French Polynesian to American when Sophie Marceau was cast as the leading lady, Elektra King. The studio did not want two French actresses in the two key female roles. They also wanted to Christmas to appeal more to the younger American demographic', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('466980d8-375d-4c63-b64d-d94cd1259493'), 'Tiffani Thiessen was considered for the role of Dr. Christmas Jones', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('029bfec7-8232-42ec-b345-c4d3a4325001'), 'The scene where Zukovsky (Robbie Coltrane) is splashing around in a pool of his own caviar was filmed on Coltrane''s birthday', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('594ae675-e035-4fb0-9b14-6a8dd2d2b91b'), 'Dr. Christmas Jones has a tattoo of the dove/olive branch symbol for World Peace on her stomach. Her tattoo is displayed prominently on the US Release Poster and is glimpsed briefly when she takes off the radiation suit at the Kazakhstan test site where she first meets Bond. The tattoo is meant to add subtle character detail defining Jones as a younger idealistic Gen-X scientist who specifically sought to work for the International Decommissioning Agency (IDA)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'The World Is Not Enough'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('6f464c2d-32ab-46e5-8186-7793ba00b5b4'), 'The book that 007 picks up from the Cuban sleeper, along with a revolver, is "A Field Guide to Birds of the West Indies", written by James Bond. Ian Fleming, an avid birdwatcher, named Bond after the author', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('24652c57-9a95-478a-82b2-04805a1959a7'), 'Pierce Brosnan disliked the gadgets and overblown effects of this movie. He suggested to the producers that the franchise go back to its more low-key, darker roots. Coincidentally, after Brosnan left, the next Bond movie was the low key and darker Casino Royale (2006), which was stripped of gadgets and extravagant visual effects and stunts', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('82061fcc-4cc7-4cc4-bfc8-7f5be9f0df15'), 'The use of hovercraft by the North Korean Army to circumvent the minefields of the Demilitarized Zone is entirely fictional. However, the science show MythBusters (2003) tested the concept and found it plausible', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9017c696-9d8e-4ba8-81a2-c6d73eb2b368'), 'Pierce Brosnan''s least favorite Bond movie in which he appeared', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a0aebb1b-6f47-43cc-9c39-9fc0f4b5b25b'), 'For the sword fight, the filmmakers decreased the film speed to make it look as if the actors were moving faster than they actually were', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1a49930a-b257-4363-99dc-cab3b85e7fa3'), 'Sir Roger Moore actively voiced his displeasure with this movie, citing the invisible car and the weak CGI as being a low for the franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40f77b8d-482f-482f-9609-dd31336e3ccc'), 'One of the problems the crew encountered when shooting the North Korean segments in England was that there were only two fully qualified stuntmen of Asian descent in the U.K. To get around that, they tapped local martial arts clubs for more talent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8a3e89c4-533e-4944-875f-398a325d6c00'), 'While filming their love scene in Cuba, Halle Berry choked on a fig, requiring Pierce Brosnan to perform the Heimlich maneuver', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56bfde98-ea4b-476d-8831-0f708bce19f1'), 'Theatrical movie debut of Rosamund Pike (Miranda Frost)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('be69f034-51e9-44e8-b835-5b5602e7733d'), 'Debris from a smoke grenade landed in Halle Berry''s eye during filming. She required a thirty-minute operation to remove it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e54537ab-2224-4efb-8b90-8057f68cf16a'), 'Q (John Cleese) says he believes the watch he gives James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) for the assignment is his twentieth. This is a reference to the fact that this movie was the twentieth James Bond movie in the EON Productions franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d6b16cd8-3978-413a-9005-dae18d8079fb'), 'The ice palace took approximately six months to construct', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('89fa2264-474b-4ae2-ad62-db20611ec3c1'), 'Rosamund Pike was cast five days before the start of principal photography. Her first acting on-screen was her scene opposite Dame Judi Dench, something she found to be overwhelmingly daunting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('18c83566-e1d6-47e8-a276-ba2607d24121'), 'A spin-off was planned, featuring Halle Berry''s character Jinx Johnson as the lead. Neal Purvis and Robert Wade wrote for two months, and even a director was hired (Stephen Frears). However, after the low box-office performances of other female-character-driven action movies like Charlie''s Angels: Full Throttle (2003) and Lara Croft: Tomb Raider - The Cradle of Life (2003) (they weren''t failures, but they only managed to make a small profit worldwide), MGM pulled the plug on the project. Halle Berry has said that she would love to return as Jinx in another Bond movie. She has allegedly said that she would like to do it so much, she would do the role for free', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2a1c9e74-cf06-4e4f-b405-a7316b09e769'), 'Producers Michael G. Wilson and Barbara Broccoli, and screenwriters Neal Purvis and Robert Wade have admitted that they completely misjudged what the fans wanted from the franchise, and accept the blame for the outlandish tone of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dde71263-d9ec-4065-86e9-44e4136a984a'), 'Rosamund Pike had to leave the film set for one day to go to her English Literature graduation ceremony at Oxford University', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dca02259-207a-43c7-87a6-5cca3a634457'), 'Twenty companies paid $70 million to have their products featured in this movie, a record at the time. Upon release, the amount of product placement throughout the film became a contemporaneous point of criticism with many critics mockingly referring to the film as "Buy Another Day". The producers subsequently decided to limit the companies involved in product placement to eight for the next film, Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5df6d871-c896-44ec-b191-ae5348ee9cb0'), 'Pierce Brosnan''s knee injury, which he incurred in doing one of his own stunts in the opening hovercraft segment, aggravated an old injury and caused the production to stop shooting for seven days as with him being in virtually every scene in this sequence it was impossible to film around him. This was the first time any Bond movie has had to shut down production due to injury', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ca9807b5-9cf7-459b-9d27-59baf3b3da93'), 'Halle Berry''s bikini scenes were shot in Cadiz, and were not sunny and warm as they appeared on-screen, but quite the opposite. Berry had to be wrapped up in thick towels in between takes to avoid catching a chill', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('55307a81-3203-417a-8c54-04474c5e175b'), 'The frozen lake in Iceland that is the location for some car chases, does not naturally freeze very often. This is due to its closeness to the sea, and its high salt content. When the filmmakers had troubles getting the Icelandic lake to freeze properly, they considered filming the car chase scenes on ice in New Zealand. To rectify this situation, the river that links the lake to the sea was dammed, and within two days, the entire lake was frozen to a depth of over two meters (six and a half feet). Once they solved that problem, filming could take place in Iceland as planned', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d0d8391-f699-4a80-acfa-9942a34ea885'), 'This is the first James Bond movie to feature an Aston Martin as the car issued to Bond by Q Branch since The Living Daylights (1987). Although Pierce Brosnan drove a vintage Aston Martin in GoldenEye (1995), it is not shown to be anything other than a private car, with no special features other than a fax machine and an intercom', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('457cecba-9715-4ed0-9caa-b73311e15988'), 'Only the second James Bond movie to feature James Bond''s office. It was last seen in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3637d160-95f3-407f-a01d-f54d9db03253'), 'According to the book "The Bond Legacy", it was decided to delay production of this movie in order to have a 2002 release date, to coincide with the 40th anniversary of the first James Bond movie (Dr. No (1962)) and the 50th anniversary of the writing of the first Bond novel (Casino Royale)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bffc7012-b4ef-4e94-b236-ca206f6e172a'), 'Halle Berry left the production for a couple of days to attend the 2002 Oscars, where she won Best Actress for Monster''s Ball (2001)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2022ec7b-98f2-404d-8056-cfabac7573dc'), 'Miranda Frost (Rosamund Pike) refers to James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) at one point as "a blunt instrument." Ian Fleming, on more than one occasion, had described his idea of James Bond as a "blunt instrument wielded by a government department." In Casino Royale (2006), M (Dame Judi Dench) also described Bond as a blunt instrument', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('68696efe-adbb-48d3-a7cd-d0984f1cd31a'), 'In the middle of the sword fight, Gustav Graves (Toby Stephens) fetches two broadswords. As he walks back towards James Bond (Pierce Brosnan), Bond kicks his épée away towards camera. This move was never planned, and just happened on the day', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('78d30984-5ade-4a3a-8d05-e25238caedcd'), 'When Bond walks through the cigar factory, we see El Lector, the reader, reading aloud to the cigar rollers. The readers work for the factory workers to entertain and educate them while they work. The readers have been at their jobs since the mid 1800s. As of 2017, UNESCO is considering designating the profession a form of "intangible cultural heritage"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0cdc3d1-065a-4474-9222-c0433a94c3f0'), 'Although one quarter of this movie is set in Iceland, none of the main cast went there. Only the second unit and stunt crews did', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('434e954f-752c-4bce-8927-52590121a7e9'), 'The North Korean sequences were deliberately bleached of color to emphasize the inhospitality of the location', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d70b9535-035d-422b-a097-3681e3014d6b'), 'It was the last James Bond movie to use the famous "gun barrel" sequence before a pre-titles sequence as usual. In Quantum of Solace (2008) and Skyfall (2012), the sequence was placed at the end of those movies (a radically different version of the sequence was used at the end of the pre-titles scene in Casino Royale (2006)). However, the beginning gun barrel sequence was brought back for Spectre (2015)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('306962ec-89e0-494b-b2a4-28da08d5991c'), 'Gustav Graves arrives in London to be knighted. In fact, both of Toby Stephens'' parents have received this honor: Sir Robert Stephens and Dame Maggie Smith', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('82cc60d2-fa38-4b51-bd24-2a376ad96800'), 'This is the first time since 1962 (when Peter Burton played "Major Boothroyd" (Q) in Dr. No (1962)) when someone other than Desmond Llewelyn has played "Q". Llewelyn died in 1999, and John Cleese (who played "R" in The World Is Not Enough (1999) was named as his successor. One of the extras in the fencing scene is Justin Llewelyn, son of Desmond Llewelyn', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('217727ed-d099-476f-acf5-58e92287dcce'), 'All of the Aston Martins used in the ice high speed chase had to be converted to four wheel drive, by a firm in Wilmslow, Cheshire, England', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7ff12503-107e-486b-8ed9-3513cc34fcf3'), 'The budget of this movie, Pierce Brosnan''s last Bond film, was over two and a half times the budget of his first movie, GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3925736e-bbae-4878-bef1-e73e6f376063'), 'Sir Roger Moore, George Lazenby, Timothy Dalton, and Pierce Brosnan attended the premiere, because it was the franchise''s 40th anniversary. Sir Sean Connery claimed he could not be there due to filming commitments. His movie, The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen (2003), was filmed June 28, 2002 through November 24, 2002', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4f095bd5-a9b0-4904-a1ad-f65278f69cdf'), 'Although the production went to Cuba to source locations, they were unable to shoot there, due to U.S. legislations, so Cuba was re-created in a combination of Pinewood Studios outside London, England, and Cadiz, Spain', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bbf0d326-7408-4a9e-9e59-b90104f9d80f'), 'Filming had already begun when director Lee Tamahori decided he wanted a car chase through the ice palace set. Set designer Peter Lamont had to rebuild the set with steel girders to support the cars racing around it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f7bdfbac-467d-44b4-8a6c-41f0eff900db'), 'For his scenes as the captive Bond, Pierce Brosnan spent three hours in make-up every day having a false beard and long hair applied', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3444ddae-2f9d-4e1a-bc0a-8a0311192eeb'), 'Bond has suits and shirts made in Hong Kong by his "usual tailor". This is a reference to Diamonds Are Forever (1971), where Bond tells Tiffany he knows a good tailor in Hong Kong', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('65d73ef9-d919-4f99-a631-cdb988b26e35'), 'Less than a month after this movie''s release, U.K. fencing clubs saw an increase in the number of people interested in taking up the activity', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('45cdad2c-2390-4f24-8efb-2f78ac1d7334'), 'The love scene between Jinx and James Bond had to be trimmed of 7 seconds to get a PG-13 rating in the United States', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3cdfd526-48a7-4022-970c-ca947f7dded7'), 'For the first time, the famous gun barrel sequence now includes a bullet zooming by after Bond fires. This idea was suggested by director Lee Tamahori', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('123d534e-986a-4fda-af80-b68b728c8007'), 'When confronting James Bond (Pierce Brosnan), Miranda Frost (Rosamund Pike) says, "I know all about you, 007. It''s sex for dinner and death for breakfast." The line "Death for breakfast" is the title of chapter eleven in the Ian Fleming novel "On Her Majesty''s Secret Service". Other novel references: the cigarette poster of a sailor seen behind John Cleese, is referenced in "Thunderball", the basic plot is from "Moonraker", and the sheet of protective glass between Bond and M (Dame Judi Dench) references "The Man With The Golden Gun"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1322db78-bb83-4198-9a72-d092be25e768'), 'The scene where Gustav Graves (Toby Stephens) first demonstrates Icarus to his party guests required the most amount of lights ever required in a British movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eb3079cd-86c8-46bd-a44f-c935721aa5bc'), 'When Q (John Cleese) explains how the Vanquish works, he is explaining technology that the U.S. Air Force is actually developing for use in a new "daylight" stealth aircraft. However, the "invisibility" capability is only useful at extreme distance (several miles), and would not in any way be as good as depicted on the car in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c7d13fb2-e29f-45d8-8f2c-8be7a7216179'), 'Icarus was originally called "Solaris", but was changed when the producers found out that Solaris (2002) was in production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5ab49568-3278-46ba-b784-de6b45068946'), 'Contains the biggest explosion ever on film outside of America', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('358a0fb8-4079-47b6-8afd-2c8f0a02660e'), 'The movie''s title song "Die Another Day", sung by Madonna, debuted in the U.S. charts on October 19, 2002, and peaked at the number eight spot. The song was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Original Song, and a Golden Raspberry Award (Razzie) for Worst Original Song. Pop legend Sir Elton John called it the "worst Bond tune ever"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4900ee95-b85e-4ced-9785-c6ac20fc9edb'), 'The magazine with the picture of Gustav Graves that James Bond reads on the British Airways flight is the real in-flight magazine for British Airways. Called "High Life", the edition seen was for November 2002. The magazine interviewed Toby Stephens, the actor who played Graves, about his part, and included an article on all previous Bond movies and their respective stunts', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('de64e66f-0e0f-496f-b3ca-fc0ed0a57167'), 'Although it ranked fifth in the box office on its opening weekend in South Korea, there was protest at the movie''s depiction of Americans giving orders to the South Korean military. This movie dropped out of the top ten by its second week, and one theater in Seoul pulled it from the screens in response to the protests. Some smaller theaters that usually get second-run movies refused to pick it up', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e4697353-f6b4-4ff0-8b81-e760e56d4f47'), 'The hovercraft chase sequence was filmed near a working airport. Pilots were understandably nervous about seeing gunfire and explosions at an airport, so a schedule had to be worked out whereby filming could take place whenever the airport wasn''t too busy', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6de90d9f-f7a1-4af0-8a70-93a7efd6c991'), 'Wai Lin, played by Michelle Yeoh in Tomorrow Never Dies (1997), was originally supposed to make her return, aiding James Bond in Hong Kong, but no arrangement could be worked out with her, and she was replaced by Chinese Intelligence Agent (and hotelier) Chang (Ho Yi). Wai Lin''s presence is confirmed by an extra on the DVD release concerning the writing of the script: Barbara Broccoli is shown leafing through an early script, and it clearly contains lines for Wai Lin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0094d7ca-20bb-48d6-ad96-8047cce596ee'), 'Iceland had a noticeable increase of tourist interest in year following the premiere, mostly from people seeking to stay in an ice hotel such as shown in this movie. No such structure exists in Iceland, which is not nearly cold enough for such a building in the first place, despite its name', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e319e7ea-4841-4b6c-96ae-2204d1c9232a'), 'Pierce Brosnan was very glad to rename John Cleese''s character "Q", rather than "R", because his native Irish accent made it difficult to pronounce "R" with a convincing English accent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0654546e-d38c-4c5e-b528-369886fc53db'), 'Due to Desmond Llewellyn''s death in 1999, it was decided R (John Cleese) would be promoted as the new Q and that the original Q had officially retired from MI6', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f5130acd-d476-4488-a871-9742fa705fad'), 'One of the few James Bond movies to openly use alternate source music, in this case, The Clash''s "London Calling". The previous movie to do this was A View to a Kill (1985), which utilized The Beach Boys'' "California Girls"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b166b19a-41f2-4dc5-b618-01f79bcda824'), 'The idea of the car chase inside the Ice Palace was an idea conceived by director Lee Tamahori. He believed such a fantastic set should not be wasted, and thought they should stage a car chase through it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('19a7a94f-c1fe-4e82-ad10-5784dcb4a471'), 'The device used to identify James Bond in the beginning is a Sony Ericsson P800 mobile phone, making it the first appearance in a Bond movie of a smartphone. Although Bond gadgets usually precede reality by being unrealistically capable for the time when their respective movies are released, this device actually did have the potential to perform the task, had it just been given some custom programming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ed52b04d-78a0-44d7-a222-deeda8866078'), 'In Goldfinger (1964), the original "Q" (Desmond Llewelyn) tells James Bond (Sir Sean Connery) that he never jokes about his work while introducing the ejection seat feature of the "first" Aston Martin. His successor (John Cleese) also reminds James Bond (Pierce Brosnan) that "like his predecessor" never jokes about his work while introducing the invisibility feature of the "newest" Aston Martin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('719da7de-e80d-43b4-a788-04eb747e6caf'), 'The Aston Martin and the Jaguar were completely stripped of engine and running gear. These were replaced by V8 engines, four-wheel-drive kits, and four-speed automatic transmissions from Ford Explorers. This was to help them perform on ice', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9b3f29c0-967c-462b-a8c9-9c53c73fa9bf'), 'Director Lee Tamahori cut a scene where Verity (Madonna) and Miranda Frost (Rosamund Pike) were closer than it is shown in the movie: "I shot some moments with Madonna giving Rosamund little touches, but I didn''t want to turn the film into a male fantasy thing. Madonna still has all these little looks with Rosamund, which was enough"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c0f7e61b-fcb0-4aeb-a4c6-d9bb9f8c6f8c'), 'First love scene between James Bond and Miss Moneypenny in a James Bond movie, albeit in a virtual reality sequence. The lovemaking scene with Bond and Jinx is considered to be the first time in the franchise to show 007 having sex, as opposed to a post-coital scenario. This scene had to be trimmed for the American market. Previously in the franchise, a sex scene in GoldenEye (1995) did not have Bond in it. A Bond sex scene appeared in Never Say Never Again (1983) which is not part of the official EON Productions franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9543a94c-6a06-44a5-8f77-37e2fa4e65e1'), 'The name of the hotel that James Bond visits in Hong Kong is The Rubyeon Royale Hotel: "Ruby" for the 40th anniversary of the Bond film franchise; "Eon" for EON Productions, producers of the franchise; and "Royale" for "Casino Royale", the first Ian Fleming James Bond novel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2638d85b-ef5c-49c7-a5e7-141fe1f974ec'), 'The route diagram on the station wall in the unused tube station, where Q introduces Bond to the new Aston Martin, indicates that the station is on the Piccadilly line, and that the next station is Hyde Park Corner, followed by Knightsbridge, et cetera. Reference to the current tube map, suggests that this station is Green Park (the station before Hyde Park Corner). However, there is a real unused station on the Piccadilly Line between Green Park and Hyde Park Corner. It was called Down Street, and was closed in the 1930s. It was used during the war as temporary Cabinet War Rooms, and later by the Railway Executive as offices. Even today, much of the internal infrastructure is complete, but it could not be used in the way shown in the film, because although the station is closed, the tracks through it are still in normal daily use by Piccadilly line trains', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d6c5012f-74a4-42fd-a648-62f9b0afb2ad'), 'Pierce Brosnan''s final appearance as James Bond. Four years later, Daniel Craig took over the iconic role for Casino Royale (2006), adapted from Ian Fleming''s book. Producers Michael G. Wilson and Barbara Broccoli saw Batman Begins (2005), and decided to make the new James Bond darker and more realistic, and since Casino Royale (2006) was about James Bond at the beginning of his career as a British secret agent, it ruled out Brosnan in the role, and it required a younger actor for the role, and thus, Craig got the part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a06d322e-a61f-456a-b546-25f026973c20'), 'The translation of the conversation between the North Korean soldiers in the first scene is "What the hell is the taste of this cigarette? I can give you Chinese tobacco"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d9c378d-8377-4682-9e62-8262d62ba765'), 'The fuchsia crystal dress Jinx Johnson wears during the Ice Palace party was designed by Donatella Versace. Costume designer Lindy Hemming saw a similar Versace design in a fashion magazine, and requested Donatella to make one to Halle Berry''s specifications', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f7603b9-4b07-493b-b6b8-4f9f158e099f'), 'The opening surfing sequence was shot off the coast of Maui on Christmas Day 2001', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2470d38b-276b-4d08-8f6b-fc79dd72bf76'), 'Rick Yune''s diamond-encrusted make-up took three hours to apply', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('02b560d9-efbf-4ffa-897e-38fedc1d7960'), 'Pierce Brosnan was unavailable to screentest potential Bond Girls, so Colin Salmon stepped into his shoes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a233c9e8-7690-40ff-af3c-cb7da17f197c'), 'Pierce Brosnan is the only James Bond to have a gadget filled car from Q in all of his movies. Sir Sean Connery had one (the Aston Martin DB5 in Goldfinger (1964) and Thunderball (1965)), Sir Roger Moore had one (the Lotus Esprit in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) and For Your Eyes Only (1981)) and Timothy Dalton had one (the Aston Martin Vantage Volante in The Living Daylights (1987)). He is also the only Bond to have an Aston Martin in all of his movies. He has the DB5 in his first three movies. (It is visible via an infrared imaging camera at the end of The World Is Not Enough (1999))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7c8c3c77-5aea-4055-a6ff-180058c5d293'), 'A huge 160,000-watt light array, which took a week to construct, was used for the Icarus demonstration scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff3f25c4-20c1-4d88-a4f9-fa2fd3663784'), 'Second unit director Vic Armstrong had trouble finding stunt drivers who were able to handle a hovercraft', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2791cc36-c4b5-4966-bade-0130056b07a7'), 'Four weeks before filming began, the only parts that had been cast were the regulars, Pierce Brosnan, Dame Judi Dench, Samantha Bond, Colin Salmon, and John Cleese', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('085c27c5-7b78-42c8-a8d7-30223b6d9943'), 'When Pierce Brosnan learned that the Aston Martin Vanquish (launched during production) was chosen by the producers to be featured in this installment, he asked the producers through his agent, Fred Specktor, whether he could have a replica of the car. After being told that it could be agreed, they wrote an amendment to Brosnan''s contract on paper (at Brosnan''s insistence) that he gets the car in lieu of a portion of his salary. Three months after filming wrapped, the car was delivered to his Malibu residence. Unfortunately, it was destroyed during the Woolsey wildfire disaster in November 2018 save for two custom plaques bearing his name', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2d97a01e-c625-4cd2-89cc-57a5a1e2e726'), 'Tang Ling Zao (Rick Yune) ("The Man Who Never Smiles") is the first Korean henchman to appear in the franchise since Oddjob in Goldfinger (1964)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('20327bcf-3b6c-4cfe-bd68-768b112a8404'), 'Miranda Frost was originally named "Gala Brand", which was the name of the female lead in the novel "Moonraker"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bd7b314f-85fb-4c6e-be94-4cf2c4826720'), 'When Q (John Cleese) walks behind the invisible Aston Martin in the otherwise abandoned underground station, due to the light refraction effect, he appears briefly to do a "silly walk", a reference to a sketch that Cleese did for Monty Python''s Flying Circus (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7283002b-ac51-4939-a418-4a3761ae3988'), 'The ice chase sequence, which lasts just over two minutes on-screen, took four weeks to film, with the cars doing no more than twenty miles per hour, being filmed with under cranked cameras, so that when the film was projected at normal speed, the cars would seem to be going at high speed. Close-ups and control filming was done on sets created in an airship hanger in England', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Die Another Day'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('7cb075c0-a3d5-4460-a15f-8a23a3f98953'), 'The way Bond orders his first vodka martini is lifted directly from the Ian Fleming novels', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('48fc7776-b8e6-4b58-801c-c3fdeec5d62c'), 'Daniel Craig initially rejected the part of James Bond, as he felt that the series had settled into a standard formula. He changed his mind when he read the finished script. Timothy Dalton had turned down For Your Eyes Only (1981) for the same reason, and, like Craig, ended up playing a different, more grounded interpretation of Bond in The Living Daylights (1987) and Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5abf3c43-bc97-4373-b470-6888030c04e9'), 'In the shower scene, Vesper (Eva Green) was originally scripted to be wearing nothing but her underwear. Daniel Craig argued that Vesper would not have stopped to take her clothes off, and the scene was changed', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b24648e8-4710-4311-ac54-e6d516dc820f'), 'To prepare for the role, Daniel Craig read all of Ian Fleming''s novels and talked with Mossad and British Secret Service agents who had served as advisers on Munich (2005)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a893ca07-4841-4077-8127-9dc8096a5cd8'), 'The car barrel roll stunt by the Aston Martin DBS broke the world record for the most barrel rolls assisted by a cannon. Originally, the racing specifications of the DBS meant that a standard ramp would not be sufficient to get the car to roll, so the special effects team were called in to install an air-powered cannon behind the driver''s seat. This allowed the car to complete seven full rolls. The stunt was officially entered into the Guinness Book of World Records on November 5, 2006', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('405e872d-3675-43b2-9584-d8cea0129808'), 'Daniel Craig claimed to be in a state of pain for most of the shoot due to the many vigorous stunts he was required to perform', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4ee6f5f6-0b34-4e8a-814d-d5b0ad51c699'), 'The opening parkour chase took several weeks to film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('81f763bf-e9e8-4024-ba6f-ede99a456d63'), 'Daniel Craig gained twenty pounds of muscle for the role by adhering to eating mostly proteins, minimizing his carbohydrates intake, training five days a week, only doing cardio exercises on weekends', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('72fabed0-5474-4e1b-9791-e9112c33c7ac'), 'For Daniel Craig''s now iconic scene where he rises out of the sea in a pair of Speedos, many of the crew were out of camera range in boats fending off the paparazzi', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('49f64e71-8d1e-461d-a71b-dbbcd93379b7'), 'Daniel Craig became the first actor to be nominated for a BAFTA (British Academy) Award for playing James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cd6b8164-d2e9-4314-9e14-a38719f359ec'), 'Daniel Craig said he was shopping for groceries when he got the call from producer Barbara Broccoli that he had won the James Bond role. She apparently told him, "Over to you, kiddo." Craig left the groceries behind and celebrated with martinis (shaken, not stirred)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e61e0b4-8553-4422-9193-01028bc0f9ad'), 'In one afternoon''s shooting, three Aston Martin DB9 cars, were destroyed for the car roll sequence. The cars were old engineering prototype/development mules fitted with DBS bodywork', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('91aa7be1-a9be-4534-bfef-3d1438547338'), 'M''s (Dame Judi Dench) partner, sleeping next to her when she receives a call in the night, was played by the transport coordinator', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eced0f83-2abe-4460-9cf8-51851303adec'), 'The first film to show James Bond as a rookie in MI6. In all previous movies, he had long been a spy', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('971e4c8c-fef2-41b0-8fae-a3235a3ebe03'), 'Andreas Daniel, who plays the card dealer, got the role by chance. While the production company was looking for a card dealer, they called the casino he was working in. Coincidentally, Daniel was on the phone, saying "You are looking for a card dealer? You have just found him. Take me!" He got the part and then flew to Prague to film his scenes, without telling his colleagues. He bought himself a new car from the salary', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('62488566-7f20-4500-a228-196e8e251fbb'), 'Daniel Craig''s first day of shooting was the scene where Bond storms the fictional "Nambutan" embassy', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4419e09-bec1-4382-bfc6-827565f1ea92'), 'First James Bond movie to be based on a full-length Ian Fleming novel since Moonraker (1979). Until 2019, it remains as the last James Bond movie based directly on an Ian Fleming novel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80270067-6382-4dfe-90a3-04551c4c25fb'), 'The scene where James Bond comforts a distraught Vesper Lynd in the shower after she''s witnessed her first death was shot in one take', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff430f54-70e8-4e1a-800f-eec650458aff'), 'Daniel Craig lost his two front teeth while filming a fight scene in Prague (the first action scene to be shot), and his dentist had to fly from London to replace them', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a10e7b60-0af5-4393-9351-da46b18816b8'), 'A mere two days after the premiere, pirated copies were already on sale in London. Daniel Craig was offered one such copy while walking anonymously through the streets of Beijing, China. Casino Royale was also the first Bond film that was shown in China, as all the previous Bond films were banned and could only be watched via pirated copies', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('29670276-fe9c-4c66-836b-7264ca682bb6'), 'Producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson didn''t secure the rights to Casino Royale until 2000 when Sony exchanged them for MGM''s rights to Spider-Man', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0149e108-a7f8-4e34-8871-cb430244d16b'), 'Much was made at this movie''s release about Daniel Craig''s buff body. Being in such prime condition was not new to Craig, as at one point, he had been a semi-professional rugby player', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('00a2ad3c-5faa-42bc-8537-21579e568dbb'), 'According to Daniel Craig, the only CGI in this movie was to erase safety wires in a lot of the stunt sequences, and to integrate the models for the sinking palazzo into the real Venetian location', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('452a1b2a-555c-4011-9c60-ad23e3fc44fa'), 'There is a story visible on Le Chiffre''s computer on the same page that has the story of Bond''s latest mission at the Embassy. It states that a French football player called Neil Pinkawa has stated he is not retiring from the national soccer team. Neil Pinkawa is this movie''s lead screen graphics artist, who would have been in charge of creating all of the mock web pages in the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('992c15ff-d990-41f4-8241-fc8f58408465'), 'Ian Fleming is said to have based the character of Le Chiffre on English occultist Aleister Crowley', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('feba7847-e48f-4aba-b186-57cf7dbb0b91'), 'Daniel Craig quit smoking and had Simon Waterson as a personal trainer to get into shape', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e38187f-95e8-4562-8393-4adfb983e121'), 'This is the first movie in the forty-four years of James Bond where it rains', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a092dde1-9a33-4003-8990-befbb52abe15'), 'In one scene, James Bond was supposed to be swimming at the beach when he sees Solange (the wife of the villain, played by Caterina Murino) riding on a horse and the two make eye contact. Craig says that while shooting the scene, he accidentally hit an awkwardly situated sandbank that forced him to stand up and walk out of the water, instead of just floating off as the script said. The image of Craig stepping out of the water ended up being plastered all over the promotional material for this movie, with many people assuming that it was a nod to Ursula Andress emerging from the beach in the first Bond movie, Dr. No (1962). The perceived homage to Bond''s legacy likely helped win over many reluctant fans, many of whom were leery when it was announced that an unknown actor was taking over the helm of the franchise. It also helped launch James Bond as a more modern and rugged 007. But the main effect was on Daniel Craig''s career: The scene single-handedly turned him into an international sex symbol. Craig said he realized right away that the moment would draw comparisons to Andress, but he didn''t think that he "would be haunted by it for the rest of my life"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('36a3461d-5fd2-424f-9305-9beb8b204410'), 'A promotional leaflet used to promote this movie in Japan headlined the "Seven rules to receive 00 status". The MI6 fansite has it translated as: "1) You don''t fear death, and won''t give in to torture. 2) You have Olympic level shooting skills. 3) Even if you double-cross your own parents, you will never double-cross the organization. 4) You have knowledge that would surprise even a scholar, and a sense of humor that would make even a bad girl grin. 5) You have the sociability of a lamb, but remain a lone wolf. 6) You have the highest level of experience with alcohol, gambling, cars, and food. 7) You can fall in love, but you can never love"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc192f47-24cb-47a8-a91d-e5d401e5fb75'), 'One week after filming was completed, the 007 Stage at Pinewood Studios burned down on July 30, 2006. This was the second time this had happened, the first being before filming A View to a Kill (1985). The filmmakers had just finished using the stage for filming interiors set in Venice for the movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e588597b-08e9-41ba-ae6b-5c6a10a7af7a'), 'Authorities in Venice granted producers permission to sail James Bond''s yacht, called "Spirit 54", along the Grand Canal between the Accademia and Rialto bridges. No one can remember exactly the last time a pleasure yacht sailed in the Grand Canal, but it''s believed to have been several centuries ago', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('85f56175-82a3-4d11-a058-7750e0ca00fc'), 'Daniel Craig is the first actor to play James Bond who is younger than the series itself', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db5b56f5-f3d9-4a53-9b43-a27038fdd9e8'), 'The idea of the Palazzo sinking building was conceived by screenwriters Neal Purvis and Robert Wade, who had seen coverage of the leaning Tower of Pisa having its footings stabilized, while propped up by gigantic bladders full of air. They also came up with Le Chiffre''s bleeding eye', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('58e7432b-9fd6-4d52-8283-3617e11b11b8'), 'According to the book "Bond on Bond" (2015) by Sir Roger Moore, producer Kevin McClory (who previously owned the movie rights to S.P.E.C.T.R.E., the character Ernst Stavro Blofeld, any Thunderball (1965) remake, and other various outlines, scripts, and treatments) "had been a long-time pain in EON''s behind, and they couldn''t use the Blofeld character or his organization (S.P.E.C.T.R.E.) for fear of litigation, which is how the Quantum idea came about, as originally the producers had hoped to introduce Spectre as the villains in Casino Royale (2006) and Quantum of Solace (2008), but now (in 2013), seven years after McClory''s death (when a settlement was made by MGM and EON Productions with McClory''s estate), they could finally bring everything back under one roof"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('42dab1f5-ed93-4c9f-a086-6f33bea105db'), 'The location used in the Bahamas as the Madagascar Construction site was an abandoned hotel site at Coral Harbour that was under construction thirty years ago. It was used to film hotel rooms for the James Bond movie Thunderball (1965), and it was also used for the Bond movie The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) as a camera platform with models and workshops. It is now part of a military base', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ef974cbb-62c9-4cf7-b9b0-1526c808798a'), 'Although Dame Judi Dench as M doesn''t really sit with the chronology of a rebooted James Bond, director Martin Campbell was very keen to have her on board, as he really admired what she had done with the character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d541f7a-2a7d-4dc0-8663-364ea157ab37'), 'Product placement was deliberately scaled back following the criticism levelled at Die Another Day (2002), which earned itself the nickname "Buy Another Day"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5c28b672-8c68-467a-a47e-91c278d67b33'), 'According to director Martin Campbell, Henry Cavill was the only actor in serious contention for the role of James Bond, but at 22 years old, was considered too young. Timothy Dalton was the same age when he was approached for On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), but he declined because he also felt he was too young. Dalton and Cavill are the youngest actors ever considered to play Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4bb1f6bc-4239-4017-ae49-f373e635fe29'), 'Daniel Craig was producer Barbara Broccoli''s first choice for the role of Bond. She had him in mind after seeing his performance in Layer Cake (2004)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7a685196-3bb1-4bc7-9b4c-0ee9f37bf376'), 'During the Bahamas horse riding sequence, Caterina Murino (Solange) was having leg pain, and the filmmakers were thinking of using a stunt double for that sequence. Murino insisted on doing the scene without body doubles, saying that it will be her "classic Bond Girl" moment', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9df94456-67d7-4ef0-843b-e5147f706feb'), 'This was highest-grossing Bond film, until Skyfall (2012) surpassed it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('052d01d8-57a3-483d-bc52-7cfb2e901a65'), 'The climactic Venice sinking sequence took three weeks of filming with an average of nine hours per day', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ca6bdfc7-8b2e-43e1-aaa2-e9424d68a441'), 'Ian Fleming celebrated the completion of the "Casino Royale" novel''s first draft by purchasing a gold-plated typewriter. Former James Bond actor Pierce Brosnan reportedly bought the typewriter a few years ago for $52,000', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d9918a67-24d4-491e-99e6-9dfd2abf5e43'), 'Sir Sean Connery, Sir Roger Moore, Timothy Dalton, Pierce Brosnan, and George Lazenby all supported the casting of Daniel Craig as James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c1e0dd28-7f22-4e52-ad15-a2a125f659c2'), 'First James Bond movie approved by Chinese censors. All of the other films were available in China only as illegal bootlegs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc1a8e99-263a-4fd3-95f4-0af32e94e15d'), 'This is the first James Bond movie since Dr. No (1962) where there were no nude dancing females during the opening title sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e3c35111-98a5-4c58-a5df-76d18341aa3d'), 'The "Vesper" that James Bond orders at Casino Royale is taken from the novel. It consists of three parts gin (Gordon''s was Bond''s choice), one part vodka [Bond preferred a grain vodka be used (Absolut)] and half part of Kina Lillet. The ingredients are shaken over ice until cold, served in a cocktail glass with a slice of lemon peel for garnish. In 1985, Kina Lillet was reformulated to reduce sugar and quinine (the "Kina" in the name) and was rebranded just as "Lillet". The addition of red and rose versions of the aperitif have caused the original to be known as "Lillet Blanc"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('efb00273-3432-4015-ab90-143ca9283e51'), 'The chase around Miami airport was filmed at three separate airports in three different countries. They were: Nassau International Airport in Nassau, Bahamas; Dunsfold Park Aerodrome in Dunsfold Park, Dunsfold, Surrey, England; and Ruzyne International Airport in Ruzyne, Prague, Czech Republic', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a3a3230b-6460-47c2-9469-bc9d2381218b'), 'Ian Fleming once said on writing the "Casino Royale" novel: "Writing about 2,000 words in three hours every morning, ''Casino Royale'' dutifully produced itself. I wrote nothing and made no corrections until the book was finished. If I had looked back at what I had written the day before, I might have despaired"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0b42f07f-939b-45f9-b038-64ac8f15cc8b'), 'Sir Roger Moore was reportedly so impressed with this movie that he went out and bought a DVD of it', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0cfc6fea-bc9a-4a7f-8210-7ec5f4ddbc08'), 'Most BAFTA nominations ever received by a James Bond movie, totalling nine. The previous record had been two each for GoldenEye (1995) and The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). The nine nominations were for Best British Film, Adapted Screenplay, Actor in a Leading Role, Film Music, Cinematography, Editing, Production Design, Sound, and Special Visual Effects. It only won for Best Sound', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('55caccd4-9c05-4888-87c0-30322044b0df'), 'Le Chiffre''s (Mads Mikkelsen''s) left eye is deformed and weeps blood. Le Chiffre''s girlfriend Valenka (Ivana Milicevic) almost always has her hair styled to cover her left eye. She hides her eye in deference to his damaged one', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('33aaa6fc-b19b-48af-81ab-c1e089a5bb52'), 'Caterina Murino was filming in Argentina when the first casting session was held for this movie in Paris, then filming in Rome when a second session was announced. However, the day before her appointment, she fell from a horse while rehearsing, and she ended up going to the casting interview filled with pain killers and hardly able to walk. When she was asked if she could ride a horse, she said that she''d just fallen off of one. Despite that, she got the part, making it her first in English', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2de8d27e-5cd5-4047-9d7e-2901b0cd348f'), 'When he was cast as 007, Daniel Craig had his own ideas on playing the role and in an interview with Jonathan Ross on the set of this movie, he stated that he wanted to be faithful to the book and show the character''s raw vulnerability by having him make a few mistakes and that the drama would be there when he gets it right and make the audience think that it''s all going to go wrong and that when it all goes right, the audience would get more excited', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dfb7ccd7-b3fd-45fc-8ab8-256a1c5afc2e'), 'Le Chiffre is the first leading Bond villain in the EON Productions series to have two readily apparent physical dysfunctions. He has an inhaler for breathing, which is a character trait from the original novel, but he also has tear ducts that weep blood. This bleeding of the eye is a real medical condition, which is known as haemolacria. This usually manifests itself as either partially blood-tinged tears, which are part teardrops and part blood, or as full blood drops. Haemolacria can be an indicator of a tumor in the lacrimal apparatus of the eye, and can also be an indicator of a variety of other diseases', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('24953019-2fa6-4b74-bfe0-9f896ea25d43'), 'This is the first time that Felix Leiter returned to the James Bond films since Licence to Kill (1989), the second being Quantum of Solace (2008), and the third being No Time to Die (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec6f1e7c-3405-46f2-84a6-74d6e8fdd406'), 'Having Pierce Brosnan return for a fifth engagement as James Bond would have cost the producers $30 million', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2eda33b2-845a-4dda-80c4-78d1c9d355f4'), 'James Bond''s alias in this movie was "Arlington Beech". His alias for Vesper Lynd was "Stephanie Broadchest", a typical Ian Fleming-esque name moniker', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bc7494d5-8949-40a7-9aed-c78142beb21b'), 'The old woman that played poker with James Bond and Alex Dimitrios is Diane Hartford, who also appeared in Thunderball (1965) as the woman with whom Bond decides to dance at the Kiss Kiss Bang Bang Club', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('88789e9f-9595-40c6-be3d-8b453175c48d'), 'The three-piece navy blue suit worn by Daniel Craig at the end of this movie resembles the gray suit worn by Sir Sean Connery in Goldfinger (1964). The Goldfinger suit has lapels on the waistcoat and other distinct differences appropriate for the different era and Connery''s height', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ae9e0243-9fe1-470b-be39-ff84dbd11ec6'), 'Daniel Craig''s suits and tuxedos were made by Italian fashion house Brioni (their logo can briefly be seen on the suit bag for the tuxedo that Vesper gives him). His shirts and neckties were made by the British company Turnbull and Asser. In addition, he wears sunglasses by Persol, cufflinks by S.T. Dupont, suspenders by Albert Thurston, polos and t-shirts by Sunspel, shoes by Converse, John Lobb, and Nike, Ted Baker pants, La Perla swim trunks, a Giorgio Armani leather jacket, and an Omega watch. Brioni also dressed every player at the Casino Royale poker table', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('55e95fc7-8870-4899-a2a8-185a0c51e8ef'), 'The black-and-white opening of this movie was an idea of director of photography Phil Meheux, who conceived it so as to give a surprise to viewers, as well as a nod to The Spy Who Came in from the Cold (1965) and Reflections in a Golden Eye (1967). The opening sequence required six thousand feet (one hour and six minute''s worth, at twenty-four frames per second) of Eastman Double-X 5222 black-and-white negative film. At the time of its release, this movie is the only film in the official series to have a significant sequence filmed in black-and-white. However, some of the shots of James Bond in the gun barrel sequences in the early movies were in black and white. Also, Climax! (1954) season one, episode three, "Casino Royale", was completely in black-and-white', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7b7d970a-e1f9-4e99-a9d8-fc2ba99e3032'), 'While in the "Miami" airport, there is a call for flight 007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d3e51e1-2f69-4326-a427-ab4c495f7210'), 'Quentin Tarantino showed interest in adapting Ian Fleming''s novel "Casino Royale" with an "out of continuity" universe that would feature Pierce Brosnan as James Bond. He claimed his treatment for the Bond movie was different, shooting the movie in black and white, with no classic John Barry theme, no opening title credits, or the familiar one-liners, and using voice-over narration in order to incorporate Fleming''s text. The movie would have been more film noir, set firmly in the cold war era, about which time Ian Fleming wrote, and would have been set immediately after the death of Bond''s wife Tracy in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969). It''s frequently reported that EON rejected his offer. The truth is, EON would not have been able to hire Tarantino, as he refuses to join the Directors Guild, and it''s doubtful the Directors Guild would be willing to grant a waiver. Tarantino would not be able to develop a Bond project on his own, as he does not have rights to the character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e11bcff-df59-47a3-bf05-62a2879d4d38'), 'When M talks to James Bond about the financial loss Le Chiffre has taken as a result of his plot in Miami being foiled, she mentions how the CIA discovered he short-sold large quantities of airline stocks after 9/11, and when the stocks plummeted in the wake of the attacks, someone made a fortune. This really was alleged to have happened in real life, as people noted seemingly suspicious stock trading the day before 9/11, but a thorough investigation by the FBI, among others, concluded there was no al-Qaeda connection', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('df7876ec-6293-448b-8d93-95d0d5c4e407'), 'Pierce Brosnan was initially asked back by the producers for this movie, after the then-record breaking success of Die Another Day (2002). However after seeing The Bourne Identity (2002) and other contemporary spy movies raise the bar on realism and physicality in spy movies, in addition to Pierce''s agent reportedly demanding thirty million dollars plus royalties for Brosnan to return as Bond, the producers reconsidered hiring Brosnan back, opting to cast the role instead with the younger, more virile Daniel Craig to reset the franchise', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8c1ca18b-584b-4174-9413-c07a61198ac2'), 'Chris Cornell''s title song, "You Know My Name", debuted on the U.S. charts on December 9, 2006, where it went to the number seventy-nine spot, it peaked at number seven on the U.K. Singles chart, sold 148,000 copies in the U.K. in 2006, and has sold 323,000 digital copies and 3.5 million streams in the U.S. as of 2017. The song does not appear on the soundtrack. This is the first time that the title song has not been included on the soundtrack', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d63206b-694e-4489-9c4d-a86ede35f866'), 'The style of free-running and movement Mollaka the bomb maker uses in the Madagascar chase near the beginning of this movie is called "parkour". Sebastien Foucan (Mollaka) is one of the main publicists of parkour, and has appeared in many other media events. In the earliest versions of the script, Mollaka was known as "Two Fingers"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0d61a448-ae92-4c5f-9384-82e94d2c2d5a'), 'Daniel Craig is the first James Bond not to act with Desmond Llewelyn, who played Q in seventeen of the previous twenty movies, and died in 1999', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9af8b7dd-ac6d-46e3-9aa7-d57010866e58'), 'Unlike previous Bond films, images of semi-nude girls were omitted from the opening titles, as Bond is finally becoming current with the times, as the "Playboy era" had long past. An example of the earlier mentality was seen in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) in which Bond not only reads the magazine but he steals the centerfold. While romance continues to be a major Bond theme, the objectification of women is definitely out', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('74f73742-9a89-4318-b835-433a185e9e6a'), 'This marks the second time there is a foot chase in a James Bond movie, the first being the foot chase through the parade in Thunderball (1965)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b854ef18-e7c8-4448-a729-a17fc71700cf'), 'The camp in Uganda where we first meet Mr. White (Jesper Christensen) and Le Chiffre (Mads Mikkelsen) was filmed just outside of London', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e4413b7-a8e0-4152-a003-0f8fbbf0032e'), 'In the opening sequence, the shape into which clubs symbol "grows" is called a Mandelbrot Set in chaos theory, and has infinite complexity', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56321ba3-13e7-4722-ba31-cb6bdd64e2ca'), 'Ian Fleming started writing the novel on his Imperial typewriter at "Goldeneye", Jamaica, around January 15-17, 1952, and completed it on Tuesday, March 18, 1952', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cd778005-dabb-456a-9c66-0d179e8f2a75'), 'The set interior of the sinking house in Venice measured forty-five feet by forty feet, and was forty-five feet high. It was built around the existing indoor tank at Pinewood Studios, which was increased to twenty feet, so the whole set could sink sixteen feet', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('744b70cd-92a6-4ec4-9010-68acfb0aa442'), 'Although the password that James Bond entered on the alpha-numeric keypad at the Casino Royale was supposed to be VESPER (837737), the password he entered was 836547', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('41efcf09-f0f9-4350-9d9e-8e8a4dd27c70'), '"Casino Royale" was the first James Bond novel written by Ian Fleming, and is the last of the original Fleming novels to be filmed by EON Productions. The shooting of this movie now means EON Productions has filmed the entire canon of Fleming James Bond novels, although some just in title (for example: The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), Moonraker (1979), and You Only Live Twice (1967))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7789df7f-35a7-4aee-ae8a-e880cb5c93c8'), 'Before Daniel Craig was officially announced to play James Bond, there were several other actors considered for the part. Producer Michael G. Wilson said that they looked over two hundred actors, searching for the right one. Some of them were Julian McMahon, Hrithik Roshan, Dominic West and Gerard Butler. Most of them were deemed not appropriate to fit the role, while some others were nothing but media speculation. Antony Starr, Goran Visnjic, Sam Worthington, Alex O''Loughlin, and Rupert Friend were also considered. Hugh Jackman reportedly turned the role down', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c688a8a-1062-4a70-9819-640b08bef3ad'), 'The first EON Productions James Bond movie to feature the Columbia Pictures logo. Columbia Pictures produced the James Bond spoof Casino Royale (1967), and was attempting to make a second adaptation of the novel, before it bought MGM', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('52f2fddd-1a13-4efc-bbd2-aa05aa70f3b5'), 'When Daniel Craig was announced as the new Bond, the press and many fans reacted by questioning the concept of a blonde Bond. The producers responded by reminding the press that not only was the longest-serving actor in the role the blonde-haired Roger Moore (who was in seven bond films) but that when the first Bond film was being cast Ian Fleming suggested Moore for the role, seeing him as the ideal Bond. Even so, many would refer to Craig as "James Blonde"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('be1d9f62-8ba8-464d-8003-b54eae4a0e97'), 'The Bodyworks exhibition in Miami was shot on a very cold night in Prague, Czech Republic. Most viewers are unaware that the figures in the display are actual vivisected and preserved remains (obtained legally, of course). This is the first time that actual human remains appeared prominently in a major motion picture', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6acd6a58-6b39-473d-b9e1-e40e1f84e6f0'), '"Le Chiffre" is a French word which translates into English as "The Number". Other translations in different languages include German, "Die Nummer" - "The Number", "Herr Ziffer" - "Mr. Numeral", and Romanian, "Ochiu Spart" - "Broken Eye"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8dca901d-e461-4f0c-a1d7-2a7f6861f8c5'), 'Marks the first time since The Living Daylights (1987) that a James Bond movie has used an original Ian Fleming short story or novel title', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2f895539-15ae-4684-b5ba-b08ead35dc9e'), '"You Know My Name" has no mention of "Casino Royale", because according to Chris Cornell, he "couldn''t imagine it fitting into a song lyric that would come out of my mouth." He added, "''Casino Royale'' didn''t make a good rock title, but I would write a song named Octopussy just for fun"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fb8692d4-3885-4e2f-9e9d-7857861cc615'), 'The Brioni tuxedos worn by James Bond at the Casino Royale poker tournament are rumored to have cost $6,000 each', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('23f816e8-0286-4ec4-aa73-68a16d8112fb'), 'Jessica Miller, who plays the dealer at the poker game at The Ocean Club, is the Poker Room Manager at the Crystal Palace Casino in Nassau, Bahamas', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('919b68e2-0e20-40d1-84ca-7f12d89195f7'), 'In designing the credit sequence for this movie, graphic designer Daniel Kleinman was inspired by the cover of the 1953 British first edition of the novel, which featured Ian Fleming''s original design of a playing card bordered by eight red hearts dripping with blood. Kleinman said, "The hearts not only represent cards, but the tribulations of Bond''s love story. So I took that as inspiration to use playing card graphics in different ways in the titles", like a club representing a puff of gun smoke, and slashed arteries spurting thousands of tiny hearts. In creating the shadow images of the sequence, Kleinman digitized the footage of Daniel Craig and the stuntmen on the Inferno visual effects system at Framestore CFC in London. The actors'' silhouettes were incorporated into more than twenty digitally animated scenes depicting intricate and innovative card patterns. Kleinman decided not to use the female silhouettes commonly seen throughout the James Bond title sequences, considering that the women did not fit with this movie''s spirit and the storyline following Bond falling in love', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7f545698-554a-40b1-b045-449a169ea81c'), 'Despite being second billed to Daniel Craig, Eva Green does not appear until fifty-eight minutes into this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('09223668-2541-4c49-8f5f-c9da8db87d6b'), 'The Skyfleet S570 prototype at Miami International Airport is meant to be a take on the new Airbus A380. The S570 was built off of an old 747-200, which was originally used by British Airways (under the designation "G-BDXJ"), and had flown for European Aircharter and Air Atlanta Europe before being retired from service. It was refitted with two mock-up engines on each inner pylon, and external fuel tanks on the outer pylons, somewhat resembling a B-52 Stratofortress', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77953fc4-5065-4bc7-a821-628b78b0ceeb'), 'During the black-and-white sequence at the beginning, Dryden goes up in an elevator, showing the floor indicator. The scene cuts before the elevator goes higher than six, because Bond has not yet earned his "double-0" status, 007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a016351f-328e-4a87-bba8-1752339c5b06'), 'Daniel Craig''s role in Layer Cake (2004) clinched the role of James Bond for him over the other competing rival actors. DVD and video rentals of the movie went up after the announcement Daniel Craig would be the new James Bond. The Layer Cake (2004) end-of-movie Bondesque line has Craig say "My name? If you knew that, you''d be as clever as me", evoking the famous catchphrase "The name is Bond, James Bond"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('641e312f-688f-4940-b14e-00895436413e'), 'Vesper''s purple evening gown was made by Roberto Cavalli, while her black one was by Versace. In addition, she wears Versace 4061 sunglasses in Venice, and her unique Algerian love knot necklace was made by Sophie Harley. She also wears Melograno perfume by Santa Maria Novella. Valenka (Le Chiffre''s girlfriend) wears a Versace swimsuit and an evening gown by Roberto Cavalli. Solange (Dimitrios'' wife) wears a green La Perla bikini and an orange evening dress by Jenny Packham', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a0330a98-9eee-4aaf-85a1-eac649afabdd'), 'According to Spirit Yachts, "the scene portraying Daniel Craig and Eva Green cruising into Venice on-board a Spirit 54 is now world famous. Having been handcrafted by Spirit Yachts'' skilled team of boat-builders in Suffolk, the yacht (a 54 foot design named Spirit) was shipped to the Bahamas. From there, Spirit Yachts sailed her to Puerto Rico and through the British Virgin Islands for filming. After shooting scenes in the Caribbean, the yacht was shipped to Croatia and sailed on to Venice. During filming in Venice, the yacht''s rig was taken in and out a total of 10 times to fit under multiple canal bridges. She was the first sailing yacht to go up the Grand Canal in 300 years"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db3b7c69-826a-4a04-a658-be6eab17d37d'), 'Poker playing was a common pastime amongst cast and crew on the set, even after production had wrapped. This, however, is not new for a James Bond movie. Sir Roger Moore and Albert R. Broccoli, during breaks in filming, played and bet on backgammon. Many of the James Bond movies have been known to have cast and crew participate in some high-stakes gambling', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c7adadde-f7b3-47ae-9330-2b463cc4fa51'), 'The 2007 Ford Mondeo sport model used in the beginning of this movie is a special, one-off handbuilt prototype vehicle, constructed at Ford of Europe''s Design Studio in Cologne, Germany in January 2006, and shipped to the Bahamas in secrecy for shooting. Production was not due to start until the second quarter of 2007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('48549112-3b12-424f-8759-231ad8457dc6'), 'When Bond plays poker at the Ocean Club, and wins Dimitrios'' car, the dealer running the game is a professional poker dealer who works at that establishment', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f02cbca5-a9db-404f-a857-898ed13f5c93'), 'Vesper Lynd''s official job was that of International Liaison Officer for the Financial Action Task Force of H.M. Treasury. Her work address was 1 Horse Guards Road, London, SW1A 2HQ. Like the use of the real Vauxhall Cross address of MI6 in the James Bond movies of the last decade, this is the real address of Her Majesty''s Treasury', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d3c9c473-acf1-4e47-841a-f0a02eaeb876'), 'Martin Campbell claimed that the only reason he agreed to direct was that he had no other projects in development', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e7a7826-60d5-4f8b-a999-c3e19b1e8357'), 'Casino Royale has two danish actors on the role list. Mads Mikkelsen as Le Chiffre and Jesper Christensen as Mr. White', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d69d104e-ed64-4691-9352-51826af28b4d'), 'Pierce Brosnan had expressed an interest in making this movie, but was considered too old at the age of fifty-three', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9364287a-eba8-4b60-9196-1e738b9a2578'), 'Daniel Craig is the first actor to play James Bond who was not cast by founding James Bond producer Albert R. Broccoli', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f0937990-b39d-4bc5-b350-d2281aa7c7a1'), 'This is the first EON Productions film to feature ally Rene Mathis. Mathis appeared in the original Ian Fleming novel, but not the movie From Russia with Love (1963), and variations of this character''s name have appeared in Climax! (1954) season one, episode three, "Casino Royale" (as Valerie Mathis) and Casino Royale (1967) (as Inspector Mathis). Rene Mathis returned in Quantum of Solace (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d367f397-446c-4f9d-9244-9e0f301240a6'), 'Angelina Jolie, Naomi Watts, Scarlett Johansson, Sienna Miller, and Charlize Theron were strongly considered for the part of Vesper Lynd', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87cc0c53-9342-4b00-bfe9-4c5fb4d0faa3'), '"Q" does not appear in this movie. The last time this happened was in Live and Let Die (1973), which was Sir Roger Moore''s debut as Bond. (It is possible however that the unnamed MI6 Technician who implants a tracking device in Bond''s is, if not the current Q, at least someone who works in Q Branch.)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a143b392-5db6-495b-8312-63b2fa2ba7b7'), 'In the original novel, Le Chiffre is described as an overweight, unattractive man. Mads Mikkelsen doesn''t fit that description', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ee593073-92a7-44a0-8879-22662195b4da'), 'Producers Michael G. Wilson and Barbara Broccoli decided to re-hire GoldenEye (1995) director Martin Campbell to direct this movie, as they felt he was the right man to direct Daniel Craig''s debut as James Bond. GoldenEye (1995) was Pierce Brosnan''s debut in the role of James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Casino Royale'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('d5b21f4d-ddc4-4d3d-9ce3-99269a520c1a'), 'Daniel Craig was injured at least three times during the making of this movie. The most prominent ones included an injury to his face, which required four stitches, another to his shoulder, which required six surgical screws to be inserted in an operation, and his arm in a sling, and then his hand was injured when one of his finger tips was sliced off. He laughed these off, noting they did not delay filming, and joked his finger wound would enable him to have a criminal career (though it had grown back when he made this comment). He also had minor plastic surgery on his face', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c9492584-4b1e-4234-a21b-c02cf65e3432'), 'Chile''s Atacama Desert (where the finale was filmed) is the driest region on Earth, with no record of any measurable rainfall ever having occurred there', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b7fc8ac9-0ab8-437b-8938-3ae3b7b8a35a'), 'According to Mathieu Amalric (Dominic Greene), his character does not have any distinguishing features to make him more formidable, and to represent the hidden villains of society: "He has no scars, no eye that bleeds, no metal jaw. I tried everything to have something to help me. I said to Marc Forster: No nothing? A beard? Can I shave my hair? He said: No, just your face." Amalric also described Greene as "not knowing how to fight, so James Bond would be more surprised. Sometimes anger can be much more dangerous. I''m going to fight like in school"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ced8a315-5e98-4087-a413-96811dd51276'), 'In a later interview, Daniel Craig revealed that the script originally wasn''t intended to be as much of a sequel to Casino Royale (2006) as it ended up being. However, because of the writer''s strike, they had only the "bare bones" of a script, and Craig and director Marc Forster ended up re-writing a lot of scenes between them, with many decisions being made on the fly, and at the last second. Much of the content that made it such a direct sequel to Casino Royale (2006) was a last-second addition. Also, the title was chosen more or less at random, with Craig saying that most Bond movie titles are "meaningless" anyway, and they hoped it would sound intriguing. The title didn''t really connect with the script they had at the time, and the revenge story elements that actually made the title relevant were last-second additions', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e5ae5e29-3658-47c4-a0bc-b783ffbcd24f'), 'Daniel Craig wasn''t fond of how production went, saying that thanks to this, he''d never do a movie without a script nailed down again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6412f24d-41fe-4864-9170-8ae38beff8ad'), 'Director Marc Forster thought Dame Judi Dench was underused in the previous movies, which is why she has such a bigger part to play this time. He had her interact with James Bond (Daniel Craig) more because "she is the only woman Bond doesn''t view in a sexual context", which Forster always found interesting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d41d0ea4-cc69-4402-a90e-5bdef137ffae'), 'The Aston Martin DBS makes a return in this movie, due to a three-movie, $100 million deal that Ford Motor Company has for exclusive vehicle product-placement rights', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9ad52cf7-712c-46df-8017-87d1cdc176b5'), 'A free-fall scene with James Bond (Daniel Craig) and Camille (Olga Kurylenko) was shot in the Bodyflight Wind Tunnel in Bedford, with seventeen small digital cameras. It was going to be shot in the conventional way (with a large fan blowing in the cast members'' faces), but Craig disliked the idea of a fan in his face, and stunt coordinator Gary Powell suggested filming in a wind tunnel. For safety, Daniel Craig and Olga Kurylenko shot for only thirty seconds periodically, and wore wind-resistant contact lenses that enabled them to open their eyes as they fell. The Body Flight Wind Tunnel is twenty-six feet (about eight meters) long with a diametric width of about sixteen and a half feet (about five meters) and can simulate free falling at one hundred seventy miles per hour (about two hundred seventy-four kilometers per hour)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a49eea5-f783-4e81-9c1d-5a39a1120aa9'), 'Daniel Craig felt Casino Royale was physically "a walk in the park" compared to this movie. His training was extremely intense, involving more boxing, running, speedboating, and stunt driving. He was injured at least three times in the making of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e3903025-5f51-4bd6-9c15-0d74d9d242c5'), 'James Bond and leading Bond Girl Camille (Olga Kurylenko) share a kiss in this movie, but do not make love, making it a first for a James Bond film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6c715945-30a6-4844-af85-443c035c5ba1'), 'It turned out to be cheaper to shoot the Siennese rooftop chase in the town, rather than try to re-create it at Pinewood Studios', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56a42768-83af-4c68-81ee-08576f6a33d3'), 'As with Casino Royale (2006), the traditional movie characters of Q and Miss Eve Moneypenny do not appear. Producer Barbara Broccoli has said: "In Casino Royale, the book, there was no Moneypenny or Q, so that is why they are not in that story and, in this follow-up, there didn''t seem to be a reason or a place for them"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ee2fe74c-0015-497e-9bdb-34e5e398c5a5'), 'This movie marks the first time since You Only Live Twice (1967) that Bond does not introduce himself with the catchphrase "Bond, James Bond." The line was shot for several different scenes, but was completely cut out, as director Marc Forster and the producers found it unnecessary. (From Russia with Love (1963), and Thunderball (1965) also do not use the line) The other staple Bond line stating a "vodka martini, shaken not stirred" does not appear in this movie either', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bb1277af-09d5-4718-adae-75f6aabefae5'), 'Screenwriter Paul Haggis finished his final draft of the script only two hours before the Writers Guild of America writers'' strike started', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4c626970-d803-40d7-9051-26aaf687c0b2'), 'As the first direct sequel, Daniel Craig commented: "We felt we needed to tie up the loose ends from Casino Royale (2006), and make sure people realize we are back making Bond movies. For me, it''s about creating something that is going to stand alone, but if you put the two films together, you''re going to have an incredible experience, because you will see one continuous story"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('11651116-5260-4f4d-9675-49563d95038b'), 'According to Olga Kurylenko, she was chosen by Marc Forster out of the four hundred women who auditioned for the role of Camille because she seemed the least nervous of them all. She spent three weeks training with weapons and learned how to fight and body fly, a form of indoor skydiving. Kurylenko dislikes filming stunts, but Daniel Craig''s compassion helped her to carry them out. Kurylenko also trained with a dialect coach to perform with a Spanish accent, which was easy since "she has a good ear and can imitate people." She was also given a DVD box set of all of the 007 movies, since she had not seen many of them, although the James Bond movies are quite well-known in her homeland of Ukraine. This later sparked controversy because most of the women they passed over were of Latin descent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a034bf35-cd62-40d9-856d-a5c4115552e7'), 'Greene''s plot in the movie is a clear reference to the "water wars" in Bolivia in 2000, when water rights were sold to a corporation, which sharply increased the price beyond the ability of many Bolivians to pay for it, inciting demonstrations that forced the government to reverse the decision. The U.S. agreement in the movie to support a coup, in order to get oil, also recalls America''s swift support for (and possible involvement with) the attempted coup against Chavez in Venezuela in 2002. Interestingly, the evil plot from the movie is less evil than the real-life one, as the intended price hike is less than the one that really happened', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1ad5e4d5-02c8-4f10-8bea-9f01e689dbb8'), 'Gemma Arterton found out she got the role of Strawberry Fields when her agent called and just sang the James Bond theme on the phone to her', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e40eb2e-cf61-4af1-95b3-90f15558eabc'), 'Reportedly, Daniel Craig was paid £4.5 million for this movie, more than twice as much as the £2 million he received for Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4087a517-6333-4cb3-890a-8d6ecfc51a10'), 'According to Mathieu Amalric, it was easy to accept the role of Dominic Greene because "it''s impossible to tell your kids that I could have been in a Bond film but I refused!" Having played a paralyzed newspaper editor in The Diving Bell and the Butterfly (2007), Amalric found the role refreshingly physical', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('36cefe75-ce24-43f2-a29e-7e62d6573cd9'), 'First time that an actor (Jeffrey Wright) has played the Bond ally character of Felix Leiter in a consecutive Bond movie. It is only the second time that an actor has played Leiter twice. David Hedison played him in Live and Let Die (1973) and Licence to Kill (1989)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c664e642-af9b-4894-a91e-a1ae47bdd84f'), 'Bond''s confrontation with Vesper''s boyfriend is taken from the short story "007 in New York", in which Bond warns a female intelligence employee that her boyfriend is an enemy agent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('00b2744e-afbf-4fe2-992a-fd24caf37d74'), 'While filming in Panama, Daniel Craig had to change hotels several times after the press discovered his whereabouts. Problems for the cast and crew were caused by the increased attention of the paparazzi', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('68ab77df-0e66-409a-b669-7802569aab71'), 'This is the first James Bond movie where James Bond is seen inebriated. Bond has never actually been shown drunk (he may have appeared as this in Casino Royale (2006), but he had been poisoned). The scene in a bar on the plane in this movie clearly shows he has been affected by alcohol, and it is mentioned that he drank six Vesper martini cocktails', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c865ae7d-985a-4508-8914-6e53793bfc15'), 'The title was selected only a few days before its announcement on January 24, 2008. For a long time, it had been considered unsuitable for a James Bond movie. Daniel Craig admitted he was unsure about it, but it seemed to fit in the context of the movie: "Bond is looking for his quantum of solace, that''s what he wants. Ian Fleming says that if you don''t have a quantum of solace in your relationship, you might as well give up. Bond doesn''t have that because his girlfriend has been killed, therefore he''s looking for revenge to make himself happy with the world again." Quantum is also the name of the organization in this movie, a kind of new-age S.M.E.R.S.H., or the fictitious S.P.E.C.T.R.E.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('51198462-c8c6-4902-a0cb-8eb79490804c'), 'Editing this movie was so stressful that co-editor Richard Pearson was brought in to assist Matt Chesse, to speed up editing. Director Marc Forster only had five weeks to edit the entire movie. In his previous movies, Forster would take an average of fourteen weeks to edit', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1b2d48db-520d-4b02-abd4-2929aac5e3ae'), 'The movie was filmed in more locations than any other 007 film: U.K., Panama, Chile, Italy, Mexico, and Austria', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('36c6d139-8119-4871-93b5-883760d13ca5'), 'When Olga Kurylenko read the script, she was glad she had no love scene with Daniel Craig, as she felt it would have distracted viewers from her performance', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a6ba478b-e46c-4fb8-af22-5bb199184638'), 'On April 19, 2008, Fraser Dunn, an engineer driving James Bond''s Aston Martin DBS to the set, lost control of the car and ended up in Northern Italy''s Lago di Garda (Lake Garda). Some media labelled the incident "Dry Another Day" (a take on Die Another Day (2002)). The technican suffered only minor injuries, but the car, valued at £120,000 ($155,761), was completely totalled. Reportedly, a fan later paid about £200,000 for the wrecked car, which is about £80,000 more than what the car was worth brand new. More surprising is the fact that this particular car (one of six) was not part of even any filming for the movie, and is not seen in the final cut', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4ec72d09-179a-48db-a7f5-6a4b943d8e54'), 'The already huge budget blew out when many of the action scenes took longer than thought to shoot. The opening car chase, in particular, was a long shoot, and several stunt cars were accidentally destroyed before they could be used', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ceb566c3-75f7-4180-b70e-aa7e4db35a06'), 'Pre-production work began before Casino Royale (2006) started filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('45c09711-8d32-4e76-b1ac-8b0e684792f2'), 'American fashion giant Tom Ford was personally commissioned by Daniel Craig to design exclusive clothing for his 007 character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d0a92e7-287c-4f34-b7a0-afedd07034c5'), 'On April 1, 2008, while filming was going on in the village of Baquedano, Mayor Carlos Lopez drove his sedan into the village of Baquedano, nearly running over a policeman. He was reportedly furious that the filmmakers did not seek his permission to film in the village. He was outraged that this movie portrayed the region of Antofagasta as part of Bolivia, when Chile had conquered it in 1883; and criticized security measures like "special forces and water cannons to prevent people walking in the street" for the small town, which reminded him "of the worst of the Augusto Pinochet years." He was arrested, detained briefly, and put on trial two days later. His claim that they needed his permission to film in the area was dismissed: Michael G. Wilson explained that Bolivia was essential to the plot, due to its history of water problems, and was surprised the two countries disliked each other a century after the War of the Pacific. When the Chilean newspaper "La Segunda" ran a poll on the incident, seventy-five percent of its readers disagreed with Lopez''s actions, feeling it now presented a negative image of Chile', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('99a9d69f-7483-4c43-b3b8-e1220c5fbf72'), 'The Perla de las Dunas Hotel in this movie is actually the ESO Hotel, which is part of the Paranal Observatory in northern Chile. The hotel is only open to scientists and astronomers who work at or visit the observatory and is not open to the public', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6995981d-0ade-48ad-b63b-b2751dece731'), 'Sir Paul McCartney turned down the offer to write a new James Bond song for this movie, and recommended singer-songwriter Amy Winehouse for the job. Winehouse recorded a demo with music producer Mark Ronson. The demo was not used for reasons linked to Winehouse''s inability to record music at a time due to her well publicized personal situation', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('86b225fe-3dc4-4c9b-adec-64aea394dc78'), 'The floating opera stage sequence utilized 1,700 extras, who were paid £42 a day for three days'' work. CGI visual effects enabled the audience to appear as almost 7,000 patrons', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b2fdf86d-889b-4174-ad50-9177cd3c238a'), 'Real-life Intelligence operatives acted as on-set consultants for the movie, including spies and assassins from MI6 and the Israeli Secret Service', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('27c19c29-a904-4160-85d4-9125bfd6fb7b'), 'The fifth highest-grossing James Bond film worldwide, after Skyfall (2012), Spectre (2015), No Time to Die (2021), and Casino Royale (2006)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('866da447-5bb9-4e61-928c-d7d4c154179e'), 'To shoot the foot chase in Siena, officials supplied one million Euros to the filmmakers for them to build four camera cranes, alter rooftops, and hire three hundred extras needed for the scene. The centuries-old rooftop tiles had to be removed by the production from the old houses, and the roofs reinforced, so cast members and stuntmen would not fall through them', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a7b4c856-46e5-4031-96c8-ec8508032bae'), 'When Elvis (Greene''s rug-wearing assistant) calls Universal Exports, the voice that answers belongs to Gemma Arterton', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80aee2f7-2a2e-408e-98d4-24d210f1f233'), 'Bond hands a Universal Exports business card to one of Greene''s men in Haiti that shows the pseudonym R. Sterling. The same name was used by him in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) when he introduced himself as Robert Sterling to Stromberg, with Anya Amasova as Mrs. Sterling', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cddaa1d6-e232-4c7c-ac43-d84d333b6015'), 'Screenwriter Paul Haggis described James Bond in this movie as "a very human and flawed assassin, a man who has to navigate a morally complex and often cynical world while attempting to hold onto his deep beliefs of what is right and wrong." Daniel Craig further described Bond as "an unfinished article with a sense of revenge, who is still headstrong and doesn''t always make the right decisions"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('be2830b0-69f1-400c-84b2-4448ab733fdd'), 'James Bond''s eleven costume changes required about four hundred twenty pieces of clothing. There were nine versions of every suit used in the movie. Three were normal, three were battered with blood and debris, and three were waterlogged, in addition to being also battered with blood and debris', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b28536f3-754a-4b30-a43d-33e7495852e3'), 'The movie shoot used 200,000 rounds of blanks, which were used for training, testing, and filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d8813f6-f0b9-4c94-ae8e-2fae7e95dd0b'), 'Stuntman Gary Powell, and other members of his family, have worked on every EON Productions Bond movie since Dr. No (1962). Father and uncle Nosher Powell and Dinny Powell worked on all the early 1960s and 1970s Bonds, with Sir Sean Connery and George Lazenby; brother Greg Powell worked on the 1970s and 1980s Bonds, with Sir Roger Moore and Timothy Dalton, and Gary worked on all of the 1990s and 2000s Bonds, with Pierce Brosnan and Daniel Craig', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('54850bee-97c2-43e6-ae7f-fb914d2c58c0'), 'This is the first James Bond film that has no gun barrel sequence at the start of the movie, and the first to use it at the end of the movie. This is also the first James Bond movie where we see Daniel Craig perform the gun barrel walk synonymous with the sequence and the films. The gun barrel walk was not part of the alternative gun barrel sequence in Casino Royale (2006), which had a gun barrel sequence at the start, but with different graphics, and was not the traditional sequence. Daniel Craig became the seventh person to perform the traditional gun barrel walk and sequence after the first five actors who played James Bond, and stuntman Bob Simmons, who did it in the first three Bond movies. It''s also the first gun barrel sequence to be presented in color since Die Another Day (2002), and the first to show Bond wearing a business suit since The Man with the Golden Gun (1974)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('307427f5-4964-4795-9994-7d3cee2b8792'), 'It was once extensively rumored that Al Pacino would be making a cameo appearance at the end of this movie as the head of the Quantum criminal organization in a brief role equivalent to that of a master villain like Ernst Stavro Blofeld. Apparently, Pacino was interested in taking the role of General Medrano', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35d6f390-2800-4452-b1d0-9cb0c425658f'), 'Mathieu Amalric based his character of Dominic Greene on two political figures: France''s then-President Nicolas Sarkozy and former British Prime Minister Tony Blair', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('548014a2-5dcc-42cb-a27a-3d10c8d9a8ee'), 'Jeffrey Wright''s role as Felix Leiter was originally much bigger, but on-set re-writes curtailed his part', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f662dd58-684f-4cd7-ab0f-a409e0576a6a'), 'The meaning of the title according to different sources. The Governor character in the Ian Fleming short story of the same name defines it as "a precise figure defining the comfort, humanity, and fellow feeling required between two people for love to survive. If the quantum of solace is 0, then love is dead." He then introduces the Law of the Quantum of Solace as follows: "I''ve seen flagrant infidelities patched up, I''ve seen crimes, and even murder foreign by the other party, let alone bankruptcy, and other forms of social crime. Incurable disease, blindness, disaster, all of these can be overcome. But never the death of common humanity in one of the partners. I''ve thought about this, and I''ve invented a rather high-sounding title for this basic factor in human relations. I have called it the law of the Quantum of Solace." In the same story, James Bond comments on the Law of the Quantum of Solace as follows: "That''s a splendid name for it. It''s certainly impressive enough, and of course I see what you mean. I should say you''re absolutely right. Quantum of Solace, the amount of comfort. Yes, I suppose you can say that all love and friendship is based in the end on that. Human beings are very insecure. When the other person not only makes you feel insecure, but actually seems to want to destroy you, it''s obviously the end. The Quantum of Solace stands at zero. You''ve got to get away to save yourself." In an interview, the producers explained: "It means that a relationship cannot be salvaged unless there is a ''quantum of solace'' between the two parties, ''Quantum'' meaning ''measure'', and ''solace'' meaning ''comfort'', so if they are not willing to share that, then their relationship is not redeemable. In our case, it is a couple of things: Bond is looking for a ''quantum of solace'' after his experiences in Casino Royale (2006), and QUANTUM also happens to be the name of the villainous organization in the film"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8fa5035-8385-48af-b59c-7ce1fa1fd4f1'), 'At one hour and forty-six minutes long, this is the shortest James Bond movie in the EON Productions official series. This movie is a direct sequel to Casino Royale (2006), which coincidentally was the longest movie in the official series until ''Spectre'' (2015). ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008) was also the first Bond movie to run under two hours since Tomorrow Never Dies (1997). The non-EON made-for-television season one episode three of ''Climax! (1954)'', "Casino Royale", has the all time record for being the shortest Bond film, with a running time at only fifty-one minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e1b5b50-b5a4-433f-b5fb-9d4d1d2d5224'), 'This is the first James Bond movie to have a boat chase and a car chase since The Man with the Golden Gun (1974). This movie is the only Bond movie that has a foot chase, a car chase, a plane chase, and a boat chase', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('00fd01f4-7f6f-439d-b767-c7cd4c19e07b'), 'Gemma Arterton won the part of of Agent Strawberry Fields over fifteen hundred other applicants. The full name of her Miss Fields character is never revealed in the movie and is only ever referred to as "Fields". Her full name is given in the closing credits and publicity documents as "Strawberry Fields", named after the 1967 song by The Beatles. She has red hair, like strawberries. Strawberry Fields can be considered a typical Ian Fleming-esque moniker. Arterton has reportedly based her character on a few 1960s Bond Girls, particularly Pussy Galore (Honor Blackman) and Tracy di Vicenzo (Dame Diana Rigg), on whose hairstyle Arterton based Fields'' hair. She''s the fifth major redheaded Bond Girl, the first four being Fiona Volpe (Luciana Paluzzi) in Thunderball (1965), Tiffany Case (Jill St. John) in Diamonds Are Forever (1971), Helga Brandt (Karin Dor) in You Only Live Twice (1967), and Tracy di Vicenzo in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f83ce6a-7025-45fe-aada-ddac7f61d90c'), 'An early draft of the script involved James Bond discovering that Vesper Lynd had a child (by a previous relationship) and who had been kidnapped by Quantum. Paul Haggis'' submitted script included a scene at a U.N.-style international conference, with Bond having to follow a Quantum secret conference by constantly switching frequencies. The scene was re-written to take place at an opera, as director Marc Forster feared that it wouldn''t be visually interesting', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('92a37d1b-1765-42c2-b924-7f932e60f2ca'), 'Director Marc Forster wanted to film in the Swiss Alps, which was a location for On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), and is where he grew up. Switzerland was also the nationality of the literary James Bond''s mother. However, the Swiss Alps location was written out of the movie for cost reasons. The climax originally featured there. There were concerns that the locale would be too similar to On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969). The finale now takes place in the desert, a terrain which has never before housed a villain''s lair in a Bond movie. Forster also wanted the action sequences to be based around the four classical elements of earth, water, air, and fire', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9ac335f9-0a09-4470-ae4f-d1eb7d550787'), 'Olga Kurylenko found Michelle Yeoh in Tomorrow Never Dies (1997) inspiring "because she did the fight scenes by herself"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('be078595-4a80-4abd-81d0-19b6bc652197'), 'In trailers for the movie, the "007" part of the title logo shifted to form the "November 7" release date. While this was a great visual gimmick in the trailer, the release date was pushed back to November 14 in the U.S.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('07ef0fd7-109f-4072-87b8-06a0c608e862'), 'A sequence where James Bond was to come out of the underground cisterns at Siena Cathedral was cut from the script, as it was considered culturally insensitive, disrespectful, and offensive to have the character arise from this location. Instead, Bond emerges from the Fonte Gaia', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2bbb3c76-91c1-4dd0-8bbf-e6865e8bb8a8'), 'As with Casino Royale (2006), the fully orchestrated James Bond theme isn''t heard until the end of this movie, this time during Daniel Craig''s new official gun barrel sequence, as well as the start of the ending credits, marking the first time that a gun barrel sequence with Daniel Craig is accompanied by the James Bond theme, since the version of the sequence used in Casino Royale (2006) dropped it completely, being accompanied instead by the opening bars of the theme song of that movie, "You Know My Name" by Chris Cornell. It is also the second consecutive Bond movie that ends with the James Bond theme during the credits, followed by a vocal or instrumental track', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0c59154c-dca6-4ad1-9715-172cdf3084bf'), 'For the Lake Garda sequence, where a truck explodes and falls into the lake, a custom-made net was designed to catch the truck', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('20c1569a-04d7-4188-a4a3-2168570a210d'), 'Marc Forster is the first director in the EON Productions James Bond series not have a nationality from the British Commonwealth. Forster was born in Germany, whereas all previous directors were from England or New Zealand', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b20f9912-5036-4bd8-9ee6-f480a04af8e5'), 'First time that an official James Bond movie title song has been sung by two artists as a duet. The theme is called "Another Way To Die" and was sung by Jack White and Alicia Keys. They were officially announced to be performing the song on July 29, 2008', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6ee4fe5f-a1ec-4e40-817b-df64c189e113'), 'The character of MI6 Agent Strawberry Fields (Gemma Arterton) is a tribute to the Bond Girls of the 1960s, notably Tracy Bond from On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) and Goldfinger (1964)''s Pussy Galore, both of which are Arterton''s favorite performances. Arterton described Fields as "not as frolicsome or femme-fatale as other Bond Girls, but is instead fresh and young"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Quantum Of Solace'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('c1b20548-4a64-43e2-8a9f-3ec61f4fa03d'), 'In fifty years of James Bond movies, this is only the second one in which Bond suffers a gunshot wound. He was also shot in Thunderball (1965) during the Junkanoo chase', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cc2e62e5-3b58-4304-b88e-c89b3d9094ab'), 'Daniel Craig performed the stunt of leaping and sliding down the escalator rail himself', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0c13a5fd-4282-4b21-a78b-837ab91a1364'), 'If you watch the scene in the Komodo dragon pit closely, you will notice Daniel Craig has strange-looking, pudgy hands. This is because during filming, Craig had gone to the shops and purchased a pair of gloves that he thought were fitting for 007. Director Sam Mendes let him wear them in the scene, but later during editing, they realized the gloves didn''t work with the logic of the scene: James Bond''s gun is picked up by a henchman, who is unable to fire it because the gun has been coded to Bond''s palm print, only allowing Bond to fire it. Therefore, Bond wearing gloves makes no sense, as he wouldn''t be able to fire his gun. After some frantic calculations on how much re-shooting the scene would cost, it was deemed too expensive, and Craig''s hands were CGI''d in', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1caa5dda-1fc9-4288-a695-b4ba835dea6b'), 'The role of Kincade (Albert Finney) was originally written with Sir Sean Connery in mind. Producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson originally wanted Connery to come out of retirement and make a surprise cameo. Director Sir Sam Mendes told "The Huffington Post", "There was a definite discussion about (Connery playing Kincade), way, way early on. But I think that''s problematic. Because, to me, it becomes too... it would take you out of the movie. Connery is Bond, and he''s not going to come back as another character. It''s like, he''s been there. So, it was a very brief flirtation with that thought, but it was never going to happen, because I thought it would distract"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fc6c5ea7-f557-4206-8672-d1ca10f0be3f'), 'Daniel Craig bonded with Javier Bardem on the set over their shared love of rugby. In his youth, Craig played for Hoylake Rugby Football Club in Wirral, Merseyside. Bardem played for Club de Rugby Liceo Francés in Madrid, and even made the Spanish national team at underage level', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8dbec473-568c-498b-8fc3-9b8ffcb0e548'), 'The first James Bond film to gross $1 billion worldwide', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ac46b8c5-0357-446c-a4c1-60518d7c3710'), 'Dame Judi Dench played the role of M in this movie at the age of seventy-seven. The performance is also Dench''s seventh time playing M. This is Dench''s largest on-screen role playing M, the most significant James Bond movie ever to explore a relationship between M and James Bond. Producer Barbara Broccoli said that this movie explores this relationship perhaps more than in any of the twenty-two previous movies. She said, "We wanted to really mine the relationship between Bond and M, because it is the most significant relationship he has in his life. M is the only person who represents authority to him. You have two extraordinary actors, and we just thought, let''s go all the way. It''s worked extremely well. It''s a very emotional story"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1c94518-07c1-42a7-aac1-c84812146923'), 'There were eighty-five versions of James Bond''s Tom Ford suit tailor-made for the opening chase sequence. Thirty were made for Daniel Craig, and thirty for his double and stunt double. Each version of the suit was made specifically for a particular scene of the opening sequence. For example, when Craig was riding the motorcycle, a suit with longer sleeves was worn so that it wouldn''t raise up over his forearms. Costume designer Jany Temime said: "Each suit had three fittings, like a real traditional Saville Row suit. It was very high class tailoring. The first suit was mohair, very lightweight, woolen silk. The tuxedo is woolen silk. They were all (made of) beautiful fabric. He (would be) jumping and fighting, and then he would stand up, and the suit would be perfect." Also, Craig''s tie had to be weighted for the motorcycle section of the chase. The weight kept the tie from flying around when he rode at high speeds', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('634d626c-1999-4563-9d05-e54097af9311'), 'Daniel Craig said that he was worried by the delays in the production, and was eager to get back into the role because, at the age of forty-three, he felt he was already getting too old to cope with the extreme physical demands of playing James Bond. Craig starts preparation for a Bond movie about six months prior to filming, and works out for about two hours each day of principal photography after shooting has wrapped', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e3cdbee0-1933-4e67-9c2c-0d9acd8f6de9'), 'After receiving a personal invitation from Her Majesty Queen Elizabeth II, Daniel Craig appeared as James Bond in promotion of this movie at the Opening Ceremony of the 2012 Olympic Games in London in the games'' introductory video originally titled, "The Arrival", but later known as "Happy and Glorious". The Daniel Craig and Queen Elizabeth II pretend entertainment segment featured Craig as James Bond who meets with the Queen to escort her safely to the stadium. They are seen going to a helicopter, which flies along the Thames River to the cauldron, whereby stunt doubles then "skyfall" jumped out of the helicopters down to the awaiting ceremony to familiar James Bond music. The segment has been said to be the Queen''s first acting role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9eb7bb25-59f0-4843-ac0b-acdd6d59c60f'), 'The passport used by Daniel Craig was not created by the prop department, but an authentic document as issued by the British Home Office, according to producer Michael G. Wilson. Everything from the paper, print, photograph, and jacket are entirely genuine on James Bond''s "official passport". However, as a security measure, the passport is encoded with information that would instantly flag its improper use in any official transaction. The actual details shown on Bond''s passport in this movie are as follows: Name = John Adam Bryce; Date of Birth = 16th December 1968; Sex = Male; Place of Birth = London; Date of Issue = 22nd June 2012; and Expiry Date = 22nd August 2029', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2fcfb414-1080-4a5d-8f31-8f50cbc31300'), 'Hashima Island, the site of Tiago Rodriguez, a.k.a. Raoul Silva''s lair, is a tiny deserted industrialized island situated off the southwest coast of Japan, fifteen kilometers (nine and a half miles) from Nagasaki, and running just four hundred eighty meters (three tenths of a mile) long and one hundred sixty meters (one tenth of a mile) wide. The small isle is one of five hundred five uninhabited islands in the Nagasaki Prefecture. The isle is also known as "Ghost Island", as well as "Gunkanjima", which translates as "Battleship Island". The island was last significantly inhabited in 1974, and was once a thriving coal mining community. The island is notable for its character, due to its sea wall, and its untouched abandoned and derelict concrete buildings', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2ed00c09-461b-485d-a2ec-3b3d34f325c2'), 'The porcelain bulldog on M''s desk (which she later gives to Bond) is draped in the Union Jack. These bulldog figurines were created by Royal Doulton during World War II to represent patriotism. In Tinker Tailor Soldier Spy (2011), Control (Sir John Hurt), the head of MI6, has two Royal Doulton bulldogs sitting on his desk', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('afd731e1-2548-4526-8dce-23d321148420'), 'Daniel Craig performed many of his own stunts, including the signature rooftop fight on the top of a moving train travelling at fifty kilometers per hour (thirty-one miles per hour) during the opening sequence. Producer Barbara Broccoli has said: "Daniel contributes a great deal to designing the action and the fights in particular, and he''s the one who really pulls it off, because he wants to do as much of it as he possibly can. We were in Turkey for the train sequence, and I had my heart in my mouth the whole time. He and Ola (Rapace) were fighting on the roof of a moving train, and the moves that they were doing were just heart stopping. Daniel''s the reason why the action works as well as it does, because he sells it, he''s up there, and I think audiences know that"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2b2b3dd3-9768-4cab-bfe8-47895ced258a'), 'The opening sequence shot in Adana and Istanbul, Turkey took around two months to film, three months of rehearsals, four months of preparation, 200 crew members from England, and another 200 local crew, in order to produce around twelve to fourteen minutes of screentime', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0370731b-8c3c-4658-a7a5-8dce32c7ea9d'), 'Dame Judi Dench has more screentime in this movie alone than Desmond Llewelyn had in his seventeen movies as Q, making her portrayal of M the most recurrent character in the franchise, after Bond (as measured by screentime)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d437e7fa-58a7-4aa6-b8ac-c1002a6d57db'), 'Final of twenty-three James Bond movies for trumpet player Derek Watkins, who had worked in the music department as a trumpeter on every James Bond movie since he was 17 years old, when he worked on Dr. No (1962). Watkins died in 2013, four months after the release of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('29bf4b3c-2b62-4edf-a94d-85e9a0454d27'), 'Filming of one of Javier Bardem''s first scenes - the interrogation of Silva by M and Bond at the new MI6 headquarters - had to be stopped in one of the early takes when Bardem interrupted the scene by excitedly proclaiming that he couldn''t believe that he was making a movie with Dame Judi Dench and Daniel Craig', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6b66264a-541a-442c-a0db-8c311c69e65a'), 'Adele was pregnant when she recorded the theme song. In an interview with the BBC, she said her pregnancy hormones caused her voice to go deeper, hence why her singing tone in this song is so low. She also said she is not able to re-create this low tone now', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1fac3e7d-7045-4673-95b7-38fc07288634'), 'A few days after this movie debuted in Britain, the real MI6, the Secret Intelligence Service (S.I.S.), took out a full page advertisement in "The Times" and "The Sunday Times" running with the headline "If the qualities that make a good spy were obvious, they wouldn''t make a very good spy." The aim of the ad was to debunk the legend and mythology associated with movie fiction spies, like James Bond in this movie, saying that real-life spy work is not "high-speed chases and shoot-outs", an average spy is not a "globe-trotting secret agent" and that psychological profiles of real-life agents show that they are actually "far more ordinary". The ad also dismisses the white male spy stereotype, saying that "the truth is, we don''t care what sex you are, or where you''re from, as long as you''re a British national." The humorous advertising campaign is considered one of MI6''s most open recruitment drives. But in true espionage fashion, the ad still warns of utmost secrecy and strict confidentiality, advising potential candidates that they cannot disclose that they are making an application to anyone', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e76cd0a-dcd2-42db-b49e-df89fd47159a'), 'M''s (Dame Judi Dench''s) house in this movie is the former home of legendary James Bond composer John Barry. The filmmakers thought it would be a loving tribute to the late composer, who scored many of the James Bond movies, and defined the signature theme music in the franchise, his work being a core inspiration for the modern Bond music composed by David Arnold. John Barry died in 2011. Thomas Newman''s score for this movie has been said to pay tribute to Barry', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('794ba6bd-28fe-4c96-ae17-808d5c6da93b'), 'On an October 2012 episode of The Graham Norton Show (2007), Dame Judi Dench revealed how her mobile cell phone has a ringtone with the James Bond theme, and how when it rang during filming on the set, it would often produce laughter, and after a while, her annoying 007 cell phone ringtone became an on-set running joke', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5a41fcd8-0afd-4c7d-a99a-8c1d82363fd7'), 'Daniel Craig told Rolling Stone Magazine that he wanted this to be his third and final Bond movie, saying, "I''ve been trying to get out of this from the very moment I got into it, but they won''t let me go." Craig signed on for two more James Bond movies, Spectre (2015) and No Time to Die (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1b75daaa-1bc5-4bc9-91b9-b56ed26a6a7e'), 'The quotation that M recites is from Alfred Lord Tennyson''s poem "Ulysses", "To strive, to seek, to find, and not to yield". First published in 1842, its recitation in this movie''s 2012 release occurred on the poem''s 170th anniversary', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f9517890-813a-42c0-b981-7b0e280e6087'), 'This movie deals with James Bond''s Scottish ancestry. Bond''s family history was created by Ian Fleming in the Bond novel "On Her Majesty''s Secret Service". Fleming was inspired to add the backstory of Bond''s genealogy into the book after seeing the character played by Sir Sean Connery (a Scotsman) in Dr. No (1962). This is the second time in the official James Bond film franchise that Bond discussed the death of his parents. The first time was in GoldenEye (1995). The Clan of Bond names, created by the production for the plaques and headstones at the chapel and graveyard, include: Andrew Bond, Robert Bond, Monique Delacroix Bond, Celia Bond, Kathleen Bond, Elsa/Elsie Louise Bond, Ramsay William Bond, and Margaret Jean Davidson Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1ecccd7f-9581-4007-9157-64e771698af8'), 'This marks the third consecutive James Bond movie which ends with him alone, where most other films in the franchise, he is seen with one of the leading Bond Girls', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('55bda839-0ad8-4976-8fff-31b29cac2a09'), 'Early into his casting, Javier Bardem told director Sir Sam Mendes that he wanted to make some particular changes to his own appearance, notably in his hair and eye color. When Bardem showed up on set on his first day of filming in his Silva make-up and effects, he wasn''t recognized', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('63ac5eb3-2694-441e-a105-7a8f6fa84888'), 'For the motorcycle chase in Turkey, Coca-Cola was sprayed on the tarmac of the streets in Istanbul to keep the bikes from sliding. While Coca-Cola is not an official product placement in the movie, there was a Coke Zero marketing campaign that tied in with the movie. Coke Zero would have been less effective, as the sugar in Coca-Cola makes it sticky', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0ea18f9b-b70d-4542-a640-7af4f30177ba'), 'The komodo dragons in the floating casino scenes were completely computer generated. The difficulties in filming with components that weren''t actually there were sufficient to convince director Sir Sam Mendes never to use CGI-created characters ever again', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8da239c3-c6b0-4bfe-8e14-4211378caefb'), 'Naomie Harris stated on The Graham Norton Show (2007) that, because she would be using a real razor blade she spent six weeks with a professional barber training for the razor shaving scene, trying it on members of the crew along the way', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c034b1d1-55fd-4c69-bea7-5591f8f83b98'), 'The provocative scene where James Bond meets Tiago Rodriguez, a.k.a. Raoul Silva in what appears to be some kind of homosexual seduction often provoked giggles between Daniel Craig and Javier Bardem to alleviate the tension between the two', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('03aef953-0dce-47d8-b4b8-1b88aba4671f'), 'Skyfall Lodge is not a real-life building, but a purpose-built exterior set, made of plywood and plaster stone. The custom-built artificial house in this movie''s story is a countryside residence. Its setting is in Glencoe, Scotland, but the filming location for it was Hankley Common in southwest Surrey, England', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('11f4fa0b-47f2-45df-b33b-37d3e5c07387'), 'The shooting location of Shanghai makes this the first Bond movie to have filmed in China. Originally, Licence to Kill (1989) was to be filmed in China, but when the Chinese government made several restrictive demands, such as veto rights over the script, the viability of the location fell through. This was once rumored to feature a motorcycle chase along the Great Wall of China, a chase sequence originally intended for Licence to Kill (1989), but instead there is a rooftop motorcycle chase, filmed in Istanbul, Turkey. Another sequence, a fight sequence in the then recently discovered museum of ancient terracotta statues at Xian, was also scheduled for Licence to Kill (1989), but this sequence wasn''t used for this film either. Screenwriter John Logan wanted to use Shanghai as a filming location because, "What we were looking for was opposition to London. We wanted exotic locations that seem so unlike the world that he grew up in, the world that he functions in, in a way trying to find places for Bond to be uncomfortable"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e39629b1-bf51-404e-b0e2-624dc3a6dfa6'), 'Numerous cast members, playing smaller parts in the movie, never received a script with which to work, due to the production''s strict secrecy protocols, so stringent and tight that they reflect real-life intelligence espionage. Tonia Sotiropoulou did not know what she would be doing in this movie until the time her scenes were shot. She commented, "I was one of the people who never had a script. I just got told what I''d be doing on the set by the director. They have to be so careful. You have quite strict contracts that say you can''t say anything about the plot, and everyone respects that"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3d8096c6-71d8-480a-b354-8b9e0f60368f'), 'This movie was influenced by Batman Begins (2005) and The Dark Knight (2008) by director Sir Christopher Nolan, according to director Sir Sam Mendes. Several early reviews of this movie likened the mood of the movie to that of The Dark Knight Rises (2012). Interestingly, a recurring line of dialogue in The Dark Knight Rises (2012) was "permission to die", this is also the title of a 1989 James Bond comic book. A shot of Bond standing on top of a building, looking out over London with a flag of England, evoked Batman perched on rooftops looking out over Gotham City. Mendes said: "In terms of what (Nolan) achieved, specifically The Dark Knight (2008), the second movie, what it achieved, which is something exceptional. It was a game changer for everybody. What Nolan proved was that you can make a huge movie that is thrilling and entertaining, and has a lot to say about the world we live in, even if, in the case with The Dark Knight (2008), it''s not even set in our world. That did help give me the confidence to take this movie in directions that, without The Dark Knight (2008), might not have been possible." Nolan has often stated that the classic James Bond movies were an influence on his The Dark Knight trilogy. As such, one can say that Bond has inspired Batman and that Batman has inspired Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0a8cea23-2ada-4f18-b01c-762197f71e82'), 'At the 2013 Academy Awards ceremony, this movie became the first James Bond movie to achieve several records in the franchise''s history: The highest number of Academy Award nominations ever received by a Bond movie (five: Best Song, Score, Sound Mixing, Sound Effects Editing, and Cinematography). The first Bond movie in three decades to receive Oscar nominations. The last time was in 1982, when For Your Eyes Only (1981) was nominated for Best Song. 1982 also saw producer Albert R. Broccoli receive the Honorary Thalberg Award. First Bond movie to win two Oscars (Goldfinger (1964) and Thunderball (1965) won just the one each). The third Bond movie to win an Academy Award, and the first in forty-seven years, the last being Thunderball (1965). This movie''s tied Oscar for Sound Editing was not actually the first in that category, as Goldfinger (1964) had won for Best Effects, Sound Effects; and Diamonds Are Forever (1971) had been nominated for Best Sound. Although many Bond songs have been nominated for the Best Song Oscar (Live and Let Die (1973), For Your Eyes Only (1981), The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), and the unofficial Casino Royale (1967)), Adele''s "Skyfall" became the first James Bond theme to win the Academy Award for Best Original Song', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e8440497-d44c-4121-8202-48ac847bcae6'), 'In preparing for his role, Javier Bardem had the script translated into his native Spanish to better understand his character, which director Sir Sam Mendes cited as being a sign of the actor''s commitment to this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6221485f-6508-4b17-a9db-eb7c96e36830'), 'Javier Bardem described his character as "An angel of death, a very cleanshaven person who happens to be rotten on the inside. He has a very personal objective, he''s not trying to destroy the world, and he is on a straight line to that objective. He is a man seeking revenge. It''s about being focused on the one person he wants to eliminate." Bardem has also explained about finding the character inside the villain: "It''s always about who''s the person behind the character. It would be very difficult for me to play a role that I just saw as some kind of symbol. In this case, there is a man suffering, a man full of pain and frustration, who simply wants to fix the situation. Within that journey, there was room to be funny or aggressive, but I could perfectly understand who he was, and that helped me to portray him"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e2b61798-1f87-4ecf-a646-8328b077a77c'), 'Albert Finney''s last movie role before his retirement the same year this came out. He died on February 7, 2019 at the age of eighty-two', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('df7b19bc-e721-4634-954b-cd2350f8f5e0'), 'Ben Whishaw is the fourth actor to play Q in the official James Bond franchise. This marks the first time that Q is younger than James Bond. The producers have said that "When it came to trying to reintroduce the character of Q, it made sense that he would now be a young technical genius, and the character was written with that in mind." Whishaw''s Q has been likened to that of computer genius-types like Jack Dorsey and Mark Zuckerberg. Coincidentally, Whishaw has said that he doesn''t even own a computer. Peter Burton first played Q under the character''s real name of Major Boothroyd, and nicknamed "the Armorer" in Dr. No (1962), then Desmond Llewelyn played Q in seventeen Bond films between 1963 and 1999, followed by John Cleese (as Q''s assistant "R") in The World Is Not Enough (1999), then as Q in Die Another Day (2002), the latter being the last time the character appeared in the official franchise before this movie. Whishaw is the sixth actor to play Q when one counts the unofficial Bond films Casino Royale (1967) and Never Say Never Again (1983), where Q was played by Geoffrey Bayldon and Alec McCowen, respectively. Q is an abbreviation for the word "Quartermaster"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('abffe6d4-e01f-48ba-bd62-058bb697e8c5'), 'Adele''s "Skyfall" is the first Billboard Top 10 hit to win the Academy Award for Best Original Song since Eminem''s "Lose Yourself" from 8 Mile (2002)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c8915c98-69e7-4f17-bdad-609b4aedabde'), 'The scene where Bond takes M to his secret garage and his Aston Martin was shot in early December 2011 on a freezing cold night that just also happened to be Dame Judi Dench''s 77th birthday. She was presented with a birthday cake in a parking lot at 4 a.m.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0cca8111-f07f-41cf-be0e-3e81ce9d7f97'), 'The production was criticized during principal photography in Turkey for allegedly damaging the rooftops of buildings in Istanbul, where a rooftop motorcycle chase was being filmed. One such incident that made local headlines was when a stunt rider rode off a roof and smashed the window of the renowned Bobeyi jewelery store. Producer Michael G. Wilson held a press conference and the claims were quashed, as the roofing had been removed for the stunt riding, and replaced with replicas until filming wrapped, whereupon the original tiling was returned. This is not the first Bond movie to feature a rooftop motorcycle chase, it''s the second, as one appeared in Tomorrow Never Dies (1997)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0fd9041e-31f8-46f0-a081-0b3ba73f5e50'), 'Eminönü Square, a busy business district in Istanbul, Turkey, was used for filming the opening sequence, and had to be closed for three weeks in order to do this. The place is one of Istanbul''s oldest and most magnificent squares, and is surrounded by the ancient Spice Bazaar and the fabulous Yeni Mosque. In a curious requirement for the bazaars, the shops could open, but could not trade, due to the area being off-limits to the public, traffic, and pedestrians. Shopkeepers were reimbursed 750 Turkish Liras per day to cover their losses. The Turkish bazaar sequence in this movie featured over 250 dressed market stalls, created by the Art and Prop departments, and was populated by around 500 extras', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3b922c8b-d3fa-48e0-b8fb-c00213b07b96'), 'The computer mainframe room, in which Silva gives his introductory speech, was specially constructed so that it would be the right length for a one-take shot, in which Javier Bardem leisurely walks and ends up right at Bond when at the end of the speech. The other significant room in which Silva is seen is a plexiglass enclosure, which was nicknamed by Javier Bardem as a "Crystal Cage"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e877b455-9848-486e-8f57-5e1348bcbd97'), 'According to the U.K. Sun newspaper, Bond Girl Bérénice Marlohe said that Daniel Craig was coy and hesitant before filming their love scene in the shower. Marlohe said: "He was very shy, and when he saw me entering the shower, he was like, ''Oh, my God''. He tried to keep his underpants on for the shower scene, but I said, No, come on, don''t be shy. I will do anything to make you feel comfortable"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d68ecd8c-ecd6-4cfd-a810-f354d2656443'), 'Second time in the official James Bond film franchise that Bond broke into M''s (Dame Judi Dench''s) house, as he did in Casino Royale (2006). That time, M said, "Don''t ever break into my house again", though she fails to mention that in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2afa0bda-b006-4f97-aa86-650adc0af85b'), 'This movie has a lot in common with The World Is Not Enough (1999). Both involve abduction victims left to their fate by M, who they view as a quasi-maternal figure, and M is forced to deal with the consequences of her decisions when said victims want revenge. They are also the only James Bond movies where M is actually part of the story, rather than just giving Bond his briefing and sending him on his way. Both feature scenes in Istanbul, Turkey, as well as a chase scene in London (a rarity for the franchise, despite London being in nearly every movie), an explosion at MI6, MI6 being temporarily relocated, Bond recovering from a shoulder injury sustained in the teaser, the introduction of a new Q, a female lackey, who is terrified of her male terrorist employer, Bond being held captive in a chair by the Big Bad, the Big Bad using Bond to get to M, Bond pursuing a villain underground, a helicopter destroying Bond''s car, Bond using gas to blow up a helicopter, and the bad guy being impaled by a metallic object', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ad9a49a7-f74e-4d2a-83b5-da11551a5b91'), 'During the martini scene at the bar, the famous James Bond drink catchphrase "shaken, not stirred", wasn''t spoken, but the martini was explicitly concocted on-screen, and the bartender is shown shaking the martini before pouring it. Also, the bottle of alcohol that Tiago Rodriguez, a.k.a. Raoul Silva (Javier Bardem), offers Bond (Daniel Craig) on his island says "1962" on its label, referencing the franchise''s 50th Anniversary. The beer is Heineken, who contributed a rather large amount of money for the product placements. Bill Tanner (Rory Kinnear) was also seen drinking the beverage', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3e91643a-cfdd-4ef6-8903-483d4ea84822'), 'This movie is not a follow-up from the two previous movies. Producer Barbara Broccoli said that the franchise "will go on to other different stories from now on." However, the reappearance of the QUANTUM organization in later movies is still a possibility. Broccoli said: "I think in some way, he will go after the (QUANTUM) organization. So in that sense, it may become a trilogy, but we haven''t really structured it that way"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('69942cd1-9d97-4454-bac6-7aa2b4e6e8f2'), 'Glencoe, Scotland is a filming location that portrays its own setting: Glencoe. In the James Bond novel "On Her Majesty''s Secret Service", Ian Fleming gave Bond a sense of family background, writing that Bond''s father Andrew was from Glencoe. The Glencoe region has one of the most iconic landscapes in Scotland, the mountains contain some of the oldest sedimentary and volcanic strata in the world. In this movie, these mountains served as a beautiful backdrop for Bond and M''s drive through Glencoe''s scenic roads, in the iconic silver-birch Aston Martin DB5', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e5f8f4a0-7e79-481e-a41a-74bf46c01cc6'), 'Kevin Spacey was considered for a role, but declined due to scheduling conflicts. It is believed that director Sir Sam Mendes originally offered Spacey the role of the villain, Tiago Rodriguez, a.k.a. Raoul Silva. Spacey worked with Mendes on American Beauty (1999), in which Kevin Spacey''s character complained to his wife about missing a James Bond marathon on television', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a65417ef-e57d-44de-ab7b-4b8da5514d21'), 'During principal photography, three Turkish youths bypassed tight security in Adana, Turkey, to infiltrate a closed movie set, where they filmed footage of a train scene being shot with their mobile phones. Fitting of the intrigue from the earlier Turkey-set Bond movie, From Russia with Love (1963), the three snuck through alleyways and jumped a wire fence into a train station where this movie was being filmed. The trio slipped under train cars and rendezvoused at the repair depot, where they went into spy disguise and put on off-duty worker''s helmets and overalls. They were later caught by security, interrogated, and removed from the set', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5622d8c6-5ce1-47f3-9c07-ba69726a206d'), 'The promotional tie-in with Heineken lager beer for this movie has been valued at being £28 million ($45 million American). The product placement caused a controversy in the media prior to release, criticism being made for lacking integrity, blatant commercialization with Daniel Craig appearing in a Heineken ad, and being disrespectful to James Bond''s traditional drink, the shaken, not stirred martini. Producer Michael G. Wilson and Daniel Craig defended the financing by indicating that the Bond movies cost a lot of money to make, and this movie could not be completed without this support; that many of the product placements are based around supply of the products, with technical support, and the fact that James Bond is still seen drinking a vodka martini', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8591a288-df4c-4b45-9746-fcec97e6f995'), 'The train fight scene was supposed to shoot in India, with a lot of people travelling on the roof of the train. However, the Indian government would not give permission, saying that it would give a bad impression about India and its culture', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6fae70aa-bfdd-494c-a183-f976ac42f68b'), 'According to Dame Judi Dench, the secrecy surrounding the details of the plot were such that advance copies of the script were individually stamped, so they can be specifically traced to each official recipient in the event of negligent disclosure of plot details', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('828ec1d3-8def-4188-8f49-10ff92595150'), 'The license plate number of the Aston Martin DB5 is BMT 216A, the same as it was in Goldfinger (1964) and Thunderball (1965). Also, the garage out of which the Aston Martin DB5 drives in this film resembles the villain''s facility in Goldfinger', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c85d7c4c-eae2-46ec-b5ae-f11530097aba'), 'The marketing has been said to have gone to a new level with (Daniel Craig) appearing in several commercial television advertisements for product placements seen in this movie, such as Heineken, Omega watches, and Sony Electronics. However, this has been justified, Daniel Craig has said, "The simple fact is that, without them, we couldn''t do it. It''s unfortunate, but that''s how it is. This movie costs a lot of money to make, it costs nearly as much again, if not more, to promote, so we go where we can"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b21b83d2-4332-4f95-8c4f-440c8bea3d53'), 'The top-secret Intelligence career of original James Bond producer Harry Saltzman was first revealed by fellow Canadian David Giammarco in his acclaimed 2002 book "For Your Eyes Only: Behind the Scenes of the James Bond Films", published for the 40th anniversary of the James Bond movies. For this 50th anniversary 007 movie, longtime Bond franchise collaborator David Giammarco, along with contributions from Hilary Saltzman and Steven Saltzman, disclosed the full extent of their father''s Intelligence work, including previously-classified documents, photos, and analysis in an exclusive feature for Vanity Fair Magazine titled "50 Years of 007: The Secret Spy Life of James Bond Producer Harry Saltzman". As part of the James Bond worldwide publicity for the golden milestone of cinema''s longest-running franchise begun in 1962 by Albert R. Broccoli and Saltzman, this remarkable package of revelations, kept under extremely tight wraps by Giammarco and Vanity Fair for nearly a year, immediately sparked thrilling media headlines around the globe in the countdown to the highly-anticipated theatrical release of this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1e17fa4a-c907-4a5d-b35e-80986045a05a'), 'For the first time in the famous gun barrel sequence, Bond is seen wearing a grey suit rather than a black one', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('539bc5d6-fdbb-4e8f-9078-851d0850957d'), 'During the final assault on Skyfall Lodge, the downdraft from the helicopter (an Agusta Westland Merlin AW101) was so powerful, it blew the false teeth out of Javier Bardem''s mouth', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c6fba416-ff75-470c-a2af-f1bf4cb56b35'), 'When Bond (Daniel Craig) and Q (Ben Whishaw) meet in the National Gallery in London, Q jokes about giving Bond an exploding pen when Bond moans about the tools received to fulfill the mission. Two previous movies had Q giving Bond such a pen: Never Say Never Again (1983) and GoldenEye (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3f046ae1-9dc2-4fa8-9c37-2548209c1326'), 'The title is not a word taken from any Ian Fleming James Bond story. Screenwriters Neal Purvis and Robert Wade thought up the title, "Skyfall", at two in the morning. Neal and Robert have said: "We needed a haunting place name. I just plucked it out of the air, and it turned out to be something that struck a chord with the filmmakers." This is the only Bond movie where the team provided the title. The World Is Not Enough (1999)''s title was taken from a real-life Bond family motto, and was mentioned by Ian Fleming in the novel of On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), while the title of Die Another Day (2002) was taken from a phrase in A.E. Housman''s poem "A Shropshire Lad". Casino Royale (2006) and Quantum of Solace (2008) were titles taken from original Ian Fleming stories', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a50859b5-424b-4d09-a103-de23fa76e61f'), 'The Aston Martin in this movie, while having many of the gadgets of the original, is not identical. Specifically, the original had a noticeable panel in the roof for the ejection seat. The one in this movie has a smooth roof without the panel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fb6087ed-6afb-43df-9569-d89b52572bd9'), 'M''s name is "Olivia Mansfield". A 2013 prop exhibition revealed her full name to be visible in an inscription on the box given to James Bond from Miss Eve Moneypenny containing M''s porcelain bulldog figurine. In 1995, the original script for GoldenEye (1995) had revealed M''s name as "Barbara Mawdsley", but early drafts of scripts aren''t considered canon, only what ends up on-screen, and this was before the reboot with Casino Royale (2006), so Dame Judi Dench''s interpretation of M could be two different characters (however unlikely). Curiously, "Olivia" is Dench''s middle name, and the first head of the British Secret Service was (George) Mansfield Smith-Cummings (known by the first letter of his last name "C"). According to fellow spy novelist John le Carré, Ian Fleming (ever tongue-in-cheek), designated the head of S.I.S. as "M", using Cummings'' first name. Keeping the Mansfield as a surname is a twist, but not intended in any of Fleming''s original works. Fleming''s "The Man With The Golden Gun" gave M''s name as "Myles Messervy"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('06531b6c-a1cb-48fe-9450-7fa108706c63'), 'Second time in the official James Bond franchise that Bond is seen with a beard, the first time was Pierce Brosnan in Die Another Day (2002). In both movies, the character only has the beard for a portion of the movie. In both instances, we see the beard being shaved', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cc6eaf47-bb7c-4858-9f19-d7660828912e'), 'The Paddock Tank (the Exterior Tank) at Pinewood Studios doubled as the exterior of the Shanghai Golden Dragon Casino. The set was lit by three hundred floating lanterns, and two thirty-foot high dragon heads. Twelve artisans were flown in from China, to create the authentic structures. They were made from wound steel cables, silk fabric, and lit from within, by four hundred light bulbs', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e1bfebb-bf12-4368-becf-72a52c1be492'), 'In the Macau casino scene, Fukutu (Tom So), one of the high stakes gamblers from Casino Royale (2006), can be clearly seen playing billiards in the background', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bbcd0aac-8c6a-4802-a1b6-0535568ca438'), 'The name of the World War II-era French song heard playing on Silva''s island lair is "Boum!", and is sung by French singer and songwriter Charles Trenet. The song won the Grand Prix du Disque, and was released in 1938', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8b598abb-5af0-4e6b-a995-7477ba5f696e'), 'The painting that Q (Ben Whishaw) and James Bond (Daniel Craig) view at the National Gallery is "The Fighting Temeraire" (1839) by J.M.W. Turner. His best known painting, it depicts H.M.S. Temeraire, one of the last 90-98 gun "second class" warships, which had played a distinguished role in the Battle of Trafalgar in 1805. In 1838, it was decommissioned and towed from Sheerness to Rotherhithe to be broken up for scrap. Turner''s main motive of painting was to evoke a sense of loss in the demise of a ship that had once seen great glory. It is evocative of this movie''s theme of the aging warriors M (Dame Judi Dench) and Bond, which is touched on again in M''s quoting of Tennyson. The painting in the private sale is is Woman with a Fan (1919) by Italian artist Amedeo Modigliani. The reason for this being a private sale is that it was stolen from the Museum of Modern Art in Paris in May, 2010. This same painting appeared in Spectre (2015), hanging in Madleine''s room at Blofeld''s facility in Morocco', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5731d208-ecd5-4bfb-ab47-090915cf2ec0'), 'The exotic Calis Beach, a remote beach in Fethiye, Turkey, was a great challenge for the locations department to secure for filming a sequence featuring James Bond. EON Productions had to negotiate with the 613 part-owners of the beach to allow filming to take place there', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9714e540-9608-46f0-a185-5a536ee98e39'), 'The Grand Bazaar in Istanbul, Turkey was featured prominently during the opening chase sequence. The Grand Bazaar is one of the largest and oldest covered markets in the world, with sixty-one covered streets, and over three thousand shops attracting up to four hundred thousand visitors daily. Due to the hazardous nature of the sequence, access to the location for this movie unit could only to be granted on Sunday, when the bazaar is closed. Through a combination of efforts from the locations department, production design, art department, and prop department, the bazaar was dressed overnight on preceding Saturday nights to look like the hive of activity that the one would expect from the location. 500 Turkish extras were brought into the Grand Bazaar to provide the location with its usual crowded and buzzing atmosphere. The rooftops of the Bazaar served as a spectacular platform to view Istanbul''s ancient and dynamic skyline. The production went to great lengths to protect and preserve the Grand Bazaar''s historic architecture, which included floating reinforced steel roof panels over the existing tiles to protect the original structure. The age of the Grand Bazaar shop, where a motorcycle crashes through its window, was around 330 years old', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e33a04a2-3f4f-4ca3-9533-2490fbd7a8a2'), 'In early drafts of the script, when M (Dame Judi Dench) enters her house to find James Bond (Daniel Craig) waiting for her, the line "007 reporting for duty" was followed by "You''re supposed to be dead." Bond''s response was "I came back", and M said, "You only live twice, Mr. Bond". This would have been a reference to You Only Live Twice (1967), starring Sir Sean Connery', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('52e0d855-3193-4fe1-adbc-fc30b70116e7'), 'While speaking via microphones in "The Golden Dragon Casino", James Bond (Daniel Craig) warns Miss Eve Moneypenny (Naomie Harris) to stop touching her ear. This is a reference to Casino Royale (2006), where Bond warned Agent Carter (Joseph Millson) to stop touching his ear while speaking to him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('823afba1-1796-4442-8d78-c3c3d79a614c'), 'Raoul Silva, the main villain, does not appear until around seventy minutes into this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fd21ef63-8d9a-4253-b40c-969793e31880'), 'Dame Judi Dench''s seventh and final major appearance playing M. Dench has played the role of M for seventeen years from 1995 until 2012, her first being in GoldenEye (1995). This record ties with Bernard Lee, who played M for the same amount of time, except Lee appeared in eleven James Bond movies, while Dench appeared in seven. Additionally, this puts Dench at the same number of Bond movies as Sir Roger Moore, as well as Sir Sean Connery (if one counts the unofficial Bond movie Never Say Never Again (1983)) and Walter Gotell (who played the roles of Morzeny in From Russia with Love (1963), and then General Gogol for six movies consecutively from The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) to The Living Daylights (1987)). However, Dench played a cameo role in Spectre (2015) in a special video appearance', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2c98ccd4-1adf-42d7-a16c-50ad086400a5'), 'Daniel Craig was injured during the rehearsal period for this movie, whereupon rescheduling took place requiring two weeks rest for his injuries. Craig was not injured during principal photography. This is the second time in the franchise''s history that a delay has been forced by an injury to the actor playing James Bond. The first was on Die Another Day (2002), where Pierce Brosnan blew his knee out during filming of the opening hovercraft sequence, shutting down production for around one to two weeks', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dc758130-9afd-4105-8841-4318d1132b51'), 'Tiago Rodriguez, a.k.a. Raoul Silva''s (Javier Bardem''s), helicopter was an AgustaWestland AW101. Even though this was one of the newest, and most advanced, helicopters when this movie was made, sound effects editor William R. Dean did the common practice of dubbing in the sound of a two-bladed Bell Huey Vietnam-era helicopter, developed in the late 1950s', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2e6840bd-c5d0-4714-b1f0-31dd08ff4abd'), 'Director Sir Sam Mendes used to be in a relationship with Rachel Weisz, who was once rumored to going to be cast in this movie. Weisz is now married to Daniel Craig. Weisz has also appeared in espionage movies, such as The Bourne Legacy (2012) and The Constant Gardener (2005), for which she won an Academy Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role, and which coincidentally also starred Ralph Fiennes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('856d28c0-7782-4c3e-8951-fe7b10240893'), 'At first, Q and Bond look at the painting "The Fighting Temeraire" by J.M.W. Turner, depicting the old ship of the line HMS Temeraire being towed for scrap. This mimics Bond himself as an aging warrior being retired. Yet, at the end of the movie, when Bond is talking to the new M there is another painting in the background, this time depicting the Battle of Trafalgar, with HMS Temeraire in her prime, symbolizing the return of 007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f33e99be-3df9-4ac3-8399-659ac48bea4f'), 'Bond''s father''s hunting rifle is a .500 caliber Nitro Express, an extremely powerful elephant gun. During the final shoot-out, Bond is shown firing it from the hip. Its recoil would make this a very foolish thing to do, and a human being struck by one of the bullets would not merely fall down. A shot placed at center-mass would explode the entire chest cavity, and likely blow the target''s arms out of the shoulders', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('69449064-bfdf-415f-ad50-42e38273e8a2'), 'The first James Bond movie to be shot entirely digitally. Previously, only part of one scene in Quantum of Solace (2008) was shot digitally. It is also the first movie to use the Arri Alexa Studio camera, which cinematographer Sir Roger Deakins selected because, unlike the other Alexa models, it has an optical viewfinder. Deakins shot with Arri''s sole Studio prototype, as the camera was not yet in production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d0c1954d-3f18-4ead-b13d-d473df6c9394'), 'The glass set, depicting the inside of the Shanghai office skyscraper, was nicknamed "The Jellyfish". It was built at Pinewood Studios, and was likened to being like "a hall of mirrors". Cinematographer Sir Roger Deakins said: "Because it was all glass, the crew walking through it kept bashing into things". For filming, Deakins lit the set with two gigantic LED panels, which were used to represent electronic billboards exterior to the skyscraper''s office windows. The production had originally location scouted for a Chinese skyscraper, but this proved to be unsuccessful, the substitute set providing improvements by being multi-dimensionally made of glass. The sequence in this movie, that "The Jellyfish" is seen, is when Bond is on the track of an assassin on the way to a Shanghai office complex. In The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), a hall of mirrors was seen during the opening sequence, and at the finale', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7c58a3cd-f8b5-4d48-b220-cdd10f9d5eaa'), 'The gun barrel sequence was re-shot specially for this movie, as it was in the previous movie. With this third Daniel Craig Bond movie, Craig has still never appeared in a traditional franchise gun barrel sequence shown at the start of the movie (the last movie to use the sequence at the beginning was Die Another Day (2002)). According to Sir Sam Mendes, there was an attempt to put the gun barrel walk before the pre-title sequence, but it did not work out artistically. It was also put at the end of the movie, so as to be able to mark the Golden Anniversary of the franchise with Bond''s 50th Anniversary logo. Daniel Craig is also the first actor to film three different gun barrel sequences, which depict Bond wearing different suits, and having different stances as he shoots. For the first time in the famous gun barrel sequence, Bond is seen wearing a grey suit, rather than a black one. Sir Roger Moore is the other Bond actor to have shot more than one gun barrel sequence, as he had filmed one for Live and Let Die (1973), which was re-used in The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), and eventually filmed a second one for The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), that would be re-used for the rest of the Bond movies starring Moore', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a22441b8-bb33-4b70-8969-059ca026694e'), 'Grossed $100 million at the international box office in its first week', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3f1f8b5b-6b90-47cf-8c2e-a2174c3d976a'), 'The London underground tube train crash that occurs when Bond chases Silva was filmed at Pinewood Studio''s mammoth 007 Stage, which has been the filming home to most of the super-scale Bond set pieces of the past. For the crash, filmed on "The Catacombs Set", the crew built two full-size fabricated replica Tube train carriages, each weighing around five to seven tons, the real ones weigh around twenty-five to thirty tons. The Tube carriages were raised onto a track about twenty feet above the base of the set. Near the ceiling of the set, broken Tube tracks curved downwards, with a monorail supporting the carriages from above. The trains were then accelerated on the elevated track guided by the monorail as they veer off the tracks and crash through the catacombs ceiling, which was composed of breakaway elements. When the train crashed, it dismantled the majority of the 007 Stage. Digital visual effects were later added in post-production to supplement the practical special effects. It was too dangerous to allow people to stay on the soundstage during the filming of the crash, so eleven remotely-operated cameras were placed around the 007 Stage to cover the crash from various angles', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7601a3c4-a8f3-4b5b-b4c0-d1c36a3cdc7b'), 'Raoul Silva was modelled on The Joker from The Dark Knight (2008) and Colonel Hans Landa from Inglourious Basterds (2009)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('60abb572-8e78-43d4-8e7d-1788ea875fd0'), 'The stags depicted at the entrance to the Skyfall estate were inspired by the pair at Duntrune Castle in Argyll', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('585d3027-950e-4595-a18a-daa027e44187'), 'The mug from which Q drinks in his lab has the letter "Q" from the game Scrabble printed on it, complete with the number "10", the letter''s point value in the board game', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('21e20c8d-4619-4654-b11f-66dcdec34a49'), 'Development and production was delayed for almost nine months during 2010 to 2011 due to the bankruptcy and delayed sale of MGM, with the production being officially suspended on April 19, 2010. The press release from producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson for this movie, then known as "Bond 23", stated: "Due to the continuing uncertainty surrounding the future of MGM, and the failure to close a sale of the studio, we have suspended development on ''Bond 23'' indefinitely. We do not know when development will resume, and do not have a date for the release of ''Bond 23''". During this period, some development and pre-production work continued on this movie, despite the cancelled financing, with the goal to have this James Bond movie in theaters for the 50th anniversary of the franchise. Production resumed in January 2011', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56041ff0-6e59-4c0f-b963-b621d5695e9a'), 'The names of the leaked MI6 agents in the YouTube video are names of members of the production crew, though the corresponding faces shown are of actors. The names used include: art director Paul Inglis, assistant executive producer Andy Surry, and special effects technician Steve Benelisha. The other two MI6 agent names, Mansur Dimka and Ben Daheer, appear not to be based on anyone in particular. The handle of the YouTube poster posting the video in this movie is "vials", which is an anagram for "Silva", the last name of villain Raoul Silva. Also, the runtime on the YouTube video is 0:07, a reference to James Bond''s code number of 007', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d52857d0-df00-4f41-a90f-84ed152df0cd'), 'The Royal World Premiere of this movie marked a rare reunion for the families of James Bond producers Harry Saltzman and Albert R. Broccoli and author Ian Fleming on the franchise''s 50th anniversary year. Since Saltzman was able to secure the movie rights for the 007 novels in 1962 from Fleming, given both men''s shared experience as Intelligence operatives, the unique seating arrangement at Royal Albert Hall reflected that relationship. In the Royal Box adjacent to His Majesty King Charles III (then the Prince of Wales) and the then-Duchess of Cornwall (Queen Camilla), the surviving family of Ian Fleming, including niece Lucy Fleming, and cousin Sir Christopher Lee, who also served in British Intelligence, were seated alongside Saltzman''s daughter Hilary Saltzman, son Steven Saltzman, and Canadian print and broadcast journalist David Giammarco, a longtime associate of the James Bond movies and author of the book "For Your Eyes Only: Behind the Scenes of the James Bond Films". The Gala Charity Premiere of this movie benefited retired members of Britain''s Intelligence agencies, for which His Majesty is England''s Royal Patron', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('393c09bb-e2c0-4e16-a273-b368614dae5b'), 'Tonia Sotiropoulou, who appears as a minor Bond Girl early in the movie, had auditioned for the other Bond Girl role of Sévérine, but lost out to Bérénice Marlohe. After casting director Debbie McWilliams suggested that the production might be able to find another part for her, her management company, Back Door Management, resubmitted her for this movie, and she was successful. Tonia''s Bond Girl character has no name, and is billed in the credits only as "Bond''s Lover". Also, her brief role is entirely mute, making her the first Bond Girl to visibly consummate a relationship with Bond (as opposed to one that is only implied), without saying one word', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('23e77d23-bbfa-4fad-b4ab-520869674794'), 'In Shanghai, the man who is assassinated is looking at a painting that is revealed to him. The painting is "Woman with a Fan" (1919) by Amedeo Modigliani, which had been stolen from the Paris Museum of Modern Art in 2010. The thief, 49-year-old Vjeran Tomic was known as "Spiderman" for his climbing ability. He was arrested one year after the theft, but the painting was never found. Presumably, it''s being sold by a fence to this art collector. This is a callback to the stolen portrait of the Duke of Wellington by Goya we see on Dr No', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dfd5be5f-3ef6-4a34-9043-7b03dcb0b055'), 'When it came time to casting Silva''s mercenaries, director Sir Sam Mendes wanted actors rather than stuntmen. In order to find actors that could fit the physical bill, stunt coordinator Gary Powell set up a stunt training camp. Starting with forty-two men, the group had to learn how to throw punches, react to punches, hold guns, and react to being shot. The group was eventually narrowed down to the seven men who looked most natural', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1a7b6100-6101-44f4-9117-6e365bf97073'), 'M writing James Bond''s obituary after he''s presumed dead is from the novel "You Only Live Twice"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e0342d55-936f-46d4-b8ef-40116d8fd828'), 'Stuntman and James Bond stunt double Andy Lister performed the opening sequence''s fall from the bridge into the river. Riggers were set up a crane on a train carriage, to hold a safety line. Andy then reacted to the gun shot by limply diving backwards off of the three hundred foot (ninety-two meter) drop. This jump stunt is a typical Bondian "Skyfall" jump synonymous with the franchise. Skyfall jumps having appeared regularly since The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), with others in Moonraker (1979), For Your Eyes Only (1981), Octopussy (1983), A View to a Kill (1985), The Living Daylights (1987), Licence to Kill (1989), GoldenEye (1995), Tomorrow Never Dies (1997), The World Is Not Enough (1999), Die Another Day (2002), and Quantum of Solace (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e2a54f8-ba82-45e0-a704-00f470af976b'), 'The four-year gap between the release of Quantum of Solace (2008) and this movie ties for the third-longest period between James Bond movies. This gap between movies also represents the longest time between movies without a casting change to the actor playing James Bond. Previous hiatuses between Licence to Kill (1989) and GoldenEye (1995) (the longest period between movies in the franchise), and then between Die Another Day (2002) and Casino Royale (2006) were both accompanied by casting changes to the actor playing James Bond. The gap between Spectre (2015) and No Time to Die (2020) is now in second place, at five years', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8a126821-d274-47f6-ad1b-3a4f45a83f21'), 'At two hours and twenty-three minutes, this film was at one time the second-longest Bond movie of all time, the longest then being Casino Royale (2006), at two hours and twenty-four minutes. At that time, the third-longest running time for a Bond movie was two hours and twenty-two minutes for On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), which had previously held the record as the longest for 37 years. With a running time of 163 minutes, or two hours and 43 minutes, ''No Time to Die'' (2020) has the longest ever running time for a Bond movie. At two hours and twenty-four minutes, ''Casino Royale'' (2006) was once the longest James Bond movie, beating the previous record holder On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) by four minutes, until the release of Spectre (2015), which beat it by another four minutes. ''Spectre'' (2015) was previously the longest James Bond movie record holder, with a running time of two hours and twenty-eight minutes. Daniel Craig has now played Bond in the four longest Bond movies of all time: ''No Time to Die'' (2020, ''Spectre'' (2015), Skyfall (2012), and Casino Royale (2006). The former long-time record holder, On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), is now in fifth place, with Skyfall (2012) in fourth. Conversely, Daniel Craig has also starred in the shortest theatrical Bond film to date, Quantum of Solace (2008), which has a running time of only one hour and forty-six minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4d8cb03-c4c3-4964-8c7e-dc81bd78dfda'), 'The first Bond movie seen by Sir Sam Mendes was Live and Let Die (1973), and his favorite is From Russia with Love (1963). During pre-production, Mendes was originally hired as a consultant during the MGM bankruptcy period, so as to avoid a direct connection payment to Mendes from having been classified as a bona fide director to the production, and as such, requiring an official director''s payment. Reportedly, Mendes was offered the director''s job at a party by Daniel Craig. A meeting was then arranged for Mendes with the producers and things rolled on from there. As a boy, Mendes owned a die-cast Corgi Toys model car of Bond''s Aston Martin DB5 car, which inspired him to include the vehicle in this movie. Around the time of Casino Royale (2006), Mendes originally thought Craig was miscast as Bond. Mendes told "Metro": "I was one of the people who said I didn''t think he was the right casting. At the time, I was asked in an interview and I said, ''I''m not sure, I would advise him not to do it.''" With a rating of PG-13, this is also Mendes'' first non-R-rated movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3d500838-f314-4fbc-94b8-3612a2d9d372'), 'The opening few seconds are an homage to the traditional gun barrel openings of previous James Bond movies. The long, dark corridor with a bright light at its end, is similar to the shape of a gun barrel. Bond walks into frame from off-stage holding a gun, and is shillouetted at the end of the corridor. Just the first three notes of the Bond theme are then played', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d0cd8fa-de2a-47d1-9d3c-156b622f3c6e'), 'Miss Moneypenny''s and M''s office at the end of the movie is a re-creation of the original office from Dr. No (1962). However, the ship painting that had been above the fireplace behind the desk was now between the windows, and a picture of the new MI6 building hangs in its place', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('30df7250-dfbd-438d-b6eb-41c1578e2fc0'), 'Naomie Harris'' mother is from Jamaica, where Ian Fleming wrote the James Bond stories at his Goldeneye estate. At thirty-five, at the start of filming, Harris is one of the oldest actresses to play a major Bond Girl. Honor Blackman is tied for eldest to ever play one, being thirty-seven at the time of filming Goldfinger (1964), and Maud Adams was also thirty-seven at the time of filming Octopussy (1983). Harris attended this movie''s Royal World Premiere with twenty-six members of her family', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('70e02a5c-a493-4d17-ae8a-70c3669da432'), 'With his casting, Javier Bardem became the second Academy Award winner to play a major Bond villain. The first was Christopher Walken in A View to a Kill (1985), who had won an Oscar for The Deer Hunter (1978). Both Academy Awards were for Best Actor in a Supporting Role, Bardem''s statuette was for No Country for Old Men (2007). Bardem is not the only cast member in this movie to have a Best Supporting Acting Oscar, Dame Judi Dench has one for Shakespeare in Love (1998)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('60b8e270-5c37-467d-a355-fe91b7097ff2'), 'With the cooperation and assistance of the London Mayor''s Office and Transportation For London, the production was able to shut down Vauxhall Bridge and Millbank for a scene where M witnesses a terrorist attack on MI6 Headquarters. The explosion of the MI6 Headquarters was represented by a few fireworks on the day, but then an MI6 model miniature was built at one-third scale on the backlot at Pinewood Studios, where long-time James Bond special effects expert Chris Corbould, this movie''s special effects and miniature effects supervisor, used twenty-eight explosives to replicate the attack', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e9af5d32-9f8e-46dc-a736-489ccc96f2c1'), 'This marks the first time the "f" word is audibly said in a Bond movie. M exclaims in the third act that she "really f***ed this up"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('98066f66-e3aa-4827-80ac-078c931b886e'), 'Second unit director Alexander Witt and the second unit travelled to Shanghai, China to shoot establishing shots and driving sequences. The crew worked nights in the busy week leading up to the Chinese New Year to capture the exhilarating, ever-changing metropolis that is one of the most dynamic cities in the world. An aerial unit, piloted by Marc Wolff, was granted rare access to the sky above the city to shoot from a helicopter on loan from the Chinese government. Production designer Dennis Gassner and the art department worked to create the rest of the Chinese environment on soundstages at Pinewood Studios', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2afaabec-c10c-46df-80f8-7b0f3e0c4600'), 'Stuntman Gary Powell, and other members of his family, have worked on every EON Productions official film franchise James Bond movie since Dr. No (1962). Father and uncle Nosher Powell and Dinny Powell worked on all the early 1960s and 1970s Bonds with Sir Sean Connery and George Lazenby; brother Greg Powell worked on the 1970s and 1980s Bonds with Sir Roger Moore and Timothy Dalton, and Gary has worked on all of the 1990s and 2000s Bonds with Pierce Brosnan and Daniel Craig, as well as this one, the first Bond movie of the 2010s', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('367213ed-ef69-40ce-8111-681f98e2ea2d'), 'This is the only James Bond movie where there is no leading Bond Girl. Dame Judi Dench, as M, has the pivotal female role by participating in the climax, and holding the emotional crux of the story, but she is not a Bond Girl, since she and Bond don''t have a romantic relationship. The secondary Bond Girls in the movie are played by Naomie Harris as Miss Eve Moneypenny; Bérénice Marlohe as Sévérine, and Tonia Sotiropoulou as Bond''s Lover. Freida Pinto, Olivia Wilde, Rachel Weisz, Esti Ginzburg, Margarita Levieva, Alice Eve, Ana Ventura, Emilia Fox, and Ebru Akel were rumored or considered to appear as Bond Girls in the movie. Reportedly, this is the first film in the official franchise, where production notes and publicity materials generally refer to the leading actresses in the movie as "Bond Women", and not as "Bond Girls"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Skyfall'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('80b603f8-588a-4870-88fb-7aad9053d282'), 'The Day of the Dead parade at the beginning was made up for the film. The Mexicans loved the idea so much that Mexico City held its first Día de Muertos parade the following year, complete with floats, dancers, and giant marionettes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7d301f84-9a4a-4b28-9506-a4e797e44ac5'), 'In the Ian Fleming James Bond stories, Hannes Oberhauser, who is the father of this movie''s Franz Oberhauser (Christoph Waltz), was a skiing and climbing instructor who taught Bond while he was at Fettes College in Edinburgh, Scotland. In Fleming''s "Octopussy" (1966) short story, Bond says of him: "He taught me to ski before the war, when I was in my teens. He was something of a wonderful man. He was something of a father to me at a time when I happened to need one"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2acd870e-6512-4088-8146-06c9155a8372'), 'Daniel Craig said that it was getting harder and harder to get fit for his shirtless scenes as James Bond at the age of 47, saying, "Am I getting my kit off in this movie? Of course I''m getting my kit off. I seem to be bare-chested throughout this film again. Yes, I''ve been working out for six months. I work myself to death to get fit. No secret method involved, just sheer hard graft. It''s getting harder I will admit, but such is life. I''ll keep going as long as I''m physically able"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7bf771a6-226f-48cf-8e4e-6647a00f1f9e'), 'In order to complete the London scenes involving low-flying helicopters, the production had to send out 11,000 letters to residents and businesses that fell within the fly zone. Supervising locations manager Emma Pill said: "The biggest challenge, however, was to light the river at night. This involved several weeks of preparation. We lit under each arch of Vauxhall, Lambeth, and Westminster Bridge, 17 arches in total. These lights then remained in position for five weeks. We also lit the river from 10 rooftops along the bank of the Thames, from Vauxhall Bridge to Hungerford Bridge, working with Lambeth Palace, Tate Britain, and the Royal Parks to gain permission. We also worked very closely with the House of Commons, County Hall, and The London Eye to keep various lights on or off, or to change the color of their lights for each night shoot." Each night shoot involved a location team of nearly 200 personnel that included Marshals, security, traffic management, and police officers. Pill laughed, adding: "That''s a lot of radios to hand out and coordinate on a night, but it ran extremely smooth each time"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9607b192-d297-4797-9dc3-5464f5facda2'), 'First James Bond movie not to feature the iconic trumpet playing of Derek Watkins. Since Dr. No (1962), Mr. Watkins had featured on the soundtrack of every Bond movie until his death shortly after the release of Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ae7a33b4-82a8-439f-bdf0-21395de0fefb'), 'The opening scene, set during The Day of the Dead (Día de Muertos) parade, is quite unique for a James Bond movie, in that it marks the first time it appears to be shot in one take. Actually done in three shots, it begins from the moment the camera pans down to the massive crowd, following a masked Bond and his lady partner, following them back to their hotel room, and ending at the point Bond has his gun sight set on Marco Sciarra. The interior of this shot is the Gran Hotel Ciudad de Mexico. The exterior is another building, a few blocks away, which is across the street from the Palace of Mining (the large building in the background as Bond is walking on the roof). When Bond has his gun sight set on Marco Sciarra, he is on top of the building where the Mexican Senate met for 80 years', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('222e233c-4488-45e7-bb51-1a373c930e8b'), 'Reportedly, Sir Christopher Nolan was being seriously considered to direct this movie, until Sir Sam Mendes decided to come back for another movie. Associate producer Gregg Wilson said: "Christopher Nolan would be a ''dream'' choice for a future Bond director. We would of course be interested to have a discussion with him. We would like to do the same type of movie. It would be a dream to be with Nolan. But we always have an open mind when it comes to directors"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c6f6134d-27bc-4e1e-ad2a-81b3da25bf68'), 'Monica Bellucci previously auditioned for a Bond Girl role prior to being cast in this movie. In 1997, in an interview with Playboy Magazine, former James Bond Pierce Brosnan said that Bellucci had screentested for one of the two leading Bond Girl roles, as Paris Carver, in Tomorrow Never Dies (1997), the part in the end being cast with Teri Hatcher. Brosnan said: "Monica Bellucci is a ravishing beauty, a gorgeous, gorgeous woman. She screentested to be a Bond Girl a while back, and the fools said no. Teri Hatcher stole the day instead"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('530a0b65-8b75-4d32-b8ba-f0401f502455'), 'Since this movie does not use an original Ian Fleming story title, there are still only four unused original titles remaining: "The Property of a Lady", "The Hildebrand Rarity", "Risico", and "007 in New York" ("Agent 007 in New York"). The word "Hildebrand" does appear in the name of the closed "rarities" shop and safe house in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('37a765d6-0147-411c-9d93-a8711a96624c'), 'Despite Skyfall (2012) being shot entirely on digital, and rumors that James Bond movies would be shot digitally from then on, this and No Time to Die (2021) were shot on 35mm film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3f85534a-3aca-4310-bafa-54fbab349513'), 'James Bond''s new car in this movie is an Aston Martin DB10. The C.E.O. of Aston Martin tweeted that it is "strictly created for James Bond, and strictly limited to ten cars only. It is the most exclusive car of the DB series ever." New styling direction has also been taken, with a more angular look, that has ever been witnessed on an Aston Martin', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7a52d9d3-728d-4ce0-b801-d80ff86ad9cf'), 'Third James Bond movie to show Bond''s home after Dr. No (1962) and Live and Let Die (1973). Producer Barbara Broccoli said of Bond''s apartment in this movie: "At the beginning of pre-production I said to (production designer) Dennis (Gassner) that Bond''s apartment will be one of the most difficult sets to get right, and after we shot it, he said, ''You were right about that'', because everyone has an idea in their minds about the kind of place where Bond would live." Broccoli added: "When you actually sit down and figure out what that should be, everyone has different expectations. We knew it would be tricky, but Dennis did a great job, and Daniel (Craig) was also very involved in that set design, because it indicates a lot about the character of Bond himself, and what he calls home." Craig personally selected many of the items found in Bond''s home in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9b7772fc-86c0-4509-ae56-925b335c3bde'), 'Gary Oldman was approached for the role of Franz Oberhauser/Ernst Stavro Blofeld, but he was unwilling to commit to six months production worldwide', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35b862b5-928e-4f63-a7ff-04ebc063df45'), 'When out in the Moroccan desert, the production had to make sure that everyone within a 20-mile radius knew to expect loud explosions, so the locations department drove out to speak to nomad tribes and village folk. In fact, local nomads were hired as guides and security throughout the explosions preparation and filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('82b63b14-7113-4cac-a38f-93a2eb809838'), 'S.P.E.C.T.R.E., in the earlier James Bond movies, stood for Special Executive for Counterintelligence, Terrorism, Revenge, and Extortion. S.P.E.C.T.R.E. has also been known as the Special Executor for Counterintelligence, Terrorism, Revenge, and Extortion. James Bond creator Ian Fleming originally had the acronym meaning slightly more simply, the Special Executive for Terrorism, Revenge, and Extortion', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('76c48099-35e9-41d5-8b67-1513de885ebe'), 'The video message Bond receives from M (Dame Judi Dench) features her character wearing a blue blouse, sitting on a sofa in her flat, as seen in Skyfall (2012). In that movie, she is wearing the same outfit, sitting in the same place in the scene where she clicks on Silva''s link to view the YouTube video containing the identity of the N.A.T.O. agents. This means that M filmed her message directly after that scene took place, meaning that she knew about Marco Sciarra (Alessandro Cremona) as far back as that moment in Skyfall (2012). Not coincidentally, an excerpt from Skyfall''s soundtrack is used for this scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7f283d4-eb73-40ba-b27f-26018e6ce605'), 'Before her audition, Léa Seydoux said she drank some alcohol, forgot some of her lines, and basically botched up her reading. Seydoux asked if she could come back another day, which the filmmakers allowed, and was, in the end, successful in landing the lead Bond Girl role of Dr. Madeleine Swann', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('81fe7616-b10a-42c5-b825-b709a8c03dbb'), 'The painting the art dealers are selling in Shanghai, China in Skyfall (2012) is in Dr. Madeleine Swann''s (Léa Seydoux''s) room at the desert S.P.E.C.T.R.E. base, on the wall to the left of her as she looks at the dress. In real-life, the real painting is missing, having been stolen a few years previously', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('23a2218c-c8fd-4585-a93c-bafc0ef60432'), 'Pierce Brosnan, who played James Bond in four movies released from 1995 to 2002, commented on this movie in November 2015, in an interview with "HitFlix". Brosnan said: "I was looking forward to it enormously. I thought it was too long. The story was kind of weak, it could have been condensed. It kind of went on too long. It really did. (It) is neither fish nor fowl. It''s neither Bond nor Bourne. Am I in a Bond movie? Not in a Bond movie? But Daniel, in the fourth go-round, has ownership of it. He had a nice looseness to him. He''s a mighty warrior, and I think he found a great sense of himself in this one, with the one-liners and a nice playfulness there. Just get a tighter story, and he''ll have another classic. I think the guy was just fairly banjaxed by playing it. By the time you finish making a Bond movie, you don''t want to hear the name, see the name, or have anything to do with it, because you just want to go to ground. Give him another year off here, and he''ll be ready to rock and roll for sure"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4a232f05-6e8f-4baf-83c0-73bb3948ec74'), 'Fourth appearance by Daniel Craig as James Bond. Speculation around the time of the release of this movie was mounted as to whether Craig would do a fifth movie. After long speculation, he said that he would do a fifth and final film', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a36af97b-de47-4908-94cb-fadb1c7d8f27'), 'In December 2014, nine high-end Land Rover Discoverys, including five customized Range Rover Sports, valued at about £630,000 ($1 million U.S. dollars), set for filming in the Austrian Alps were stolen from a parking lot in Neuss near Düsseldorf, Germany', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ebcea53a-6201-4bbf-be53-3761d4597247'), 'According to Robbie Collin in the U.K. newspaper "The Telegraph", "Bond author Ian Fleming invented S.P.E.C.T.R.E. in 1959 to replace James Bond''s usual Soviet enemies. Fleming believed the Cold War might be about to end, and wanted to keep his spy thrillers relevant." Fleming''s S.P.E.C.T.R.E. Executive Cabinet included "21 people, including former Gestapo members, Soviet spy group S.M.E.R.S.H., Josip Broz Tito''s secret police, Italian, Corsican, and Turkish organized crime gangs", its goals were "profiteering from conflict between the superpowers, eventual world domination", and its methods included "counterintelligence, brainwashing, murder, and extortion using weapons of mass destruction (nuclear, biological and orbital)"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da76523d-11d0-46ea-b9f1-1d6eda0071bb'), 'This is the first James Bond movie since Die Another Day (2002) to feature the iconic gun barrel sequence at the start of the movie. While the gun barrel sequence was used as part of the title sequence in Casino Royale (2006), the sequence was only shown at the end of Skyfall (2012) and Quantum of Solace (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('62375450-f7a8-46f4-adc8-7b813d5b9017'), 'Reportedly, the movie went over budget and was on track to be the most expensive movie of the James Bond franchise ever made, with costs over $300 million U.S. Its estimated cost at completion was expected to be around $350 million U.S. A Bond movie with an estimated $300 million-plus U.S. budget would be the most expensive Bond movie ever, by far. The previous had been Quantum of Solace (2008), with an estimated budget of approximately $200 million U.S. However, the reports regarding this movie were exaggerated, and the budget actually ended up being "just" $245 million U.S.', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f85c9335-9149-4d91-a640-567d48cafb14'), 'The logistics of filming the car chase in Rome, Italy were difficult to marshal, according to stunt coordinator Gary Powell, who said: "In Rome, we saw a load of roads we liked, and sometimes the road is specific to a stunt, because it had a feature which would be really nice to jump. A lot of the time when we asked for permission, we would get a yes, but some of the time we''d get a no, so we would have to try and find other roads. It was a constant process to find the right location to fit the stunts. There was a lot of toing and froing in Rome." In the end, the production was able to shut down key portions of the city, including a section alongside the Tiber, looking towards St. Peter''s Square and the Coliseum. Though the audience only ever sees two cars on-screen, the second unit used a total of eight Aston Martins, and seven Jaguars to shoot the chase. Vehicle supervisor Chris Corbould stated that the Rome car chase allowed no room for error: "The stunt drivers were driving around Rome at one hundred miles (one hundred sixty kilometers) per hour, so absolutely everything had to be perfect as far as their performance was concerned. We didn''t want the drivers to get injured, and also we didn''t want them damaging buildings that are thousands of years old. The stakes were pretty high. We spent a lot of time testing the cars, making sure they could cope with the punishing regiment that the guys put them through"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('df75c708-3cd1-438d-896b-22709ec3635d'), 'As an in-joke amongst cast and crew, a prescription for Viagra for James Bond was put in the set of the clinic on the mountain top. It may have been a response to the outcome of a study published in the British Medical Journal, whereby doctors had kept track of Bond''s alcohol consumption in the novels. They concluded that Bond consumes an average of 92 alcoholic units per week, which would make him an alcoholic, at high risk for liver problems and impotence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6d62f13f-5b4a-4e77-924f-defd039341d1'), 'Reportedly, Daniel Craig''s salary on this movie was £25.4 million ($39 million U.S.), allegedly making Craig the highest-paid actor to portray James Bond', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('847dffec-7a15-45d9-92d3-da784d6446f8'), 'Director Sir Sam Mendes and screenwriter John Logan came up with the main concept for the plot together, according to former James Bond screenwriters Neal Purvis and Robert Wade, who ended up returning to the franchise to do re-writes on the screenplay, because the inner sanctum of the production (the star, director, and producers) were not allegedly satisfied with the script', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2135fabb-72de-4638-9f76-f99330da04fd'), 'Approximately 1,500 people were hired as extras for the pre-opening titles sequence in Mexico, which included the Day of the Dead festival. CGI effects meant the number would be able to be multiplied to represent an estimated crowd scene totalling around 10,000 people', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('210e3c88-9ba2-4c62-a1da-84b0be744def'), 'Apart from a cameo in ''Star Wars: Episode VII - The Force Awakens'' (2015), this was the first acting role in a feature film of Daniel Craig in three years. Craig''s previous movie had been the previous Bond movie Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5ee49134-f837-4e7e-9732-c7be1015c210'), 'The movie shares several of the same shooting locations as The Living Daylights (1987), including Tangier, Morocco, London, England, and Austria', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eda0c8da-7ad5-41b1-898f-260242bc1142'), 'The Rome chase sequence between James Bond''s (Daniel Craig''s) Aston Martin DB10 and Mr. Hinx''s (Dave Bautista''s) Jaguar C-X75 marks the first time two prototype vehicles have been featured in a Bond movie. It''s also the first time any prototype car has been used in a Bond movie. However, in Casino Royale (2006), he drove a Ford Mondeo sport model, which was not on the market at time of production', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('62827ff7-7422-430c-b9b1-b78b2a528fd8'), 'The make and model of James Bond''s new Aston Martin car to be seen in this movie is a custom made-to-order silver two-door Aston Martin DB10 coupé. The car, a "nod to future designs", was made and developed specifically for the purpose of this movie, has not been put up for sale until after its screen appearance, as Aston Martin feared other manufacturers "may try to copy its sleek design". Also, the gadgets in the new car were labelled with Dymo Tape, a cheap punched adhesive labelling system, which is an in-joke nod to the labels in the original Aston Martin car from Goldfinger (1964)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('46da4ac4-0a16-416e-864d-a9c321db315b'), 'When James Bond shoots at Franz Oberhauser (Ernst Stavro Blofeld) in the derelict MI6 Headquarters, his bullet strikes on the armored glass, taking the shape of the S.P.E.C.T.R.E. octopus. This type of broken glass octopus image has been used in publicity for this movie in trailers and movie posters', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e08f4f58-04cc-41c2-b280-23d702876cbc'), 'The casting agency character specifications for "Mr. Hinx" (Dave Bautista), according to James Bond Radio, stated his persona as being "Hinx (Male, 30-45). Ideally over 6'' 2". Hinx is the main henchman/assassin. We are looking for an imposing, extremely physically fit actor. He has several fights with Bond, and will have to have stunt training. He has to drive. We are looking for someone very unusual, possibly from a sports background. Height: 180cm-195cm"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9ab08d40-2ae2-4c84-a678-a1d101076545'), 'Dave Bautista is the fourth actor with a professional wrestling background to play a James Bond villain, following in the footsteps of Harold Sakata (Goldfinger (1964)), Peter Fanene Maivia (You Only Live Twice (1967)), and Pat Roach (Never Say Never Again (1983))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b8b5fb03-a3ae-41c5-b616-6a172621e8ca'), 'The "Day of the Dead" (Día de los Muertos) festival seen in this movie''s trailer and in the opening sequence, is a real-life Mexican national holiday where all banks are closed. The public holiday is particularly celebrated throughout Mexico, but also in other countries across the globe. Elegant Skulls or La Calavera Catrinas, used in the Day of the Dead celebrations, are artistic manifestations of altars and calavera costumes of the Day of the Dead. An image of one of these skulls featured in the background of one of the main movie posters. Nevertheless, there are no Day of the Dead parades in Mexico City, as shown in the movie: the writers somehow mixed Brazil''s Carnaval celebrations with the Day of the Dead Mexican tradition, two completely different events', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dec07f74-84d5-43d9-8dd8-1017c4ebf98c'), 'The opening long take actually comprises six separate shots digitally combined to make it look like one seamless take', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('24deb09f-809d-42e2-8de2-b58fabe2ee09'), 'Initially, financing and distribution arrangements for this movie and No Time to Die (2020) were frequently reported together, suggesting that development of these two James Bond movies were being set up for a two-year cycle, with No Time to Die (2020) being targeted for a 2017 release. However, Daniel Craig stated that there was a plan by the studio to film two Bond movies back-to-back, but he balked at the idea, due to the enormity of their productions', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c542bec6-4edf-4842-bc14-4d34dc4f02d8'), 'Daniel Craig''s favorite James Bond movie is From Russia with Love (1963), and also Sir Sean Connery''s favorite movie. That movie contained an action scene involving a brutal train fight, where Bond fought against a powerful adversary. Similar to this, in this movie, Bond engages in a brutal train fight with another powerful adversary. And still another Bond movie, The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), had a similar fight onboard a train', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dd2e6cf5-6a85-465c-8dd8-c3101e5d54d6'), 'The Royal Doulton bulldog figurine with the Union Jack on it, which James Bond inherited from M at the end of Skyfall (2012), can be seen on the coffee table in James Bond''s (Daniel Craig''s) apartment when Miss Eve Moneypenny (Naomie Harris) visits there', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bd1dae8e-daa3-4bd3-a262-a210687078c4'), 'S.P.E.C.T.R.E. Agents in the earlier James Bond movies often wore a gold "Ring of Evil". According to the book "James Bond: The Secret World of 007" (2006) by Alastair Dougall, "Top operatives of S.P.E.C.T.R.E., and (Ernst Stavro) Blofeld himself, could sometimes be recognized by a distinctive octopus ring, which symbolized the organization''s tentacular reach into the murkiest depths of world crime"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3ee695f9-5cea-4d72-99e3-18028843cf81'), 'According to the book "Bond on Bond" (2015) by Sir Roger Moore, producer Kevin McClory (who previously owned the movie rights to S.P.E.C.T.R.E., the character Ernst Stavro Blofeld, any Thunderball (1965) remake, and other various outlines, scripts and treatments) "had been a long-time pain in Eon''s behind, and they couldn''t use the Blofeld character or his organization (S.P.E.C.T.R.E.) for fear of litigation, which is how the QUANTUM idea came about, as originally the producers (Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson) had hoped to introduce Spectre as the villains in Casino Royale (2006) and Quantum of Solace (2008), but now (in 2013), seven years after McClory''s death (when a settlement was made by MGM and EON Productions with McClory''s estate), they could finally bring everything back under one roof"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0eb187ff-a4d5-4b95-9933-52f1edbdaae8'), 'The movie''s trailers and some movie posters featured a black background with a ballistics bullet hole mark with a subtle version of the original S.P.E.C.T.R.E. octopus in the shattering glass. This is evocative of the final scene of On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969). The bullet hole octopus shape is seen in this movie when James Bond (Daniel Craig) shoots unsuccessfully at Ernst Stavro Blofeld (Christoph Waltz)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7b52695b-2133-4273-ac5d-8d2d0f8cb247'), 'At one point, the story outline was a well-guarded top secret, the contents known only to Daniel Craig, producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson, and a few other selected personnel at EON Productions', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('77e76df9-faa5-4a99-9ccf-269427d13093'), 'The dining establishment where M (Ralph Fiennes), Q (Ben Whishaw), and Miss Eve Moneypenny (Naomie Harris) meet is Rules Restaurant. Located on Maiden Lane in Covent Garden, it was established by Thomas Rule in 1798, and is the oldest restaurant in London', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ded86e4a-4163-4529-bcd4-40074b6f13d8'), 'The title is one of a few James Bond movies which utilized text written by James Bond creator Ian Fleming, but were not the actual titles of Fleming Bond novels or short stories. The others were GoldenEye (1995) (the name of Fleming''s home in Jamaica named by him), Licence to Kill (1989) (the Bond character''s level of authority in the stories) and The World Is Not Enough (1999) (the James Bond family motto, referenced in both the novel and movie of On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969))', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a8170724-a7fe-4c44-a5fd-70ad55e314e1'), 'Daniel Craig confessed in publicity interviews that this particular 007 movie was the most enjoyable of all that he''d worked on, as of its release', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d596ec66-07a8-4161-a3b0-5ca0833b09b8'), 'Third time in the history of the franchise that an actress playing a leading Bond Girl is older than the actor portraying James Bond. Monica Bellucci (Lucia Sciarra) is three years and five months older than Daniel Craig. Honor Blackman, who played Pussy Galore in Goldfinger (1964), is five years and three days older than Sir Sean Connery, and Dame Diana Rigg, who played Teresa "Tracy" Bond (Teresa "Tracy" Draco, Contessa Teresa di Vicenzo) in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), is a year older than George Lazenby', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3495ea95-bcd4-4efd-9bed-5e8d8953387b'), 'First James Bond movie to be shot with anamorphic lenses since Die Another Day (2002). Also, this movie is director Sir Sam Mendes'' first experience shooting with this format', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0953c346-2635-4a8b-a6d6-eca4d36118a7'), 'Ang Lee, Tom Hooper, David Yates, Danny Boyle, Shane Black, Sir Christopher Nolan, and Nicolas Winding Refn were considered to direct before Sir Sam Mendes agreed to return after directing Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fe69443c-6a13-4961-b4c6-501201c46e79'), 'Kevin Spacey was rumored at one time to play the main villain, as he had been also for Skyfall (2012). While Spacey was considered to play the villain in Skyfall (2012), before production delays and scheduling conflicts with his play Richard III interfered with his casting, he has indicated, on the record, that he was never offered nor considered to play the James Bond villain in this movie, and doesn''t know why and from where these rumors keep eventuating', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('38bf10f6-9437-45fa-a382-778ba2be10d1'), 'Before Christoph Waltz was cast as the villain, Chiwetel Ejiofor was considered for the role', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ff5c7944-4983-4900-aa6d-3fa2701c3711'), 'Although supposedly acting as a lone wolf rogue agent in this movie, James Bond gets more help in this movie from MI6 than ever before, M (Ralph Fiennes), Q (Ben Whishaw), Bill Tanner (Rory Kinnear), and Miss Eve Moneypenny (Naomie Harris), who all actively assist him', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('60af6b28-e97d-4748-ab26-2a1628614ad9'), 'In this movie, and also seen in the trailer, there is a shot of a war memorial with a list of names of "Those who died in the service of their country". The names are largely members of the movie crew, such as art department assistant directors Fergus Clegg and Archie Campbell-Baldwin. As James Bond see the names on the memorial wall at the old MI6 Headquarters, the camera focuses on one name, Chloe Chesterton, who served as second assistant producer. It has been suggested that the name of Emma Pill perhaps was a tribute to Emma Peel, the famous secret agent of The Avengers (1961), who was portrayed by Dame Diana Rigg, who also appeared in On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), but is actually a reference to this movie''s supervising locations manager, Emma Pill', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('285ac62c-2227-458f-95a6-c71867f70525'), '(At around 15 minutes) One of the eyes seen in the opening credits sequence is that of actress, model, writer, and director Karen Gillan. Gillan had expressed interest in playing a Bond villain so she could lick Daniel Craig''s head', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8f0d1c7a-bcd7-4b6a-847e-a12864009cdd'), 'Jesper Christensen is the first actor to play the same Bond villain or henchman more than twice in a James Bond movie. Christensen beat the tie between Anthony Dawson playing Ernst Stavro Blofeld in Thunderball (1965) and From Russia with Love (1963); and Richard Kiel playing Jaws in Moonraker (1979) and The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). Kiel also portrayed Jaws in the video game James Bond 007: Everything or Nothing (2003)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5913f034-d06d-4f72-8e92-214b30dac579'), 'During this movie and in the movie''s trailer, Ernst Stavro Blofeld''s penchant for Nehru collarless jackets are another clue to his real identity, that it is not really Franz Oberhauser, as Blofeld is seen wearing one in each of the previous James Bond movie where he appeared as the major villain. These movies being You Only Live Twice (1967), On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), and Diamonds Are Forever (1971), but not Thunderball (1965) and From Russia with Love (1963), where Blofeld was only seen in silhouette behind a screen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f8c904f-e482-4312-9b69-5bb7e858b2c4'), 'With a running time of 163 minutes, or two hours and 43 minutes, ''No Time to Die'' (2020) has the longest ever running time for a Bond movie. At two hours and 24 minutes, ''Casino Royale'' (2006) was once the longest James Bond movie, beating the previous record holder On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) by four minutes, until the release of Spectre (2015), which beat it by another four minutes. ''Spectre'' (2015) was recently the longest James Bond movie record holder, with a running time of two hours and 28 minutes. Daniel Craig has now played Bond in four longest Bond movies of all time: ''No Time to Die'' (2020, ''Spectre'' (2015), Skyfall (2012), and Casino Royale (2006). The former long-time record holder, On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), is now in fifth place, with Skyfall (2012) in fourth. Conversely, Daniel Craig has also starred in the shortest theatrical Bond film to date, Quantum of Solace (2008), which has a running time of only one hour and 46 minutes', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('58cb3062-3c03-4b7b-ae76-97f5f29ad9c8'), 'First James Bond movie where Bond is ejected from an Aston Martin ejector seat. An Aston Martin ejector seat first featured in Goldfinger (1964). It was also referred to but not used on the drive to Scotland with M in Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('80aba11b-60e7-4522-bb4f-92a9f5457293'), 'A huge sandstorm blew in on the first day of filming in Erfoud, Morocco, shutting down production for the entire afternoon, as there was no visibility at all. The crew had to take cover in their vehicles as winds reached 50 miles per hour. The temperature in Erfoud usually was at an average of 113 degrees Fahrenheit (45 degrees Celsius). On the hottest day of all, the temperature during the shoot reached one hundred 122 degrees Fahrenheit (50 degrees Celsius)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ca784108-9528-496d-bd8d-ac97471d9c23'), 'First James Bond movie to show the home of Miss Eve Moneypenny', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('fef7d169-8d5c-46ab-bf43-24bcd1345d34'), 'The costumes worn by the leading Bond Girls, according to costume designer Jany Temime, who also designed the costumes for Skyfall (2012), were inspired by real-life movie stars of from the 1950s. Léa Seydoux''s clothes were inspired by Grace Kelly, while Monica Bellucci''s outfits were inspired by Sophia Loren and Gina Lollobrigida, Italian screen goddesses, who were, according to Temime, "all waist and hips and boobs"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e9434b6e-4249-4c70-b8eb-255bfab74d6f'), 'It was rumored that the classic James Bond henchman Jaws would make an appearance in this movie. What was publicized was that there was a definite intention for there to be a villain in this movie who was iconic, like Jaws, Oddjob, or Ernst Stavro Blofeld', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3995f995-969b-415c-a8bc-d2fe52a85b9a'), 'When M meets James Bond at the safe house, the sign on the door states the premises as being "Hildebrand & Company - Rarities & Antiquities". The Hildebrand safe house is a reference to Ian Fleming''s short story in the "For Your Eyes Only" (1960) anthology called "The Hildebrand Rarity". Large portions of "The Hildebrand Rarity" were used in Licence to Kill (1989) starring Timothy Dalton as James Bond. These included the Milton Krest character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87ec56b3-df3c-43ac-95a6-588ea75b4ebb'), 'Pre-production on this movie began during the making and release of Skyfall (2012). Similarly, pre-production on Quantum of Solace (2008) began before Casino Royale (2006) started filming', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a7d7232d-bb54-4ca4-984e-bdf33c121b6c'), 'First James Bond movie for Daniel Craig where he received billing as a producer, credited for the job and duties of "co-producer"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b33acfb6-e7c5-4889-9281-0c8d918597e0'), 'Andrew Scott allegedly replaced Chiwetel Ejiofor. Rumors have reported Scott was cast because his salary was $1 million less than Ejiofor', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('130e8f02-2de4-4905-987d-26564f3856fd'), 'While at the bar in the clinic, when James Bond (Daniel Craig) asks Q (Ben Whishaw) about his hotel in the Alps, Q says "The Pevsner". This is a reference to Tom Pevsner, former executive producer of the Bond film franchise from For Your Eyes Only (1981) until GoldenEye (1995), who died in 2014', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('88b3819c-f97a-45f7-8fbf-93ab46d951fb'), 'In From Russia with Love (1963), the storyline dealt with the Lektor Decoding Machine, the name of which was called the Spektor Decoding Machine in the Ian Fleming novel "From Russia with Love" (1957). Its name was changed because of its similarity with the name of the fictitious criminal spy organization S.P.E.C.T.R.E. Fleming based this device on his knowledge of the Enigma Decoding Machine from World War II. Fleming was involved with the Ultra Network, who cracked the Enigma Code in 1939. The Ultra Network''s activities were not released until 1975, in a book called A Man Called Intrepid (1979). Fleming''s friend Sir William Stevenson wrote the book, which was published at the time when the closed period on wartime secrets expired, and the records were finally declassified', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('eb76833b-7015-4a87-878f-ae216c9d7a33'), 'This movie shot in three different locations in Mexico City, The Gran Hotel, Plaza Tolsá, and the Zócalo, the latter which is the main square in the center of town. The stunt team later replicated a massive explosion involving the hotel at Pinewood Studios, although the Zócalo played host to a huge sequence involving an out-of-control helicopter piloted by the world-famous Red Bull aerobatic pilot Chuck Aaron. The Red Bull helicopter is built especially for barrel rolling and free diving. Due to the altitude in Mexico City, Aaron was limited in the aerobatics he could perform. However, he still pushed the boundaries, flying just 30 feet above the extras with two stuntmen re-enacting the fight while hanging out of the helicopter. Stunt coordinator Gary Powell said: "The world of stunts has changed a lot, and we''re very story-orientated with all of our action scenes, which is great, because a lot of films forget the story, and just do ''crash, bang, wallop!''" Powell says the Mexico helicopter scene is integral to the story: "We don''t just blow stuff up because it looks good. With all of the action in a James Bond film, we tell a story while we''re doing it." As much action as possible was shot in-camera, as is the case with every Bond movie. Special effects supervisor Chris Corbould said: "We try and do as much as we can for real, and then the visual effects guys come along and make what we''ve done look better, tweaking it, painting things out, adding things in. But everything is based in reality. In Mexico City, you can see thousands of people in the Zócalo responding to this amazing helicopter sequence unfolding in the sky above them"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('67ddff31-4464-42f2-8f1a-c153fb1ff438'), 'Director Sir Sam Mendes originally declined working on another James Bond movie, first around the time that Skyfall (2012) launched, and again in March 2013. Reportedly, the production of this movie was delayed a year to get Mendes back, as he could not do the movie earlier due to theater commitments', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('de564add-09fb-4adc-a8ae-fdb4f752d5cd'), 'Before the aerial battle above the main plaza in Mexico City, as The Day Of The Dead procession was taking place, Bond is seen walking, not running after Marco Sciarra. This is because Daniel Craig had hurt his leg filming a previous scene and couldn''t run. A physiotherapist was flown in (from Nottingham) to aid Craig', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e46df8c4-5da8-4de3-b396-017c7f385d0a'), 'Third James Bond movie featuring Jesper Christensen, who appeared in Casino Royale (2006) and Quantum of Solace (2008). Skyfall (2012) is the only Daniel Craig Bond movie in which Christensen has not appeared', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d92f3928-e0dd-4966-adbe-301e591daf04'), 'The character name of Franz Oberhauser (Christoph Waltz) is the son of Hannes Oberhauser from the Ian Fleming James Bond short story "Octopussy" (1966), which featured flashback sequences in Austria, where this movie was partially filmed. Hannes Oberhauser, in the story, was murdered by Major Dexter Smythe, who, in the movie, Octopussy (1983), is the title character Octopussy''s (Maud Adams''s) father. An octopus is the traditional symbol of the criminal organization S.P.E.C.T.R.E. (Special Executive for Counterintelligence, Terrorism, Revenge, and Extortion). The name of the criminal organization in the James Bond video game From Russia with Love (2005) is O.C.T.OP.U.S., which was used instead of S.P.E.C.T.R.E., for legal reasons', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6e78c271-8ee5-445c-acf8-06cd99bc3467'), 'Director Sir Sam Mendes said of the movie''s pre-titles sequence featuring the Mexican Day of the Dead parade and festival: "I wanted the audience to be dropped right into the middle of a very, very specific, very heady, rich environment. It''s the Day of the Dead, everywhere you look, there''s color and detail, and life. We''ve built floats and maquettes, the costumes are extraordinary, and the craftsmanship is amazing"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5ef4ba58-13f1-4369-bde8-15e68ff70d27'), 'Radiohead had recorded a song called "Spectre", which was going to be the film''s main theme. However, the song was rejected for being "too dark". The producers opted for Sam Smith''s "Writing''s On the Wall" in the end. Radiohead later released their song as a free download on Soundcloud on December 25, 2015', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('93117b37-0fce-4f11-b16f-bca7fdc79022'), 'First Naomie Harris James Bond movie where Miss Eve Moneypenny fulfills the traditional role of the character of being mostly office bound at MI6 Headquarters. Harris says: "Moneypenny, in this film, is behind the desk again. She''s not out with Bond in the field. She is still assisting him, but this time doing something much more secretive"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('30d88ae0-db16-4cdb-8c08-27a045d5d516'), 'First James Bond movie to feature the character with the code name "C" (as with "M", "Q", and "R"). "C" is Max Denbigh, head of MI5, portrayed by Andrew Scott. Denbigh is the fourth main character in the franchise in the British Secret Service to have a single code letter name, and he''s the fifth if one counts the Russian Major Anya Amasova (Barbara Bach) from The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) who was code-named Agent XXX', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec8d895b-68b8-48d7-88d6-535f1bbbb391'), 'Paramount Pictures brought forward the release of Mission: Impossible - Rogue Nation (2015), the fifth in their spy film franchise, as the movie was completed earlier than expected, so as to avoid competing with this movie at the international box-office', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db7ff17f-7467-4020-aa1e-76f3d9be632d'), 'Reportedly, Dave Bautista had publicly declared himself to be a big James Bond fan several years prior to him being cast as henchman Mr. Hinx in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40486df7-7bac-4e39-a302-f8349af282b1'), 'The production team had been reported as wanting to include an iconic henchman for this movie, in the tradition of Jaws and Oddjob. This has resulted in the character of Mr. Hinx (Dave Bautista). Sadly though, prior to principal photography starting in December 2014, two of the James Bond franchise iconic henchmen died in 2014, they being Geoffrey Holder in October 2014, who played Baron Samedi in Live and Let Die (1973), and Richard Kiel in September 2014, who portrayed Jaws in Moonraker (1979) and The Spy Who Loved Me (1977)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a1ad373d-1a6a-4063-9f5f-8bebbadef28c'), 'First James Bond movie where Daniel Craig is not seen shirtless during the movie, except for the opening credits sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2fceed34-b489-452a-bf2f-c3c64e17ac52'), 'Hoyte van Hoytema replaced Sir Roger Deakins as director of photography when the latter, who had lensed Skyfall (2012), withdrew from this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('66e26d1b-73f4-44bd-a398-bfaaf037cee0'), 'As James Bond approaches the meeting of S.P.E.C.T.R.E., the members are talking about how their vaccinations against HIV and malaria are a success. There is no vaccination available for HIV as of 2022, but a malaria vaccine was released six years after the movie, in 2021', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('35a7a670-946c-4910-bdda-23d5eaab0192'), 'Léa Seydoux and Monica Bellucci didn''t believe they would be successful in obtaining their respective Bond Girl roles in the movie, for the latter, predominantly because of her age. Also, when Bellucci was first approached about appearing in this movie, Bellucci thought it was for her to play a new "M" character to replace Dame Judi Dench', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e6d1392b-602b-47a2-9b94-e1150ff95a01'), 'Early drafts of The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) featured S.P.E.C.T.R.E., but had to be removed for legal reasons, due to a dispute with then rights owner Kevin McClory, who owned the movie remake rights to Thunderball (1965) (which he remade as Never Say Never Again (1983)) as well as to the names "S.P.E.C.T.R.E." and "Ernst Stavro Blofeld". An early version of the script intended to have Blofeld return as the villain for the first time since Diamonds Are Forever (1971). Richard Maibaum''s original draft script for The Spy Who Loved Me (1977) featured an alliance of international terrorists entering S.P.E.C.T.R.E.''s headquarters and deposing Blofeld, before trying to destroy the world for themselves, to make way for a New World Order. This script was deemed too political by producer Albert R. Broccoli. Also, later, for legal reasons, the name of the villain could not be called "Stavros", and had to be changed, so was called "Stromberg" (Curd Jürgens) instead, because of its similarity with the middle name of Ernest Blofeld which was "Stavro". The traditional black suited S.P.E.C.T.R.E. Army could not wear that color either, and instead wore red outfits in The Spy Who Loved Me (1977). According to the book "The Complete James Bond Movie Encylopedia" by Steven Jay Rubin, the initial hypothesized S.P.E.C.T.R.E. of The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), included "members of the Bader-Meinhof Gang, the Japanese Red Army, and other modern terrorist organizations." S.P.E.C.T.R.E. does appear briefly in the original Ian Fleming novel "The Spy Who Loved Me" (1962), one of few of Fleming''s Bond novels to do so', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c87ea8db-26f0-4acb-9807-4795ee6829c1'), 'Daniel Craig was injured at least twice during principal photography. Craig suffered a knee injury when filming in Austria, then hit his head on the interior of an Aston Martin DB10. However, the head injury was reportedly not serious according to the Italian publication "La Republica"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9670213a-68b8-4509-b2aa-d11a13ec4d0f'), 'The train featured in the movie is the Oriental Desert Express, its make and model being the locomotive ONCF-series DH 370 (EMD GT26CW-2), owned by the Office National des Chemins de Fer du Maroc (ONCF), which runs on the Oriental Desert Express route, that travels between Oujda to Bouarfa in Morocco (which is nowhere near the orient)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6b8f34dd-d911-4aaf-bdb3-4a9029950478'), 'The Day of the Dead sequence involved 1,500 extras, including 77 dancers and 170 make-up artists, as well as ten giant skeletons and 250,000 paper flowers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8f4704f2-5592-4d9f-9a54-082f74b34708'), 'The CNS building seen from the River Thames and from aerial shots is a computer-generated graphic. At the time of filming, the area was a construction site. However, the building that was actually constructed was an apartment block. Similarly, the MI6 Headquarters across the river was replaced by a digital model to achieve the bomb damaged appearance and final destruction. The real MI6 building is still there and still in business', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('58ed97d8-a14e-412c-8c49-a295429ca76b'), 'John Logan was once reportedly commissioned to write scripts for this movie, as well as No Time to Die (2020) at the same time, but this is apparently not the case. According to Daniel Craig, there was an idea at the studio of filming two consecutive James Bond movies back-to-back, to which Craig apparently balked at the idea, due to their enormity. The James Bond Wikia website states: "A popular news story, started by the blog Deadline, reports the Skyfall (2012) writer John Logan has been commissioned by (producers) Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson to pen Spectre (2015) and Bond 25 as a two-parter." Several months later, this rumor was repudiated, but no official announcement either way had been made. Logan did pen the script for this movie, and may have been considered a front-runner for helming the No Time to Die (2020) script', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a12e47e4-67dc-4389-a1fb-cb1caa8812b7'), 'Composer Thomas Newman, scoring his second consecutive James Bond movie, started composing the music during filming, rather than via the usual custom of composing during post-production. However, large parts of the music were re-used from Skyfall (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40133af2-6c7d-4a99-bbab-79f844d4fe4e'), 'When James Bond (Daniel Craig) and Dr. Madeleine Swann (Léa Seydoux) are in Oberhuser''s Moroccan lair, two paintings can be seen hanging over their respective beds in their rooms. In Bond''s, Le Pigeon aux Petit Pois (The Pigeon with Green Peas) by Picasso, and in Madeleine''s, Woman with a Fan by Modigliani. The latter was first seen in Skyfall (2012) when James Bond spots Sévérine (Bérénice Marlohe) for the first time, showing the painting to a potential buyer, who is subsequently assassinated. When Blofeld (Christoph Waltz) refers to the deaths of all the women in Bond''s love life, his association with this painting serves to underscore this. These paintings are amongst the five that were stolen from the Musée d''Art Moderne de la Ville de Paris in May 2010, which together are worth about one million euros ($118 million US). This could be a nod to Dr. No (1962) where Goya''s painting Portrait of the Duke of Wellington, stolen from the National Gallery, London in 1961, displayed in Dr. No''s lair. The fact that the Modigliani was being shown in a private transaction reflects the fact that it was stolen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'Spectre'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
INSERT INTO trivias (id, content, movie_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
(UUID_TO_BIN('2542858b-24be-4c3f-921a-59c991100bc5'), 'Ana de Armas (Paloma) was so worried that her action sequences would not be good enough with only three weeks of training, she has shared "I kept telling Cary, ''I just have three weeks of training'' and I said it so many times he said, ''Say that in the movie.''". Her line to Bond that she had had been "training for three weeks, more or less", was kept in the final version', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d4ec51d4-e251-481f-8011-7d2fd51c1806'), 'Reportedly, James Bond actor Daniel Craig personally hand-picked Cuban actress Ana de Armas to play Paloma in this Bond movie, after working with her on Knives Out (2019), which first released about only four months before No Time to Die was originally meant to release', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('cd68be23-71fe-4625-a45a-ef37ee72ae0d'), 'Daniel Craig has said that he would retire from the role of James Bond if he felt he was too old to play the character. Craig has also said that it has become harder to be fit enough for the role and that there has been more use of doubles for action sequences', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d96f3f4-a67d-4a00-a090-bb04faee2bfd'), 'Director Cary Joji Fukunaga wanted one great bike stunt to feature in Matera, Italy. Stunt coordinator, Lee Morrison came up with the spectacular wall jump, performed by stuntman, Paul Edmondson. To perform the stunt, Edmondson rides up an 8m ramp at approximately 60kmh (37mph), gets airborne over a wall and lands on a cobbled terrace. This scene, along with the bridge attack jump, are two of the movie''s signature stunts', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7e7286a3-68e5-40a3-9218-68b9fc3af319'), 'In January 2021, a number of brand sponsors and partners demanded re-shoots pertaining to their product placement. Some products seen in the movie became outdated or obsolete due to the eighteen months delay caused by the global health pandemic. Reportedly, the Nokia phone ad starring Nomi (Lashana Lynch) had a smartphone which became both outdated and obsolete during the wait. The speed at which smartphones get new models and releases is particularly fast. In the relevant Nokia tie-in commercial, CGI was used to replace the phone in the advert, but the original smartphone in the movie remained the same', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c4565b07-4720-49ef-ac0c-92d34a130d3f'), 'The porcelain Royal Doulton "Union Jack" bulldog statuette which M (Judi Dench) gave James Bond as a present in ''Skyfall'' (2012) can be seen just before James Bond (Daniel Craig) uncovers his Aston Martin V8 Vantage in his garage. The British Flag Bulldog figurine is seen at the bottom right corner of the screen', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1c08d496-1e57-4e22-a0e6-9f2fce3e42fa'), 'Star Daniel Craig, after having gotten injured on earlier Bond movies, injured his ankle by slipping during the shoot in Jamaica in May 2019, requiring minor surgery. He said in a 2021 interview that the accident was so unnecessary as he wasn''t performing a stunt or anything physically dramatic, he just tripped over whilst walking and broke his ankle. The media at the time reported he was performing an action scene', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('518aeaa1-807b-41b2-84b7-61b53cddeb0c'), 'Composer Hans Zimmer took inspiration from the music composed for the theatrical trailer of the previous Bond film, not only by taking a similar approach to the James Bond theme for various action sequences, but also by incorporating the main theme from On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8740903e-36e0-42a6-94b6-e582fa234cc3'), 'The type of mask seen in the film being worn by Safin (Rami Malek) is known as a "Noh" mask. They are made by carving from blocks of Japanese cypress and then later painted with natural pigments. The similarity of the words ''''No'''' and ''''Noh'''' contributed to the belief prior to release that Malik''s character was a new incarnation of classic Bond villain Dr. Julius No', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da23d946-8970-45e1-ad51-6b78df25657d'), 'Christoph Waltz''s return as villain Ernst Stavro Blofeld was supposed to be a secret and a surprise for moviegoers. However, he was spotted on the lot at Pinewood Studios during principal photography, where Waltz allegedly said to some passersby, something like "You haven''t seen me". Once the secret was out, Waltz''s appearance in the movie became part of the picture''s publicity and promotion, with him appearing in credits and trailers', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('20c91e8a-f9f8-4adb-8969-9c20fcae08fb'), 'The official launch and announcement for the film took place at GoldenEye in Jamaica, once the home of Ian Fleming, where he created the James Bond character in 1952. Ian Fleming wrote twelve novels and two collections of short stories on the island. GoldenEye is owned and operated by Island Outpost, founded by Chris Blackwell who formerly owned Island Records. GoldenEye was not used as a filming location for the movie, but key creatives and principal cast did stay at GoldenEye for this launch event and during the Jamaican leg of the shoot', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87c7626d-29a7-4fda-ad9a-dd97173ff489'), 'Paloma''s gown, designed by Michael Lo Sordo, was chosen as her costume by the costume department (Suttirat Larlarb told Vogue) because it allowed her to fight without restriction while still being elegant enough to wear to a black-tie event', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4ea2a096-f5b4-4d86-8c7a-45b8c0aee6f4'), 'This is the first James Bond movie to be shot with an IMAX Camera. Previous Bond films exhibited in IMAX theaters were converted by up-scaling to the IMAX format i.e. they were optimized for IMAX theaters. This movie was also filmed with 65mm Panavision cameras', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d76e9d37-a5cf-4119-9a48-117e7bf30b11'), 'This film is Daniel Craig''s fifth and final appearance as James Bond. Released in 2021, the movie is also Craig''s 15th year in tenure as James Bond since his first in Casino Royale (2006). By tenure, this makes Craig the longest running actor playing James Bond in the official series. Connery''s tenure is the longest if one counts the period between ''Dr. No'' (1962) and the unofficial ''Never Say Never Again'' (1983), albeit with breaks, totaling a 21 year time-span', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('07520a81-28c8-4cc0-8e15-8f268be43fc2'), 'One the most emotional moments during the shoot came when James Bond actor Daniel Craig''s final scenes and last day filming were shot. These were, fittingly, shot at Pinewood Studios, the traditional home of the Bond films. Producer Michael G. Wilson recalled the feeling on set by saying: "It was late at night and usually people go home when they''re done but everyone came on set. It wasn''t a party atmosphere exactly but it was a special moment and people wanted to be there. They called ''Wrap!'' and Daniel said some beautiful words and everyone was tearful and hugging. We were all sorry to see this era end. It was very emotional for the crew"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d090f45-42fe-4dfa-9046-d2bfd22085a6'), 'David Dencik''s role as the Russian scientist Obruchev was originally supposed to be smaller, but director Cary Joji Fukunagi enjoyed Dencik''s performance so much that he expanded the role and looked for ways to keep the character in the film longer', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4436bb32-ccf2-4300-97e6-ef3fa82316f7'), 'All three James Bond movies to film in Jamaica: Dr. No (1962), Live and Let Die (1973), and No Time to Die (2021), have featured the CIA agent Felix Leiter. He is played in each of these films by different actors; Jack Lord, David Hedison, and Jeffrey Wright respectively. Thunderball (1965), which was also filmed in the Caribbean, featured Rik Van Nutter as Felix', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4ca6d1a4-229d-479d-af23-c83918a2f1de'), 'Daniel Craig told GQ magazine that there were "four versions of the ''No Time to Die'' script [that] came and went during the movie''s development"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('000ea11f-b567-458f-8751-f5f4a96c0003'), 'Phoebe Waller-Bridge was a late addition to the screenwriting team, following several delays in production including the replacement of director Danny Boyle with Cary Joji Fukunaga. In interviews, Daniel Craig has denied rumors that Waller-Bridge was added to the writing team for reasons of gender inclusiveness and making the script more feminist. He insisted that she was invited at his own request because he considers her a great writer, and wanted her input in sharpening the script and punching up the dialogue', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2db9db02-bd5b-4fc2-aab0-201e4097f59c'), 'Despite Skyfall (2012) being shot entirely in digital, and rumors that Bond movies would be shot digitally from then on, Spectre (2015) was shot on 35mm film and No Time to Die (2021) on 65 mm', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2bce2bbe-547f-4797-a131-ec338f94acae'), 'Originally, the movie''s antagonist, Lyutsifer Safin, had an associate henchman, and they were to both wear masks based on Siberian bear-hunting armour. These masks are spiked and somewhat resemble the ''Hellraiser'' character, ''Pinhead.'' Ultimately, the henchman character was written out, and new director Cary Joji Fukunaga wanted changes to Safin''s costume, including a new mask, as the spiked hunting mask dominated the costume. A new mask based on the Noh from Japanese theatre replaced the spiked Siberian hunting mask', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('60b4b916-b399-447e-9aac-34ad62baa6e5'), 'Rami Malek nearly didn''t get the part of Safin as his agents didn''t bother to respond to phone calls from the producers. It was casting director Debbie McWilliams who managed to meet him and secured the invitation to audition when she attended a preview screening of Malek''s hit film, Bohemian Rhapsody (2018). He agreed to the role on the condition that he didn''t want Safin to be an ethnic-religious terrorist and a cackling megalomaniac, which he felt was too much of a stereotype', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e1421f08-9c8a-4156-83f5-7a8778f25226'), 'Daniel Craig helped design Bond''s exclusive Swiss "Omega Seamaster Diver 300M" watch for this, his final film as 007. The watch comes in two editions: one with a NATO style strap for $8,100, and the more expensive one with a titanium mesh bracelet for $9,200 (RRP). Bond has steadfastly worn the Omega Seamaster since GoldenEye (1995), the Swiss company''s longest-running line', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9799dea1-a71d-4358-ba99-0313680dc601'), 'Composer Hans Zimmer replaced director Cary Joji Fukunaga''s regular music composer Dan Romer during late 2019 due to creative differences. According to show-business trade paper ''Variety'', this picture "marks the first time in the 58-year history of Bond films that a composer has been replaced during post-production"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7b107111-4745-444a-8440-8ba17fdb886a'), 'Longest pre-titles sequence in the official James Bond film series running at about 24 minutes before the opening titles roll. With its boat chase down the River Thames, the 14 to 15 minutes previous record holder had been ''The World is Not Enough'' (1999), which held the title for around twenty-two years. That opening pre-credits sequence was so long that in theaters the opening song and titles didn''t run until about one minute into the second reel', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d5b7f767-08fd-4b0a-bd7e-c1383cd1b7ee'), 'Lashana Lynch had not watched any of the Bond films prior to taking part in this one. So, once her casting had been confirmed, she did precisely that and watched all of them during her preparations for the role, starting from the very beginning with ''Dr. No'' (1962) right up to ''Spectre'' (2015)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a1edc432-bb6d-4121-952b-b9c527a0290f'), 'Eight stunt replicas of the classic James Bond silver-birch gun-metal gray car, the Aston Martin DB5, were especially designed and constructed for this movie. Two of the vehicles housed a mine dispenser and machine guns, while another two could be controlled by stunt drivers sitting in a cage on the roof while the actors were inside as the cars sped along. James Bond actor Daniel Craig commented: "It''s great to have the DB5 again. It was returned to Bond in ''Spectre'' [2015] and is now in perfect condition... with a few added extras"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e773da38-e05c-4b4b-95ac-74eb70fc58f7'), 'Third time actor Jeffrey Wright has played the Felix Leiter character and the first appearance of the character in the series since ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008) which is an interval of about a twelve years. In reprising the role, Wright is the first actor to play the character in three James Bond movies. Previously, Wright was tied with actor David Hedison as the only actors to play Leiter twice. Wright previously played Leiter in ''Casino Royale'' (2006) and ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8e4d4335-427f-4412-aad1-aaf674bb1dea'), 'Cary Joji Fukunaga replaced Danny Boyle as the film''s director about three months before the start of principal photography. On Thursday 20th September 2018 it was announced that Cary Joji Fukunaga will direct the 25th Bond film. Boyle, the previous director signed to the project, had left one month earlier on 21st August of that year. Many directors were considered for replacement, with the short-list rumored to include Jean-Marc Vallée, David Mackenzie, Denis Villeneuve, Yann Demange, Edward Berger, and Edgar Wright. Fukunaga is known for his directorial work on the first season of True Detective (2014), Beasts of No Nation (2015), and Netflix limited series Maniac (2018), which premiered the day after his announcement', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('51e2b190-416e-4c75-a51c-7ecf0205b379'), 'Reportedly, both this Bond movie and the previous film Spectre (2015) are not based on any original Ian Fleming James Bond story. However, ''No Time to Die'' (2021) features some story elements from ''Dr No'', ''You Only Live Twice'' and ''On Her Majesty''s Secret Service''. The opening title sequence from ''Spectre'' was inspired by ''Live and Let Die'' whilst ''Spectre'' also featured story elements from both ''Octopussy'' (the name Oberhauser) and ''The Hildebrand Rarity'' (for the Hildebrand Safe House)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a7ce9357-81ba-4929-8e4a-1f98460b5827'), 'The Matera location in Italy, which is featured in the pre-credits action sequence in this film, reportedly was actually first location scouted for the pre-titles sequence for the earlier Daniel Craig James Bond movie ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008). Both of the sequences feature car chases. Another Daniel Craig James Bond, ''Spectre'' (2015) also features a car chase in Italy', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('da66c4fd-086d-45d2-ac42-280b260338b9'), 'The visually outstanding bridge where Bond, Madeleine and Mathilde first pass the enemies in their cars, is Storseisundbrua ("the Storseisundet Bridge"), world famous for its peculiar shape that creates an illusion for approaching motorists that it ends in nothingness. For this, it has been called "The Bridge to Nowhere" and "the drunk bridge"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('919567ac-b4d3-42d4-b703-8edf9a506504'), 'First James Bond movie to feature four different models of Aston Martin vehicles. The cars are the classic 1964 silver-birch Aston Martin DB5, the classic 1985 Cumberland grey Aston Martin V8, the 2018 Aston Martin DBS Superleggera and the new forthcoming 2020 mid-engine hypercar the Aston Martin Valhalla', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d6437824-1c18-4a5e-8819-ed833050dd62'), 'Of the movie''s ''No Time to Die'' title, producer Barbara Broccoli has said: "We were struggling to find a title. We wanted a title that wouldn''t give away anything but would be understandable, and after you see the movie, have a deeper resonance, because that''s often what [Ian] Fleming titles are all about"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('22cee8ee-4afb-4a36-88de-79c1a771752c'), 'Filmmaker Cary Joji Fukunaga is the first film director of a James Bond movie in the official film series to receive a writing credit for a Bond movie which they directed whilst Phoebe Waller-Bridge is the second female screenwriter credited for writing on a James Bond film after Irish screenwriter Johanna Harwood for both Dr. No (1962) and From Russia with Love (1963)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e7b26e09-7529-4565-a554-1b7a8174ff42'), 'Financing and distribution arrangements for this picture and Spectre (2015) have frequently been reported together suggesting that development of these two Bond films are being set up for a two-year cycle, with No Time to Die (2021) originally targeted for a 2017 release, then pushed back to 2019, and once again to 2020. Reportedly, Daniel Craig has previously stated that there was a plan by the MGM studio to film two Bond movies back-to-back but he had balked at the idea due to the enormity of their productions', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5f19bddf-aef2-4a81-bca8-578386c940b9'), 'The interior design of the ground floor bar of the ''''El Nido'''' Bar of the old grand hotel in Havana, Cuba was inspired by the classic ''''Nighthawks'''' (1942) oil on canvas painting by Edward Hopper. The bar is featured in the film when Bond (Daniel Craig) has a drink with Paloma (Ana de Armas) during the Cuban sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('65d50a5d-468f-453c-92c2-011e0c727ad2'), 'Producer Barbara Broccoli has said of this Bond movie: "Bond is not on active service when we start the film. He''s enjoying himself while in Jamaica, start his journey here. We built a extraordinary house for him. Five hundred local people are working on the film already"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d56ae6be-a384-4670-861a-4753792b88c8'), 'The name of the Cuban night-club in Havana, Cuba was the ''''El Nido Bar''''. The words ''''El Nido'''' are Spanish and translates into the English language as ''''The Nest''''. Set Decorator Véronique Melery has said: "This hotel was a composite set, with a grand entrance, a theatre, a ballroom, and some bars. The feeling of this place is of an old palace, all faded glory. The frescoes'' patina lends to the nostalgic atmosphere, and the elegance of the dated Art Deco furniture shows signs of age, like so many places in Cuba"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d886c0db-0c1a-46ff-8441-7d698effd2e7'), 'In James Bond''s home in Jamaica there is a replica of creator Ian Fleming''s writing desk in the corner of the bedroom. The real desk however resides in Jamaica at Fleming''s Villa at the Goldeneye Resort in Oracabessa, Jamaica', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('f1c2245f-7364-478b-ba12-e9d154d6920b'), 'Daniel Craig is the only actor to play James Bond who is never seen smoking in the movie. Though there is the appearance of ''Delectado'' cigars at his Jamaican home in ''No Time to Die'' (2021). His iteration of the character though was the first time Agent 007 was seen drunk on screen which was in ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('122957c9-1f43-41db-9222-cbec7ef2c522'), 'The name of the Italian town featured in the film where James Bond (Daniel Craig) and Madeleine Swann (Léa Seydoux) stay at the "Palazzo Lucareschi" hotel and later go to a train station is "Civita Lucana". Both these Italian place names are fictional and do not exist in real life. In the movie, "Civita Lucana" is portrayed by the town of Sapri in Salerno, Campania, Italy whilst the "Palazzo Lucareschi" hotel was comprised of two set constructions. These hotel scenes were filmed in Italy at Matera in Basilicata at the "Rione Pianelle" (for the lobby entry) and the "Piazetta Pascoli" (for the hotel room with balcony)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ce3c7e61-74bc-4f9b-9cc4-657e8cddc996'), 'About five days before the film''s world premiere, actor Daniel Craig was made an honorary Commander in the British Royal Navy. The rank matches that of James Bond in the novels and movies whilst the filmmakers worked closely with them and the Ministry of Defence in the production of the picture. Commander Craig''s appointment as an Honorary Officer was made to reflect his personal support for Her Majesty''s Armed Forces and links it with the legacy created through the guise of the famous fictional British secret agent. Commander Craig has stated that he is keen to support personnel with the Royal Navy with a particular interest in service families. Commander Craig said: "I am truly privileged and honoured to be appointed the rank of Honorary Commander in the senior service." The word ''commander'' actually features in a working title of an Ian Fleming Bond novel. That was for the other ''No'' titled Bond story - ''Dr. No'' - and it was ''Commander Jamaica'' - and it''s a popular title amongst fans for being be used one day as a James Bond movie title. ''No Time to Die'' (2021) features Jamaica as a setting and filming location and in the film Bond in Jamaica is called Commander by Nomi (Lashana Lynch). As such, there is a little bit of ''Commander Jamaica'' in ''No Time to Die'' (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2cf37834-720f-4433-9176-ac0b30b436d3'), 'Jamaican actress Grace Jones, who starred as May Day in A View to a Kill (1985), was going to make a cameo appearance in this film during the Jamaica scenes, however she quit shortly after shooting began upon learning how small her part was. Two of this movie''s actresses: Lashana Lynch and Naomie Harris, are of Jamaican descent', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('21a5ce75-187f-40d3-8c71-15823fa8e897'), 'With the announcement of Christoph Waltz returning to play Ernst Stavro Blofeld, this marks the first time in fifty-four years that an actor (the uncredited Anthony Dawson before) played the SPECTRE mastermind more than once', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b6c815fd-e053-45ae-afd2-ef1cd790493b'), 'Most expensive James Bond movie ever with a budget of about US $250 million beating previous Bond movie record holder of ''Spectre'' (2015) which had a budget of around US $245 million', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6eb2d254-143e-4761-bb12-033137bf9966'), 'In March 2021, the movie''s title ''No Time to Die'' song won the Grammy for Best Song written for Visual Media making it the first time that a Grammy has been awarded in this category for a film that has not even been released. The song is sung by Billie Eilish and was written by her and Finneas O''Connell who both won the Grammy. The ceremony was held on 14th March 2021 approximately 7 months prior to the film''s North American release date of 8th October 2021', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3cdb2e36-26ec-4cfa-8c7a-b70f48907fd5'), 'During principal photography, actor Rami Malek had to wear a wig to portray the arch-villain Lyutsifer Safin because he was still shooting the fourth and final season of the television series ''Mr. Robot'' (2015-2019) and had to hide his haircut for his Elliot Alderson character', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('12bb525e-5d38-4b61-b200-6cae89fcb2a0'), 'According to IndieWire, this movie "will go large-format with 65mm Panavision and IMAX 65mm (to shoot the action sequences) for the first time in the series'' history"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('25976e72-4759-4fdf-887f-dbcb7a0fdb95'), 'The seventh screenplay for a James Bond movie written by regular Bond screenwriters Neal Purvis, and Robert Wade. Their first was for The World Is Not Enough (1999)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('825c3566-9d3c-48ab-8c25-ef1288ea2771'), 'The name of the drink that James Bond in retirement pours at his home in Jamaica is "Blackwell''s Rum". The beverage makes its film debut in a James Bond movie in ''No Time to Die'' (2021). The rum is produced by Chris Blackwell who was a location scout on ''Dr. No'' (1962). In 1956, Fleming met Chris'' mother, Blanche Blackwell, who lived next door. They became close friends and Chris became a location scout in 1961 for ''Dr. No'' (1962) upon Fleming''s recommendation. Chris and his mother spent many afternoons at Goldeneye, enjoying lunch in Fleming''s sunken garden and swimming in the crystalline lagoon. Of the rum in the film, Chris Blackwell said: "This is a rum that celebrates Jamaica, my friendships, and also my family legacy." The involvement of the Blackwell family with the 25th James Bond film ''No Time to Die'' (2021) has made this very special relationship between Bond and Blackwell in existence since ''Dr No'' (1962) now come full circle with ''No Time To Die'' (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0d09f9ed-bb18-4d4f-a783-9c5db7fd3d1a'), 'First James Bond film to feature a major leading Bond Girl from Cuba with the casting of Cuban born actress Ana de Armas who plays Paloma', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('87768308-11fc-4acb-8bd7-caccc9f052cd'), 'The name of the French hand-made knitted woolen stuffed toy rabbit teddy doll that Mathilde (Lisa-Dorah Sonnet) had in the film was a "doudou" or ''''dou dou''''. This is a French word which translates into the English language as ''''blankie''''. It is manufactured by a French company entitled "Une Pelote de Laine". Reportedly, sales for the French toy went up after the movie came out', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1931c703-b0ab-4e0d-8622-76a94621e0f0'), 'S.P.E.C.T.R.E. Agents in the earlier Bond films often wore a gold "Ring of Evil". According to the book "James Bond: The Secret World of 007" (2006) by Alastair Dougall, "Top operatives of S.P.E.C.T.R.E., and (Ernst Stavro) Blofeld himself, could sometimes be recognized by a distinctive octopus ring, which symbolized the organization''s tentacular reach into the murkiest depths of world crime"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('372b0b13-29b7-44a5-aa9f-d12809ddc72e'), 'Andy Serkis was rumored to be replacing Christoph Waltz as Blofeld if Daniel Craig didn''t come back for this film, assuming the Blofeld character would be in this movie, as Waltz has reportedly stated that he won''t play Blofeld again without Craig also playing James Bond. Reportedly, on 26th October 2017, Waltz said to Italian film website ''Talky Movie'' on the red carpet at the Festa del Cinema di Roma, that he would not be returning as Blofeld for this movie and said: "No, I''m sorry. I''m really sad, but that''s the tradition, that there is a new...name. Sorry. I would''ve liked to." However, in the end, Waltz did return to play Blofeld in this picture', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ebfe57bb-8988-42de-bdf8-71a7ef45a7cd'), 'Rami Malek didn''t want his character to be purely Russian, so he decided that Safin should be speaking in an ambiguous accent but based his character on an amalgam of several personalities including former Ukrainian president Viktor Yushchenko (scarred face from poisoning, slow deliberate movements) and former tennis player Marat Safin (name). The scarred face makeup required 2.5 hours to apply daily', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4238fbf3-add3-4ef4-b898-647dfbccee21'), 'In the French version, Léa Seydoux (Madeleine) and Dali Bensallah (Cyclops) dubbed themselves. Ms Seydoux also provides her dialogue in her native language in scenes with Lisa-Dorah Sonnet who plays her daughter', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9d61bde9-1ea4-4ff5-b521-73dfc82aae98'), 'On 21st August 2018, star Daniel Craig and producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson, announced via the official James Bond Twitter account, that due to creative differences, the film''s director Danny Boyle had decided to no longer direct ''Bond 25'', later named as ''No Time to Die'' (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('203ab94e-3d9d-4801-9846-31795b25ee0a'), 'The film was much rumoured to be called "Shatterhand" as this was the picture''s official working title. This was not the first Bond-themed film to have this title. Shatterhand (2012) was a James Bond tribute film which debuted in the same year as Skyfall (2012). Other official Bond movies that share titles with previous Bond-related movies include GoldenEye (1995), which shares its title with a TV movie about Ian Fleming, Goldeneye (1989) (aka "The Man with the Golden Pen"); and Casino Royale (2006), of which there had been two earlier versions, Casino Royale (1967) and Casino Royale (1954). Since, Bond producer Barbara Broccoli has confirmed ''Shatterhand'' will not be the title of this movie. In the Fleming novels "Shatterhand" is an alias used by Ernst Stavro Blofeld', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('25eb810f-8e9e-4c6f-9d1c-9279f0602200'), 'The British Royal Air Force (RAF) granted access to key assets and personnel to the production. RAF Brize Norton, in Oxfordshire, was used as a backdrop in the film, standing in for a NATO airbase in Norway, where James Bond (Daniel Craig) joins MI6 allies and later boards a C-17 Globemaster aircraft. Meanwhile, for the production, the British Army supplied troops from the Household Cavalry. They offered their time at a pivotal moment in their calendar, just before the Changing of the Guard at Buckingham Palace in London, England', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5c74a801-9bee-4198-b759-863c6f5fab49'), 'When actress Lashana Lynch first auditioned for the role of Nomi and a Double-O Agent she has stated that she did not initially know she was auditioning for a Bond movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('db843920-81a4-4169-8239-b80f9430c3be'), 'In Jamaica, James Bond discovers that someone has been in his home smoking a cigar. He finds one there and notices that it is a ''Delectado''. According to ''Cigars of the Silver Screen'' published by Alexanders Cigars Merchants, ''in a very British take on the genre, in [the earlier Bond movie] ''Die Another Day'', Bond [Pierce Brosnan] visits a Cuban cigar factory ostensibly asking for a Delectado cigar whilst searching for a sleeper agent. At the time the movie was made there was no such thing as a Delectado but of course there is now.'' Both ''Die Another Day'' (2002) and ''No Time to Die'' (2021) feature Cuba as a setting as does ''GoldenEye'' (1995)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('3d4824be-475a-4daa-a314-11cc2fc23965'), 'First motion picture feature film of stunt driver Jessica Hawkins who was hand picked by stunt coordinator Lee Morrison who had scouted her from the Formula 3 W Series. She said: "It doesn''t get any more exhilarating than being a stunt driver in a James Bond movie and it''s an honour to be a part of this incredible movie driving the new Defender"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d79f244c-29c4-4796-a307-c45d9ffd6614'), 'The warship seen in the film is portrayed by the British Royal Navy vessel HMS Dragon. The ship filmed its scenes for the film prior to the pandemic in The Solent. A Royal Navy spokesman declared though ''''no weapons were fired during the filming'''' of the movie indicating that any missiles fired in the film were the result of VFX and CGI. The 152 metre Portsmouth-based ship is a Daring-class Type 45 air-defence destroyer and has a gigantic red dragon emblem on its hull. In actual use, it performs weapons operation, helicopter maintenance, long-range air target searching and long-distance target engagement. Ten of the Dragon''s crew attended the Royal World Premiere Charity Benefit of ''No Time to Die'' (2021) on 28th September 2021 where images of the ship were shown on big screens over the red carpet and about fifty musicians from the Portsmouth Band of the Royal Marines played at the end of the live cross', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('bf5c74f1-fdb8-47ee-a462-2421cd6988c2'), 'Kenyan-Mexican actress Lupita Nyong''o was reportedly sought for a role in the James Bond movie ''No Time to Die'' (2021) but was unavailable due to scheduling conflicts as she was contractually committed to both ''The 355'' and ''The Killer''. The relevant part is believed to have been filled by actress Lashana Lynch who played Nomi', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ec4152d6-76c6-4459-b942-da4535605620'), 'Prince Charles visited the set at Pinewood Studios on 20th June 2019 where he met with star Daniel Craig, producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson, director Cary Joji Fukunaga, cast members Ralph Fiennes, Naomie Harris, and Lashana Lynch, special effects head Chris Corbould, and various other dignitaries, studio heads and crew members. He was shown two Aston Martin vehicles - the traditional gun metal grey DB5, and the 1985 5.3 litre Aston Martin V8 Vantage, last seen in the series in ''The Living Daylights'' (1987). It was for this earlier James Bond film, which was the last time that Prince Charles visited a James Bond set, in 1986, with Princess Diana, where they met actor Timothy Dalton, who was playing James Bond at the time', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c7321e42-a614-4490-99d4-fa6e8d1ef520'), 'The breed of Q''s two cats seen in the film are Hairless Egyptian Sphynx cats which are the same breed as the cat Mr. Bigglesworth in the ''Austin Powers'' spy spoof series. Mr. Bigglesworth himself is a cat spoof of Blofeld''s Cat from the Bond series whose breed is a blue-eyed white-haired Chinchilla Turkish Angora Persian cat. Blofeld''s Cat actually appears in a starring role in a ''No Time to Die'' (2021) tie-in advert. In ''Meow'' (2020) (V), aka the ''Royal Mail James Bond Stamps ''No Time to Die'' Television Commercial'', Blofeld''s Cat has his first ever starring role in an official Bond video in a comic commercial promoting a series of James Bond stamps. Ironically, the name of the director of the commercial is Austen Humphries', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('6ca42bfb-db14-4181-84fa-59450729630d'), 'Nomi''s ( Lashana Lynch ) rectangular sunglasses are a nod to former A View to a Kill (1985) Bond girl Grace Jones, who wore a similar pair of sunglasses in one of her music videos', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d1cb896b-c3cd-4979-875f-ddde1fb66904'), 'Actor Christoph Waltz, who appeared as Ernst Stavro Blofeld in ''Spectre'' (2015), has said multiple times ever since that movie that he wasn''t interested in returning in a future James Bond movie, if Daniel Craig didn''t return. When Craig announced that he would return for ''No Time to Die'' (2021), Waltz later changed his mind in late-2017 and said he wasn''t interested in returning at all, because he felt his character had served his purpose in the James Bond story. On 13th July 2019, Waltz had a change of heart again, as it was confirmed that he would in fact return as Blofeld in ''No Time to Die'' (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9e474c7d-2e12-4463-842a-624d5e9a7adf'), 'The film features the first ever female 00 agent character in the official James Bond series. The character is Nomi portrayed by actress Lashana Lynch, who in a 21 January 2020 interview on Entertainment Weekly''s video special ''Around the Table with No Time to Die'' (2020) stated clearly that she portrays a 00 agent in this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('767c0766-efdc-4fff-8bde-cac7cf0be98e'), 'No Time to Die (2021) cost roughly 250 times more than the first James Bond movie. Dr. No (1962) cost about £800,000, while No Time to Die (2021), according to May 2020 UK newspaper reports, was at the £200 million mark', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('4073cdf3-24a6-42d9-9c75-1d29eca837bf'), 'Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer produces the James Bond movies but does not generally theatrically release them. The agreement between MGM and Sony expired with Spectre (2015). Originally it was a two picture deal with Casino Royale (2006) and Quantum of Solace (2008) for Sony to distribute which then got renewed for two more films of which Skyfall (2012) was the first. At the time of the theatrical release of Spectre (2015), MGM was in discussions with three studios, which were believed to be Sony, Paramount and Warner Bros. Reportedly, it was stated that MGM was looking for a more lucrative deal, and was looking to drive a hard bargain. In the end, Universal Pictures became this film''s worldwide distributor on 24th May 2018', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5d2505ad-ef82-45e6-8bd6-dfce4e4abc4a'), 'The "Safin" name of Rami Malek''s villain character in the film is of Arabic origin. Its meaning is "Boat". It is a male name for a boy and can also be spelled "Safeen". Actor Rami Malek actually has ancestry from an Arab country (Egypt) and was raised until the age of four being able to speak colloquial Masri, which is Egyptian Arabic. Malek is the second actor with ancestry from an Arab country to win the Academy Award (Oscar) for Best Actor. F. Murray Abraham, who won for ''Amadeus'' (1984), was the first, whilst Malek won about 34 years later for ''Bohemian Rhapsody'' (2018)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ce778bb5-18f9-4aa0-80ba-7519ea6e5a7c'), 'The film''s title song sung by Billie Eilish broke the record for the biggest ever opening week for a James Bond theme/title song in the UK. The track sold about 90,000 copies in its first week of seven days in release and also had 10.6 million streams in the same, racing to the UK No. #1 spot on the pop charts. Previously, Sam Smith''s theme song from Spectre (2015), entitled ''Writing''s On The Wall'', held the record, selling almost 70,000 copies when it debuted in late 2015, also hitting the UK No. #1 spot on the music single charts. Adele''s title song for ''Skyfall'' (2012) sold about 84,000 copies when it debuted in late 2012 which at the time made it to the UK No. #2 rank on the UK top of the pops chart', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7cc9b72f-f2b0-4964-a2ae-ed8f95f23d3d'), 'Producers Barbara Broccoli and Michael G. Wilson did state after Spectre (2015)''s theatrical release that they felt reasonably confident that Daniel Craig would return for this movie', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('40461fab-a133-4ce7-bcad-17fe51590e4c'), 'First James Bond movie in the official series since ''Dr. No'' (1962) where Jamaican scenes were filmed on location. ''Dr. No.'' (1962) was the first James Bond movie in the official series. The interval between the two pictures is fifty-eight years. In ''Live and Let Die'' (1973), Jamaica was the filming location for the fictitious state of "San Monique"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('9825514b-8a4f-490b-a214-c0d119b75d12'), 'The total number of production crew personnel that worked on this picture amounted to about 650', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('ab87076a-2290-452a-993f-5402c3c8d86e'), 'An accident during the shoot occurred when three explosions accidentally went off on the set at the 007 Stage at Pinewood Studios in Buckinghamshire. Reportedly, part of the 007 Stage roof fell off, as well as some wall panels. One crew member suffered minor injuries. The official press release stated: "During the filming of a controlled explosion on the set of ''Bond 25'' today at Pinewood Studios, damage was caused to the exterior of the 007 Stage. There were no injuries on set, however one crew member outside the stage has sustained a minor injury." A source told ''The Sun'' newspaper that ''''there were three loud explosions, one after another, and a member of the crew was lying on the floor outside the building injured." It reported that the stunt was being rehearsed wherein "a fireball was supposed to go through the set." However, apparently things went "horribly wrong". ''The Sun'' reported that "part of the roof and some wall panels were blown off in the explosion misfire"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('8cd7bdaa-243c-4069-8a5c-9cb1bd1d1b2e'), 'There were no changes made to the new Land Rover Defender vehicles seen in the movie except for the use of safety roll cages for the drivers. Nick Collins, Vehicle Line Director for Jaguar Land Rover Defender, said of the New Land Road Defender vehicles seen in the movie: "We developed a new test standard for Defender, the most challenging we''ve ever had and unique to this vehicle. Physical strength and durability is measured by a number of different tests including a bridge jump test which gave us confidence to deliver what the stunt team needed to create for ''No Time To Die'', with no modifications to the body structure except the installation of a roll cage"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('dff5f723-fd80-4b63-b3db-259fa658f970'), 'Third James Bond movie to film in Norway. The first was ''You Only live Twice'' (1967) where the exterior of the Russian radar station was filmed at Mågerø in Norway for that Bond movie''s opening sequence. The second was ''Die Another Day'' (2002) where Spitsbergen in Svalbard, Norway was used for filming ice cliffs for a cgi plate. Additional filming was also conducted at the Jostedal Glacier National Park in Luster, Sogn og Fjordane, Norway for the ice car chase and the ice palace environs. However, this third time filming in Norwayfor a Bond film is the first time that Norway is featuring as a central major filming location in a Bond movie as the amount of filming for the earlier two Bond films shot in Norway was only minimal', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7a46a62c-2aae-41fb-9666-9d2833d47d92'), 'This film was the first major movie production scheduled to open in 2020 that had to move its release date due to the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic. The release date changed three or four times and in the end the picture premiered on 28th September 2021', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('c2a8d19b-8c28-486b-abf5-55fdb2df4460'), 'Where once the James Bond films played as separate adventures, linked by characters both malevolent and benign, EON Productions wanted the Daniel Craig series to unfold as a unified whole. ''Quantum Of Solace'' (2008) picked up immediately after ''Casino Royale'' (2006), which had tracked Bond''s initiation into the life of a Double-O agent. ''Skyfall'' (2012) slotted into the series to reveal important aspects of Bond''s early life. Now, the 25th film in the EON series, ''No Time To Die'', begins in the aftermath of ''Spectre'' (2015) where the film''s conclusion saw Bond (Craig) and Madeleine Swann (Léa Seydoux) drive away in the Aston Martin DB5', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('0770ebf0-155c-445b-b6ec-c040f638a352'), 'Cars and road vehicles featured in the film include Bond''s classic 1964 silver-birch Aston Martin DB5 gadget-car; Bond''s Cumberland grey 1985 Aston Martin V8 Vantage Mark IV previously seen in The Living Daylights (1987); a 2020 Aston Martin Valkyrie; the forthcoming mid-engine Aston Martin Valkyrie hypercar seen behind M in a wind tunnel; Nomi''s new model Aston Martin DBS Superleggera coupé; numerous black Land Rover Defender 110 SUVs; Bond''s old Toyota Land Cruiser Prado J90; 2018 Land Rover Range Rover Sport SVRs; Classic 1987 Range Rover ORVs; Bond''s old blue Land Rover Series III off-road vehicle; Triumph Tiger 900 Rally Pro motor-bikes; a 2019 Triumph Scrambler 1200 XE motor-cycle which jumps over the tall wall; 2016 black Jaguar XF saloon sedans; Paloma''s old 1957 Chevrolet Bel Air sedan, a 1994 Maserati Quattroporte IV sedan in the bridge attack; a blue 2006 Citroën C3 Série 1 hatchback; a black 2002 Lancia Thesis sedan; a red 1974 Dino 308 GT4 Ferrari coupé; small white Soviet Lada Riva 1600 sedan marked patrol cars (aka VAZ-2106 aka Zhiguli 2106); a grey 1950 Cadillac Fleetwood 60 Special sedan; and Nomi''s white Royal Alloy GT 125 scooter in Jamaica', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2a4527df-e338-4096-baed-29ca5c711e8a'), 'In January 2020, it was announced that Billie Eilish would write and perform the film''s theme song. Being just 18 at the time, this makes her the youngest artist in the history of the Bond series to do so', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('b8a88e00-1593-4594-84e4-f80154f16c81'), 'Reportedly, the movie would apparently have cost another UK £47million if it had not been for a producers'' tax incentive scheme which was targeted for making movies at UK-based film studios', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('43dc84a2-f977-4cc0-aa90-fcbc647b2cbe'), 'Key creatives and principal cast and crew stayed at James Bond creator Ian Fleming''s renowned ''Goldeneye'' resort during the production shoot during filming the movie in Jamaica', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d7e4254d-faca-4ab8-9508-8ef55ab92bb1'), 'Featuring in the pre-credits sequence in this Bond movie is the Italian stone city of Matera, which is, according to TV Tropes, "a rare instance of [a] non-Italian film where the city appears as itself"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('1516ec7f-555b-4734-97bf-49e1953f5d5b'), 'At 163 minutes, this is the longest James Bond film by approximately 13 minutes, beating out Spectre (2015)''s 150 minutes. At two hours and twenty-four minutes, Casino Royale (2006) was once the longest James Bond movie, beating the previous record holder On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969) by four minutes, until the release of Spectre (2015), which beat it by another four minutes. Spectre (2015) was recently the longest James Bond movie record holder, with a running time of two hours and twenty-eight minutes. Daniel Craig has now played Bond in the four longest Bond movies of all time: ''No Time to Die'' (2021), Spectre (2015), Skyfall (2012), and Casino Royale (2006). The former long-time record holder, On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), is now in fifth place, with Skyfall (2012) in fourth. Conversely, Daniel Craig has also starred in the shortest theatrical Bond film to date, Quantum of Solace (2008), which has a running time of only one hour and forty-six minutes, four minutes shorter than the second shortest movie, Dr. No (1962)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('56a76035-bb08-44b6-a2db-c3201f6852a3'), 'The New Defender Land Rover ''No Time to Die'' tie-in television commercial featured actual test and rehearsal footage used from a chase sequence in the movie. These are scenes where the vehicle drives through rivers and swamps and launches into the air', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('a3a62543-fb71-49dc-a029-c51a3f41302e'), 'For every one of Daniel Craig''s five James Bond films, there has never been a consistent returning gun-barrel walk sequence. In these, Craig''s Bond movies have only used the classic Maurice Binder graphics once. In each of the movies, a new gun-barrel walk sequence was filmed with the actor. In ''Casino Royale'' (2006), the sequence was worked into Bond''s first kill as a Double-O Agent. For ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008) and ''Skyfall'' (2012), the gun-barrel walk was moved from their traditional place right at the start of the film to just before the end credits roll. ''Spectre'' (2015)''s gun-barrel walk used the Binder graphics and were sequenced in their traditional opening spot. In ''No Time to Die'' (2021), the gun barrel sequence is still at the beginning but is uses CGI (computer generated imagery) for the contours graphics of the inside of the gun. There is no red blood falling colour at the end of the gun-shot component of the gun-barrel walk, the first time this has happened in the series. Further, it is also the first time in a Daniel Craig Bond movie that he is seen wearing a tuxedo during a gun-barrel walk sequence', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('2b33cde6-4359-4b8a-b5d4-5f4e17d2dd4d'), 'RAF Globemaster C17 callsign ZZ177 The RAF C17 seen in the film is also the same C17 that carried the UK''s Queen Elizabeth II coffin on her journey from Scotland to London for her state funeral in September 2022', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('7647e3b1-0508-4488-9f04-13c4ecf827c7'), 'The on-board yachting scenes in Jamaica with James Bond (Daniel Craig) sailing were not directed by the film''s director Cary Joji Fukanaga but by Spirit Yachts CEO and founder Sean McMillan whose company provided the 14 metre Spirit 46 yacht to the production. Boat International reported: "During filming McMillan was charged with directing Craig on board and ensuring Bond appeared a convincing experienced sailor. At times, this involved McMillan lying on the floor - out of shot - barking instructions up to Craig as the cameras rolled." McMillan said: "By the time you''ve got cameras, cameramen and sound-men on a very small boat, there''s not much room. Everybody just muddles on and gets along with it. There''s no real difficulty about it at all because everyone wants the same end goal"', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('e2c6f5ee-fe64-4ac6-979e-2b1318ad2219'), 'Despite the film extensively referencing the early Bond movie ''On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'' (1969) and its "All the Time in the World" music and dialogue, director Cary Joji Fukunaga, who admitted to having being a Bond series fan-boy, had not seen ''On Her Majesty''s Secret Service'' (1969) prior to directing ''No Time to Die'' (2021)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('5e8c9ffa-524d-42a8-9097-7cdcd254d075'), 'The movie''s title song secretly features an Easter Egg: the famous classic opening Bond sting from the many Bond theme songs. Singer Billie Eilish confirmed this Easter Egg in the track in the music episode of the ''No Time to Die'' Official Podcast. She said: "You can''t do a Bond song without it sounding like a Bond song. If you listen closely, you can hear [the Bond sting] in the second verse. It''s very subtle, and it''s very echoed. We decided to do that though." Her brother and the song''s producer Finneas O''Connell said: "It was recorded in London, and then like there was a version without [the Bond sting]. Then, we were like, put it back in, it''s great.'''' (A "sting" is a trademark set of notes. For this theme song, the four notes occur just after the second verse begins.)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('624b8b83-56de-4b86-ba65-97e76817b14e'), 'Fifth James Bond movie to film in Scotland. The fourth and most recent has been ''Skyfall'' (2012) which shot in the Highlands at Glencoe and Glen Etive. The first, From Russia with Love (1963), filmed at various locations in the Argyll and Bute region. The second, The Spy Who Loved Me (1977), filmed at the Faslane Naval base, whilst the third, The World Is Not Enough (1999), filmed at Eilean Donan Castle at Kyle of Lochalsh in the Highlands. ''No Time to Die'' (2021) is the sixth Bond film to shoot in Scotland, if one includes the unofficial Bond spoof Casino Royale (1967) which shot in Killin in Stirling. Sir Sean Connery, the first actor to play James Bond on the big screen, was a Scot. The Scottish Dalness Estate once belonged to the Fleming family and James Bond creator Ian Fleming loved the Scottish region so much that he gave the James Bond character a Scottish ancestry. The character''s father, Andrew, comes from Glencoe, where ''Skyfall'' (2012) filmed alongside the Buachaille Etive Mor mountain. In On Her Majesty''s Secret Service (1969), James Bond is seen wearing a kilt', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('09dfba1c-b7b5-480f-a9aa-31ea422ca3e9'), 'The theatrical release of this movie will mark the second longest hiatus in the official James Bond series. The interval between this picture and ''Spectre'' (2015) is five years and eleven months. The longest gap between Bond movies was six years and five months between ''Licence to Kill'' (1989) and ''Goldeneye'' (1995). The third longest interval, a four year gap, occurred twice, between ''Die Another Day'' (2002) and ''Casino Royale'' (2006), and once again, between ''Quantum of Solace'' (2008) and ''Skyfall'' (2012)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('d24ccd97-de37-4e6b-82e5-b026da596a5a'), 'The nick-name of Primo (Dali Benssalah) was "Cyclops". He is so named after the fact that he has one bionic eye and one normal eye. According to ''The Bond Bulletin'', "henchman Primo (Dali Benssalah) seems to have a fake eye, an idea that had previously been in the script for ''SPECTRE'' (2015)." In the earlier James Bond movie ''Casino Royale'' (2006), the henchman Gettler (Richard Sammel) wore eye-glasses with different shades - one clear and one dark', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('337d1e6a-e8a8-410e-af3d-95149d062eba'), 'No Time To Die marks the only Bond film in Craig''s era to not start the end credits with the James Bond Theme. As the song "We Have All The Time In The World" was played instead during the beginning of the credits', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6)),
(UUID_TO_BIN('379e2ad7-659f-4520-8335-2b2f9267002c'), 'To celebrate the return of James Bond''s iconic Aston Martin DB5 to the big screen in ''No Time to Die'' (2021), Aston Martin and Corgi unveiled a full-size replica of the original 1965 Corgi DB5 model. Located at The Coaling Jetty, outside Battersea Power Station, the life size model which measures 5.66 metres long, 2.7 metres tall and 2.7 metres deep, replicates the original Corgi design and houses a new Aston Martin DB5 Goldfinger Continuation car. The vehicle is complete with a broad selection of working gadgets, albeit the ejector seat, that fans will recognize from the classic James Bond films cand Thunderball (1965): a retractable bullet proof rear shield, pop out machine guns, extending front over-riders and of course rotating number plates. The DB5 also previously appeared in Skyfall (2012), where Bond nearly ejected an argumentative M and added machine guns behind the headlights like it was in Goldfinger (1964)', (SELECT id FROM movies WHERE title = 'No Time To Die'), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6), CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(6));
